ustom Laser Systems ][97]\n* [ Robotic Automation ][98] Go to child menu\n* Back\n* #### [Robotic Automation][99]\n* [Robotic Laser Systems ][100]\n* [Robotic Arc Welding Systems ][101]\n* [Robotic Arc/Laser Welding Systems ][102]\n* [Custom Robotic Laser Systems ][103]\n* [LightWELD Cobot System ][104]\n* [ Solutions ][105] Go to child menu\n* Back\n* #### [Solutions][106]\n* [E-Mobility Manufacturing ][107] Go to child menu\n* Back to Solutions\n* #### [E-Mobility Manufacturing][108]\n* [Battery Cells ][109]\n* [Battery Busbars ][110]\n* [Battery Packs ][111]\n* [Electric Motors ][112]\n* [Power Electronics ][113]\n* [Fuel Cells ][114]\n* [Materials Processing ][115] Go to child menu\n* Back to Solutions\n* #### [Materials Processing][116]\n* [Laser Cutting ][117]\n* [Laser Welding ][118]\n* [Laser Cleaning ][119]\n* [Laser Heating & Drying ][120]\n* [Laser Drilling ][121]\n* [Laser Additive Manufacturing ][122]\n* [Laser Marking ][123]\n* [Laser Cladding ][124]\n* [Laser Brazing ][125]\n* [Micromachining ][126]\n* [Advanced & Scientific Applications ][127]\n* [Application Development ][128] Go to child menu\n* Back to Solutions\n* #### [Application Development][129]\n* [Application Labs ][130]\n* [Custom Systems & Tooling ][131]\n* [Virtual Engineering & Simulation ][132]\n* [ Technology ][133] Go to child menu\n* Back\n* #### [Technology][134]\n* [IPG Innovation ][135]\n* [Fiber Laser 101 ][136]\n* [Single-Emitter Laser Diodes ][137]\n* [On-The-Fly Welding ][138]\n* [Real-Time Weld Measurement ][139]\n* [Dual-Beam Lasers ][140]\n* [High-Efficiency Lasers ][141]\n* [Deep-UV Lasers ][142]\n* [Ultrafast Lasers ][143]\n* [ Company ][144] Go to child menu\n* Back\n* #### [Company][145]\n* [About Us ][146]\n* [Our Leadership ][147]\n* [Careers ][148]\n* [Investors ][149]\n* [Newsroom ][150]\n* [Events ][151]\n* [Social Responsibility ][152]\n* [Locations ][153]\n* [Policies & Standards ][154]\n* [ Contact Us ][155]\n* [ Support ][156]\n[ India | EN ][157]\n* [Home][158]\n* [Solutions][159]\n* E-Mobility-Solutions\n[E-Mobility Manufacturing Solutions]\n\n## E-Mobility Manufacturing Solutions\n\nManufacturers of electric vehicles and the battery sources that enable them come to IPG for\nlaser-based manufacturing solutions. Covering the range of battery production steps from processing\nof electrode films through welding the structural components of the battery trays, IPG\u2019s technical\nleadership in the area of laser-material interactions allows us to provide industry-leading guidance\nand support to automotive manufacturers and their chosen production line integrators.\n\nWhether it is the unmatched power levels of pulsed foil cutting lasers, the unique capabilities of\nthe adjustable mode beam lasers for spatter-free welding of copper and aluminum, or patented\nreal-time weld measurement technology, IPG is continually working to optimize laser materials\nprocessing capabilities to keep you ahead of rapidly evolving e-mobility trends.\n\n[Li-ion Cell Manufacturing]\n\n#### Li-ion Cell Manufacturing\n\nDespite the differences between cylindrical, prismatic or pouch designs, cell manufacturing\ntypically relies on laser processing for the cutting and notching of foils, welding of the foil\nstacks to tabs, cell case injection hole sealing, safety valve welding, and cap-to-case sealing.\nTogether with emerging technologies such as laser drying of the electrode coating, these processes\nconsistently deliver the high speed and high yield required for high-volume Li-ion cell production.\n\n[Learn More][160]\n[Busbar Welding]\n\n#### Busbar Welding\n\nFor all battery cell technologies, whether cylindrical, prismatic or pouch, conductive busbars are\nused to connect individual cells into modules. Laser welding enables the creation of busbar-to-cell\nconnections that meet critically important electrical performance requirements while also offering\nunmatched production speed, reliability, and ease of automation.\n\n[Learn More][161]\n[Battery Packs]\n\n#### Battery Packs\n\nBattery pack and tray welding encompasses two processes. First, making a high quantity of electrical\nconnections to increasingly thick conductors, frequently of dissimilar or coated materials. Second,\nsealing the robust mechanical cases that enclose the battery itself. Laser welding offers the speed\nand reliability to create both high numbers of welds and strong, high-quality welds, even in\nreflective materials like aluminum.\n\n[Learn More][162]\n[Electric Motors]\n\n#### Electric Motors\n\nElectric vehicle motors are designed with hairpin conductors that require several manufacturing\nsteps. Laser ablation, or material removal, enables electric motor manufacturers to rapidly and\nreliably strip insulation coating from the hairpin ends. Once the underlying copper is exposed,\nlaser welding is a high-speed method of creating low-resistance joints with high accuracy and\nvirtually no spatter.\n\n[Learn More][163]\n[Power Electronics]\n\n#### Power Electronics\n\nIn addition to batteries, vehicle electrification requires additional electrical components such as\ninverters, control boxes, and power distribution units (PDUs) to handle the flow of electrical\nsignals and currents to the drivetrain components. Fiber lasers enable the welding of the\ninter-component connectors and busbars to meet critically important performace requirements while\nalso offering unmatched production speed, reliability, and ease of automation.\n\n[Learn More][164]\n[IPG Image]\n\n#### Fuel Cells\n\nHydrogen fuel cells, an alternative to Li-ion batteries, are used to power a variety of systems\nincluding vehicles and other energy storage applications. Fuel cells rely on bipolar plates and MEAs\nas key components. Laser processing solutions are able to meet the demanding requirements of these\ncomponents, offering precision, quality, and speed in applications including welding, slurry drying,\ncutting, and more.\n\n[Learn More][165]\n* [ Resources ][166]\n* [ Legal Notice ][167]\n* [ Privacy Policy ][168]\n* [ Cookie Policy ][169]\n* [ Imprint ][170]\n\n\u00a9 2026 IPG Photonics Corporation All Rights Reserved.\n\n[1]: /\n[2]: javascript:void(0);\n[3]: /en-us/products/handheld-lasers/lightweld-handheld-laser-welding-and-cleaning\n[4]: /products/lightweld/lightweld-handheld-laser-welding-and-cleaning\n[5]: javascript:void(0);\n[6]: /products/lasers\n[7]: /products/lasers/industrial-cw-fiber-lasers\n[8]: /products/lasers/industrial-cw-fiber-lasers\n[9]: /products/lasers/industrial-cw-fiber-lasers/high-power-fiber-lasers\n[10]: /products/lasers/industrial-cw-fiber-lasers/high-efficiency-fiber-lasers\n[11]: /products/lasers/industrial-cw-fiber-lasers/ultra-compact-industrial-lasers\n[12]: /products/lasers/industrial-cw-fiber-lasers/amb-adjustable-mode-beam-lasers\n[13]: /products/lasers/industrial-cw-fiber-lasers/industrial-single-mode-lasers\n[14]: /products/lasers/industrial-cw-fiber-lasers/dual-mode-lasers\n[15]: /products/lasers/industrial-cw-fiber-lasers/erbium-thulium-raman-fiber-lasers\n[16]: /products/lasers/laser-heating-sources\n[17]: /products/lasers/quasi-cw-fiber-lasers\n[18]: /products/lasers/nanosecond-pulsed-fiber-lasers\n[19]: /products/lasers/nanosecond-pulsed-fiber-lasers\n[20]: /products/lasers/nanosecond-pulsed-fiber-lasers/infrared-nanosecond-lasers\n[21]: /products/lasers/nanosecond-pulsed-fiber-lasers/green-nanosecond-fiber-lasers\n[22]: /products/lasers/nanosecond-pulsed-fiber-lasers/ultraviolet-nanosecond-fiber-lasers\n[23]: /products/lasers/ultrafast-pulsed-fiber-lasers\n[24]: /products/lasers/diode-lasers\n[25]: /products/lasers/deep-uv-lasers\n[26]: /products/lasers/specialized-lasers\n[27]: /products/lasers/specialized-lasers\n[28]: /products/lasers/specialized-lasers/linearly-polarized-and-single-frequency-cw-lasers\n[29]: /products/lasers/specialized-lasers/cw-amplifiers\n[30]: /products/lasers/specialized-lasers/single-mode-low-order-mode-lasers\n[31]: /products/lasers/specialized-lasers/mid-ir-hybrid-lasers\n[32]: /products/lasers/specialized-lasers/ultrafast-lasers-and-solutions-for-science\n[33]: /products/beam-delivery\n[34]: /products/beam-delivery\n[35]: /products/beam-delivery/laser-processing-heads\n[36]: /products/beam-delivery/laser-processing-heads\n[37]: /products/beam-delivery/laser-processing-heads/la"
