ustom Laser Systems ][97]\n* [ Robotic Automation ][98] Go to child menu\n* Back\n* #### [Robotic Automation][99]\n* [Robotic Laser Systems ][100]\n* [Robotic Arc Welding Systems ][101]\n* [Robotic Arc/Laser Welding Systems ][102]\n* [Custom Robotic Laser Systems ][103]\n* [LightWELD Cobot System ][104]\n* [ Solutions ][105] Go to child menu\n* Back\n* #### [Solutions][106]\n* [E-Mobility Manufacturing ][107] Go to child menu\n* Back to Solutions\n* #### [E-Mobility Manufacturing][108]\n* [Battery Cells ][109]\n* [Battery Busbars ][110]\n* [Battery Packs ][111]\n* [Electric Motors ][112]\n* [Power Electronics ][113]\n* [Fuel Cells ][114]\n* [Materials Processing ][115] Go to child menu\n* Back to Solutions\n* #### [Materials Processing][116]\n* [Laser Cutting ][117]\n* [Laser Welding ][118]\n* [Laser Cleaning ][119]\n* [Laser Heating & Drying ][120]\n* [Laser Drilling ][121]\n* [Laser Additive Manufacturing ][122]\n* [Laser Marking ][123]\n* [Laser Cladding ][124]\n* [Laser Brazing ][125]\n* [Micromachining ][126]\n* [Advanced & Scientific Applications ][127]\n* [Application Development ][128] Go to child menu\n* Back to Solutions\n* #### [Application Development][129]\n* [Application Labs ][130]\n* [Custom Systems & Tooling ][131]\n* [Virtual Engineering & Simulation ][132]\n* [ Technology ][133] Go to child menu\n* Back\n* #### [Technology][134]\n* [IPG Innovation ][135]\n* [Fiber Laser 101 ][136]\n* [Single-Emitter Laser Diodes ][137]\n* [On-The-Fly Welding ][138]\n* [Real-Time Weld Measurement ][139]\n* [Dual-Beam Lasers ][140]\n* [High-Efficiency Lasers ][141]\n* [Deep-UV Lasers ][142]\n* [Ultrafast Lasers ][143]\n* [ Company ][144] Go to child menu\n* Back\n* #### [Company][145]\n* [About Us ][146]\n* [Our Leadership ][147]\n* [Careers ][148]\n* [Investors ][149]\n* [Newsroom ][150]\n* [Events ][151]\n* [Social Responsibility ][152]\n* [Locations ][153]\n* [Policies & Standards ][154]\n* [ Contact Us ][155]\n* [ Support ][156]\n[ India | EN ][157]\n* [Home][158]\n* [Company][159]\n* Our Leadership\n[image]\n\nCompany\n\n## Leadership\n\nCharting the Course for Ongoing Success\n\n[Background Image]\n\n## Our Leadership\n\nOur management and board of directors play a pivotal role in steering the company towards enduring\ncontinuity. With a collective vision for sustained growth and progress, our leadership plays a key\nrole in charting the course for the company's ongoing success.\n\nWe are governed by a 10-member board of directors, 7 of whom are independent directors under Nasdaq\nguidelines with separate roles of Chairman and CEO; Non-executive Board Chair. The Board is\nstructured to empower shareholder rights through annually elected directors with no supermajority\nvoting provisions.\n\n[Dr. Mark M. Gitin]\n\n### Mark M. Gitin, Ph.D.\n\n#### Chief Executive Officer\n\nDr. Gitin is the Chief Executive Officer of the company as of June 05, 2024. He heads this\norganization bringing proven success as a strategic industry leader with the ability to identify and\nexecute growth opportunities while driving operational excellence and managing both organic and\ninorganic growth.\n\nIn 2017, Dr. Gitin joined MKS as Vice President and General Manager of the Photonics Business Unit,\nand in 2018 he also assumed responsibility for the Instruments and Motion Business Unit. From 2019\nto 2023 he served as Senior Vice President and General Manager of the Photonics Solutions Division,\nthen in 2023 served as Executive Vice President for the same division.\n\nPrior to joining MKS, from March 1995 to September 2017, Dr. Gitin held various management positions\ncovering a wide range of technologies at Coherent, Inc., including Vice President of Strategic\nMarketing, Vice President of Business Development, and Vice President and General Manager of the\nDiodes, Fibers and Systems Business Unit.\n\nDr. Gitin holds a B.S. in Electrical Engineering from University of California, Davis and an M.Eng.\nand Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering from Cornell University.\n\n## IPG Senior Management Team\n\nThe dynamic IPG leadership team not only fuels IPG's enduring success but also places a paramount\nfocus on our customers. Through the leadership team's strategic direction, IPG is driven towards\ncontinuous growth, lasting excellence, and unwavering dedication to meeting and exceeding customer\nneeds.\n\n[Paulus Bucher, Ph.D.]\n\n#### Paulus Bucher, Ph.D.\n\n##### Senior Vice President, Global Operations\n\nPaulus Bucher joined IPG as Senior Vice President of Global Operations in June 2025. Prior to\njoining IPG, Dr. Bucher served as Senior Vice President of Global Operations at Adtran.\n\nEarlier in his career, he held senior operations roles at ADVA, CommScope, and Ericsson.\n\nDr. Bucher holds a Ph.D. in Aerospace Engineering from Princeton University and a Master of Science\nin Mechanical Engineering from Virginia Tech, where he studied under a Fulbright Scholarship. He\nalso holds a Dipl.-Ing. (FH) from Fachhochschule Wiesbaden and earned his Fachhochschulreife at\nWaldorfschule Wahlwies in Germany.\n\n[Adolpho Chin]\n\n#### Adolfo Chin\n\n##### Vice President, Corporate Development\n\nAdolfo Chin joined IPG Photonics in August 2022 as Vice President of Corporate Development and leads\nthe company\u2019s global M&A strategy and execution.\n\nBefore joining IPG, Mr. Chin served as Vice President of Business Development for the Electronics\nInstruments Group of AMETEK Inc, leading the acquisition development efforts from 2007 to 2022.\nEarlier in his career, he held several strategy and operational roles at United Technologies\u2019\nCarrier Corporation.\n\nMr. Chin holds an MBA from Purdue University, where he was a Krannert Scholar, and a B.S. in\nIndustrial Engineering from the University of Costa Rica, where he graduated Valedictorian.\n\n[Jennifer Kartono]\n\n#### Jennifer Kartono\n\n##### Senior Vice President, Chief Human Resources Officer\n\nJennifer Kartono joined IPG Photonics in June 2025 as Senior Vice President, Chief Human Resources\nOfficer.\n\nPrior to joining IPG, she served as CHRO of Crane NXT and held a series of senior HR roles at Iron\nMountain. Ms. Kartono holds a BSBA in Business Marketing from the University of Denver.\n\n[Angelo P. Lopresti]\n\n#### Angelo P. Lopresti\n\n##### General Counsel, Secretary and Senior Vice President\n\nAngelo P. Lopresti has served as IPG\u2019s General Counsel and Secretary and one of the Company\u2019s Vice\nPresidents since February 2001. He was promoted to Senior Vice President in February 2013.\n\nPrior to joining IPG, Mr. Lopresti was a partner at the law firm of Winston & Strawn LLP from 1999\nto 2001. Prior to that, he was a partner at the law firm of Hertzog, Calamari & Gleason from 1998 to\n1999 and an associate there from 1991 to 1998.\n\nMr. Lopresti holds a B.A. in Economics from Trinity College and a J.D. from the New York University\nSchool of Law.\n\n[Tomoth P.V. Mammen]\n\n#### Timothy P.V. Mammen\n\n##### Chief Financial Officer and Senior Vice President\n\nTimothy P.V. Mammen has served as IPG\u2019s Chief Financial Officer since July 2000 and a Vice President\nsince November 2000. He was promoted to Senior Vice President in February 2013.\n\nBetween May 1999 and July 2000, Mr. Mammen served as the Group Finance Director and General Manager\nof the United Kingdom operations for IPFD. Mr. Mammen was Finance Director and General Manager of\nUnited Partners Plc, a commodity trading firm, from 1995 to 1999 and prior to that he worked in the\nfinance department of E.I. du Pont de Nemours and Company.\n\nMr. Mammen holds an Upper Second B.Sc. Honours degree in International Trade and Development from\nthe London School of Economics and Political Science. Also, he is a Chartered Accountant and a\nmember of the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Scotland.\n\n[Andrey Mashkin]\n\n#### Andrey Mashkin\n\n##### Vice President, GM Global Lasers\n\nMr. Mashkin has built his career at the company, progressing through roles in R&D, product line\nmanagement, and executive operations. He most recently served as Vice President of Operations Europe\nand Managing Director of IPG Laser GmbH & Co. KG, where he led large, multinational teams across\nGermany, Italy, and Poland, successfully steering operations through periods of significant change\nand expansion. Mr. Mashkin hold"
          },
