ustom Laser Systems ][97]\n* [ Robotic Automation ][98] Go to child menu\n* Back\n* #### [Robotic Automation][99]\n* [Robotic Laser Systems ][100]\n* [Robotic Arc Welding Systems ][101]\n* [Robotic Arc/Laser Welding Systems ][102]\n* [Custom Robotic Laser Systems ][103]\n* [LightWELD Cobot System ][104]\n* [ Solutions ][105] Go to child menu\n* Back\n* #### [Solutions][106]\n* [E-Mobility Manufacturing ][107] Go to child menu\n* Back to Solutions\n* #### [E-Mobility Manufacturing][108]\n* [Battery Cells ][109]\n* [Battery Busbars ][110]\n* [Battery Packs ][111]\n* [Electric Motors ][112]\n* [Power Electronics ][113]\n* [Fuel Cells ][114]\n* [Materials Processing ][115] Go to child menu\n* Back to Solutions\n* #### [Materials Processing][116]\n* [Laser Cutting ][117]\n* [Laser Welding ][118]\n* [Laser Cleaning ][119]\n* [Laser Heating & Drying ][120]\n* [Laser Drilling ][121]\n* [Laser Additive Manufacturing ][122]\n* [Laser Marking ][123]\n* [Laser Cladding ][124]\n* [Laser Brazing ][125]\n* [Micromachining ][126]\n* [Advanced & Scientific Applications ][127]\n* [Application Development ][128] Go to child menu\n* Back to Solutions\n* #### [Application Development][129]\n* [Application Labs ][130]\n* [Custom Systems & Tooling ][131]\n* [Virtual Engineering & Simulation ][132]\n* [ Technology ][133] Go to child menu\n* Back\n* #### [Technology][134]\n* [IPG Innovation ][135]\n* [Fiber Laser 101 ][136]\n* [Single-Emitter Laser Diodes ][137]\n* [On-The-Fly Welding ][138]\n* [Real-Time Weld Measurement ][139]\n* [Dual-Beam Lasers ][140]\n* [High-Efficiency Lasers ][141]\n* [Deep-UV Lasers ][142]\n* [Ultrafast Lasers ][143]\n* [ Company ][144] Go to child menu\n* Back\n* #### [Company][145]\n* [About Us ][146]\n* [Our Leadership ][147]\n* [Careers ][148]\n* [Investors ][149]\n* [Newsroom ][150]\n* [Events ][151]\n* [Social Responsibility ][152]\n* [Locations ][153]\n* [Policies & Standards ][154]\n* [ Contact Us ][155]\n* [ Support ][156]\n[ India | EN ][157]\n* [Home][158]\n* [Products][159]\n* [Laser Systems][160]\n* FlexCell\n[IPG Image]\n\n# FlexCell\n\n## Dual-Purpose Arc/Laser Robotic Welding Systems\n* [Overview][161]\n\n[ Overview ][162]\n[Contact Us][163]\n[Modular-Icon]\n\n#### Arc or Laser Welding\n\n[Configurable-Icon]\n\n#### Modular Design\n\n[Productive-Icon]\n\n#### Production Optimized\n\nFlexCell robotic welding systems are highly-configured pre-engineered platforms designed to increase\nwelding productivity and precision for a wide variety of part sizes and geometries.\n\nOffered in both arc and laser configurations, FlexCell systems deliver process flexibility that can\nbe tailored for the specific demands of many complex welding tasks.\n\nAll IPG robotic welding systems are backed by decades of welding automation experience and 24/7/365\ntechnical support.\n* [IPG Image]\n* [IPG Image]\n[IPG Image][IPG Image]\n* [IPG Image]\n* [IPG Image]\n[IPG Image][IPG Image]\n[Modular-Icon]\n\n#### Arc or Laser Welding\n\n[Configurable-Icon]\n\n#### Modular Design\n\n[Productive-Icon]\n\n#### Production Optimized\n\nFlexCell robotic welding systems are highly-configured pre-engineered platforms designed to increase\nwelding productivity and precision for a wide variety of part sizes and geometries.\n\nOffered in both arc and laser configurations, FlexCell systems deliver process flexibility that can\nbe tailored for the specific demands of many complex welding tasks.\n\nAll IPG robotic welding systems are backed by decades of welding automation experience and 24/7/365\ntechnical support.\n\n## Arc and Laser Welding Process Flexibility\n\n[Diagram demonstrating switching between robotic arc and laser welding]\n\n### Welding Automation Doesn't Have to Be All or Nothing\n\nWill you still be welding the same parts the same way in six months? A year? Five years?\n\nA rigid machine forces you to commit to a welding process now. A flexible machine grows and adapts\nto your needs.\n\nThat\u2019s why we created the FlexCell system line. Integrate a turnkey arc welding solution and add\nlaser capability later. Or start with laser welding and change to MIG to address new part designs.\n\nEither way, our welding automation team is prepared to offer you a solution that meets you where you\nare.\n\n### FlexCell is built for manufacturers...\n* New to robotic welding automation\n* Trying to mitigate risk while increasing productivity and reliability\n* Transitioning from arc welding automation to laser welding automation\n* Expecting to alternate between laser and arc to address new requirements\n* Looking for easier robotic welding system implementation\n* That value 24/7 support and service and expert training\n* In need of part, application, and welding process optimization\n\n### FlexCell is built for industries like...\n* General manufacturing and fabrication\n* Contract manufacturing\n* Automotive\n* Aerospace\n* Appliances and white goods\n* Agricultural equipment\n* Heavy industry\n* [Arc Welding][164]\n* [Arc Welding Options][165]\n* [Arc Welding Advantages][166]\n\n[Laser ablation provides easy and fast coating & paint removal]\n\n### Reliable, acessible welding automation.\n\nLaser welding is powerful, but it's not a real-world fit for every production line or shop floor.\nPart tolerancing, material quality, and gap variations can make arc welding a more reliable and\nconsistent process.\n\nSound familiar? If it does, or if your operation just isn't ready for a laser system yet, then we\nare happy to offer a powerful robotic arc welding solution and decades of experience to go with it.\nYou can always trade up to a laser welding configuration in the future.\n\n### Arc Welding Options & Configurations\n\n#### **Your choice of arc welding power source**\n\nWhether you have an in-house preference or are trying to optimize process variables like heat input,\ngap bridging, spatter, and weld stability, we offer major automation-ready GMAW brands like Miller,\nLincoln, Fronius, and ESAB.\n\n#### **Welding torch cleaning stations**\n\nRobotic welding systems are at their best when they are able to offer both increased productivity\nand increased joining consistency. An automated torch cleaning station helps with both, ensuring\nstable gas and arc behavior and reducing planned and unplanned system downtime.\n\n#### **Flexible part handling**\n\nWhether you are working with large weldments and complex fixturing or can trade work space for\nmaximum machine utilization, a variety of FlexCell part positioning, staging, and tooling options\nmatch your machine to the needs of your application.\n\n[IPG Image]\n\n**More tolerant of variation:** Automated arc welding is more tolerant of fit-up gaps and joint\nvariation, reducing upstream production demands.\n\n**Increased heavy-duty flexibility:** Arc welding is often the best process for thicker materials,\nheavy structural work, or designs that require wider weld seams.\n\n**Increased accessibility:** Robotic arc configurations come with reduced initial costs and more\nstraight-forward integration.\n\n**Familiarity:** For manufacturers with robotic arc welding experience, configuration and\nimplementation is easier and more familiar.\n* [Laser Welding][167]\n* [Laser Welding Options][168]\n* [Laser Welding Advantages][169]\n\n[Robotic arm with wobble welding head]\n\n### Power. Precision. Productivity.\n\nLaser welding offers the speed, precision, and process control that enables the fabrication of a\nwide variety of cutting edge products. From aerospace components to household appliances and from\nsmall part runs to serial production, laser welding is a high-quality process that delivers\nsignificant ROI.\n\nNot sure if you\u2019re ready for laser welding? With decades of experience in arc and laser welding\nautomation, we\u2019re here to make integrating a laser solution painless, from process development to\ntechnical support.\n\n### Laser Welding Options & Configurations\n\n#### **Lasers optimized for your requirements**\n\nFrom our standard high-reliability IPG industrial fiber laser sources to dual-beam lasers\npurpose-built to maximize weld quality and reliability, our laser experts identify the best IPG\nlaser technology for your applications.\n\n#### **Purpose-built laser welding heads & optics**\n\nIPG high-power laser welding optics and dedicated welding heads are designed to optimiz"
          },
