ustom Laser Systems ][97]\n* [ Robotic Automation ][98] Go to child menu\n* Back\n* #### [Robotic Automation][99]\n* [Robotic Laser Systems ][100]\n* [Robotic Arc Welding Systems ][101]\n* [Robotic Arc/Laser Welding Systems ][102]\n* [Custom Robotic Laser Systems ][103]\n* [LightWELD Cobot System ][104]\n* [ Solutions ][105] Go to child menu\n* Back\n* #### [Solutions][106]\n* [E-Mobility Manufacturing ][107] Go to child menu\n* Back to Solutions\n* #### [E-Mobility Manufacturing][108]\n* [Battery Cells ][109]\n* [Battery Busbars ][110]\n* [Battery Packs ][111]\n* [Electric Motors ][112]\n* [Power Electronics ][113]\n* [Fuel Cells ][114]\n* [Materials Processing ][115] Go to child menu\n* Back to Solutions\n* #### [Materials Processing][116]\n* [Laser Cutting ][117]\n* [Laser Welding ][118]\n* [Laser Cleaning ][119]\n* [Laser Heating & Drying ][120]\n* [Laser Drilling ][121]\n* [Laser Additive Manufacturing ][122]\n* [Laser Marking ][123]\n* [Laser Cladding ][124]\n* [Laser Brazing ][125]\n* [Micromachining ][126]\n* [Advanced & Scientific Applications ][127]\n* [Application Development ][128] Go to child menu\n* Back to Solutions\n* #### [Application Development][129]\n* [Application Labs ][130]\n* [Custom Systems & Tooling ][131]\n* [Virtual Engineering & Simulation ][132]\n* [ Technology ][133] Go to child menu\n* Back\n* #### [Technology][134]\n* [IPG Innovation ][135]\n* [Fiber Laser 101 ][136]\n* [Single-Emitter Laser Diodes ][137]\n* [On-The-Fly Welding ][138]\n* [Real-Time Weld Measurement ][139]\n* [Dual-Beam Lasers ][140]\n* [High-Efficiency Lasers ][141]\n* [Deep-UV Lasers ][142]\n* [Ultrafast Lasers ][143]\n* [ Company ][144] Go to child menu\n* Back\n* #### [Company][145]\n* [About Us ][146]\n* [Our Leadership ][147]\n* [Careers ][148]\n* [Investors ][149]\n* [Newsroom ][150]\n* [Events ][151]\n* [Social Responsibility ][152]\n* [Locations ][153]\n* [Policies & Standards ][154]\n* [ Contact Us ][155]\n* [ Support ][156]\n[ India | EN ][157]\n* [Home][158]\n* [Products][159]\n* [Beam Delivery][160]\n* Beam Switches, Shutters & Couplers\n[IPG Image]\n\n# Beam Switches, Shutters, & Couplers\n\n## Maximize Your Fiber Laser Capabilities\n* [Overview][161]\n\n[ Overview ][162]\n[Contact Us][163]\n[Six-Axis-motion-Icon]\n\n#### Up to 6 Output Channels\n\n[High-Power-Icon]\n\n#### Up to 50 kW Laser Power\n\n[Productive-Icon]\n\n#### Laser Time & Energy Sharing\n\nThe ability to couple light from one fiber to another greatly expands upon fiber laser\nfunctionality. Flexible control over beam delivery enables IPG fiber lasers to utilize power and\nspace more effectively by addressing multiple applications simultaneously or sequentially or\nincreasing process speed and laser duty cycle.\n\nOptions include single port couplers, beam shutters, multi-port beam switches for 2, 3, 4, or 6\nchannels, and a 2 port energy sharing function.\n\n* [IPG Image]\n* [IPG Image]\n[Six-Axis-motion-Icon]\n\n#### Up to 6 Output Channels\n\n[High-Power-Icon]\n\n#### Up to 50 kW Laser Power\n\n[Productive-Icon]\n\n#### Laser Time & Energy Sharing\n\nThe ability to couple light from one fiber to another greatly expands upon fiber laser\nfunctionality. Flexible control over beam delivery enables IPG fiber lasers to utilize power and\nspace more effectively by addressing multiple applications simultaneously or sequentially or\nincreasing process speed and laser duty cycle.\n\nOptions include single port couplers, beam shutters, multi-port beam switches for 2, 3, 4, or 6\nchannels, and a 2 port energy sharing function.\n\n## Process-Feed Fiber Couplers\n\nFiber couplers are often used to protect the feed fiber and the laser from the process. The use of a\ncoupler between the fiber and beam delivery head also allows for flexible fiber changeout for quick\nadjustment of beam characteristics for different applications and easy fiber replacement.\n\n## Beam Shutters\n\nA beam shutter, also known as a one-channel beam switch, is mainly used to increase process speed in\na production line. Shutters decrease laser off time by allowing the laser to remain on while the\nshutter controls laser output.\n\n## Multi-Channel Beam Switches\n\n#### **Time Sharing**\n\nBeam switching allows one laser source to supply up to six different process fibers across multiple\nstations or work cells. This enables a single laser to address multiple different applications\nwithout manually swapping process heads or fibers. In the time sharing mode only one beam is emitted\nat any given time.\n\n#### **Energy Sharing**\n\nBeam switches can be used to \"split\" laser energy and direct power to multiple workstations\nsimultaneously, enabling a single laser source to perform multiple operations at once. Energy\nsharing is a good option for reducing equipment costs by using a single high-power laser rather\nthan several lower power lasers.\n\n[A Unique Combination of Advanced Technologies]\n\n### Get the Most Out of Your Laser\n\nAll IPG beam switches, shutters, and couplers can be integrated with virtually any IPG fiber laser\nby being built in to the laser enclosure to save space and simplify installation.\n\n## Beam Switches, Shutters, & Couplers\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n[Optical Couplers] \u2502[Beam Shutters] \u2502[Multi-Channel Beam Switches]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u250