ustom Laser Systems ][97]\n* [ Robotic Automation ][98] Go to child menu\n* Back\n* #### [Robotic Automation][99]\n* [Robotic Laser Systems ][100]\n* [Robotic Arc Welding Systems ][101]\n* [Robotic Arc/Laser Welding Systems ][102]\n* [Custom Robotic Laser Systems ][103]\n* [LightWELD Cobot System ][104]\n* [ Solutions ][105] Go to child menu\n* Back\n* #### [Solutions][106]\n* [E-Mobility Manufacturing ][107] Go to child menu\n* Back to Solutions\n* #### [E-Mobility Manufacturing][108]\n* [Battery Cells ][109]\n* [Battery Busbars ][110]\n* [Battery Packs ][111]\n* [Electric Motors ][112]\n* [Power Electronics ][113]\n* [Fuel Cells ][114]\n* [Materials Processing ][115] Go to child menu\n* Back to Solutions\n* #### [Materials Processing][116]\n* [Laser Cutting ][117]\n* [Laser Welding ][118]\n* [Laser Cleaning ][119]\n* [Laser Heating & Drying ][120]\n* [Laser Drilling ][121]\n* [Laser Additive Manufacturing ][122]\n* [Laser Marking ][123]\n* [Laser Cladding ][124]\n* [Laser Brazing ][125]\n* [Micromachining ][126]\n* [Advanced & Scientific Applications ][127]\n* [Application Development ][128] Go to child menu\n* Back to Solutions\n* #### [Application Development][129]\n* [Application Labs ][130]\n* [Custom Systems & Tooling ][131]\n* [Virtual Engineering & Simulation ][132]\n* [ Technology ][133] Go to child menu\n* Back\n* #### [Technology][134]\n* [IPG Innovation ][135]\n* [Fiber Laser 101 ][136]\n* [Single-Emitter Laser Diodes ][137]\n* [On-The-Fly Welding ][138]\n* [Real-Time Weld Measurement ][139]\n* [Dual-Beam Lasers ][140]\n* [High-Efficiency Lasers ][141]\n* [Deep-UV Lasers ][142]\n* [Ultrafast Lasers ][143]\n* [ Company ][144] Go to child menu\n* Back\n* #### [Company][145]\n* [About Us ][146]\n* [Our Leadership ][147]\n* [Careers ][148]\n* [Investors ][149]\n* [Newsroom ][150]\n* [Events ][151]\n* [Social Responsibility ][152]\n* [Locations ][153]\n* [Policies & Standards ][154]\n* [ Contact Us ][155]\n* [ Support ][156]\n[ India | EN ][157]\n* [Home][158]\n* [Products][159]\n* [Lasers][160]\n* Laser Heating Sources\n[IPG Image]\n\n# Laser Heating Sources\n\n## High-Efficiency Laser Heating & Drying\n* [Overview][161]\n\n[ Overview ][162]\n[Contact Us][163]\n[Wall-Plug-Efficiency-Icon]\n\n#### 55%\n\nEnergy Efficiency\n\n[Power-Tunability-Icon]\n\n#### 10X Faster\n\nHeating & Drying\n\n[High-Power-Icon]\n\n#### Up to 100 kW\n\nOutput Power\n\nIPG DLS laser heating sources are the highest efficiency laser source for high-power applications\nwith constant uptime like heating and drying.\n\nLaser heat treatment is the fastest, most efficient, and most cost-effective solution available for\napplications like battery electrode drying, powder coat curing, and paint drying.\n\n* [IPG Image]\n* [IPG Image]\n\n[Wall-Plug-Efficiency-Icon]\n\n#### 55%\n\nEnergy Efficiency\n\n[Power-Tunability-Icon]\n\n#### 10X Faster\n\nHeating & Drying\n\n[High-Power-Icon]\n\n#### Up to 100 kW\n\nOutput Power\n\nIPG DLS laser heating sources are the highest efficiency laser source for high-power applications\nwith constant uptime like heating and drying.\n\nLaser heat treatment is the fastest, most efficient, and most cost-effective solution available for\napplications like battery electrode drying, powder coat curing, and paint drying.\n\n## Higher Efficiency, Higher ROI\n\nIncluding a projection head for emitting wide area laser light, IPG laser heating sources direct\nvirtually all energy onto the target material. Combined with extremely high power conversion\nefficiency, the cost of ownership and return on investment of a laser heating source is unequalled.\n\nInfrared light is a remarkably effective source of heat, enabling faster, more sustainable heating\nprocesses across a wide variety of applications.\n\n[DLS Lasers: The Most Sustainable Heating and Drying Method]\n\n### The Most Sustainable Heating & Drying Method\n\nDLS and DLS-ECO series lasers offer dramatically improved efficiency and productivity, enabling\nmanufacturers to both increase their profitability and engage in more sustainable,\nenvironmentally-friendly production.\n\nOver 120 countries, including the U.S., have set a target date of 2050 for reaching carbon\nneutrality. Stricter government regulations to decrease carbon emissions, as well as rising energy\ncosts, are pushing manufacturers to replace outdated or inefficient equipment.\n\n## More Efficient. More Cost-Effective.\n\n[Comparison between convection furnace, infrared lamp and IPG DLS-ECO Laser]\n\n[A Cold Oven with Unmatched Energy Efficiency]\n\n### A \"Cold\" Oven with Unmatched Energy Efficiency\n\nBy nature, lasers direct energy extremely efficiently, heating only the part while radiating little\nwaste heat into the factory or oven walls. The cool environment allows for in situ thermal metrology\nthat enables tighter process control and development.\n\nLearn more about how IPG laser heating R&D workstations make developing a more sustainable and\nefficient heating and drying solution easy.\n\n[Learn More][164]\n[Integrated Heating & Drying Optics]\n\n### Integrated Beam Delivery\n\nDLS and DLS-ECO lasers are integrated with IPG projection process heads that distribute laser energy\nover areas as small 25 cm\u00b2 and as large as 10,000 cm\u00b2.\n\nSmaller illumination areas are well-suited for applications like annealing or R&D while large\nillumination areas are a good choice for replacing convection furnaces and infrared lamps in high\nthroughput industrial applications like battery foil drying, paint drying, and powder coat curing.\n\n### Ask Us Anything\n\nWhether you need a custom laser solution or just want to learn more from our global team of laser\nexperts, we're here to help.\n\n[Get Started][165]\n\n## Laser Heating Sources Comparison\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\