        "crawl_text": "Kongsberg Gruppen ASA Oslo Stock Exchange Listed on the Oslo Stock Exchange, subject to Norwegian securities legislation. Kongsberg, Norway Kongsberg, Norway Norway [Skip to content][1]\n[Home - Corporate][2]\n* What we do\n* Support and services\n* Careers\n* Sustainability\n* Investors\n* Company\n1. [Home - Corporate][3]\n2. [Company][4]\n\n# This is KONGSBERG\n\nKONGSBERG protects people and critical infrastructure \u2013 from deep sea to space. Through innovation,\ncollaboration and determination, we develop technologies and solutions to serve the defence,\nsecurity and surveillance markets.\n\n## About us\n\nWe combine military and civilian expertise to drive rapid innovation for defence, research, and\ncommercial applications.\n\nOur defence and security solutions include strike missiles, remote weapon stations, air defence\nsystems, command and control systems and digital remote towers for customers worldwide. Our\nsolutions help strengthen countries' security and defence capabilities.\n\nKONGSBERG also serves the ocean space with technology \u2013 from sensors to autonomous systems \u2013 to\nensure sustainable management of marine resources, monitor climate change and critical\ninfrastructure, and safeguard national security.\n\nKONGSBERG delivers to every part of the space value chain \u2013 from launch services and production of\nsmall satellites to downloading and managing satellite data.\n\nThe company was founded in 1814 in the town of Kongsberg, Norway. Today, we are more than 7,500\nemployees in about 20 countries. The company is headquartered in Norway and listed on the Oslo Stock\nExchange. The Norwegian government controls about 50.01 percent of the shares in KONGSBERG.\n\nThrough innovation and state-of-the-art industrial production, we create jobs and value for our\nsuppliers, partners, customers and owners.\n\nWe protect people and planet by innovating technology today, for a better tomorrow.\n\n### Three strong divisions\n\nKONGSBERG consists of three divisions:\n* Defence Systems\n* Missiles & Aerostructures\n* Discovery\n\n#### Defence Systems\n\nThis division focuses on land systems, air and coastal defence, naval systems and advanced defence\nsolutions. It includes core defence capabilities such as integrated defence systems, weapon\nplatforms and advanced operational solutions. The division carries significant responsibility for\ndeliveries within highly regulated defence environments and plays a central role in meeting growing\ndemand from NATO and allied markets.\n\n#### Missiles & Aerostructures\n\nThis division brings together missile programmes, aerostructures and maintenance capabilities. It\nincludes both subsonic and supersonic missile programmes, aerostructures production and maintenance\nof airborne platforms. It also has a dedicated Emerging Business unit to support innovation and new\ngrowth areas. The division consolidates advanced manufacturing and programme execution under one\nstructure, strengthening end-to-end accountability across complex value chains.\n\n#### Discovery\n\nThis division integrates the former business area Kongsberg Discovery with Space and Surveillance\nactivities. It combines capabilities in underwater technology, sensors, satellite systems and\nsurveillance, creating a cohesive environment for dual-use and cross-domain innovation. Most\ncivilian-oriented activities are gathered within this division. This allows these businesses to\noperate with the flexibility required to compete in international civilian markets, without being\nsubject to defence-specific rules and processes that apply elsewhere in the company. At the same\ntime, the division benefits from close collaboration with defence and space activities,\nstrengthening technology development across domains.\n\n### Ownership structure\n\nKongsberg Gruppen ASA is listed on the Oslo Stock Exchange and is subject to Norwegian securities\nlegislation and stock exchange regulations. The Norwegian state owns 50.004 per cent of the shares\nin the company.\n\n## More about the company\n\nUse the links below to dive deeper into our background, values and purpose, strategic direction, and\norganisation.\n* [\n\n### The foundation of our identity and behaviour\n\nOur values, purpose and vision define who we are and how we create impact.\n\n][5]\n* [\n\n### Strategy and ambitions\n\nKONGSBERG\u2018s strategic ambition is to be a leading technology company, delivering advanced\ntechnology solutions to solve critical challenges for our customers that enhance and support the\nsecurity and\u2026\n\n][6]\n* [\n\n### Management and organisation\n\nThe management of KONGSBERG, consisting of ten members with varied backgrounds and experiences, is\ncommitted to develop the company\u2019s leading position and technology platform.\n\n][7]\n* [\n[Historical picture of working men at Kongsberg Arms Factory]\n\n### Our history\n\nKONGSBERG has a long and proud history \u2013 from its starting point in Norway in 1814, to the\ninternational corporation of today, KONGSBERG has been an innovative technology environment.\n\n][8]\n\n### Sustainability and corporate social responsibility\n\nSustainability and corporate social responsibility are important for KONGSBERG and are an integral\npart of our strategy. We shall conduct our business in a sustainable and accountable manner, and we\nmust carry out our corporate social responsibility in accordance with the applicable expectations of\nsociety. This gives KONGSBERG the necessary \u2018licence to operate\u2019 in order to execute our business.\n\nThe UN has defined 17 sustainability development goals the world should reach by 2030. Several of\nthese goals can only be achieved through innovation and the sensible application of technology. To\nKONGSBERG, this involves business opportunities in several markets viewed in the light of our broad\ntechnology and skills platform.\n\nKONGSBERG has acceded to the UN Global Compact initiative. We support and respect international\nhuman and employee rights such as the UN\u2019s Universal Declaration of Human Rights, the UN Convention\non the Rights of the Child, ILO Core Conventions and the OECD Guidelines for Multinational\nEnterprises. KONGSBERG uses the Global Reporting Initiative (GRI) guidelines for the voluntary\nreporting of sustainable development.\n\n## Our commitment\n\nLearn more about our commitment to sustainability and social responsibility\n* [\n\n### Our commitment and your expectation\n\nWe believe that business must play an active role in the success of global sustainable\ndevelopment, supporting the UN Sustainable Development Goals. We protect people and planet by\ninnovating\u2026\n\n][9]\n* [\n\n### Caring for people\n\nWe aim to be a workplace where people thrive. We view our employees as a key prerequisite for our\nsuccess, and our ambition is to attract, develop and retain a competent, dedicated and diverse\u2026\n\n][10]\n* [\n\n### Responsible Business Conduct\n\nWe are dedicated to ensuring responsible business conduct throughout our operations and value\nchain. Our values are embedded in our Code of Ethics and Business Conduct, which provides the\nfoundation\u2026\n\n][11]\n\n### Value creation\n\nKONGSBERG is an active value creator in the areas and countries where we are present. Our presence\ncreates significant effects that extend beyond our own business area. First and foremost, we create\nvalue for our customers through our products and solutions. These products help to meet the needs\nand challenges that customers face, and thus generate added value and improvements in various\nsectors and industries.\n\nWe are also a significant economic actor. This includes our contributions through tax and fee\npayments, dividend distribution to our shareholders and salary payments to our dedicated employees.\nThese economic contributions play an important role in the communities where we operate, and support\neconomic stability and growth. In addition to direct contributions, we also create indirect values\nthrough our cooperation with our suppliers.\n\nOur procurement of goods and services from various partners helps to strengthen and maintain a broad\necosystem of business relationships that promote value creation at multiple levels. We invest\nsignificantly in research and development. This focus on innovation drives forward new thinking and\ntechnological [Skip to content][1]\n[Home - Corporate][2]\n* What we do\n* Support and services\n* Careers\n* Sustainability\n* Investors\n* Company\n1. [Home - Corporate][3]\n2. [Company][4]\n\n# This is KONGSBERG\n\nKONGSBERG protects people and critical infrastructure \u2013 from deep sea to space. Through innovation,\ncollaboration and determination, we develop technologies and solutions to serve the defence,\nsecurity and surveillance markets.\n\n## About us\n\nWe combine military and civilian expertise to drive rapid innovation for defence, research, and\ncommercial applications.\n\nOur defence and security solutions include strike missiles, remote weapon stations, air defence\nsystems, command and control systems and digital remote towers for customers worldwide. Our\nsolutions help strengthen countries' security and defence capabilities.\n\nKONGSBERG also serves the ocean space with technology \u2013 from sensors to autonomous systems \u2013 to\nensure sustainable management of marine resources, monitor climate change and critical\ninfrastructure, and safeguard national security.\n\nKONGSBERG delivers to every part of the space value chain \u2013 from launch services and production of\nsmall satellites to downloading and managing satellite data.\n\nThe company was founded in 1814 in the town of Kongsberg, Norway. Today, we are more than 7,500\nemployees in about 20 countries. The company is headquartered in Norway and listed on the Oslo Stock\nExchange. The Norwegian government controls about 50.01 percent of the shares in KONGSBERG.\n\nThrough innovation and state-of-the-art industrial production, we create jobs and value for our\nsuppliers, partners, customers and owners.\n\nWe protect people and planet by innovating technology today, for a better tomorrow.\n\n### Three strong divisions\n\nKONGSBERG consists of three divisions:\n* Defence Systems\n* Missiles & Aerostructures\n* Discovery\n\n#### Defence Systems\n\nThis division focuses on land systems, air and coastal defence, naval systems and advanced defence\nsolutions. It includes core defence capabilities such as integrated defence systems, weapon\nplatforms and advanced operational solutions. The division carries significant responsibility for\ndeliveries within highly regulated defence environments and plays a central role in meeting growing\ndemand from NATO and allied markets.\n\n#### Missiles & Aerostructures\n\nThis division brings together missile programmes, aerostructures and maintenance capabilities. It\nincludes both subsonic and supersonic missile programmes, aerostructures production and maintenance\nof airborne platforms. It also has a dedicated Emerging Business unit to support innovation and new\ngrowth areas. The division consolidates advanced manufacturing and programme execution under one\nstructure, strengthening end-to-end accountability across complex value chains.\n\n#### Discovery\n\nThis division integrates the former business area Kongsberg Discovery with Space and Surveillance\nactivities. It combines capabilities in underwater technology, sensors, satellite systems and\nsurveillance, creating a cohesive environment for dual-use and cross-domain innovation. Most\ncivilian-oriented activities are gathered within this division. This allows these businesses to\noperate with the flexibility required to compete in international civilian markets, without being\nsubject to defence-specific rules and processes that apply elsewhere in the company. At the same\ntime, the division benefits from close collaboration with defence and space activities,\nstrengthening technology development across domains.\n\n### Ownership structure\n\nKongsberg Gruppen ASA is listed on the Oslo Stock Exchange and is subject to Norwegian securities\nlegislation and stock exchange regulations. The Norwegian state owns 50.004 per cent of the shares\nin the company.\n\n## More about the company\n\nUse the links below to div"
