Company\n  * [About Us][67]\n  * [Leadership][68]\n  * [Why Laserax?][69]\n  * [Environment & Quality][70]\n  * [ISO Certifications][71]\n* [Contact Us][72]\n* [Get a Quote][73]\n\n# **Advanced** Laser Solutions **for**\n# **Next-Gen Manufacturing**\n\nLaserax works with the world\u2019s leading manufacturers to implement laser cleaning, welding,\ntexturing, and marking solutions.\n\n[Talk with an Expert][74]\n[Or Explore Our Products][75]\n\n## Trusted by\n\n[Ford Logo]\n[Stellantis Logo]\n[Borgwarner Logo]\n[Magna Logo]\n[Cummins Logo]\n[ZF]\n[Daimlertruckag Logo]\n[Brose Logo]\n[Linamar Logo]\n[Dana Logo]\n[Scania Logo]\n[Form logo]\n[Lear Corporation]\n[Nexteer]\n[Mahle R Textimage]\n[Harbinger Logo]\n[ABS Logo]\n[Briggs Stratton Vector Logo]\n[Adient Logo]\n[Fisher Barton]\n[Denso Logo]\n[BRP Logo]\n[Solaredge Logo]\n[IBM Logo]\n[Honda Logo]\n[Michelin Logo]\n[Hexagon Logo]\n[Allison Transmission Logo.svg]\n[Denor Logo]\n[Mercury Logo]\n[Tenneco Logo]\n[Nemak Logo]\n[Teksid Logo]\n[St Jean]\n[Martinrea Logo]\n[Aludyne Logo]\n[Henkel Logo.svg]\n[RSR Logo]\n[79a5e9e9 9ced 4389 Ab87 B98aeb0a9da]\n[Arconic Logo]\n[Trace100x Logo]\n[Saint Gobain]\n[Riotinto Logo]\n[Alcoa Logo]\n[Meridian Logo]\n[Rassini Logo]\n[Hydro Logo]\n[Ega Logo]\n[Stark Logo]\n[Glencore Logo]\n[ALBH.BH]\n[Teck Resources Logo.svg]\n[Sun Metals Logo]\n[CTDI Logo]\n[Matalco Logo]\n[Uacj Logo]\n[Diamond Foundry Logo]\n[Flex N Gate Vector Logo]\n[Ljunghall Logo]\n[EMEA Logo]\n\n## Complete Laser Solutions\n\nOur complete laser solutions are fully integrated turnkey machines built to simplify the adoption of\nlaser technology in production environments. Combining a high-performance laser system with\nenclosures, safety features, automation, and auxiliary equipment, they provide a complete,\nready-to-use solution for cleaning, marking, and welding applications.\n\nCleaning & Texturing Marking Welding\n\n### **Laser Cleaning** Machines\n\n[Robot Laser Cleaning Machine Open] [CCM] [BCM] [RCM] [DCM] [MCW] [RCW]\n\nOur laser cleaning machines are complete solutions with fume extraction, laser safety, performance\noptimization, and more. They are ready for robot lines, conveyor lines, or manual loading by\noperators. In high-volume production lines, they provide a high return on investment and achieve\nsuperior cleaning and texturing quality.\n\n[View Our Machines][76]\n\n### **Laser Marking** Machines\n\n[Flex] [RTW] [RTM] [OAM] [ADM] [CSM]\n\nClass-1 certified, our laser marking machines are complete solutions ready for robots, conveyors, or\nmanual loading. Each machine is designed to address specific challenges, whether you need to\nminimize the impact on cycle time, mark multiple parts, minimize the machine\u2019s footprint, or manage\npart positioning variations.\n\n[View Our Machines][77]\n\n### **Laser Welding** Machines\n\n[Battery laser welding machine] [Versa Laser Welding Machine] [Battery laser welding workstation]\n\nDesigned for battery welding applications, our laser welding machines can be used for R&D or\nfull-scale production. They are powered by continuous wave lasers of up to 2000W, enabling\nhigh-speed welding for both cylindrical and prismatic battery pack designs.\n\n[View Our Machines][78]\n\n## Laser Systems\n\nOur [Skip to main content][1]\n\n## Top menu\n* [Blog][2]\n* [Support][3]\n* [Careers][4]\n\nSearch\nSearch\n* [Search][5]\n[ Language EN ][6]\n* [English][7]\n* [Fran\u00e7ais][8]\n* [Deutsch][9]\n* [\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e][10]\n* [Espa\u00f1ol][11]\n* [Swedish][12]\n[Laserax][13] [Menu][14]\n\n## Main menu\n* Products\n  * [Laser Markers][15]\n  * [Laser Cleaners][16]\n  * [Laser Marking Machines][17]\n  * [Laser Cleaning Machines][18]\n  * [Laser Welding Machines][19]\n  * [Laser Software][20]\n* Services\n  * [Laser Process Development][21]\n  * [Laser Machine Rental][22]\n  * Laser Batch Processing\n    * [Laser Welding Service][23]\n    * [Laser Texturing Service][24]\n    * [Laser Cleaning Service][25]\n    * [Laser Marking Service][26]\n  * [Laser Safety Certification][27]\n  * [After Sales Support & Services][28]\n* Applications\n  * [Laser Marking][29]\n    * [Part & Product Traceability][30]\n    * [Direct Part Marking (DPM)][31]\n    * [Etching & Engraving][32]\n    * [E-Coat Resistant Marking][33]\n    * [Shotblast Resistant Marking][34]\n  * Laser Marking By Material\n    * [Metal][35]\n    * [Plastic][36]\n    * [Sand][37]\n  * Types Of Markings\n    * [Data Matrix Code][38]\n    * [Barcode][39]\n    * [Alphanumerics][40]\n    * [Logo][41]\n  * [Laser Cleaning][42]\n    * [Laser Rust Removal][43]\n    * [Laser Oxide Removal][44]\n    * [Laser Paint Removal][45]\n    * [Battery Modules Cleaning][46]\n  * [Laser Texturing][47]\n    * [Adhesive Bonding][48]\n  * [Laser Welding For EV Batteries][49]\n  * [Laser Drilling][50]\n* [Industries][51]\n  * [Batteries][52]\n  * [Electric motors][53]\n  * [Automotive & Electric Vehicles][54]\n  * [Energy][55]\n  * [Aerospace][56]\n  * [Medical][57]\n  * [Semiconductor][58]\n  * [Foundries & Casting Plants][59]\n  * [Metals][60]\n  * [Aluminum Extrusion][61]\n  * [Solar Photovoltaics][62]\n  * [Manufacturing][63]\n  * [Agriculture & Heavy Equipment][64]\n  * [Fuel Cells][65]\n* [Case Studies][66]\n* Company\n  * [About Us][67]\n  * [Leadership][68]\n  * [Why Laserax?][69]\n  * [Environment & Quality][70]\n  * [ISO Certifications][71]\n* [Contact Us][72]\n* [Get a Quote][73]\n\n# **Advanced** Laser Solutions **for**\n# **Next-Gen Manufacturing**\n\nLaserax works with the world\u2019s leading manufacturers to implement laser cleaning, welding,\ntexturing, and marking solutions.\n\n[Talk with an Expert][74]\n[Or Explore Our Products][75]\n\n## Trusted by\n\n[Ford Logo]\n[Stellantis Logo]\n[Borgwarner Logo]\n[Magna Logo]\n[Cummins Logo]\n[ZF]\n[Daimlertruckag Logo]\n[Brose Logo]\n[Linamar Logo]\n[Dana Logo]\n[Scania Logo]\n[Form logo]\n[Lear Corporation]\n[Nexteer]\n[Mahle R Textimage]\n[Harbinger Logo]\n[ABS Logo]\n[Briggs Stratton Vector Logo]\n[Adient Logo]\n[Fisher Barton]\n[Denso Logo]\n[BRP Logo]\n[Solaredge Logo]\n[IBM Logo]\n[Honda Logo]\n[Michelin Logo]\n[Hexagon Logo]\n[Allison Transmission Logo.svg]\n[Denor Logo]\n[Mercury Logo]\n[Tenneco Logo]\n[Nemak Logo]\n[Teksid Logo]\n[St Jean]\n[Martinrea Logo]\n[Aludyne Logo]\n[Henkel Logo.svg]\n[RSR Logo]\n[79a5e9e9 9ced 4389 Ab87 B98aeb0a9da]\n[Arconic Logo]\n[Trace100x Logo]\n[Saint Gobain]\n[Riotinto Logo]\n[Alcoa Logo]\n[Meridian Logo]\n[Rassini Logo]\n[Hydro Logo]\n[Ega Logo]\n[Stark Logo]\n[Glencore Logo]\n[ALBH.BH]\n[Teck Resources Logo.svg]\n[Sun Metals Logo]\n[CTDI Logo]\n[Matalco Logo]\n[Uacj Logo]\n[Diamond Foundry Logo]\n[Flex N Gate Vector Logo]\n[Ljunghall Logo]\n[EMEA Logo]\n\n## Complete Laser Solutions\n\nOur complete laser solutions are fully integrated turnkey machines built to simplify the adoption of\nlaser technology in production environments. Combining a high-performance laser system with\nenclosures, safety features, automation, and auxiliary equipment, they provide a complete,\nready-to-use solution for cleaning, marking, and welding applications.\n\nCleaning & Texturing Marking Welding\n\n### **Laser Cleaning** Machines\n\n[Robot Laser Cleaning Machine Open] [CCM] [BCM] [RCM] [DCM] [MCW] [RCW]\n\nOur laser cleaning machines are complete solutions with fume extraction, laser safety, performance\noptimization, and more. They are ready for robot lines, conveyor lines, or manual loading by\noperators. In high-volume production lines, they provide a high return on investment and achieve\nsuperior cleaning and texturing quality.\n\n[View Our Machines][76]\n\n### **Laser Marking** Machines\n\n[Flex] [RTW] [RTM] [OAM] [ADM] [CSM]\n\nClass-1 certified, our laser marking machines are complete solutions ready for robots, conveyors, or\nmanual loading. Each machine is designed to address specific challenges, whether you need to\nminimize the impact on cycle time, mark multiple parts, minimize the machine\u2019s footprint, or manage\npart positioning variations.\n\n[View Our Machines][77]\n\n### **Laser Welding** Machines\n\n[Battery laser welding machine] [Versa Laser Welding Machine] [Battery laser welding workstation]\n\nDesigned for battery welding applications, our laser welding machines can be used for R&D or\nfull-scale production. They are powered by continuous wave lasers of up to 2000W, enabling\nhigh-speed welding for both cylindrical and prismatic battery pack designs.\n\n[View Our Machines][78]\n\n## Laser Systems\n\nOur laser systems are standalone laser processing units designed to integrate into existing\nproduction environments or custom automation setups. Unlike our complete solutions, laser systems\nprovide maximum flexibility for OEMs, integrators, and manufacturers who want to build a customized\nsolution.\n\nCleaning & Texturing Marking\n\n### **Laser Cleaning** Systems\n\n[LXQ] [LXQ-HP] [LXQ UHP (1)]\n\nOur laser cleaning systems are designed for automated and semi automated production lines. Offering\nup to 3kW, they provide the speed and precision needed for short cycle times. They can clean and\ntexture surfaces in a single operation, and process moving parts with no impact on quality.\n\n[View Our Systems][79]\n\n### **Laser Marking** Systems\n\n[LXQ] [LXQ-HP] [LXQ-LP] [UV Laser Marker]\n\nOur OEM laser markers come with a wide range of options to make sure they meet your requirements.\nRanging from 20W to 500W, they can mark at high speed and operate in a large marking field. When you\ncontact us, our application specialists will make sure to capture all your requirements, including\nlead times and AIM-DPM specifications.\n\n[View Our Systems][80]\n\n## Applications\n\n### Laser Marking\n\nLaserax offers laser marking solutions to permanently mark parts for identification and\ntraceability. When benchmarked, our lasers provide the fastest marking speeds, making them the first\nchoice to prevent bottlenecks. We also offer various options to optimize marking quality and have\ndeveloped unique processes that protect codes from surface treatments.\n\n[Learn More][81]\n\n[Datamatrix laser marking on an engine block]\n\n### Laser Cleaning\n\nOur laser cleaning solutions are used to remove a range of contaminants from metal surfaces such as\nrust, oxide, paint, and electrolyte. As contaminants are vaporized with perfect repeatability, the\nmetal underneath is left intact. We offer up to 3kW of power to make sure the cleaning speed is as\nfast as required.\n\n[Learn More][82]\n\n[Laser cleaning of a battery tray]\n\n### Lase"
