ration of land, air, sea, space and cyber domains\nenables operations in complex scenarios by strengthening the link between observation,\ndecision-making and response. This gives rise to integrated solutions capable of protecting critical\ninfrastructure and ensuring resilience across all essential sectors. Electronics and digital\ntechnologies act as the glue that securely connects all areas of operation in real time.\n\nNext card\n\n#### Expertise and innovation\n\n[ [Next card] ][30]\n\n## Expertise and innovation\n\n[Linea di produzione terrestre_people]\n\nThe acquisition accelerates technological innovation, strengthens our expertise and empowers our\npeople. These are key factors in sustaining long-term competitiveness and ensuring stability,\nstrategic autonomy and the protection of communities.\n\nNext card\n\n#### A Multi-domain Ecosystem\n\n[ [Next card] ][31]\n\n## A Multi-domain Ecosystem\n\n[Michelangelo-dome]\n\nLand defence capabilities are part of a broader strategy in which capabilities and platforms work\ntogether across multi-domains. The **[Michelangelo Dome][32]**\u00a0is the practical application of this\nvision. Not a product, but an open, modular and scalable architecture, designed to integrate\ndifferent technologies and operate as a dynamic 'dome' of protection capable of ensuring security in\ncomplex environments.\n\nNext card\n\n#### Key points of the acquisition\n\n[ [Next card] ][33]\n\n## Key points of the acquisition\n\n[Highlights iveco defence]\n\n**Key points of the acquisition** (*)\n\n## + \u20ac1,368 mln in revenue for Iveco Defence\n\n[+ \u20ac1,368 million in revenue for Iveco Defence]\n\n## > 2,000 employees worldwide\n\n[> 2,000 employees worldwide]\n\n## 6 Manufacturing plants worldwide\n\n[6 plants worldwide]\n\n## 7 R&D centres worldwide\n\n[7 R&D centres worldwide]\n\n## 12 sales offices worldwide\n\n[12 sales offices worldwide]\n\n## > 10 new vehicles in portfolio\n\n[> 10 new vehicles in the fleet]\n\n**2025 numbers*\n\n[BANNER ASSET_INDUSTRIAL PLAN_Banner Desktop_INDUSTRIAL PLAN_1600x426]\n[discover more][34]\n\n\u20ac 0.1 BN\n\nrevenues\n\n\u20ac 0.1 BN\n\norder backlog\n\n1\n\npeople\n\n1\n\nsites worldwide\n\n\u20ac 0.1 BN\n\ninvested in R&D\n\n1 %\n\nof sources of financing linked to ESG parameters\u00a0\n* Aeronautics\n* Automation\n* Cyber & Security\n* Electronics\n* Helicopters\n* HPC\n* Space\n\n## Aeronautics\n\n\u20ac 5 BN\n\nAircaft orders 2025\n\n1,200 Aircraft\n\nmanaged at around 50 sites/bases\n\ncivil & military\n\n[Visit Aeronautics page][35]\n\n## Automation\n\n1 +\n\nyears\u2019 experience\n\nOver 30km\n\nof sorting systems in operation\n\ncivil\n\n[Visit Automation page][36]\n\n## Cyber & Security\n\n\u20ac 1.1 BN\n\nOrders 2025\n\n50 Countries\n\nworldwide using Leonardo\u2019s critical communication systems\n\ncivil & military\n\n[Visit Cyber & Security page][37]\n\n## Electronics\n\n\u20ac 10.7 BN\n\nOrders 2025\n\n1,000 Air defence\n\nand surveillance radars in 58 countries\n\nCivil & Military\n\n[Visit Electronics page][38]\n\n## Helicopters\n\n\u20ac 6.2 BN\n\nOrders 2025\n\nOver 4,500\n\nHelicopters in service across in more than 130 countries\n\nCivil & Military\n\n[VISIT HELICOPTERS PAGE][39]\n\n## HPC\n\n3x\n\ncomputing power in 2026\n\n20 PFlops Rmax\n\nwith 230+ CPU and 120+ GPU nodes with Davinci-2\n\ncivil & military\n\n[Visit HPC page][40]\n\n## Space\n\n\u20ac 1 BN\n\nOrders 2025\n\n100+\n\nsatellites per year planned by the new Space Smart Factory in Rome\n\ncivil & military\n\n[Visit Space page][41]\n[\n[Immagine Careers]\nCareers\n][42] [\n[Immagine sustainability]\nSustainability\n][43]\n[officina leonardo 1320x400]\n\nOFFICINA LEONARDO\n\n[discover more][44]\n[HP Meta 1320x400]\n\nLeonardo's Metaverse\n\n[discover more][45]\n[Leonardo deep dive]\n\nLeonardo deep dive\n\n[Apply now][46]\n\n## MEDIA HUB\n\n[navigation left] [navigation right]\n[\n[EDF 430x400 new]\nCorporate\n\nEDF 2025, Leonardo leads in space and multi-domain technologies\n\n][47]\n[\n[04_TP_Webnews_430x430]\nSustainability\n\nLeonardo Transition Plan 2026: building resilience across the transition\n\n][48]\n[\n[cebntro hpc_430x400]\nCorporate Innovation\n\nNational HPC Centre: Leonardo\u2019s Contribution to the Project\n\n][49]\n[\n[Artemis II_Mobile (1)]\nCorporate Space\n\nArtemis II, towards the Moon with Leonardo\n\n][50]\n[\n[Banner webnews_IDV]\nElectronics\n\nLeonardo strengthens its leadership in land defence, a decisive step toward integrated global\nsecurity\n\n][51]\n[\n[Lorenzo news 430x400]\nCorporate Innovation People Sustainability\n\n\u201cLeonardo, in every imaginable world\u201d: Lorenzo\u2019s story\n\n][52]\n[\n[Quadrata v2]\nCorporate Helicopters\n\nLeonardo CEO highlights renewed UK commitment in \u00a31bn AW149 helicopter deal\n\n][53]\n[\n[PIJ54_immagine-web_vf]\nCyber Security Innovation\n\nLeonardo's Modelling & Simulation, a pillar of multi-domain defence, in the new Polaris Innovation\nJournal\n\n][54]\n[\n[solvers wanted 430x400]\nCorporate Innovation People\n\nLeonardo Solvers Wanted, new challenge in quantum technologies\n\n][55]\n[\n[Webnews Premio Innovazione__430x400]\nCorporate Events Innovation People\n\nInnovation Award 2025, record edition: almost 1,000 entries\n\n][56]\n[\n[quadrata_Strappo C-27J]\nAircraft\n\nC-27J MPA, the Leonardo-Saudi Arabia agreement covered by the media\n\n][57]\n[\n[Girls@Polimi_2026-LEONARDO_430 x 430_]\nCorporate People Sustainability\n\nGirls@Polimi: scholarships for female engineers of the future\n\n][58]\n[ Discover more news ][59]\n[navigation left] [navigation right]\n[\n[Image Cover TP (1)]\n\n23.06.2026 - 09:35\n\nLEONARDO LAUNCHED THE \u201c2026 TRANSITION PLAN\u201d: BUILDING RESILIENCE ACROSS THE TRANSITION\n][60]\n[\n[9 (1)]\n\n22.06.2026 - 10:11\n\nLEONARDO AND BAYKAR SET MAJOR MILESTONE FOR ADVANCED CREWED/UNCREWED CAPABILITY DEVELOPMENT WITH\nSUCCESSFUL FIRST K-SWARM LIVE TRIALS\n][61]\n[\n[Immagine comunicati (1)]\n\n18.06.2026 - 17:04\n\nLEONARDO: BOARD OF DIRECTORS APPROVES NEW ORGANIZATION STRUCTURE\n][62]\n[\n[EDGE-Leonardo (1)]\n\n17.06.2026 - 13:55\n\nEDGE And Leonardo to Partner Through a Joint Venture on Advanced Defence Sensors and Systems\n][63]\n[\n[Vulcano_Signing Ceremony (1)]\n\n16.06.2026 - 14:50\n\nDiehl Defence, Leonardo and General Dynamics celebrate Extended Range Artillery Projectile award\nbased on Vulcano 155mm GLR\n][64]\n[\nCyber Security\n[CDS (1)]\n\n15.06.2026 - 14:17\n\nEUROSATORY, LEONARDO PRESENTS THE CYBERSEC DEFENCE SUITE\n][65]\n[\n[AW169-Avincis (1)]\n\n15.06.2026 - 13:45\n\nLEONARDO\u2019S EMERGENCY RESPONSE HELICOPTER FLEET TO GROW STRONGER IN EUROPE WITH 15 AIRCRAFT ORDER BY\nLEADING OPERATOR AVINCIS\n][66]\n[\n[Multi_domain_technologies_ Press note]\n\n12.06.2026 - 08:30\n\nEDF 2025: LEONARDO LEADS IN SPACE AND MULTI-DOMAIN TECHNOLOGIES\n][67]\n[\n[AW249 ILA 2026 (2)]\n\n11.06.2026 - 10:15\n\nILA BERLIN: LEONARDO EXHIBITS AW249 HELICOPTER\u2019S NEXT GEN DESIGN AND VIGOROUS FLYING QUALITIES AS\nINDUSTRY VALUE-PROPOSITION INTENSIFIES TO FILL EUROPE AND WORLD MARKETS\u2019 CAPABILITY GAP\n][68]\n[\n[GettyImages-1442849073 (1)]\n\n10.06.2026 - 12:35\n\nLeonardo selected for ISOS, Europe\u2019s programme for next-generation in-orbit services\n][69]\n[ Discover more press releases ][70]\n[navigation left] [navigation right]\n\nfocus\n\n[ Discover more focus ][71]\n\n## Social Media\n\n[ Load more ][72]\n* [ about ][73]\n* [ careers ][74]\n* [ media hub ][75]\n* [ business ][76]\n* [ innovation & technology ][77]\n* [ sustainability ][78]\n* [ investors ][79]\n* [ suppliers ][80]\n\nSocial Media\n\n[ [Go to Home] ][81]\n* [ Privacy Policy ][82]\n* [ Cookie Policy ][83]\n* [ Cookie preferences ][84]\n* [ Legal Notice ][85]\n* [ Sitemap ][86]\n* [ CERT ][87]\nP.IVA 00881841001 \u00a9 2026 Leonardo S.p.A.\nFor the transmission and storage of the Regulated Information, the Company uses the transmission\nsystem E-MARKET SDIR and the storage device E-MARKET STORAGE which can be consu