 Careers ][59]\n  * [ Careers Homepage ][60]\n  * [ Career Opportunities at QinetiQ ][61]\n  * [ Early Careers ][62]\n  * [ Diversity & Inclusion ][63]\n  * [ Life at QinetiQ ][64]\n  * [ Our Purpose ][65]\n  * [ Flexible Working ][66]\n* [ Investors ][67]\n  * [ Investors Homepage ][68]\n  * [ Investor Overview ][69]\n  * [ Investor Seminars ][70]\n  * [ Results, Reports & Presentations ][71]\n  * [ Consensus Estimates ][72]\n  * [ Financial Calendar ][73]\n  * [ Shareholder Services ][74]\n  * [ Regulatory News ][75]\n  * [ Investor Contacts ][76]\n* [ Contact us ][77]\n  * [ Get in touch ][78]\n* [ [F6391BE9361E47E0B1B9DDEABBBB314B.ashx] United Kingdom ][79]\n* [ [F6391BE9361E47E0B1B9DDEABBBB314B.ashx] Australia ][80]\n* [ [F6391BE9361E47E0B1B9DDEABBBB314B.ashx] Canada ][81]\n* [ [F6391BE9361E47E0B1B9DDEABBBB314B.ashx] United States ][82]\n* [ [F6391BE9361E47E0B1B9DDEABBBB314B.ashx] Germany ][83]\n\n# We are QinetiQ\n\n\nAdvancing defence technology. Securing the future.\n\nWe are a global defence and security company delivering mission-critical solutions that protect\nlives and enable operational advantage. We combine deep technical expertise with a bold approach to\ninnovation\u2014helping our customers solve complex challenges across land, sea, air, space and cyber.\n\n## QinetiQ Facts\n\n7,500\n\nMore than 7,500 employees\n\n\u00a34.3bn\n\nOrder backlog (as at HY26 results)\n\n50\n\nOperating in 50 locations across the UK, Europe, US and Australia\n\n## Core Capabilities\n\n[A boat model cuts through the water at the Haslar Ocean Basin facility Meta Description: At\nQinetiQ, we deliver world-leading test and training that helps defence and security customers\nvalidate systems, prepare personnel and ensure operational effectiveness.]\n\nWhat we do\n\n## Test and Training\n\nWe provide world-class facilities, technologies and expertise to support the testing, evaluation and\ntraining of defence systems and personnel\u2014ensuring readiness and reliability in real-world\nconditions.\n\nFind out more\n[Woman in a headset and mic looks at a screen in the Hebrides control room with several flags behind\nher]\n\nWhat we do\n\n## Mission Support and Operations\n\nOur teams deliver specialist support to enhance operational performance, resilience and\ndecision-making. From strategic planning to frontline environments, we help customers achieve\nmission success.\n\nFind out more\n[QinetiQ employee wearing a high-visibility vest working on research and development at a computer\ndisplaying technical equipment and data for defence technology innovation.]\n\nWhat we do\n\n## Research and Development\n\nWe advance science and technology to shape future capabilities. Our R&D drives innovation across\nautonomy, sensing, cyber and beyond\u2014enabling our customers to stay ahead of emerging threats.\n\nFind out more\n[A female engineers sits in a plane cockpit next to a male instructor ]\n\nWhat we do\n\n## Engineering Services\n\nWe offer deep technical expertise across the full lifecycle of capability development\u2014from concept\nand design to integration, sustainment and optimisation. Our engineers solve complex challenges with\nprecision and purpose.\n\nFind out more\n\n## News\n\n[View more][84]\n[\n\nFY26 Group Performance\n\nRecord order intake and \u00a34.8bn backlog provide strong visibility for FY27 revenue growth and beyond.\n\n][85]\n[\n\nTeam Elaris wins \u00a36 million contract to prove satellite navigation alternatives\n\nQinetiQ-led Team Elaris has been awarded a \u00a36 million contract with the UK Ministry of Defence (MOD)\nto develop a deployable solution concept for enhanced Long-Range Navigation (eLoran).\n\n][86]\n[\n\nQinetiQ\u2019s aerial tribute to iconic Spitfire\n\nThe QinetiQ operated ETPS test pilot school based at MOD Boscombe Down has taken part in the\nhistoric Spitfire90 commemorative tour.\n\n][87]\n[Four people standing in front of QinetiQ's 5 metre wind tunnel turbine]\n\nCareers\n\n## Join us\n\nOur dedicated and talented people are shaping the future of defence and security. Explore the\nexciting and diverse range of opportunities available for you to join our team.\n\nFind out more\n* [QinetiQ][88]\n* [About us][89]\n* [Purpose][90]\n* [Leadership][91]\n* [Corporate Governance][92]\n* [Sustainability][93]\n* [History][94]\n* [Facilities][95]\n* [Our locations][96]\n* [Partners][97]\n* [Who we work with][98]\n* [Frameworks][99]\n* [Work with us][100]\n* [Suppliers][101]\n* [Working with us][102]\n* [Sustainable procurement][103]\n* [JOSCAR][104]\n* [Frameworks][105]\n* [Collaborative events][106]\n* [ISO44001][107]\n* [Global][108]\n* [United Kingdom][109]\n* [United States][110]\n* [Canada][111]\n* [Australia][112]\n* [Germany][113]\n* [Contact QinetiQ][114]\n\nFollow QinetiQ on\n* [Privacy][115]\n* [Terms of use][116]\n* [Cookie policy][117]\n* [Accessibility][118]\n* [Modern slavery statement][119]\n* [Vulnerability disclosure][120]\n\n\u00a9 QinetiQ 2026\n\n[I4qOZVfvVqNv7w-BOqIfSH5GpaPeCg-SF5BQdniOtKQ=.html][121]\n\n[1]: /en/who-we-are\n[2]: /en/who-we-are\n[3]: /en/who-we-are/about-us\n[4]: /en/who-we-work-with\n[5]: /en/who-we-are/our-purpose\n[6]: /en/who-we-are/qinetiq-leadership-team\n[7]: /en/who-we-are/board-of-directors\n[8]: /en/who-we-are/qinetiq-leadership-team\n[9]: /en/who-we-are/corporate-governance\n[10]: /en/who-we-are/sustainability\n[11]: /en/who-we-are/our-history\n[12]: /en/what-we-do\n[13]: /en/what-we-do\n[14]: /en/what-we-do/test-and-training\n[15]: /en/what-we-do/test-and-training/test-and-evaluation\n[16]: /en/what-we-do/test-and-training/test-and-evaluation/facilities\n[17]: /en/what-we-do/test-and-training/test-and-evaluation/air\n[18]: /en/what-we-do/test-and-training/test-and-evaluation/land\n[19]: /en/what-we-do/test-and-training/test-and-evaluation/maritime\n[20]: /en/what-we-do/test-and-training/test-and-evaluation/weapons\n[21]: /en/what-we-do/test-and-training/test-and-evaluation/about-the-ltpa\n[22]: /en/what-we-do/test