ose\n[ High Power Diode Lasers ][111] [ Mobile High Power Diode Laser ][112] [ High Efficiency Diode\nLaser ][113] [ Compact Diode Laser ][114] [ Direct Diode Laser ][115] [ Brilliant Diode Laser ][116]\n[ Blue Diode Laser ][117] [ Blue Ultra Brilliant Diode Laser ][118]\n[ Processing Optics ][119] [ Modular | OTS Optics ][120] [ Compact & Lightweight | OTC Optics ][121]\n[ Individual Spots Geometries | Multi-Spot Optics ][122] [ Flexible-Spots Sizes | OTZ Optics ][123]\n[ Ultra-Wide-Spots | OTX Optics ][124]\n[ Beam Shaping Solutions ][125] [ Cladding & AM Applications ][126] [ Welding Applications ][127] [\nBrazing Applications ][128] [ Surface Heat Treatment Applications ][129]\n[ Technology Partnership | Tailored Laser Solutions ][130]\n[Applications][131]\n[ Overview Applications ][132] Close\n[ Laser Welding ][133] [ Heat Conduction Welding ][134] [ Keyhole Welding ][135] [ Aluminum Welding\n][136] [ Copper Welding ][137] [ Hybrid Welding ][138] [ Plastic Welding ][139]\n[ Laser Brazing ][140]\n[ Laser Cutting ][141]\n[ Laser Metal Deposition ][142] [ Laser Cladding ][143] [ MultiWire Laser Cladding ][144] [ Copper\nCladding ][145] [ ID Laser Cladding ][146] [ Repair Welding ][147] [ Additive Manufacturing ][148]\n[ Plastic Processing ][149] [ Automated Tape Laying ][150] [ Edgeband Welding ][151] [ Plastic\nWelding ][152]\n[ Surface Heat Treatment ][153] [ Laser Hardening ][154] [ Softening ][155] [ Laser Drying ][156] [\nLaser Curing ][157] [ Sintering ][158]\n[ Laser Soldering | LAB ][159]\n[ Wafer | Annealing & Inspection ][160]\n[Industries][161]\n[ Overview Industries ][162] Close\n[ Aviation & Aerospace ][163]\n[ Automotive & E-Mobility ][164]\n[ Transportation ][165]\n[ Tool- and Mold-making ][166]\n[ Oil and Gas ][167]\n[ Agriculture ][168]\n[ Semiconductor Production ][169]\n[ Renewable Energy ][170]\n[Our Services][171]\n[ Overview Our Services ][172] Close\n[ Process Development | Application Laboratory ][173] [ Application Trials ][174] [ Process\nDevelopment ][175] [ Application Expert Support ][176]\n[ Technology Partnership | Tailored Laser Solutions ][177] [ Custom Laser Solutions ][178] [\nResearch Projects ][179] [ Technology Partnership ][180]\n[ After-Sales-Service ][181] [ Training ][182] [ Comissioning & Integration ][183] [ 24/7 Hotline\n][184] [ Technical Customer Service ][185] [ Spare parts ][186] [ Technical Refurbishment ][187]\n[About Us][188]\n[ Overview About Us ][189] Close\n[ About Laserline ][190]\n[ News & Dates ][191]\n[ Locations ][192]\n[ Sustainability ][193]\n[ Quality ][194]\n[ LIVELINE Digital Forum ][195]\n[ Careers ][196] [ Professionals and Managers ][197] [ Students and Graduates ][198] [ Trainees\n][199]\nMenu\n[Contact][200]\n[Welding of a small auxiliary motor with blue diode laser by Laserline diode lasers]\n\nBlue High Power Diode Laser\n\nLaserline\u2019s blue laser series revolutionizes the processing\nof copper, gold and its alloys in various ways.\n\n[Read more][201]\n\nBlue High Brightness Diode Laser\n\nFor powder bed 3D metal printing, copper welding and more\u00a0\n\n[Read more][202]\n\nThe Brake Disc for Less Fine Dust\n\nLaser cladding High-speed process supports the cost-effective manufacturing\nof a new brake disc generation to meet new Euro 7 pollution rules\n\n[Read more][203]\nHigh Power Diode Laser Solutions\n\nIndustrial lasers | Diode lasers for materials processing\n\nWith more than 8,000 systems in field use, Laserline's industrial lasers are among the most\nsuccessful beam sources for industrial material processing in the multi-kilowatt range. Modular\ndesign, high efficiency and very high reliability with low maintenance requirements are appreciated\nby our customers worldwide.\n\nPlease feel free to contact us!\n\nAbout Us\n\nWe have been dedicated to diode lasers for over 25 years.\n\n[Learn more][204]\nProducts\n\nFrom laser beam generation to the workpiece\n\n[Learn more][205]\n[Process of cladding and additive manufacturing on copper with copper powder by Laserline diode\nlasers]\n\nApplications\n\nFrom surface treatment to joining and additive manufacturing\n\n[Learn more][206]\n[Row of finished car bodies in a production site welded together with laser by Laserline diode\nlasers]\n\nIndustries\n\nTechnology partnership & customized laser systems\n\n[Learn more][207]\n\nServices\n\nFrom initial application trials to series production\n\n[Learn more][208]\n\nSustainability\n\nSustainable use of resources is important to us.\n\n[Learn more][209]\n\nLIVELINE\n\nWe invite you to a video dialog with our experts.\n\n[Learn more][210]\n\nCareers\n\nYour Skills | Our Future: We are looking for qualified professionals.\n\n[Learn more][211]\n\nNews & Dates\n\nNewsroom\n[News][212] [Events][213] [Stories][214]\n[\n\nPress\n\n2026-06-17\n\nPress Release: Laserline Expands Corporate Headquarters in M\u00fclheim-K\u00e4rlich, Germany\n\nWith the groundbreaking ceremony on June 16, 2026, marking the start\u2026\n\n][215]\n[\n\nJournal\n\n2026-04-01\n\nDeep Dive for Laser Technology: Blue Lasers as a Promising Solution for Deep-Sea Processing\n\nBlue diode lasers might transform deep-sea processing by enabling\u2026\n\n][216]\n[\n\nPress\n\n2026-02-02\n\nPress Release: Laserline Further Expands Its Management Team\n\nLaserline is expanding its management trio to a quartet: Dr. Alexander\u2026\n\n][217]\n[\n\nTradeshow\n\n2026-07-01 - 2026-07-02\n\nPLI 2026\n\nMeet us at PLI 2026 in Limoges, France!\n\n][218]\n[\n\nTradeshow\n\n2026-07-08 - 2026-07-10\n\nLASER Korea 2026\n\nVisit us at LASER Korea 2026 in Goyang-si, South Korea!\n\n][219]\n[\n\nTradeshow\n\n2026-09-14 - 2026-09-19\n\nIMTS 2026\n\nVisit us at IMTS 2026 in Chicago, IL, USA!\n\n][220]\n[\n\nPress\n\n2026-06-17\n\nPress Release: Laserline Expands Corporate Headquarters in M\u00fclheim-K\u00e4rlich, Germany\n\nWith the groundbreaking ceremony on June 16, 2026, marking\u2026\n\n][221]\n[\n\nPress\n\n2026-02-02\n\nPress Release: Laserline Further Expands Its Management Team\n\nLaserline is expanding its management trio to a quartet: Dr.\u2026\n\n][222]\n[\n\nTradeshow\n\n2026-07-01 - 2026-07-02\n\nPLI 2026\n\nMeet us at PLI 2026 in Limoges, France!\n\n][223]\n[\n\nTradeshow\n\n2026-07-08 - 2026-07-10\n\nLASER Korea 2026\n\nVisit us at LASER Korea 2026 in Goyang-si, South Korea!\n\n][224]\n[Don't miss any more news!][225]\n\n## Industry Solutions\n\nCustomized system solutions from Laserline are used in production processes in many industries.\nUsers primarily come from the automotive industry, mechanical engineering and tool- and mold-making.\nNumerous companies in the aerospace and heavy industry also rely on Laserline today. In new\nindustries such as the manufacturing of electric motors or the production of lithium-ion batteries,\nwe work closely with our partners and customers to jointly create innovations and added value for\nthe future.\u00a0\n\n[Row of finished car bodies in a production site welded together with laser by Laserline diode\nlasers]\nAutomotive & E-Mobility\n\nIn car body construction - for brazing, aluminum welding, remote welding and more\n\n[read more \u203a][226]\n[Oil and gas platform on the ocean by Laserline diode lasers]\nOil & Gas\n\nCoatings for wear and corrosion protection with the diode laser\n\n[read more \u203a][227]\n[Closeup of a turbine engine processed with Laserline diode lasers]\nAviation & Aerospace\n\nDiode lasers for welding of metals, plastics and cladding\n\n[read more \u203a][228]\n[Transportation ship loaded with containers stationed at a port by Laserline diode lasers]\nTransport\n\nCoatings for wear and corrosion protection with the diode laser\n\n[read more \u203a][229]\n[Wind turbines and a row of solar panels in daylight by Laserline diode lasers]\nRenewable Energies\n\nCoating of wind turbine plain bearings and more\n\n[read more \u203a][230]\n[Process of a metal model being hardened by Laserline diode lasers]\nTool- & Mold-making\n\nProduction of tools as well as pressing and casting molds - Welding, hardening, 3D printing\n\n[read more \u203a][231]\n[Protection of saw-blades from wear and corrosion by means of additive manufacturing by Laserline\ndiode lasers]\nAgriculture\n\nWear protection for agricultural machinery blades and other highly stressed components\n\n[read more \u203a][232]\n[A flip chip attached on a electronic circuit board by Laserline diode lasers]\nSemiconductor\n\nOptoelectronic inspection of wafers and brazing of electronic components in plates\n\n[read more \u203a][233]\n\n# Diode Lasers in Use\n\nP"
