nabling the future.\n\n## Enabling the future.\n\n## Enabling the future.\n\nPrevious Next\n\n## CUSTOM SOLUTIONS\n\n## Unlock the full potential of your custom solution.\n\nWhile Excelitas offers a vast array of off-the-shelf premium products, our greatest offering lies in\nour unique ability to deliver bespoke solutions tailored to your specific requirements. We work with\nyou to identify the design and specifications that present the optimal level of performance, cost,\nquality and time-to-market.\n\n[ OUR CAPABILITIES ][131]\n\n## Our Products\n\nWe develop innovative products and components to enable your innovation.\n\n[Night Vision Goggle Optical Modules]\nNight Vision Goggle Optical Modules\n[Cameras]\nCameras\n[Deuterium Lamps and Systems]\nDeuterium Lamps & Systems\n[LINOS MeVis Lenses for High-Resolution C-Mount Sensors up to 1\"]\nImaging Lenses & Systems\n[Excelitas illumination, optics and detection technologies combine into custom integrated\nsub-systems for leading OEMs]\nIntegrated OEM Custom Optical Solutions\n[Industrial IR Thermal Processing Solutions]\nIR Thermal Processing\n[Cermax Xenon Lamps]\nLamps & Lamp Systems\n[Excelitas offers a wide range of diode laser modules, IR emitting diodes, pulsed laser diodes and\ntunable lasers]\nLasers & Emitters\n[Laser Optics and Electro-Optic Modules]\nLaser Optics\n[LED Chip On Board solutions and illumination systems]\nLED Components & Systems\n[UV Curing Systems]\nUV Curing Systems\n[Laser crystal coated optics]\nCustom Optical Components & Assemblies\n[LINOS Microbench the original optomechanical Cage System for precision optical experiment setups]\nOptomechanical Components\n[Excelitas Silicon Avalanche Photodiodes]\nPhotonic Detectors\n[Excelitas XLS 302 3kW Capacitor Charger]\nPower Supplies\n[Excelitas Thermal IR Sensors define state-of-the-art for Pyroelectric Detectors, Thermopile\nDetectors and range of specialized modules and arrays.]\nThermal Infrared Sensors\n[Upper Air UVC Disinfection Kepri System]\nUVC Disinfection Light Sources\n[X-Cite LED Illumination and Light sources]\nX-Cite Fluorescence Illuminators\n[LINOS Standard Optical Elements]\nStandard Optical Elements\n[LINOS Standard Optical Lenses]\nStandard Optical Lenses\nPrevious Next\n\n## Corporate Overview Video\n\n## Enabling the Future\n\nExcelitas is the leading provider of advanced, life-enriching technologies that make a difference,\nserving global market leaders in the Life Sciences, Advanced Industrial, next-generation\nSemiconductor, Aerospace and Defense end-markets. Headquartered in Pittsburgh, PA, USA, Excelitas is\nan essential partner in the design, development, and manufacture of photonic technologies, offering\nleading-edge innovation in sensing, detection, imaging, optics, and specialty illumination for\ncustomers worldwide. Excelitas is at the forefront of addressing many of the relevant megatrends\nimpacting the world today, including precision medicine, industrial automation, artificial\nintelligence, connected devices (IoT), and military modernization.\n\nWatch Now\nhttps://www.excelitas.com/#featured-story-44647\n\n## CEO Message\n\n## Meet Our CEO\n\nOur CEO shares his excitement for the tremendous opportunities that lie ahead for Excelitas with\naccolades for the company\u2019s legacy and team.\u00a0\n\nWatch Now\nhttps://www.excelitas.com/#featured-story-43738\n\n## Featured Story\n\n## Evolution of Fluorescence Illumination Is Refining Medical and Research Applications\n\nExplore how advancements in illumination solutions are shaping the future of medical diagnostics and\nsurgical visualization. In the March issue of Biophotonics, Excelitas Senior Biomedical Applications\nScientist Dr. Kavita Aswani highlights the latest LED technology innovations and their ability to\ndeliver the wavelength specificity, energy efficiency and thermal stability needed for today\u2019s\nbiomedical challenges. She also discusses how next-generation fluorescence systems, including those\noffered by Excelitas, are integrating closed-loop feedback and AI to enable real-time surgical\nguidance and automated diagnostics.\n\n[ Read More ][132]\n\n## Featured Story\n\n## UV-LED Curing for Insertable Medical Devices\n\nASI Magazine features an article from Excelitas experts that details the various ultraviolet curing\ntechnologies and innovations used for medical catheter assembly today, along with their associated\nbenefits.\n\n[ Learn more ][133]\n\n## Featured Story\n\n## Precision Matters in Fast-Paced Industrial Print Industry\n\nIndustrial Print magazine recently published an article highlighting the need for accurate\napplications that take into account the fast-paced nature of digital print industry, and\nspecifically explores how precise UV curing helps meet these requirements.\n\n[ Learn more ][134]\nPrevious Next\n\n## The Latest at Excelitas\n\nPress Release\nJun 04, 2026\nExcelitas Publishes 2025 Sustainability Report\n[Learn More][135]\nMedia Advisory\nJun 09, 2026\nExcelitas to Demonstrate Optics, Cameras, Lasers and Flashlamps for Industrial Automation at\nAutomate 2026\n[Learn More][136]\nPress Release\nJun 24, 2026\nExcelitas Expands Phoseon VeriCure Water-Cooled UV LED Curing Lamp Portfolio with Four New\nWide-Format Lengths\n[Learn More][137]\nExhibition\nJul 05, 2026\nSingle Photon Workshop (SPW) 2026\n[Learn More][138]\nExhibition\nJul 07, 2026\nAutomotive Manufacturing Technology & Material Show (AMTS)\n[Learn More][139]\nExhibition\nAug 09, 2026\nMethods and Applications in Fluorescence (MAF) 2026\n[Learn More][140]\nWebinar\nAug 11, 2026\nFast-Track Production with UV Foam-in-Place Robotic Dispensing\n[Learn More][141]\nExhibition\nAug 30, 2026\nHRMS 2026\n[Learn More][142]\nExhibition\nSep 06, 2026\n9th European Symposium of Photopolymer Science (ESPS) 2026\n[Learn More][143]\nExhibition\nSep 15, 2026\nLOUPE Americas 2026\n[Learn More][144]\nExhibition\nOct 13, 2026\nSEMICON West 2026\n[Learn More][145]\nPrevious Next\n\n## COMPLIANCE\n* [Company Compliance][146]\n* [Cybersecurity Compliance][147]\n* [ITAR Compliance][148]\n* [Privacy\u00a0Notice][149]\n* [Regional Legislative Compliance][150]\n* [Site Terms & Conditions][151]\n\n## COMPANY\n* [Company Profile][152]\n* [Locations][153]\n* [Careers][154]\n\n## NEWS & EVENTS\n* [Press Releases][155]\n* [Featured Editorials][156]\n* [Events][157]\n\n## CONTACT US\n* [Phone Directory][158]\n* [Web Inquiries][159]\n\n\u00a9 2019 Excelitas Technologies Corp., All rights reserved. [Terms & Conditions][160] | [Privacy\nNotice][161]\n[https://x.com/Excelitas][162]\n[https://www.facebook.com/pages/Excelitas-Technologies-Corp/122632277800460][163]\n[https://www.linkedin.com/company/excelitas-technologies/][164]\n[https://www.youtube.com/@ExcelitasTech][165]\n[https://www.xing.com/pages/qioptiqphotonicsgmbh-co-kg][166]\n[https://www.instagram.com/excelitas_technologies_corp][167]\n\n[1]: #main-content\n[2]: /\n[3]: \n[4]: #\n[5]: /product-category/cameras\n[6]: #\n[7]: /product-category/flim-camera-systems\n[8]: /product-category/high-speed-cameras\n[9]: /product-category/industrial-cameras\n[10]: /product-category/intensified-cameras\n[11]: /product-category/pco-camera-software\n[12]: /product-category/scientific-cameras\n[13]: /product-category/detectors-sensors\n[14]: #\n[15]: /product-category/photonic-detectors\n[16]: /product-category/thermal-infrared-sensors\n[17]: /product-category/electronics-power\n[18]: #\n[19]: /product-category/power-supplies\n[20]: /product-category/light-sources\n[21]: #\n[22]: /product-category/fluorescence-illuminators\n[23]: /product-category/industrial-infrared-thermal-processing-solutions\n[24]: /product-category/lamps-and-lamp-systems\n[25]: /product-category/lasers\n[26]: /product-category/led-components-and-systems\n[27]: /product-category/uv-curing-systems\n[28]: /product-category/uvc-disinfection-oxidation-light-sources\n[29]: /product-category/optics\n[30]: #\n[31]: /product-category/custom-optical-components-assemblies\n[32]: /product-category/imaging-lenses-systems\n[33]: /product-category/integrated-oem-optical-systems\n[34]: /product-category/laser-optics\n[35]: /product-category/night-vision-goggle-optical-modules\n[36]: /product-category/optomechanical-components\n[37]: /product-category/standard-optical-elements\n[38]: /product-category/standard-optical-lenses\n[39]: /product-category/our-brands\n[40]: \n[41]: #\n[42]: /application/autom"
