        "crawl_text": "Skylark Lasers Limited Registered in Scotland SC 445 554 Ratho Park Phase One, 88 Glasgow Rd, Ratho Station, Edinburgh, EH28 8PP Skylark Lasers \u2013 Ultra-stable single frequency CW DPSS lasers\n\nCore products\n\nSkylark 320\n\nSkylark 349\n\nSkylark 780\n\nSkylark 785\n\nApplications\n\nLithography\n\nOptical gratings\n\nWide bandgap inspection\n\nQuantum\n\nBrillouin microscopy\n\nRaman spectroscopy\n\nHolography\n\nFlow cytometry\n\nAbout\n\nNews\n\nCareers\n\nDistributors\n\nEvents\n\nResearch and innovation\n\nRequest quote\n\n&#10005;\nCore products\n\nSkylark 320\n\nSkylark 349\n\nSkylark 780\n\nSkylark 785\n\nApplications\n\nLithography\n\nOptical gratings\n\nWide bandgap inspection\n\nQuantum\n\nBrillouin microscopy\n\nRaman spectroscopy\n\nHolography\n\nFlow cytometry\n\nAbout\n\nNews\n\nCareers\n\nDistributors\n\nEvents\n\nResearch and innovation\n\nUltra-stable\nsingle frequency\nCW DPSS lasers\n\nView lasers\n\nRequest quote\n\nSKYLARK DPSS LASERS\n\nSingle frequency CW\ndiode-pumped solid-state lasers\n\nSKYLARK UV\n\nUltraviolet DPSS lasers\n\nSkylark UV laser systems achieve the highest output power available in single frequency DPSS lasers, engineered with proprietary technology for sustained long-term operation.\n\n320 nm\n\nup to 200 mW\n\nSkylark 320\n\n320 nm single frequency DPSS UV laser\n\nView specifications\n\n349 nm\n\nup to 400 mW\n\nSkylark 349\n\n349 nm single frequency DPSS UV laser\n\nView specifications\n\nSKYLARK NIR\n\nNear-infrared DPSS lasers\n\nSkylark NIR laser systems combine single frequency, low noise output and high optical efficiency \u2014 delivering precise, repeatable performance and ample power margin for complex or lossy setups.\n\n780 nm\n\nup to 400 mW\n\nSkylark 780\n\n780 nm single frequency DPSS NIR laser\n\nView specifications\n\n785 nm\n\nup to 400 mW\n\nSkylark 785\n\n785 nm single frequency DPSS NIR laser\n\nView specifications\n\n\"It\u2019s taken 15 years to find a suitable replacement for our HeCd laser. The Skylark 320 DPSS laser has a clean mode without filters.\"\n\nOPTICAL GRATING MANUFACTURER\n\nPushing the capabilities of photonics to engineer ultra-stable single frequency DPSS lasers\n\nFrom optomechanical design to software development, our team pushes the\ncapabilities of laser technology to engineer ultra-stable, spectrally pure single frequency DPSS\nlasers.\n\nGuided by our core values, we collaborate with our customers and research partners to develop DPSS lasers tailored to your application.\n\nAmbition\nOur team pursues the challenge of miniaturising laser technology to enable the world\u2019s most demanding and cutting-edge applications \u2013 reducing cost, weight, and size while maximising power and performance.\n\nInnovation\nWe develop and commercialise lasers with the purest spectral properties to reveal the unseen, detect the imperceptible, and measure the unknown.\n\nCollaboration\nWe work with our customers and partners to gain a deep understanding of their needs - connecting the dots between lasers and application to deliver tailored solutions.\n\nContinuous learning\nEmbodying a growth mindset, we value continuous learning and thrive in an environment of curiosity and exploration.\n\nROBUST AND RELIABLE DPSS LASERS\n\nBuilt for system integration and efficient performance in demanding environments\n\nSemiconductor inspection\n\nQuantum\n\nHolography\n\nMaterials analysis\n\nLaser interference lithography\n\nFlow cytometry\n\nGrating manufacturing\n\nBrillouin microscopy\n\nRaman + photoluminescence\n\nRaman spectroscopy\n\nRequest a quote\n\nTell us more about your laser and application requirements. No application is too small or too large - we are happy to collaborate with you to develop a solution suited to your requirements.\n\nIf you'd prefer to skip the form and chat to us directly, please email us at sales@skylarklasers.com.\n\nFirst name\n\nLast name\n\nEmail\n\nPhone number\n\nOrganisation\n\nWhere did you hear about Skylark Lasers?\n\nWavelength 320 nm 349 nm 780 nm 785 nm Other (specify in your message)\n\nOutput power\n\nTell us about your application area and laser requirements\n\n\"The Skylark 780 DPSS laser is very stable, we never lose the Rubidium frequency.\"\n\nMICROSCOPE SYSTEM MANUFACTURER\n\n\"It\u2019s taken 15 years to find a suitable replacement for our HeCd laser. The Skylark 320 DPSS laser has a clean mode without filters.\"\n\nOPTICAL GRATING MANUFACTURER\n\n\"I looked at 182 lasers from all different manufacturers. Skylark Lasers was the final choice.\"\n\nSEMICONDUCTOR INSPECTION OEM\n\nSkylark Lasers Limited\n\nRatho Park Phase One,\n\n88 Glasgow Rd\n\nRatho Station,\n\nEdinburgh, EH28 8PP\n\n+44 (0)131 333 2200\n\n\u00a9 2026 Skylark Lasers Limited\nRegistered in Scotland SC 445 554\n\nPrivacy policy\n\nTerms and conditions of sale\n\nSupport [[Skylark Lasers logo]][1]\n* [Core products][2]\n* [Skylark 320][3]\n* [Skylark 349][4]\n* [Skylark 780][5]\n* [Skylark 785][6]\n* [Applications][7]\n* [Lithography][8]\n* [Optical gratings][9]\n* [Wide bandgap inspection][10]\n* [Quantum][11]\n* [Brillouin microscopy][12]\n* [Raman spectroscopy][13]\n* [Holography][14]\n* [Flow cytometry][15]\n* [About][16]\n* [News][17]\n* [Careers][18]\n* [Distributors][19]\n* [Events][20]\n* [Research and innovation][21]\n[Request quote][22]\n][23]\n* [Core products][24]\n* [Skylark 320][25]\n* [Skylark 349][26]\n* [Skylark 780][27]\n* [Skylark 785][28]\n* [Applications][29]\n* [Lithography][30]\n* [Optical gratings][31]\n* [Wide bandgap inspection][32]\n* [Quantum][33]\n* [Brillouin microscopy][34]\n* [Raman spectroscopy][35]\n* [Holography][36]\n* [Flow cytometry][37]\n* [About][38]\n* [News][39]\n* [Careers][40]\n* [Distributors][41]\n* [Events][42]\n* [Research and innovation][43]\n\n### PRODUCTS\n\n# Single frequency CW DPSS lasers\n\nUltra-stable diode-pumped solid-state CW single frequency lasers developed using a proprietary\noptical architecture that delivers long-term, robust, stable, low noise performance.\n\n##### 320 nm\n\n##### up to 200 mW\n\n##### Skylark 320\n\n[View specifications][44]\n\n##### 349 nm\n\n##### up to 400 mW\n\n##### Skylark 349\n\n[View specifications][45]\n\n##### 780 nm\n\n##### up to 400 mW\n\n##### Skylark 780\n\n[View specifications][46]\n\n##### 785 nm\n\n##### up to 400 mW\n\n##### Skylark 785\n\n[View specifications][47]\n\n### WHY CHOOSE SKYLARK LASERS\n\n## Unlock new possibilities for your applications\n\nOur integrated laser platform produces the highest output power in a single box form factor \u2014\ncombining the superior optical properties of solid-state lasers with the small form-factor,\nhigh-efficiency operation of laser diodes \u2014 helping you reveal the unseen, detect the imperceptible,\nand measure the unknown.\n\n#### Absolute wavelength\n\n### \u2264 3 GHz\n\nSub-3 GHz startup repeatability ensures you stay on frequency, maintaining precise alignment for\nanalytical and quantum level tasks.\n\n#### Long term stability\n\n### \u2264 20 MHz\n\nUltra-stable output with < 20 MHz wavelength drift over 24 hours for consistent spectral precision\nand measurement reliability.\n\n#### Environmentally robust\n\n### \u2264 2.0%\n\n< 2.0% intensity drift across a 15 \u00b0C temperature range for uncompromised stability in\ntemperature-sensitive applications.\n\n#### Efficient high power\n\n### 400 mW\n\nOur low-loss, high conversion cavity design achieves up to 400 mW at 349 nm, 780 nm, and 785 nm \u2014\nand 200 mW at 320 nm \u2014 in a compact, stable platform.\n\n## Skylark Lasers commitment to quality\n\nSkylark Lasers are committed to producing precision engineered products that adhere to industry\nstandards. Each laser system is precision engineered under Class 5 cleanroom conditions at our\nheadquarters in Edinburgh, Scotland.\n\nWe are currently engaged in the rigorous process of achieving ISO 9001 certification, reflecting our\ndedication to formalising and enhancing our quality management systems. As we progress towards our\ncertification, we use comprehensive measures that align with internationally recognised standards to\nensure that our processes are consistently refined and improved.\n\nOur commitment to quality is the cornerstone of the trust we cultivate with our clients and the\nlong-lasting relationships we build. By fostering a culture of continuous improvement, we ensure\nthat each product exceeds the expectations of our customers. We strive to set new standards of\nquality and reliability within the laser manufacturing industry.\n\nREQUEST A QUOTE\n\n## Ultra-stable, ultra-reliable, low noise DPSS lasers. Get in touch to tailor a laser to your\n## application.\n\n[Request quote][48]\n[[Skylark Lasers logo]][49]\nSkylark Lasers Limited\nRatho Park Phase One,\n88 Glasgow Rd\nRatho Station,\nEdinburgh, EH28 8PP\n+44 (0)131 333 2200\n\n\u00a9 2026 Skylark Lasers Limited\nRegistered in Scotland SC 445 554\n* [Privacy policy][50]\n* [Terms and conditions of sale][51]\n* [Support][52]\n\n[1]: https://skylarklasers.com\n[2]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/\n[3]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/320-nx/\n[4]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/349-nx/\n[5]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/780-nx/\n[6]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/785-nx/\n[7]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/\n[8]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-lithography/\n[9]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/optical-grating-mastering-lasers/\n[10]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-semiconductor/\n[11]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-quantum/\n[12]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-brillouin/\n[13]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-raman-spectroscopy/\n[14]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/holography/\n[15]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-flow-cytometry/\n[16]: https://skylarklasers.com/about/\n[17]: https://skylarklasers.com/news/\n[18]: https://skylarklasers.com/careers/\n[19]: https://skylarklasers.com/distributors/\n[20]: https://skylarklasers.com/events/\n[21]: https://skylarklasers.com/research-development-innovation/\n[22]: /product-quote-request\n[23]: #\n[24]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/\n[25]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/320-nx/\n[26]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/349-nx/\n[27]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/780-nx/\n[28]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/785-nx/\n[29]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/\n[30]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-lithography/\n[31]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/optical-grating-mastering-lasers/\n[32]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-semiconductor/\n[33]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-quantum/\n[34]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-brillouin/\n[35]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-raman-spectroscopy/\n[36]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/holography/\n[37]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-flow-cytometry/\n[38]: https://skylarklasers.com/about/\n[39]: https://skylarklasers.com/news/\n[40]: https://skylarklasers.com/careers/\n[41]: https://skylarklasers.com/distributors/\n[42]: https://skylarklasers.com/events/\n[43]: https://skylarklasers.com/research-development-innovation/\n[44]: /products/320-nx\n[45]: /products/349-nx\n[46]: /products/780-nx\n[47]: /products/785-nx\n[48]: /product-quote-request/\n[49]: https://skylarklasers.com\n[50]: https://skylarklasers.com/privacy/\n[51]: https://skylarklasers.com/terms/\n[52]: https://skylarklasers.com/support/ [[Skylark Lasers logo]][1]\n* [Core products][2]\n* [Skylark 320][3]\n* [Skylark 349][4]\n* [Skylark 780][5]\n* [Skylark 785][6]\n* [Applications][7]\n* [Lithography][8]\n* [Optical gratings][9]\n* [Wide bandgap inspection][10]\n* [Quantum][11]\n* [Brillouin microscopy][12]\n* [Raman spectroscopy][13]\n* [Holography][14]\n* [Flow cytometry][15]\n* [About][16]\n* [News][17]\n* [Careers][18]\n* [Distributors][19]\n* [Events][20]\n* [Research and innovation][21]\n[Request quote][22]\n][23]\n* [Core products][24]\n* [Skylark 320][25]\n* [Skylark 349][26]\n* [Skylark 780][27]\n* [Skylark 785][28]\n* [Applications][29]\n* [Lithography][30]\n* [Optical gratings][31]\n* [Wide bandgap inspection][32]\n* [Quantum][33]\n* [Brillouin microscopy][34]\n* [Raman spectroscopy][35]\n* [Holography][36]\n* [Flow cytometry][37]\n* [About][38]\n* [News][39]\n* [Careers][40]\n* [Distributors][41]\n* [Events][42]\n* [Research and innovation][43]\n\n##### 320 nm\n\n# SKYLARK 320\n\n3"
