          {
            "url": "https://skylarklasers.com/products/320-nx/",
            "text": "[[Skylark Lasers logo]][1]\n* [Core products][2]\n* [Skylark 320][3]\n* [Skylark 349][4]\n* [Skylark 780][5]\n* [Skylark 785][6]\n* [Applications][7]\n* [Lithography][8]\n* [Optical gratings][9]\n* [Wide bandgap inspection][10]\n* [Quantum][11]\n* [Brillouin microscopy][12]\n* [Raman spectroscopy][13]\n* [Holography][14]\n* [Flow cytometry][15]\n* [About][16]\n* [News][17]\n* [Careers][18]\n* [Distributors][19]\n* [Events][20]\n* [Research and innovation][21]\n[Request quote][22]\n][23]\n* [Core products][24]\n* [Skylark 320][25]\n* [Skylark 349][26]\n* [Skylark 780][27]\n* [Skylark 785][28]\n* [Applications][29]\n* [Lithography][30]\n* [Optical gratings][31]\n* [Wide bandgap inspection][32]\n* [Quantum][33]\n* [Brillouin microscopy][34]\n* [Raman spectroscopy][35]\n* [Holography][36]\n* [Flow cytometry][37]\n* [About][38]\n* [News][39]\n* [Careers][40]\n* [Distributors][41]\n* [Events][42]\n* [Research and innovation][43]\n\n##### 320 nm\n\n# SKYLARK 320\n\n320 nm single frequency diode-pumped solid-state laser system delivering the highest ultraviolet\npower from a DPSS platform.\n\n[View specifications][44]\n[Request quote][45]\n\n#### High power\n\n### 200 mW\n\nDelivers up to 200 mW of efficient ultraviolet light at 320 nm, with ample power margin for complex\nsetups.\n\n#### TEM\u2080\u2080 mode\n\n### M\u00b2 \u2264 1.1\n\nDelivers a clean mode with ellipticity > 95%, providing uniform spatial quality and low noise\noperation.\n\n#### Stable output\n\n### \u00b1 0.2 pm\n\nMaintains \u00b1 0.2 pm wavelength stability with mode-hop-free operation over 10s of hours.\n\n#### \"It\u2019s taken 15 years to find a suitable replacement for our HeCd laser. The Skylark 320 DPSS\n#### laser has a clean mode without filters.\"\n\nOPTICAL GRATING MANUFACTURER\n\n## Skylark 320 CW DPSS laser\n\nThe Skylark 320 CW DPSS laser provides ultra-stable single frequency UV light at 320 nm.\n\nEngineered for consistent long-term, stable performance, delivering up to 200 mW of ultra-stable\noutput, low noise, and spectral purity.\n\n[Download specifications][46]\n\n## Key specifications\n\nWavelength\n\n320 nm\n\nOutput power\n\nup to 200 mW\n\nSpectral bandwidth\n\n\u2264 500 kHz\n\nSpatial mode\n\nTEM\u2080\u2080\n\nOperational mode\n\nCW, SLM\n\n## Beam parameters\n\nBeam height\n\n90.0 mm\n\nBeam diameter\n\n1.0 - 1.5 mm\n\nBeam quality\n\nM\u00b2 \u2264 1.1\n\nBeam divergence\n\n\u2264 1.0 mrad, diffraction limited\n\nBeam pointing stability\n\n\u2264 5 \u03bcrad/\u00b0C\n\nCoherence length\n\n> 100 m\n\nPolarisation ratio\n\n\u2265 100:1, vertical\n\n0 hours\n\n2,000 hours\n\n## Laser performance\n\nSpectral stability (8 hours)\n\n\u00b1 0.2 pm\n\nPower stability (8 hours)\n\n\u2264 2.0 % pk-pk\n\nPower noise (10 Hz - 10 MHz)\n\n\u2264 0.3% RMS\n\n## Laser control\n\nControl interface\n\nWeb-based GUI\n\nControl connectivity\n\nEthernet (TCP/IP) + digital I/O\n\nSafety features\n\nInterlock, mechanical shutter\n\n## Laser dimensions\n\nLaser system (L x W x H)\n\n425 x 200 x 123 mm\n\n## Operating conditions\n\nWarm up time\n\n5 - 30 mins\n\nAmbient temperature\n\n18 - 30 \u00b0C\n\nLaser interface stability\n\n\u00b1 1.5 \u00b0C\n\nStorage\n\n0 - 50 \u00b0C\n\nHumidity\n\n5 - 95 %, non-condensing\n\nPower consumption (typical)\n\n< 50 W\n\n## HeCd gas laser vs. DPSS laser\n\nLooking to replace your helium cadmium laser with an efficient, high power DPSS laser alternative?\n\nBenefit from up to 4x more usable power, stable and reliable output, and a high quality beam without\nmode cleaning.\n\nThe Skylark 320 is designed to replace HeCd lasers in applications across:\n* Laser interference lithography\n* UV Raman spectroscopy\n* Photoluminescence\n\n## Upgrade your UV workhorse\n\nHelium Cadmium (HeCd) lasers have long served the demand for ultraviolet wavelengths at 325 nm \u2014 but\nare now outclassed by a diode-pumped solid-state laser alternative.\n\nUpgrading from a 325 nm HeCd to a 320 nm Skylark DPSS laser offers four times more power, improved\nstability, lower maintenance, and a cleaner spectral performance within a compact, solid-state laser\nplatform that is ready for integration into both research and industrial environments. Discover [6\nreasons to consider replacing your HeCd system with a DPSS laser][47] on our blog.\n\n## Four times more usable power\n\nThe Skylark 320 nm DPSS laser delivers up to four times the output power of a typical 325 nm HeCd\nsystem.\n\nHigher power translates to shorter processing times, higher throughput, and improved signal strength\nin UV-sensitive materials and processes.\n\n## Long term stability\n\nHeCd lasers are prone to power drift and thermal instability, which can affect repeatability and\naccuracy in precision applications.\n\nThe Skylark 320 offers wavelength stability of \u00b1 0.2 pm and power stability within \u00b1 2% over 10s of\nhours, maintaining consistent illumination and spectral performance over extended operation.\n\n## Spectral purity\n\nThe Skylark 320 laser operates in a single frequency, TEM\u2080\u2080 mode with M\u00b2 \u2264 1.1, delivering a clean\nGaussian beam and ultra-narrow linewidth: < 1 GHz vs. < 0.00005 GHz.\n\nThis produces stable interference fringes, uniform illumination, and excellent spatial coherence,\nimproving feature uniformity in lithography and data quality in spectroscopy.\n\n## Low maintenance, compact design\n\nDPSS lasers often have a longer lifetime and double the maintenance interval of gas lasers,\nsignificantly reducing downtime and operational disruption. Paired with long-term stability, DPSS\nlasers also offer increased reliability that makes them ideal for industrial customers seeking to\nreduce time and resources spent on reactive maintenance.\n\n### APPLICATIONS\n\n## Spectrally pure ultraviolet 320 nm laser delivering scalable, high power for high throughput\n## applications\n\n### Optical characterisation\n\n##### Leverage uniform, high power ultraviolet light with low noise and long term stability.\n\nThe Skylark UV series of lasers illuminate inspection applications such as:\n* [\n\nRaman spectroscopy (UV Raman)\n\n][48]\n* Photoluminescence (PL)\n* UV fluorescence\n* UV optical manipulation\n\n### Process and fabrication\n\n##### Execute detailed patterning over large areas without compromising quality.\n\nThe Skylark UV series of lasers power manufacturing applications such as:\n* [\n\nLaser interference lithography\n\n][49]\n* [\n\nOptical grating mastering and fabrication\n\n][50]\n* [\n\nInterferometry\n\n][51]\n* [\n\nWafer inspection\n\n][52]\n\n### Inspection and metrology\n\n##### Collect data with precision, leveraging uniform power and a high quality beam.\n\nSkylark UV series of lasers enable advanced research and industrial applications such as:\n* [Semiconductor metrology and inspection][53]\n* Semiconductor inspection\n* 2D materials characterisation\n* Wide bandgap semiconductors materials\n* [UV flow cytometry][54]\n\nREQUEST A QUOTE\n\n][55]\n\n#### Leverage the highest power, single frequency ultraviolet light at 320 nm built on a stable and\n#### reliable DPSS laser platform. Get in touch to tailor a laser to your application.\n\n[Request quote][56]\n[[Skylark Lasers logo]][57]\nSkylark Lasers Limited\nRatho Park Phase One,\n88 Glasgow Rd\nRatho Station,\nEdinburgh, EH28 8PP\n+44 (0)131 333 2200\n\n\u00a9 2026 Skylark Lasers Limited\nRegistered in Scotland SC 445 554\n* [Privacy policy][58]\n* [Terms and conditions of sale][59]\n* [Support][60]\n\n[1]: https://skylarklasers.com\n[2]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/\n[3]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/320-nx/\n[4]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/349-nx/\n[5]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/780-nx/\n[6]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/785-nx/\n[7]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/\n[8]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-lithography/\n[9]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/optical-grating-mastering-lasers/\n[10]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-semiconductor/\n[11]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-quantum/\n[12]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-brillouin/\n[13]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-raman-spectroscopy/\n[14]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/holography/\n[15]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-flow-cytometry/\n[16]: https://skylarklasers.com/about/\n[17]: https://skylarklasers.com/news/\n[18]: https://skylarklasers.com/careers/\n[19]: https://skylarklasers.com/distributors/\n[20]: https://skylarklasers.com/events/\n[21]: https://skylarklasers.com/research-development-innovation/\n[22]: /product-quote-request\n[23]: #\n[24]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/\n[25]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/320-nx/\n[26]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/349-nx/\n[27]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/780-nx/\n[28]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/785-nx/\n[29]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/\n[30]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-lithography/\n[31]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/optical-grating-mastering-lasers/\n[32]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-semiconductor/\n[33]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-quantum/\n[34]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-brillouin/\n[35]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-raman-spectroscopy/\n[36]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/holography/\n[37]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-flow-cytometry/\n[38]: https://skylarklasers.com/about/\n[39]: https://skylarklasers.com/news/\n[40]: https://skylarklasers.com/careers/\n[41]: https://skylarklasers.com/distributors/\n[42]: https://skylarklasers.com/events/\n[43]: https://skylarklasers.com/research-development-innovation/\n[44]: #320-specs\n[45]: /product-quote-request/\n[46]: https://skylarklasers.com/wp-content/uploads/Skylark-Lasers-320-CW-DPSS-single-frequency-laser\n-Specifications.pdf\n[47]: /news/6-reasons-to-replace-hecd-and-argon-ion-gas-lasers-with-diode-pumped-solid-state-alterna\ntives/\n[48]: /applications/lasers-for-raman-spectroscopy/\n[49]: /applications/lasers-for-lithography/\n[50]: /applications/optical-grating-mastering-lasers/\n[51]: /applications/holography/\n[52]: /applications/lasers-for-semiconductor/\n[53]: /applications/lasers-for-semiconductor/\n[54]: /applications/lasers-for-flow-cytometry/\n[55]: /product-quote-request/\n[56]: /product-quote-request/\n[57]: https://skylarklasers.com\n[58]: https://skylarklasers.com/privacy/\n[59]: https://skylarklasers.com/terms/\n[60]: https://skylarklasers.com/support/"
