            "text": "[[Skylark Lasers logo]][1]\n* [Core products][2]\n* [Skylark 320][3]\n* [Skylark 349][4]\n* [Skylark 780][5]\n* [Skylark 785][6]\n* [Applications][7]\n* [Lithography][8]\n* [Optical gratings][9]\n* [Wide bandgap inspection][10]\n* [Quantum][11]\n* [Brillouin microscopy][12]\n* [Raman spectroscopy][13]\n* [Holography][14]\n* [Flow cytometry][15]\n* [About][16]\n* [News][17]\n* [Careers][18]\n* [Distributors][19]\n* [Events][20]\n* [Research and innovation][21]\n[Request quote][22]\n][23]\n* [Core products][24]\n* [Skylark 320][25]\n* [Skylark 349][26]\n* [Skylark 780][27]\n* [Skylark 785][28]\n* [Applications][29]\n* [Lithography][30]\n* [Optical gratings][31]\n* [Wide bandgap inspection][32]\n* [Quantum][33]\n* [Brillouin microscopy][34]\n* [Raman spectroscopy][35]\n* [Holography][36]\n* [Flow cytometry][37]\n* [About][38]\n* [News][39]\n* [Careers][40]\n* [Distributors][41]\n* [Events][42]\n* [Research and innovation][43]\n\n##### 349 nm\n\n# SKYLARK 349\n\n349 nm single frequency diode-pumped solid-state laser system delivering the highest ultraviolet\npower from a DPSS platform.\n\n[View specifications][44]\n[Request quote][45]\n\n#### Reliable power\n\n### 400 mW\n\nUp to 400 mW of efficient ultraviolet light at 349 nm, providing power margin for high throughput\ntasks.\n\n#### TEM\u2080\u2080 mode\n\n### M\u00b2 \u2264 1.1\n\nDelivers a clean mode with ellipticity > 95%, providing uniform spatial quality and low noise\noutput.\n\n#### Stable output\n\n### \u00b1 0.2 pm\n\nMaintains \u00b1 0.2 pm wavelength stability with mode-hop-free operation over 10s of hours.\n\n#### \"We\u2019re very pleased with the laser\u2019s performance compared to our aging Ti:Sapphire system. The\n#### Skylark 349 laser shows better beam profile and output stability.\n####\n#### The high quality beam gives us plenty of power headroom, allowing us to reduce the output power\n#### by 30% while still achieving the performance we need.\"\n\nOPTICAL GRATING MANUFACTURER\n\n## Skylark 349 CW DPSS laser\n\nThe Skylark 349 CW DPSS laser provides ultra-stable single frequency UV light at 349 nm.\n\nEngineered for consistent long-term, stable performance, delivering up to 400 mW of ultra-stable\noutput, low noise, and spectral purity.\n\n[Download specifications][46]\n\n## Key specifications\n\nWavelength\n\n349 nm\n\nOutput power\n\nup to 400 mW\n\nSpectral bandwidth\n\n\u2264 500 kHz\n\nSpatial mode\n\nTEM\u2080\u2080\n\nOperational mode\n\nCW, SLM\n\n## Beam parameters\n\nBeam height\n\n90.0 mm\n\nBeam diameter\n\n1.0 - 1.5 mm\n\nBeam quality\n\nM\u00b2 \u2264 1.1\n\nBeam divergence\n\n\u2264 1.0 mrad, diffraction limited\n\nBeam pointing stability\n\n\u2264 5 \u03bcrad/\u00b0C\n\nCoherence length\n\n> 100 m\n\nPolarisation ratio\n\n\u2265 100:1, vertical\n\n0 hours\n\n2,000 hours\n\n## Laser performance\n\nSpectral stability (8 hours)\n\n\u00b1 0.2 pm\n\nPower stability (8 hours)\n\n\u2264 2.0 % pk-pk\n\nPower noise (10 Hz - 10 MHz)\n\n\u2264 0.3% RMS\n\n## Laser control\n\nControl interface\n\nWeb-based GUI\n\nControl connectivity\n\nEthernet (TCP/IP) + digital I/O\n\nSafety features\n\nInterlock, mechanical shutter\n\n## Laser dimensions\n\nLaser system (L x W x H)\n\n425 x 200 x 123 mm\n\n## Operating conditions\n\nWarm up time\n\n5 - 30 mins\n\nAmbient temperature\n\n18 - 30 \u00b0C\n\nLaser interface stability\n\n\u00b1 1.5 \u00b0C\n\nStorage\n\n0 - 50 \u00b0C\n\nHumidity\n\n5 - 95 %, non-condensing\n\nPower consumption (typical)\n\n< 50 W\n\n### APPLICATIONS\n\n## Robust, ultra-stable ultraviolet laser delivering uniform light for materials research and high\n## throughput manufacturing\n\n### Inspection and characterisation\n\n##### Collect data with precision, leveraging uniform power and a high quality beam.\n\nThe Skylark 349 UV provides an excitation source for applications such as:\n* Semiconductor materials characterisation\n* Wide bandgap materials (e.g. SiC, GaN, AlN)\n* UV Raman\n* Photoluminescence (PL)\n\n### Process and fabrication\n\n##### Develop consistent, detailed patterns over large areas without compromising quality.\n\nThe Skylark 349 ultraviolet laser at 349 nm powers applications such as:\n* Laser interference lithography\n* Photoluminescence (PL)\n* Wide bandgap materials inspection (e.g. SiC, GaN, AlN)\n* UV interferometry\n* Wafer inspection\n\nREQUEST A QUOTE\n\n## Leverage the highest power, single frequency ultraviolet light at 349 nm built on a stable and\n## reliable DPSS laser platform. Get in touch to tailor a laser to your application.\n\n[Request quote][47]\n[[Skylark Lasers logo]][48]\nSkylark Lasers Limited\nRatho Park Phase One,\n88 Glasgow Rd\nRatho Station,\nEdinburgh, EH28 8PP\n+44 (0)131 333 2200\n\n\u00a9 2026 Skylark Lasers Limited\nRegistered in Scotland SC 445 554\n* [Privacy policy][49]\n* [Terms and conditions of sale][50]\n* [Support][51]\n\n[1]: https://skylarklasers.com\n[2]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/\n[3]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/320-nx/\n[4]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/349-nx/\n[5]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/780-nx/\n[6]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/785-nx/\n[7]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/\n[8]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-lithography/\n[9]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/optical-grating-mastering-lasers/\n[10]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-semiconductor/\n[11]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-quantum/\n[12]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-brillouin/\n[13]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-raman-spectroscopy/\n[14]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/holography/\n[15]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-flow-cytometry/\n[16]: https://skylarklasers.com/about/\n[17]: https://skylarklasers.com/news/\n[18]: https://skylarklasers.com/careers/\n[19]: https://skylarklasers.com/distributors/\n[20]: https://skylarklasers.com/events/\n[21]: https://skylarklasers.com/research-development-innovation/\n[22]: /product-quote-request\n[23]: #\n[24]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/\n[25]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/320-nx/\n[26]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/349-nx/\n[27]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/780-nx/\n[28]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/785-nx/\n[29]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/\n[30]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-lithography/\n[31]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/optical-grating-mastering-lasers/\n[32]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-semiconductor/\n[33]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-quantum/\n[34]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-brillouin/\n[35]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-raman-spectroscopy/\n[36]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/holography/\n[37]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-flow-cytometry/\n[38]: https://skylarklasers.com/about/\n[39]: https://skylarklasers.com/news/\n[40]: https://skylarklasers.com/careers/\n[41]: https://skylarklasers.com/distributors/\n[42]: https://skylarklasers.com/events/\n[43]: https://skylarklasers.com/research-development-innovation/\n[44]: #349-specs\n[45]: /product-quote-request/\n[46]: https://skylarklasers.com/wp-content/uploads/Skylark-Lasers-349-CW-DPSS-single-frequency-laser\n-Specifications.pdf\n[47]: /product-quote-request/\n[48]: https://skylarklasers.com\n[49]: https://skylarklasers.com/privacy/\n[50]: https://skylarklasers.com/terms/\n[51]: https://skylarklasers.com/support/"
