            "text": "[[Skylark Lasers logo]][1]\n* [Core products][2]\n* [Skylark 320][3]\n* [Skylark 349][4]\n* [Skylark 780][5]\n* [Skylark 785][6]\n* [Applications][7]\n* [Lithography][8]\n* [Optical gratings][9]\n* [Wide bandgap inspection][10]\n* [Quantum][11]\n* [Brillouin microscopy][12]\n* [Raman spectroscopy][13]\n* [Holography][14]\n* [Flow cytometry][15]\n* [About][16]\n* [News][17]\n* [Careers][18]\n* [Distributors][19]\n* [Events][20]\n* [Research and innovation][21]\n[Request quote][22]\n][23]\n* [Core products][24]\n* [Skylark 320][25]\n* [Skylark 349][26]\n* [Skylark 780][27]\n* [Skylark 785][28]\n* [Applications][29]\n* [Lithography][30]\n* [Optical gratings][31]\n* [Wide bandgap inspection][32]\n* [Quantum][33]\n* [Brillouin microscopy][34]\n* [Raman spectroscopy][35]\n* [Holography][36]\n* [Flow cytometry][37]\n* [About][38]\n* [News][39]\n* [Careers][40]\n* [Distributors][41]\n* [Events][42]\n* [Research and innovation][43]\n\n##### 780 nm\n\n# SKYLARK 780\n\n780 nm single frequency diode-pumped solid-state laser delivering spectrally pure NIR light from an\nefficient form factor.\n\n[View specifications][44]\n[Request quote][45]\n\n#### Reliable power\n\n### 400 mW\n\nProvides up to 400 mW of efficient, spectrally pure near-infrared light at 780 nm, with ample power\nfor complex setups.\n\n#### Clean beam\n\n### M\u00b2 \u2264 1.1\n\nDelivers a clean TEM\u2080\u2080 mode with ellipticity > 95%, providing uniform spatial quality and low noise\noutput.\n\n#### Stable output\n\n### \u00b1 0.2 pm\n\nMaintains \u00b1 0.2 pm wavelength stability over 10s of hours, ensuring spectral integrity for precision\ntasks.\n\n## Skylark 780 CW DPSS laser\n\nThe Skylark 780 CW DPSS laser provides ultra-stable single frequency NIR light at 780 nm.\n\nEngineered for consistent long-term, stable performance, delivering up to 400 mW of ultra-stable\noutput, low noise, and spectral purity.\n\n[Download specifications][46]\n\n## Key specifications\n\nWavelength\n\n780 nm\n\nOutput power\n\nup to 400 mW\n\nSpectral bandwidth\n\n\u2264 300 kHz\n\nSpatial mode\n\nTEM\u2080\u2080\n\nOperational mode\n\nCW, SLM\n\n## Beam parameters\n\nBeam height\n\n90.0 mm\n\nBeam diameter\n\n0.8 - 1.2 mm\n\nBeam quality\n\nM\u00b2 \u2264 1.1\n\nBeam divergence\n\n\u2264 1.0 mrad, diffraction limited\n\nBeam pointing stability\n\n\u2264 5 \u03bcrad/\u00b0C\n\nCoherence length\n\n> 100 m\n\nPolarisation ratio\n\n\u2265 100:1, vertical\n\n0 hours\n\n2,000 hours\n\n## Laser performance\n\nSpectral stability (8 hours)\n\n\u00b1 0.2 pm\n\nPower stability (8 hours)\n\n\u2264 2.0 % pk-pk\n\nPower noise (10 Hz - 10 MHz)\n\n\u2264 0.3% RMS\n\nASE noise\n\n< \u2013 80 dB\n\n## Laser control\n\nControl interface\n\nWeb-based GUI\n\nControl connectivity\n\nEthernet (TCP/IP) + digital I/O\n\nSafety features\n\nInterlock, mechanical shutter\n\n## Laser dimensions\n\nLaser system (L x W x H)\n\n425 x 200 x 123 mm\n\n## Operating conditions\n\nWarm up time\n\n5 - 30 mins\n\nAmbient temperature\n\n18 - 30 \u00b0C\n\nLaser interface stability\n\n\u00b1 1.5 \u00b0C\n\nStorage\n\n0 - 50 \u00b0C\n\nHumidity\n\n5 - 95 %, non-condensing\n\nPower consumption (typical)\n\n< 50 W\n\n### APPLICATIONS\n\n## Spectrally pure laser enabling Rubidium-based applications in microscopy, spectroscopy, and\n## quantum\n\n### Atomic physics\n\nWith ultra-stable output and ultra-narrow linewidth, single frequency DPSS lasers enable precise\ndata collection and measurement for advanced quantum applications such as:\n* Rubidium D2 line\n* \u2078\u2075Rb\n* \u2078\u2077Rb\n* Atom interferometry\n* Rb MOTs (magneto-optical traps)\n* gMOTs (grating magneto-optical traps)\n* Cold atom trapping\n* NIR pump source\n* Quantum frequency conversion\n* Optical manipulation\n* Doppler cooling\n* Entangled photon generation\n\n### Microscopy and spectroscopy\n\nOur lasers deliver up to 400 mW of near-infrared light for analytical and inspection applications\nsuch as:\n* [\n\nBrillouin microscopy\n\nBrillouin Light Scattering (BLS)\n\n][47]\n* Raman spectroscopy\n* NIR fluorescence\n* Rb optical manipulation\n\nREQUEST A QUOTE\n\n## Target rubidium transitions with low noise, ultra-stable precision at 780 nm. Get in touch to\n## tailor a laser to your application.\n\n[Request quote][48]\n[[Skylark Lasers logo]][49]\nSkylark Lasers Limited\nRatho Park Phase One,\n88 Glasgow Rd\nRatho Station,\nEdinburgh, EH28 8PP\n+44 (0)131 333 2200\n\n\u00a9 2026 Skylark Lasers Limited\nRegistered in Scotland SC 445 554\n* [Privacy policy][50]\n* [Terms and conditions of sale][51]\n* [Support][52]\n\n[1]: https://skylarklasers.com\n[2]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/\n[3]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/320-nx/\n[4]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/349-nx/\n[5]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/780-nx/\n[6]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/785-nx/\n[7]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/\n[8]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-lithography/\n[9]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/optical-grating-mastering-lasers/\n[10]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-semiconductor/\n[11]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-quantum/\n[12]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-brillouin/\n[13]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-raman-spectroscopy/\n[14]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/holography/\n[15]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-flow-cytometry/\n[16]: https://skylarklasers.com/about/\n[17]: https://skylarklasers.com/news/\n[18]: https://skylarklasers.com/careers/\n[19]: https://skylarklasers.com/distributors/\n[20]: https://skylarklasers.com/events/\n[21]: https://skylarklasers.com/research-development-innovation/\n[22]: /product-quote-request\n[23]: #\n[24]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/\n[25]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/320-nx/\n[26]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/349-nx/\n[27]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/780-nx/\n[28]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/785-nx/\n[29]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/\n[30]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-lithography/\n[31]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/optical-grating-mastering-lasers/\n[32]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-semiconductor/\n[33]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-quantum/\n[34]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-brillouin/\n[35]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-raman-spectroscopy/\n[36]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/holography/\n[37]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-flow-cytometry/\n[38]: https://skylarklasers.com/about/\n[39]: https://skylarklasers.com/news/\n[40]: https://skylarklasers.com/careers/\n[41]: https://skylarklasers.com/distributors/\n[42]: https://skylarklasers.com/events/\n[43]: https://skylarklasers.com/research-development-innovation/\n[44]: #780-specs\n[45]: /product-quote-request/\n[46]: https://skylarklasers.com/wp-content/uploads/Skylark-Lasers-780-CW-DPSS-single-frequency-laser\n-Specifications.pdf\n[47]: #\n[48]: /product-quote-request/\n[49]: https://skylarklasers.com\n[50]: https://skylarklasers.com/privacy/\n[51]: https://skylarklasers.com/terms/\n[52]: https://skylarklasers.com/support/"
