          {
            "url": "https://skylarklasers.com/team",
            "text": "[[Skylark Lasers logo]][1]\n* [Core products][2]\n* [Skylark 320][3]\n* [Skylark 349][4]\n* [Skylark 780][5]\n* [Skylark 785][6]\n* [Applications][7]\n* [Lithography][8]\n* [Optical gratings][9]\n* [Wide bandgap inspection][10]\n* [Quantum][11]\n* [Brillouin microscopy][12]\n* [Raman spectroscopy][13]\n* [Holography][14]\n* [Flow cytometry][15]\n* [About][16]\n* [News][17]\n* [Careers][18]\n* [Distributors][19]\n* [Events][20]\n* [Research and innovation][21]\n[Request quote][22]\n][23]\n* [Core products][24]\n* [Skylark 320][25]\n* [Skylark 349][26]\n* [Skylark 780][27]\n* [Skylark 785][28]\n* [Applications][29]\n* [Lithography][30]\n* [Optical gratings][31]\n* [Wide bandgap inspection][32]\n* [Quantum][33]\n* [Brillouin microscopy][34]\n* [Raman spectroscopy][35]\n* [Holography][36]\n* [Flow cytometry][37]\n* [About][38]\n* [News][39]\n* [Careers][40]\n* [Distributors][41]\n* [Events][42]\n* [Research and innovation][43]\n\n### SKYLARK LASERS\n\n# Laser manufacturer of spectrally pure, high performance CW single frequency DPSS lasers\n\nOur single frequency laser systems are precision engineered under Class 5 cleanroom conditions at\nour headquarters in Edinburgh, Scotland.\n\nWe work collaboratively with our customers and research partners to understand their needs and\ntailor our lasers to their application \u2013 helping reveal the unseen, detect the imperceptible, and\nmeasure the unknown.\n\n## Skylark Lasers origin\n\nThe skylark is a remarkable species distinguished by its ability to maintain a sustained, controlled\nascent while producing a pure, uninterrupted song. This mirrors the core engineering philosophy of\nour lasers: continuous, stable operation over an extended lifetime.\n\nWith Skylark Lasers, you get more than a beam of light \u2014 you get a commitment to precision,\nstability, and spectral purity.\n\nEstablished in 2013 with a focus on the R&D of uncommon and hard-to-reach wavelengths, Skylark\nLasers now deliver commercial systems trusted by leading researchers and OEMs worldwide.\n\n## Core values\n\nOur core values guide how we innovate, collaborate, and grow. We are driven by ambition to tackle\nthe toughest challenges, and by innovation to uncover new possibilities through leading-edge laser\ntechnology. With collaboration, we build strong partnerships that transform ideas into real-world\nsolutions. And through continuous learning, we nurture a growth mindset that keeps us curious,\nadaptable, and always moving forward.\n\n##### Ambition\n\nOur team pursues the challenge of developing spectrally pure laser technology to enable the world\u2019s\nmost demanding and cutting-edge applications \u2013 reducing cost, weight, and size while maximising\npower and performance.\n\n##### Innovation\n\nWe develop and commercialise reliable, long lifetime lasers with the purest spectral properties that\nenable customers to reveal the unseen, detect the imperceptible, and measure the unknown.\n\n##### Collaboration\n\nWe work with our customers and partners to gain a deep understanding of their needs - connecting the\ndots between lasers and application to deliver tailored solutions.\n\n##### Continuous learning\n\nEmbodying a growth mindset, we value continuous learning and thrive in an environment of curiosity\nand exploration.\n\n## Skylark Lasers team\n\n##### Executive Chairman\n\n##### Ewan McLellan\n\nDeeply embedded in the start-up and scale-up ecosystem since 2008, Ewan serves in pivotal roles\nranging from CEO to Chair. An engineer by training, his leadership experience spans across\nnanomaterials and advanced engineering. Since 2020, he has Chaired Skylark Lasers, guiding the\ncompany through strategic milestones and positioning it for long-term success.\n\n##### Non-Executive Director\n\n##### Mark Hanson\n\nMark brings a wealth of experience working for entrepreneurial technology companies, holding various\nmanagement and leadership positions across global R&D, procurement, engineering, and commercial\ndevelopment. At Skylark Lasers, Mark drives the company\u2019s commercial strategy, leveraging his broad\nexpertise to deliver sustainable growth and customer success.\n\n##### CEO\n\n##### Chris Madin\n\nChris brings over 20 years of leadership experience in the photonics and laser instrumentation\nindustry, and extensive experience in building global sales channels, managing new product\ndevelopment, and driving operational excellence in high growth photonics environments with customers\nacross semiconductor inspection and life science instrumentation.\n\n##### CTO\n\n##### Michael Summers\n\nMichael has over 20 years of experience leading the delivery of complex optoelectronic products for\nstart-ups, SMEs, and multinationals across multiple industries. At Skylark Lasers Michael drives the\nsuccessful development of products, processes, and innovations to provide real value to our\ncustomers.\n\n##### Research Project Manager\n\n##### Mark Mackenzie\n\nMark holds a PhD in Ultrafast Laser Inscription and Microfluidic Devices from Heriot-Watt\nUniversity. Since joining Skylark Lasers in 2018, he has led multidisciplinary R&D programs;\nestablishing process frameworks that enable consistent prototype-to-production transfer and\nsuccessful commercialised outcomes.\n\n##### Head of Engineering\n\n##### Gregor McDowall\n\nWith a passion for purpose-led innovation and customer-centric design, Gregor guides the engineering\nteam towards exciting new developments. Since joining Skylark Lasers, Gregor has been instrumental\nin driving our journey towards excellence, and continues to challenge the industry status quo.\n\n##### Head of Hardware\n\n##### Robin Shears\n\nRobin joined Skylark Lasers in 2021, bringing experience in delivering specialised projects from\nrocket avionics to quantum sensors. Robin leads the hardware and software team while driving a\n'right first time' approach to development, while translating customer requirements into\nplug-and-play user experiences.\n\n[Scott Early - Skylark Lasers]\n\n##### Head of Operations\n\n##### Scott Early\n\nScott has been the Skylark Lasers head of operations since 2021. With over 10 years of experience in\nsingle frequency laser development and technical management, Scott covers a wide range of roles;\ndriving operational excellence, nurturing talent, and empowering his teams to succeed.\n\n##### Head of Sales and Marketing\n\n##### Lauren Percy\n\nLauren is a driven commercial professional with a track record of developing and executing\nsuccessful marketing strategies in the deep tech sector, with experience across photonics and the\nsemiconductor industry. Lauren has a passion for solving commercial challenges and driving\nsuccessful business outcomes.\n\n[[Skylark Lasers logo]][44]\nSkylark Lasers Limited\nRatho Park Phase One,\n88 Glasgow Rd\nRatho Station,\nEdinburgh, EH28 8PP\n+44 (0)131 333 2200\n\n\u00a9 2026 Skylark Lasers Limited\nRegistered in Scotland SC 445 554\n* [Privacy policy][45]\n* [Terms and conditions of sale][46]\n* [Support][47]\n\n[1]: https://skylarklasers.com\n[2]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/\n[3]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/320-nx/\n[4]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/349-nx/\n[5]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/780-nx/\n[6]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/785-nx/\n[7]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/\n[8]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-lithography/\n[9]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/optical-grating-mastering-lasers/\n[10]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-semiconductor/\n[11]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-quantum/\n[12]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-brillouin/\n[13]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-raman-spectroscopy/\n[14]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/holography/\n[15]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-flow-cytometry/\n[16]: https://skylarklasers.com/about/\n[17]: https://skylarklasers.com/news/\n[18]: https://skylarklasers.com/careers/\n[19]: https://skylarklasers.com/distributors/\n[20]: https://skylarklasers.com/events/\n[21]: https://skylarklasers.com/research-development-innovation/\n[22]: /product-quote-request\n[23]: #\n[24]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/\n[25]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/320-nx/\n[26]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/349-nx/\n[27]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/780-nx/\n[28]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/785-nx/\n[29]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/\n[30]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-lithography/\n[31]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/optical-grating-mastering-lasers/\n[32]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-semiconductor/\n[33]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-quantum/\n[34]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-brillouin/\n[35]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-raman-spectroscopy/\n[36]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/holography/\n[37]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-flow-cytometry/\n[38]: https://skylarklasers.com/about/\n[39]: https://skylarklasers.com/news/\n[40]: https://skylarklasers.com/careers/\n[41]: https://skylarklasers.com/distributors/\n[42]: https://skylarklasers.com/events/\n[43]: https://skylarklasers.com/research-development-innovation/\n[44]: https://skylarklasers.com\n[45]: https://skylarklasers.com/privacy/\n[46]: https://skylarklasers.com/terms/\n[47]: https://skylarklasers.com/support/"
