            "text": "[Skip to main content][1]\n[ [Website Logo]\n\nGo To Homepage\n\n][2] [[Fibertek, Inc.]][3]\n[[Fibertek, Inc.]][4]\n* [Home][5]\n* [Laser Technologies][6]\n* [Engineering Services][7]\n* [About Us][8]\n* [Case Studies][9]\n* [Careers][10]\n* [Get Started][11]\n* [Laser Technologies][12]\n[Lisa lasers]\n\n### Laser Technologies\n\nCutting-edge laser technology systems revolutionizing space & defense.\n\n[View All][13]\n\n[Lidar Systems][14]\n\nWe offer both full lidar solutions and subsystem solutions, as well as mission planning, modeling,\nand support expertise.\n\n[Optical Communication Systems][15]\n\nFibertek\u2019s free-space optical (FSO) communications systems are engineered for resilience,\nscalability, and deep-space readiness.\n* [Engineering Services][16]\n\n### Engineering Services\n\nEnd-to-end engineering support across program management, R&D, logistics, testing, AI, and budget\nservices to drive mission success for defense and space customers.\n\n[View All][17]\n\n**[Program Management][18]**\n\nComprehensive support for program execution across defense and space initiatives.\n\n**[Scientific Research and Analysis][19]**\n\nCutting-edge research in sensors, energy, EW, and biotechnology to advance mission-critical\ntechnologies.\n\n**[Artificial Intelligence][20]**\n\nMultidisciplinary expertise to integrate AI tools and prototypes into Army platforms and\noperations.\n\n**[Budgetary Support][21]**\n\nReliable fiscal planning, tracking, and execution support aligned with DoD and civilian agency\nrequirements.\n\n**[Test and Evaluation Support][22]**\n\nRigorous testing and analysis to ensure system reliability, safety, and mission performance.\n\n**[Logistics Management and FSR Support][23]**\n\nEnd-to-end logistics and field service ensuring equipment readiness and operational continuity.\n\n**[Facilities Management][24]**\n\nSecure, certified support for facility operations, inventory control, and global shipping\nlogistics.\n* [About Us][25]\n* [Case Studies][26]\n* [Careers][27]\n* [Get Started][28]\n\n# ICESat-2\n\nFibertek developed and delivered space-qualified laser transmitters to power the Advanced\nTopographic Laser Altimeter System (ATLAS) for NASA\u2019s ICESat-2 mission. Fibertek also provided the\nATLAS instrument\u2019s photon-counting detector electronics.\n\n[Lidar][29] | [R&D][30]\n* [ Share this page on Facebook ][31]\n* [ Share this page on X ][32]\n* [ Share this page on Twitter ][33]\n* [ Send this link in an email message ][34]\n[Satellite Image]\n\n**Customer\n**NASA Goddard Space Flight Center\n\n**Program Webpage\n**[Home | ICESat-2][35]\n\n## Fibertek\u2019s laser transmitters enable the groundbreaking science driving this mission.\n\nFibertek developed and delivered space-qualified laser transmitters to power the Advanced\nTopographic Laser Altimeter System (ATLAS) for NASA\u2019s ICESat-2 mission. Fibertek also provided the\nATLAS instrument\u2019s photon-counting detector electronics.\n\n[Satellite demonstration]\n\n### Precise, reliable laser solution has enabled exceptional accuracy and longevity.\n* Radiation-tolerant electronics, redundancy, and precision beam control\n* Operating at 532 nm with ~1 mJ pulse energy at a 10 kHz repetition rate\n* Continued, consistent performance after 2 trillion laser shots and 7 years of operation in space\n\n[ICESat-2 Demonstration sheet]\n[Satellite image demo]\n\n## Mission and Challenges\n\nThe ICESat-2 mission, led by NASA, aims to advance our understanding of Earth\u2019s changing climate\nthrough precise, space-based measurements of ice sheet elevation, sea ice thickness, and global\nvegetation canopy height. At the heart of the mission is ATLAS, a sophisticated instrument designed\nto deliver transformative data on the dynamics of polar ice and other critical Earth systems. With\nsub-decimeter elevation accuracy, ICESat-2 provides researchers with unprecedented insight into the\nmass balance of ice sheets and the broader implications for sea-level rise and climate change.\nBeyond the cryosphere, ICESat-2 also contributes to monitoring forest biomass, mapping inland water\nbodies, and supporting ecosystem and hydrological research. By generating high-resolution, repeat\nmeasurements over time, the mission plays a vital role in building long-term climate data records\nand informing global environmental policy and decision making.\n\n## Fibertek\u2019s Contribution and Results\n\nFibertek played a critical role in enabling ICESat-2\u2019s scientific mission by developing and\ndelivering three space-qualified laser transmitters to power the ATLAS instrument. Fibertek also\nprovided the ATLAS photon-counting detector electronics for 120 individual detectors with picosecond\nresolution.\n\nOperating at 532 nm with ~1 mJ pulse energy at a 10 kHz repetition rate, one of the system\u2019s two\nlasers has fired trillions of pulses from orbit while maintaining stable, high-performance output.\nThe design features radiation-tolerant electronics, redundancy, and precision beam quality\ncontrol\u2014ensuring reliable operation in the harsh conditions of low Earth orbit. With a short 1 ns\npulse width and high repetition rate, the lasers enable ATLAS to achieve 70 cm footprint\nmeasurements with exceptional sub-decimeter accuracy.\n\nThe laser system has exceeded its expected mission lifetime, continuing to deliver consistent\nperformance after 2 trillion laser shots and more than seven years of operation, well beyond\noriginal projections. This long-lived, precise laser system has been instrumental in delivering the\nmission\u2019s high-resolution elevation data, supporting critical climate science and Earth system\nmonitoring.\n\n## See how Fibertek can advance your mission\n\n[Get Started][36]\n\n### Location\n\n[13605 Dulles Technology Dr.\nHerndon VA 20171][37]\n[(703) 471-7671][38]\n\n### Company\n* [Home][39]\n* [Laser Technologies][40]\n* [Engineering Services][41]\n* [About Us][42]\n\n### Contact Us\n* [Contact][43]\n\n\u00a9 2026\n* [Site Credits][44]\n* [Privacy Policy][45]\n* [Accessibility Policy][46]\n* [Sitemap][47]\n* [LinkedIn][48]\n\n[1]: #site-substance\n[2]: https://www.fibertek.com\n[3]: https://www.fibertek.com/\n[4]: https://www.fibertek.com/\n[5]: https://www.fibertek.com/\n[6]: https://www.fibertek.com/technologies/\n[7]: https://www.fibertek.com/services/\n[8]: https://www.fibertek.com/about/\n[9]: https://www.fibertek.com/case-studies/\n[10]: https://www.fibertek.com/career-opportunities/\n[11]: https://www.fibertek.com/contact/\n[12]: #\n[13]: /technologies/\n[14]: /technologies/lidar/\n[15]: /technologies/optical-communication/\n[16]: #\n[17]: /services/\n[18]: /services/program-management/\n[19]: /services/research/\n[20]: /services/ai/\n[21]: /services/budgetary/\n[22]: /services/testing/\n[23]: /services/logistics-field-service/\n[24]: /services/facilities/\n[25]: https://www.fibertek.com/about/\n[26]: https://www.fibertek.com/case-studies/\n[27]: https://www.fibertek.com/career-opportunities/\n[28]: https://www.fibertek.com/contact/\n[29]: /technologies/lidar/\n[30]: /technologies/\n[31]: https://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.fibertek.com%2Fcase-studies%2Fi\ncesat-2%2F\n[32]: https://x.com/intent/tweet?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.fibertek.com%2Fcase-studies%2Ficesat-2%2F&tex\nt=ICESat-2\n[33]: https://www.linkedin.com/shareArticle?mini=true&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.fibertek.com%2Fcase-stud\nies%2Ficesat-2%2F&title=ICESat-2&summary=&source=\n[34]: mailto:?subject=Fibertek%2C%20Inc.%3A%20ICESat-2&body=ICESat-2%0D%0Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.fibertek\n.com%2Fcase-studies%2Ficesat-2%2F\n[35]: https://icesat-2.gsfc.nasa.gov/\n[36]: /contact/\n[37]: https://maps.app.goo.gl/6HMzNygC2VRqDh4i9\n[38]: tel:7034717671\n[39]: https://www.fibertek.com/\n[40]: /technologies/\n[41]: https://www.fibertek.com/services/\n[42]: https://www.fibertek.com/about/\n[43]: https://www.fibertek.com/contact/\n[44]: https://www.windmillstrategy.com/\n[45]: https://www.fibertek.com/privacy-policy/\n[46]: https://www.fibertek.com/accessibility-policy/\n[47]: /sitemap_index.xml\n[48]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/fibertek"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://www.fibertek.com/case-studies/europa-landing-lidar/",
            "text": "[Skip to main content][1]\n[ [Website Logo]\n\nGo To Homepage\n\n][2] [[Fibertek, Inc.]][3]\n[[Fibertek, Inc.]][4]\n* [Home][5]\n* [Laser Technologies][6]\n* [Engineering Services][7]\n* [About Us][8]\n* [Case Studies][9]\n* [Careers][10]\n* [Get Started][11]\n* [Laser Technologies][12]\n[Lisa lasers]\n\n### Laser Technologies\n\nCutting-edge laser technology systems revolutionizing space & defense.\n\n[View All][13]\n\n[Lidar Systems][14]\n\nWe offer both full lidar solutions and subsystem solutions, as well as mission planning, modeling,\nand support expertise.\n\n[Optical Communication Systems][15]\n\nFibertek\u2019s free-space optical (FSO) communications systems are engineered for resilience,\nscalability, and deep-space readiness.\n* [Engineering Services][16]\n\n### Engineering Services\n\nEnd-to-end engineering support across program management, R&D, logistics, testing, AI, and budget\nservices to drive mission success for defense and space customers.\n\n[View All][17]\n\n**[Program Management][18]**\n\nComprehensive support for program execution across defense and space initiatives.\n\n**[Scientific Research and Analysis][19]**\n\nCutting-edge research in sensors, energy, EW, and biotechnology to advance mission-critical\ntechnologies.\n\n**[Artificial Intelligence][20]**\n\nMultidisciplinary expertise to integrate AI tools and prototypes into Army platforms and\noperations.\n\n**[Budgetary Support][21]**\n\nReliable fiscal planning, tracking, and execution support aligned with DoD and civilian agency\nrequirements.\n\n**[Test and Evaluation Support][22]**\n\nRigorous testing and analysis to ensure system reliability, safety, and mission performance.\n\n**[Logistics Management and FSR Support][23]**\n\nEnd-to-end logistics and field service ensuring equipment readiness and operational continuity.\n\n**[Facilities Management][24]**\n\nSecure, certified support for facility operations, inventory control, and global shipping\nlogistics.\n* [About Us][25]\n* [Case Studies][26]\n* [Careers][27]\n* [Get Started][28]\n\n# Europa Landing Lidar\n\nFibertek contributed to NASA\u2019s Europa Lander effort by developing a high-performance compact laser\ntransmitter to power the spacecraft\u2019s entry, descent, and landing lidar system.\n\n[Lasers][29] | [R&D][30]\n* [ Share this page on Facebook ][31]\n* [ Share this page on X ][32]\n* [ Share this page on Twitter ][33]\n* [ Send this link in an email message ][34]\n[Europa Lander]\n\n**Customer\n**Sigma Space Corporation for NASA Jet Propulsion Laboratory\n\n**Program Webpage\n**[Europa Clipper \u2013 NASA Science][35]\n\n## Fibertek developed a compact EDL lidar transmitter to meet the challenges of Jupiter\u2019s icy moon.\n\nFibertek contributed to NASA\u2019s Europa Lander effort by developing a high-performance compact laser\ntransmitter to power the spacecraft\u2019s entry, descent, and landing lidar system.\n\n### Compact laser transmitter is designed for high performance in cryogenic temperatures.\n* Endures extreme cold and deep space vacuum\n* Enables high pulse repetition rates for accurate, high-resolution 3D terrain mapping\n* Fits in the palm of the hand\n\n## Mission and Challenges\n\nThe Europa Lander mission is a proposed NASA concept aimed at investigating the potential for life\non Jupiter\u2019s icy moon Europa by analyzing surface and near-surface materials for biosignatures. To\nsupport this ambitious scientific goal, the Lander must safely descend onto and operate on one of\nthe most challenging planetary surfaces in the solar system\u2014characterized by rugged ice, steep\nridges, and a high-radiation environment, all without the benefit of GPS or real-time ground\nsupport. This makes advanced onboard navigation, terrain-relative mapping, and hazard avoidance\nsystems absolutely critical. Lidar plays a central role in enabling real-time 3D mapping of Europa\u2019s\nsurface during descent, providing the resolution and accuracy needed to detect hazards that could\ncompromise the landing or the mission\u2019s short operational lifetime. These systems must function\nautonomously, withstand intense radiation, operate in extreme cold and vacuum, and meet strict size,\nweight, and power (SWaP) constraints. Beyond ensuring a safe landing, high-resolution lidar data\nsupports the mission\u2019s broader goals\u2014selecting scientifically rich sites, maximizing the value of\nsurface operations, and paving the way for future exploration of Europa\u2019s oceanic environment and\nits potential habitability. The Europa Lander mission was ultimately not selected for development,\nas NASA deemed the mission to be premature without detailed surface data from the preceding Europa\nClipper mission to ensure scientific return and mission safety. However, future lander mission\nconcept studies are still ongoing.\n\n[Europa potential mission concept]\n\n## Fibertek\u2019s Contribution and Results\n\nBased on ICESat-2 TRL-9 heritage and designed to operate in the extreme conditions of Europa\u2019s\nenvironment, Fibertek\u2019s laser transmitter can endure deep space vacuum, cryogenic temperatures, and\nintense radiation. The laser delivers the reliability and precision needed for high-resolution 3D\nterrain mapping during descent by enabling high pulse repetition rates (pulse energies >80 \u00b5J at\n532nm, pulse widths < 1 ns) and sufficient optical power. At the same time, Fibertek\u2019s laser\ntransmitter approach achieves the Europa mission\u2019s strict size, weight, and power (SWaP) constraints\nin novel ways, resulting in a rugged and compact form factor that fits in the palm of the hand.\nFibertek\u2019s radiation-hardened design and proven laser expertise make it a key contributor to the\nproposed mission\u2019s ability to navigate Europa\u2019s complex, icy terrain with the autonomy and precision\nrequired for success.\n\n## See how Fibertek can advance your mission\n\n[Get Started][36]\n\n### Location\n\n[13605 Dulles Technology Dr.\nHerndon VA 20171][37]\n[(703) 471-7671][38]\n\n### Company\n* [Home][39]\n* [Laser Technologies][40]\n* [Engineering Services][41]\n* [About Us][42]\n\n### Contact Us\n* [Contact][43]\n\n\u00a9 2026\n* [Site Credits][44]\n* [Privacy Policy][45]\n* [Accessibility Policy][46]\n* [Sitemap][47]\n* [LinkedIn][48]\n\n[1]: #site-substance\n[2]: https://www.fibertek.com\n[3]: https://www.fibertek.com/\n[4]: https://www.fibertek.com/\n[5]: https://www.fibertek.com/\n[6]: https://www.fibertek.com/technologies/\n[7]: https://www.fibertek.com/services/\n[8]: https://www.fibertek.com/about/\n[9]: https://www.fibertek.com/case-studies/\n[10]: https://www.fibertek.com/career-opportunities/\n[11]: https://www.fibertek.com/contact/\n[12]: #\n[13]: /technologies/\n[14]: /technologies/lidar/\n[15]: /technologies/optical-communication/\n[16]: #\n[17]: /services/\n[18]: /services/program-management/\n[19]: /services/research/\n[20]: /services/ai/\n[21]: /services/budgetary/\n[22]: /services/testing/\n[23]: /services/logistics-field-service/\n[24]: /services/facilities/\n[25]: https://www.fibertek.com/about/\n[26]: https://www.fibertek.com/case-studies/\n[27]: https://www.fibertek.com/career-opportunities/\n[28]: https://www.fibertek.com/contact/\n[29]: /technologies/\n[30]: /technologies/\n[31]: https://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.fibertek.com%2Fcase-studies%2Fe\nuropa-landing-lidar%2F\n[32]: https://x.com/intent/tweet?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.fibertek.com%2Fcase-studies%2Feuropa-landing-\nlidar%2F&text=Europa+Landing+Lidar\n[33]: https://www.linkedin.com/shareArticle?mini=true&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.fibertek.com%2Fcase-stud\nies%2Feuropa-landing-lidar%2F&title=Europa+Landing+Lidar&summary=&source=\n[34]: mailto:?subject=Fibertek%2C%20Inc.%3A%20Europa%20Landing%20Lidar&body=Europa%20Landing%20Lidar\n%0D%0Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.fibertek.com%2Fcase-studies%2Feuropa-landing-lidar%2F\n[35]: https://science.nasa.gov/mission/europa-clipper/\n[36]: /contact/\n[37]: https://maps.app.goo.gl/6HMzNygC2VRqDh4i9\n[38]: tel:7034717671\n[39]: https://www.fibertek.com/\n[40]: /technologies/\n[41]: https://www.fibertek.com/services/\n[42]: https://www.fibertek.com/about/\n[43]: https://www.fibertek.com/contact/\n[44]: https://www.windmillstrategy.com/\n[45]: https://www.fibertek.com/privacy-policy/\n[46]: https://www.fibertek.com/accessibility-policy/\n[47]: /sitemap_index.xml\n[48]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/fibertek"
          },
