            "text": "top of page\n[[NP-Photonics-Logo-C5.png]][1]\n\n## Designed for Industrial operation\n* [\n\nHOME\n\n][2]\n* [\n\nPRODUCTS\n\n][3]\n* [SINGLE FREQUENCY LASERS][4]\n* [HIGH POWER CW LASERS][5]\n* [HIGH ENERGY LASERS][6]\n* [MULTI-CHANNEL LASER SYSTEMS][7]\n* [SHORT-LENGTH FIBER AMPLIFIERS][8]\n* [INJECTION SEEDERS][9]\n* [ASE SOURCES][10]\n* [MID-IR FIBERS & SOURCES][11]\n* [\n\nAPPLICATIONS\n\n][12]\n* [ACOUSTIC SENSING][13]\n* [OPTICAL TRAPPING][14]\n* [ENVIRONMENTAL SENSING][15]\n* [LIDAR][16]\n* [COHERENT COMMUNICATIONS][17]\n* [\n\nCAPABILITIES\n\n][18]\n* [ITAR][19]\n* [CORE TECHNOLOGIES][20]\n* [INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY][21]\n* [PUBLICATIONS][22]\n* [\n\nABOUT US\n\n][23]\n* [LEADERSHIP][24]\n* [CAREERS][25]\n* [CORONAVIRUS RESPONSE][26]\n* CONTACT US\n* [REQUEST A QUOTE][27]\n* [TECHNICAL SUPPORT][28]\n* [DISTRIBUTORS][29]\n* More\n\nUse tab to navigate through the menu items.\n\n# Our History\n\nFounded in 1998, NP Photonics develops and manufactures specialty fiber lasers, fiber amplifiers and\ntransport fibers for the near- and mid-infrared (IR) wavelength bands. Our proprietary fiber\ntechnology is used across a broad family of products, including narrow linewidth, low phase-noise\nfiber lasers designed for operation in industrial environments.\n\nOur core strengths are technology innovation, product development, quality engineering and\nmanufacturing world-class products for applications in sensing, defense, metrology and research.\n\nWe currently have over 1,400 lasers installed worldwide, and we continue to grow through technology\ndevelopment, strategic partnerships and engagement with markets in which the company has a clear\nsustainable advantage.\n* [[LinkedIn - White Circle]][30]\n\n[[NP-Photonics-Logo-C5.png]][31]\n\n9030 S Rita Ranch Rd #120\n\nTucson, AZ 85747\n\n][32]\n][33]\n\n520-799-7400\n\n][34]\n\n[info@npphotonics.com][35]\n\nContact Us\nbottom of page\n\n[1]: https://www.npphotonics.com\n[2]: https://www.npphotonics.co