            "url": "https://www.rpmclasers.com/product/jenlas-d2-high-power-diode-pumped-thin-disk-lasers/",
            "text": "[ [Solid State Lasers and Laser Diodes from RPMC Lasers Inc] ][1]\n* [ Contact Us][2]\n* [636-272-7227][3]\n[ ][4] [ BUY NOW ][5]\nMENUMENU\nMENUMENU\nMENUMENU\n* [Products][6]\n* * * [Laser Diodes][7]\n* [Free-Space - Multimode][8]\n* [Free-Space - Single Mode][9]\n* [Free-Space - Stabilized][10]\n* [Fiber-Coupled - Multimode][11]\n* [Fiber-Coupled - Single Mode][12]\n* [Fiber-Coupled - Stabilized][13]\n* [Custom Laser Diodes][14]\n* * [CW Lasers][15]\n* [Multimode Modules][16]\n* [Single Mode Modules][17]\n* [Stabilized Modules][18]\n* [Multi-Wavelength Combiners][19]\n* [Custom CW Lasers][20]\n* * [Pulsed Lasers][21]\n* [DPSS Lasers][22]\n* [Fiber Lasers][23]\n* [Nanosecond Lasers][24]\n* [Picosecond Lasers][25]\n* [Femtosecond Lasers][26]\n* [Micromachining Systems][27]\n* [Custom Pulsed Lasers][28]\n* * [Optical Amplifiers][29]\n* [DPSS Amplifiers][30]\n* [Fiber Amplifiers][31]\n* [Semiconductor Optical Amplifier][32]\n* [Custom Amplifiers][33]\n* [Applications][34]\n* * * [Defense & Aerospace][35]\n* [Space-Based Applications][36]\n* [Remote Sensing & Imaging][37]\n* [Targeting & Ranging][38]\n* [Laser Illuminators][39]\n* * [Industrial & Manufacturing][40]\n* [Material Processing & Surface Modification][41]\n* [Joining Processes][42]\n* [Display & Electronics Manufacturing][43]\n* [Communication & Data Transmission][44]\n* [Sensing, Measurement & Characterization][45]\n* * [Medical & Healthcare][46]\n* [Aesthetics][47]\n* [Dental][48]\n* [Photodynamic Therapy (PDT)][49]\n* * [Research & Biophotonics][50]\n* [Imaging & Analysis][51]\n* [Measurement & Analysis][52]\n* [Molecular Manipulation & Analysis][53]\n* [Spectroscopy & Analysis][54]\n* [Pump Lasers][55]\n* [Seed Lasers][56]\n* [Optical Amplifiers][57]\n* [About][58]\n* [RPMC Lasers][59]\n* [Our Manufacturers][60]\n* [Custom Services][61]\n* [Distributors][62]\n* [FAQs][63]\n* [Knowledge Center][64]\n* [Solution Examples][65]\n* [White Papers][66]\n* [Blog][67]\n* [FAQs][68]\n* [Lasers 101][69]\n* [Press Releases][70]\n[Solid State Lasers and Laser Diodes from RPMC Lasers Inc][71]\u00bb[Laser Products][72]\u00bbJenLas D2:\nHigh-Power Diode-Pumped Thin Disk Lasers\n* [Printable Page][73]\n* [Email this page][74]\n* [Save to Favorites][75]\n\n# JenLas D2\n\nDPSS Laser, Multimode, Thin-disk, 532nm or 1064nm, up to 8W\n\n### Key Features:\n* Highest efficiency in the industry\n* Proven with over 25k fielded\n* High-quality & precision\n* Peltier cooling \u2013 water-free\n* Compact & easy integration\n* Multiple levels of integration\n\n[ Advice][76]\n[ Quote][77]\n\n**Get help selecting the right configuration for you!**\n\n*If you do not see exactly what you need, please contact us!*\n\n[[various configurations of the jenlas fiber ns OEM green disk laser housing]][78]\n* [Overview:][79]\n* [Specifications:][80]\n* [Datasheets/Downloads:][81]\n* [Applications:][82]\n* [Videos:][83]\n\nThe JenLas D2 series showcases innovation in high-power disk laser technology, featuring our trusted\n532 nm laser sources with up to 8W CW output. With over 25k units installed, our CW-532 nm thin disk\nlasers are reliable in fields like ophthalmology, dermatology, and quality control. Our lasers\noperate on TEC-controlled laser diode pump sources, Nd:YVO4 gain crystals, and TEC-controlled\ninternal frequency doubling LBO crystals. Offering the highest electro-optical efficiency,\nwater-less cooling, and high beam quality, our lasers outperform other solid-state technologies. The\nseries offers multiple integration levels, including the compact OEM JenLas D2.mini 2-8W that fits\nin the palm of your hand and the fully integrated JenLas MLS Green system for medical applications.\nThe JenLas D2 series is ideal for customers seeking reliable, high-performance laser technology with\nconsistent output power and easy integration.\n\n**Your OEM Disk Laser Solution Awaits!**\n\n[ Tell us what you need!][84]\n\n##### Thin Disk Laser Examples\n\n*If you do not see exactly what you are looking for, **l****et us know what you need!***\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n**Output power (W)** \u2502**Pulse Duration/CW**\u2502**Fiber-coupling**\u2502**Datasheet**\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n2 / 3 / 5 / 8 \u2502\u2248 1ms to CW \u2502Possible \u2502[D2.mini 2 \u2013 8 W][85]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n8 \u2502\u2248 1ms to CW \u2502Possible \u2502[D2.8][86]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n3 / 5 \u2502\u2248 1ms to CW \u2502Possible \u2502[D2][87]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n3 / 8 \u2502\u2248 1ms to CW \u2502Yes \u2502[D2.mini 3/8 W\n\u2502 \u2502 \u2502FC][88]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n60 mW to 3 W (1 mW steps)\u250210 to 650 ms \u2502Yes \u2502[MLS Green][89]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n**Let us help choose the right configuration for YOU!**\n\n[ Get Started TODAY!][90]\n\n### Benefits:\n* **High Performance**:\n* The highest electro-optical efficiency & advanced technology ensure precise, reliable\nperformance for various applications\n* **Consistent Output Power**:\n* The suppression of thermal lensing and the use of waterless cooling deliver consistent output\npower, ensuring optimal performance\n* **Compact and Easy Integration**:\n* The compact and rugged design simplifies integration into various systems. The D2 mini is\nparticularly suitable for applications where space is limited.\n* **Multiple Integration Levels:**\n* From ultra-compact free-space modules that fit in the palm of your hand to fiber-coupled modules\nto fully integrated systems including fiber-coupling, control, functional safety electronics,\nand cooling. We\u2019re sure to have a solution to fit your exact needs\n* **Versatile Solutions**:\n* High power capabilities and TEC-controlled internal frequency doubling LBO crystals allow for a\nwide range of applications and uses.\n* **Proven Track Record**:\n* With over 25,000 units installed, the CW-532 nm thin disk lasers have proven their worth in\nvarious fields such as ophthalmology, dermatology, veterinary medicine, laser projection, and\nquality control.\n* **Customization**:\n* All products are fully customizable: the JenLas\u00ae family offers a fully integrated system\nincluding fiber-coupling, control electronics, cooling, and functional safety features,\nproviding a platform for customized medical lasers systems.\n* **Industry-Leading Form Factor**:\n* The JenLas\u00ae D2 series offers the industry\u2019s smallest form-factor, making it ideal for\napplications where space is at a premium.\n* **Long-Term Investment**:\n* With over 30 years of experience in the design and fabrication of diode-pumped solid-state\nlasers, investing in the JenLas\u00ae D2 series is a smart and cost-effective decision for your laser\ntechnology needs.\n\nThe JenLas D2 series is the ideal solution for customers looking for reliable, high-performance\nlaser technology. The efficient and advanced features of our lasers, such as the suppression of\nthermal lensing and the use of waterless cooling, provide consistent and precise output power. The\nrugged and compact design of our lasers makes integration into your system simple and easy. With our\nThin Disk Laser family, you can trust that you are making a smart and cost-effective investment in\nyour laser technology needs.\n\n**Don\u2019t hesitate to ask us anything!**\n\n[ Get answers today!][91]\n\n**[Back to all Jenoptik products][92]**\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nWavelength (nm) \u2502[532][93], [1064][94]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nDescription \u2502[DPSS Laser, Multimode, Thin-disk, 532nm or 1064nm, up to 8W][95]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nType \u2502[CW DPSS Lasers][96], [Collimated Beam][97], [Fiber-Coupled][98],\n\u2502[Customizable][99]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n[ R1Z6-Datasheet-JenLas-MLS-Green ][100]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n* [Laser Illuminators][101]\n* [Pump Lasers - Fiber & DPSS][102]\n* [Spectroscopy & Analysis Lasers][103]\n\n### How can we help you?\n\nTalk to one of our experienced product managers today!\n\n[Contact us][104]\n\n## Customers also bought\n\n**JDL-Unmounted Bars: 760-1070nm Unmounted Laser Diode Bars & Single Emitters**\nLaser Diode, Multimode, Unmounted bar, Infrared, 760-1070nm, up to 300W CW/500W QCW ][105] [\n**Jenlas Fiber ns: 100W Nanosecond Fiber Laser**\nFiber Laser, ns pulsed, 1085nm, up to 100W, up to 1.1mJ, up to 200kHz ][106] [\n**JOLD-FC: 760-1070 & 1470nm Fiber-Coupled Laser Diode Modules**\nLaser Diode, Multimode, Fiber-coupled, Infrared, 760-1470nm, up to 400W ][107] [\n**JOLD-Open Heatsinks: 760-1070nm Single Laser Diode Bar Package**\nLaser Diode, Multimode, Bar package, Infrared, 760-1070nm, up to 300W ][108] [\n**JOLD-Stacks: 760-1070nm High-Power Laser Diode Stacks**\nLaser Diode, Multimode, Bar stack, Infrared, 760-1070nm, up to 2400W ][109]\n\n## CW Laser Blog Posts\n* [HeNe Lasers: Fundamentals, History & Key Considerations When Selecting][110]\n* [CO2 Emission Reduction: PTB\u2019s Decarbonization Research on Hydrogen and Ammonia with QCL Laser\nDiagnostics][111]\n* [HeNe Lasers VS Diode Lasers: HeNe Laser Pros and Cons][112]\n* [Laser Alignment: HeNe Lasers, Methods, and Helpful Tips][113]\n* [The Influence of Laser Wavelength on Raman Spectroscopy][114]\n* [Multi-Mode vs Single-Mode Lasers for Raman Spectroscopy][115]\n* [What is Laser Amplifier Noise?][116]\n* [World\u2019s Smallest OEM Laser Sources for Portable, Handheld Applications][117]\n* [New Dual-Wavelength Raman Probe Enhances Flexibility & Throughput][118]\n* [Flow Cytometry: Application Basics, Source Requirements & Solutions][119]\n\n## CW Lasers White Papers\n* [Lasers for Machine Vision: Selection Criteria][120]\n* [Single Frequency Fiber Lasers for Doppler LiDAR][121]\n\n## CW Lasers FAQs\n\nHow do I align my optical system?\n**How do I align my optical system?**\n\nLaser alignment can be a challenging task, but aligning a laser beam doesn\u2019t have to be as\ncomplicated as it might seem with the right optical alignment tools and proper laser alignment\ntechniques. Multiple optical alignment techniques have been developed over the years, utilized by\ntechnicians and engineers to simplify the alignment process. With the development of these universal\nlaser beam alignment methods, along with some laser alignment tips and tricks, you don\u2019t need to be\na laser expert to perform your alignments with relative ease, ensuring your laser beam path is right\nwhere you want it to be and your beam is on target every time. Read our article, titled \u201c[Laser\nAlignment: HeNe Lasers, Methods, and Helpful Tips][122]\u201d to get the knowledge and advice you need\nfor proper optical beam path alignment utilizing [HeNe Lasers][123]. Get more information from our\nLasers 101, Blogs, Whitepapers, FAQs, and Press Release pages in our [Knowledge Center][124]!\n\nShould I choose multimode or single-mode for Raman spectroscopy?\n**Should I choose multimode or single-mode for Raman spectroscopy?**\n\nOn the surface, this seems like a simple question since [Raman][125] is a nonlinear optical effect\nand therefore the tighter the beam can be focused the higher the conversion efficiency. Seemingly a\nsingle-mode laser would be preferable, but in practice there are other factors that can complicate\nthe situation. The first question you should ask yourself when considering which type of laser to\nchoose is whether you are doing microscopy or bulk sampling. If the answer to that question is\nmicroscopy, then you immediately should go with a single mode laser. Since the goal of any\nmicroscopy system is to produce the highest resolution image possible, the number one consideration\nshould be how tightly can the laser beam be focused down. However, there are several other\nconsiderations when choosing"
          },
