            "text": "[ [Solid State Lasers and Laser Diodes from RPMC Lasers Inc][Solid State Lasers and Laser Diodes\nfrom RPMC Lasers Inc] ][1]\n* [ Contact Us][2]\n* [636-272-7227][3]\n[ ][4] [ BUY NOW ][5]\nMENUMENU\nMENUMENU\nMENUMENU\n* [Products][6]\n* * * [Laser Diodes][7]\n* [Free-Space - Multimode][8]\n* [Free-Space - Single Mode][9]\n* [Free-Space - Stabilized][10]\n* [Fiber-Coupled - Multimode][11]\n* [Fiber-Coupled - Single Mode][12]\n* [Fiber-Coupled - Stabilized][13]\n* [Custom Laser Diodes][14]\n* * [CW Lasers][15]\n* [Multimode Modules][16]\n* [Single Mode Modules][17]\n* [Stabilized Modules][18]\n* [Multi-Wavelength Combiners][19]\n* [Custom CW Lasers][20]\n* * [Pulsed Lasers][21]\n* [DPSS Lasers][22]\n* [Fiber Lasers][23]\n* [Nanosecond Lasers][24]\n* [Picosecond Lasers][25]\n* [Femtosecond Lasers][26]\n* [Micromachining Systems][27]\n* [Custom Pulsed Lasers][28]\n* * [Optical Amplifiers][29]\n* [DPSS Amplifiers][30]\n* [Fiber Amplifiers][31]\n* [Semiconductor Optical Amplifier][32]\n* [Custom Amplifiers][33]\n* [Applications][34]\n* * * [Defense & Aerospace][35]\n* [Space-Based Applications][36]\n* [Remote Sensing & Imaging][37]\n* [Targeting & Ranging][38]\n* [Laser Illuminators][39]\n* * [Industrial & Manufacturing][40]\n* [Material Processing & Surface Modification][41]\n* [Joining Processes][42]\n* [Display & Electronics Manufacturing][43]\n* [Communication & Data Transmission][44]\n* [Sensing, Measurement & Characterization][45]\n* * [Medical & Healthcare][46]\n* [Aesthetics][47]\n* [Dental][48]\n* [Photodynamic Therapy (PDT)][49]\n* * [Research & Biophotonics][50]\n* [Imaging & Analysis][51]\n* [Measurement & Analysis][52]\n* [Molecular Manipulation & Analysis][53]\n* [Spectroscopy & Analysis][54]\n* [Pump Lasers][55]\n* [Seed Lasers][56]\n* [Optical Amplifiers][57]\n* [About][58]\n* [RPMC Lasers][59]\n* [Our Manufacturers][60]\n* [Custom Services][61]\n* [Distributors][62]\n* [FAQs][63]\n* [Knowledge Center][64]\n* [Solution Examples][65]\n* [White Papers][66]\n* [Blog][67]\n* [FAQs][68]\n* [Lasers 101][69]\n* [Press Releases][70]\n[Solid State Lasers and Laser Diodes from RPMC Lasers Inc][71]\u00bb[Laser Products][72]\u00bbneoVAN: OEM Type\nSolid-State Optical Amplifier\n* [Printable Page][73]\n* [Email this page][74]\n* [Save to Favorites][75]\n\n# neoVAN\n\nDPSS Amplifier, CW to ps Pulsed, 1064 nm, 0-40 dBm input, 5-100 W output, up to 5 mJ\n\n### Key Features:\n* **Wavelength:** 1064nm\n* **Output Power:** 5 \u2013 100W\n* **Pulse Energy:** Up to 5mJ\n* **Mode of Operation:** CW to ps pulses\n* **Beam Quality:** TEM00 / M\u00b2 100 W, pulse energy of up to 50 mJ (neoVAN) or >50 mJ (neoYb),\nand repetition rates from continuous-wave (CW) to femtosecond pulses, these amplifiers can meet the\nneeds of a variety of applications. Additionally, the neoVAN OEM platform features built-in laser\ndiodes, allowing for an even more compact design and direct integration into existing laser systems\nand equipment. Overall, the neoVAN and neoYb series provide a winning combination of performance,\nflexibility, and reliability, making them the right choice for many laser system applications.\n\nIf you have any questions or need more information, please contact us.\n\n[neoVAN Output vs Input Power][neoVAN Output vs Input Power]\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nWavelength (nm)\u2502[1064][85]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nDescription \u2502[DPSS Amplifier, CW to ps Pulsed, 1064 nm, 0-40 dBm input, 5-100 W output, up to 5\n\u2502mJ][86]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n[ neoLASE_datasheet_Amplifier ][87]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n[ neoVAN-02 ][88]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n* [Display and Electronics Manufacturing Lasers][89]\n* [Material Processing & Surface Modification Lasers][90]\n\n### How can we help you?\n\nTalk to one of our experienced product managers today!\n\n[Contact us][91]\n\n## Customers also bought\n\n**neoMOS: Ultrashort Pulse Laser**\nDPSS Laser, ps/fs Pulsed, 1064nm, up to 100W, up to 500\u00b5J, up to 80MHz ][92] [\n**neoYb: OEM Type Solid-State Optical Amplifier**\nDPSS Amplifier, CW to fs Pulsed, 1030 nm, 0-40 dBm input, 5-100 W output, up to 5mJ ][93]\n\n## RPMC Lasers Blog\n* [High-Energy Air-Cooled Nanosecond Lasers: How to Choose Between QLI Q-TUNE and Fixed-Wavelength\nPlatforms][94]\n* [Bright Solutions\u2019 Deep-UV Lasers: High-Resolution 266 nm Solutions for Ophthalmic Lenses,\nMarking, and Advanced Applications][95]\n* [Laser Diode Fundamentals: Understanding Diode Gain Threshold][96]\n* [Molecular Clock Case Study: Record QCL Frequency Stabilization in Precision Metrology][97]\n* [Custom Fiber-Coupled Laser Diodes for Dental OEM Systems][98]\n* [Top Aesthetic Laser Applications: Tattoo, Hair, and Acne Solutions][99]\n* [SWIR Laser Diodes for Effective Acne Treatment][100]\n* [LDX Optronics: High-Power Multimode Laser Diodes for Precision Applications][101]\n* [Supercontinuum Lasers for Precision Spectral Imaging][102]\n* [Choosing Infrared Laser Diodes for Dental Crown Troughing][103]\n\n## RPMC Lasers White Papers\n* [Choosing the Right Connector for Your Fiber-Coupled Laser Diode][104]\n* [Advancements in High-Power Laser Diodes for Medical and Industrial Applications][105]\n* [neoMOS Laser Systems: Flexible and Versatile Solutions for Any Application][106]\n* [Laser Requirements for Time Gated Active Night Vision Imaging Systems][107]\n* [How to Improve Laser Diode Lifetime! Advice and Precautions on Mounting][108]\n* [Lasers for Machine Vision: Selection Criteria][109]\n* [Quantum Cascade Lasers (QCLs) for Infrared Countermeasures][110]\n* [Laser Requirements for Wind Turbine Monitoring LiDAR Systems][111]\