n* [White Papers][66]\n* [Blog][67]\n* [FAQs][68]\n* [Lasers 101][69]\n* [Press Releases][70]\n[Solid State Lasers and Laser Diodes from RPMC Lasers Inc][71]\u00bb[Laser Products][72]\u00bbRPK-FL:\nHigh-Power IR Fiber Laser\n* [Printable Page][73]\n* [Email this page][74]\n* [Save to Favorites][75]\n\n# RPK-FL\n\nFiber Laser, Single mode, Infrared, 1080nm, up to 1200W\n\n### Key Features:\n* Superb beam quality/stability\n* Cost-effective and low-maintenance\n* Designed for industrial use\n* CW w/ Max Mod Freq. 5kHz\n* Optional aiming beam\n* Air or water cooling\n* Up to 1200W of output power\n* Complete control by software or hardwired\n\n**Many different package types, wavelengths, output powers & options to choose from \u2013 ****Get help\nselecting the right configuration for you!**\n\n[ Advice][76]\n[ Quote][77]\n\n[][78]\n\n### POPULAR CONFIGURATIONS:\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nPicture \u2502Part \u2502Part Description \u2502Datasheet \u2502\n\u2502Number \u2502 \u2502 \u2502\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n[R1Z0-Image-RPBFL-ACW1500]\u2502RPBFL-A\u2502Fiber Laser, Air Cooled, 1200W, 1080nm, \u2502[ [PDF \u2502[Get\n[R1Z0-Image-RPBFL-ACW1500]\u2502CW1500 \u2502Aiming Beam, 12m long 20um fiber with QBH \u2502icon][PDF \u2502Quote][\n\u2502 \u2502Connector \u2502icon] ][79] \u250280]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n[R1Z0-Image-RPKBFL-CW1000]\u2502RPKBFL-\u2502Fiber Laser, Water Cooled, 1000W, 1080nm, \u2502[ [PDF \u2502[Get\n[R1Z0-Image-RPKBFL-CW1000]\u2502CW1000 \u2502Aiming Beam, 12m long 20um fiber with QBH \u2502icon][PDF \u2502Quote][\n\u2502 \u2502Connector \u2502icon] ][81] \u250282]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n* [Overview:][83]\n* [Specifications:][84]\n* [Applications:][85]\n* [Videos:][86]\n\nThe RPK-FL from RPMC Lasers is a high-power fiber laser suitable for a wide range of applications.\nThese fiber lasers can be tailored for your specific needs with output powers up to 1200W, in either\na water or air-cooled package. Our specialized fiber-coupling techniques ensure high efficiency,\nstability, and superior beam quality, while rigorous inspections and burn-in procedures guarantee\neach product\u2019s reliability, stability, and long lifetime.\n\n**Your Fiber Laser Solution Awaits!**\n\n[ Tell us what you need!][87]\n\n### Benefits:\n* **Specialized fiber-coupling** techniques result in high efficiency, stability, and superior beam\nquality.\n* **More precise and accurate results** in precision cutting and welding, 3D printing (SLS/SLM), and\nsheet metal processing.\n* **User-friendly** controls for temperature, current, and pulse width.\n* **CW operation **with a max modulation frequency of 5kHz.\n* **Highly efficient, stable, and long lifetime** for increased confidence and trust in product\nperformance and longevity.\n* **Cost-effective solution** with minimal maintenance requirements and reduced downtime.\n* **Water or Air-cooled **options to fit your performance and environmental requirements.\n* **Easy and hassle-free integration** for various applications saves you time, money, and\nheadaches.\n* **Highly customizable**, tailored solutions with different packages to meet customers\u2019 unique\nneeds.\n\nIf you have any questions or need more information, please contact us.\n\n[ Get Answers Today!][88]\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nWavelength (nm) \u2502[1085][89]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nDescription \u2502[Fiber Laser, Single mode, Infrared, 1080nm, up to\n\u25021200W][90]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nType \u2502[CW Fiber Lasers][91]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n### How can we help you?\n\nTalk to one of our experienced product managers today!\n\n[Contact us][92]\n\n## Customers also bought\n\n****\n][93] [\n**Jasper X1: High-Power Femtosecond Fiber Laser**\nFiber Laser, fs/ps pulsed, 1030nm, up to 60W, up to 200\u00b5J, <270fs-20ps, Single Shot - 20MHz ][94] [\n**RPK-TK: Fiber-Coupled Turn-Key Direct Diode Laser System**\nLaser Diode, Wavelength Stabilized, Fiber-coupled, 405-1064nm, up to 3000W ][95]\n\n## CW Laser Blog Posts\n* [HeNe Lasers: Fundamentals, History & Key Considerations When Selecting][96]\n* [CO2 Emission Reduction: PTB\u2019s Decarbonization Research on Hydrogen and Ammonia with QCL Laser\nDiagnostics][97]\n* [HeNe Lasers VS Diode Lasers: HeNe Laser Pros and Cons][98]\n* [Laser Alignment: HeNe Lasers, Methods, and Helpful Tips][99]\n* [The Influence of Laser Wavelength on Raman Spectroscopy][100]\n* [Multi-Mode vs Single-Mode Lasers for Raman Spectroscopy][101]\n* [What is Laser Amplifier Noise?][102]\n* [World\u2019s Smallest OEM Laser Sources for Portable, Handheld Applications][103]\n* [New Dual-Wavelength Raman Probe Enhances Flexibility & Throughput][104]\n* [Flow Cytometry: Application Basics, Source Requirements & Solutions][105]\n\n## CW Lasers White Papers\n* [Lasers for Machine Vision: Selection Criteria][106]\n* [Single Frequency Fiber Lasers for Doppler LiDAR][107]\n\n## CW Lasers FAQs\n\nHow do I align my optical system?\n**How do I align my optical system?**\n\nLaser alignment can be a challenging task, but aligning a laser beam doesn\u2019t have to be as\ncomplicated as it might seem with the right optical alignment tools and proper laser alignment\ntechniques. Multiple optical alignment techniques have been developed over the years, utilized by\ntechnicians and engineers to simplify the alignment process. With the development of these universal\nlaser beam alignment methods, along with some laser alignment tips and tricks, you don\u2019t need to be\na laser expert to perform your alignments with relative ease, ensuring your laser beam path is right\nwhere you want it to be and your beam is on target every time. Read our article, titled \u201c[Laser\nAlignment: HeNe Lasers, Methods, and Helpful Tips][108]\u201d to get the knowledge and advice you need\nfor proper optical beam path alignment utilizing [HeNe Lasers][109]. Get more information from our\nLasers 101, Blogs, Whitepapers, FAQs, and Press Release pages in our [Knowledge Center][110]!\n\nShould I choose multimode or single-mode for Raman spectroscopy?\n**Should I choose multimode or single-mode for Raman spectroscopy?**\n\nOn the surface, this seems like a simple question since [Raman][111] is a nonlinear optical effect\nand therefore the tighter the beam can be focused the higher the conversion efficiency. Seemingly a\nsingle-mode laser would be preferable, but in practice there are other factors that can complicate\nthe situation. The first question you should ask yourself when considering which type of laser to\nchoose is whether you are doing microscopy or bulk sampling. If the answer to that question is\nmicroscopy, then you immediately should go with a single mode laser. Since the goal of any\nmicroscopy system is to produce the highest resolution image possible, the number one consideration\nshould be how tightly can the laser beam be focused down. However, there are several other\nconsiderations when choosing between multimode and single-mode. Learn which is best for you in this\narticle: \u201c[Multimode vs Single-Mode Lasers for Raman Spectroscopy][112].\u201d Get more information from\nour Lasers 101, Blogs, Whitepapers, FAQs, and Press Release pages in our [Knowledge Center][113]!\n\nWhat is a CW Laser?\n**What is a CW Laser?**\n\nA [CW or continuous-wave laser][114] is any laser with a continuous flow of pump energy. It emits a\nconstant stream of radiation, as opposed to a q-switched or mode-locked pulsed laser with a pulsed\noutput beam. A laser is typically defined as having a pulse width greater than 250 ms. The first CW\nlaser was a helium-neon (HeNe) gas laser, developed in 1960, which you can read more about in this\nblog \u201c[HeNe Lasers: Bright Past, Brighter Future][115].\u201d If you want to read more about the types of\nCW Lasers we offer, check out the [Overview of CW Lasers][116] section on our Lasers 101 Page!\n\nWhat is the best laser for optical surface flatness testing?\n**What is the best laser for optical surface flatness testing?**\n\nIt is essential that the laser exhibit a high level of spectral stability, ensuring that any changes\nin the interference pattern are caused by features in the sample and not originating from the laser\nbeam. In addition to spectral stability, high beam pointing stability ensures consistent\nmeasurements by mitigating any beam position drift concerning the position of the sample. Lasers\nwith longer coherence lengths, and subsequently narrower linewidths, play an important role in\ndetermining the resolution of the measurement, as well as consideration of the wavelength used.\nExhibiting both single longitudinal mode and single spatial mode has excellent benefits. Get more\ninformation from our Lasers 101, Blogs, Whitepapers, FAQs, and Press Release pages in our [Knowledge\nCenter][117]!\n\nWhat type of laser is best for Doppler LIDAR?\n**What type of laser is best for Doppler LIDAR?**\n\nVarious LIDAR signal methods for measuring velocity have one critical requirement in common, the\nneed for precise control over laser frequency. While a wide variety of single-frequency lasers have\nbeen used in Doppler LIDAR research, the industry as a whole has adopted [single-frequency fiber\nlasers][118] as the ideal light source. Fiber lasers have several advantages over traditional DPSS\nlasers, all of which derive from the geometry of the fiber optic itself, namely the innate ability\nto have an extremely long single-mode optical cavity. This geometry allows for the production of\neither extremely high-power, single-mode lasers producing unprecedented brightness, or extremely\nnarrow band lasers, with near perfect single-frequency output. If you want to learn more about\nDoppler LIDAR, the critical considerations involved, and ideal laser sources, check out this\nwhitepaper: \u201c[Single-Frequency Fiber Lasers for Doppler LIDAR][119].\u201d Get more information from our\nLasers 101, Blogs, Whitepapers, FAQs, and Press Release pages in our [Knowledge Center][120]!\n\nWhat\u2019s the di"
          },
