            "text": "[ [Solid State Lasers and Laser Diodes from RPMC Lasers Inc] ][1]\n* [ Contact Us][2]\n* [636-272-7227][3]\n[ ][4] [ BUY NOW ][5]\nMENUMENU\nMENUMENU\nMENUMENU\n* [Products][6]\n* * * [Laser Diodes][7]\n* [Free-Space - Multimode][8]\n* [Free-Space - Single Mode][9]\n* [Free-Space - Stabilized][10]\n* [Fiber-Coupled - Multimode][11]\n* [Fiber-Coupled - Single Mode][12]\n* [Fiber-Coupled - Stabilized][13]\n* [Custom Laser Diodes][14]\n* * [CW Lasers][15]\n* [Multimode Modules][16]\n* [Single Mode Modules][17]\n* [Stabilized Modules][18]\n* [Multi-Wavelength Combiners][19]\n* [Custom CW Lasers][20]\n* * [Pulsed Lasers][21]\n* [DPSS Lasers][22]\n* [Fiber Lasers][23]\n* [Nanosecond Lasers][24]\n* [Picosecond Lasers][25]\n* [Femtosecond Lasers][26]\n* [Micromachining Systems][27]\n* [Custom Pulsed Lasers][28]\n* * [Optical Amplifiers][29]\n* [DPSS Amplifiers][30]\n* [Fiber Amplifiers][31]\n* [Semiconductor Optical Amplifier][32]\n* [Custom Amplifiers][33]\n* [Applications][34]\n* * * [Defense & Aerospace][35]\n* [Space-Based Applications][36]\n* [Remote Sensing & Imaging][37]\n* [Targeting & Ranging][38]\n* [Laser Illuminators][39]\n* * [Industrial & Manufacturing][40]\n* [Material Processing & Surface Modification][41]\n* [Joining Processes][42]\n* [Display & Electronics Manufacturing][43]\n* [Communication & Data Transmission][44]\n* [Sensing, Measurement & Characterization][45]\n* * [Medical & Healthcare][46]\n* [Aesthetics][47]\n* [Dental][48]\n* [Photodynamic Therapy (PDT)][49]\n* * [Research & Biophotonics][50]\n* [Imaging & Analysis][51]\n* [Measurement & Analysis][52]\n* [Molecular Manipulation & Analysis][53]\n* [Spectroscopy & Analysis][54]\n* [Pump Lasers][55]\n* [Seed Lasers][56]\n* [Optical Amplifiers][57]\n* [About][58]\n* [RPMC Lasers][59]\n* [Our Manufacturers][60]\n* [Custom Services][61]\n* [Distributors][62]\n* [FAQs][63]\n* [Knowledge Center][64]\n* [Solution Examples][65]\n* [White Papers][66]\n* [Blog][67]\n* [FAQs][68]\n* [Lasers 101][69]\n* [Press Releases][70]\n[Solid State Lasers and Laser Diodes from RPMC Lasers Inc][71]\u00bb[Laser Products][72]\u00bbOne: 10XXnm\nMiniature Q-Switched DPSS Laser\n* [Printable Page][73]\n* [Email this page][74]\n* [Save to Favorites][75]\n\n# One\n\nDPSS Laser, ns pulsed, 1030-1064nm, up to 4W, up to 200\u00b5J, passive Q-switch, 5-20 ns, up to 30kHz\n\n### Key Features:\n* Ultra-compact & rugged design\n* CW or pulsed operation\n* Factory set passive q-switching\n* Conductively cooled\n\n**There are many different package types, wavelengths, output powers, and options to choose from.\n****Get help selecting the right configuration for you!**\n\n[ Advice][76]\n[ Quote][77]\n\n[ Datasheet][78]\n\n[[gray and red compact nanosecond pulsed DPSS laser housing One by Bright Solutions]][79]\n\n### POPULAR CONFIGURATIONS:\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nPicture \u2502Part \u2502Part Description \u2502Datasheet\u2502\n\u2502Number\u2502 \u2502 \u2502\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n[gray and red compact nanosecond pulsed DPSS laser \u2502One \u2502Miniature \u2502[ [PDF \u2502[Get\nhousing One by Bright Solutions][gray and red compact \u2502100uJ-\u2502Q-Switched Laser, \u2502icon][PDF\u2502Quote\nnanosecond pulsed DPSS laser housing One by Bright \u25021030nm\u25021030nm 100uJ, up to\u2502icon] \u2502][81]\nSolutions] \u2502 \u250210kHz \u2502][80] \u2502\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n[gray and red compact nanosecond pulsed DPSS laser \u2502One \u2502Miniature \u2502[ [PDF \u2502[Get\nhousing One by Bright Solutions][gray and red compact \u25023W-103\u2502Q-Switched Laser, \u2502icon][PDF\u2502Quote\nnanosecond pulsed DPSS laser housing One by Bright \u25020nm \u25021030nm 3W, up to 30\u2502icon] \u2502][83]\nSolutions] \u2502 \u2502kHz \u2502][82] \u2502\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n* [Overview:][84]\n* [Specifications:][85]\n* [Datasheets/Downloads:][86]\n* [Applications:][87]\n* [Videos:][88]\n\nThe One Series is an ultra-compact, rugged, versatile, nanosecond pulsed (up to 200\u00b5J), passive\nq-switch laser series designed for OEM integrators and application specialists working with\nindustrial and portable applications. These lasers provide sufficient peak power for extremely\nhigh-quality metal & plastic marking in compact & portable marking systems or for airborne LIDAR.\nWith its compact & efficient contact-cooled package, attractive pricing, optional CW operation with\nup to 4 W average power, and configurable options & add-ons, this 1030nm series offers easy,\nflexible integration possibilities and exceptional, cost-effective performance for a range of\napplications.\n\n**We\u2019re experts in selecting the right laser for your application!**\n\n[ Tell us what you need!][89]\n\n##### One Miniaturized DPSS Laser Platform Examples:\n\n*Customization options are available. **Let us know what you need!***\n\n[simple text table displaying configuration options for a DPSS laser][simple text table displaying\nconfiguration options for a DPSS laser]\n\n**Let us help choose the right configuration for you!**\n\n[ Get started NOW!][90]\n\n### Benefits:\n* **Designed for compact and portable applications:**\nThis miniaturized DPSS laser is perfect for compact marking systems and portable instrumentation\napplications.\n* **Ultra-compact and easily integrated:\n**Our smallest form factor, with minimal facility requirements for easy integration into various\nportable and industrial applications.\n* **Rugged, lightweight single unit design:\n**Ensures durability and reliability for various compact & portable applications, reducing\ndowntime and maintenance costs.\n* **Conductively cooled:\n**Reduced footprint with water-free cooling, resulting in low-maintenance and cost-effective, yet\nefficient cooling.\n* **High peak power and excellent beam quality:\n**Provides precise and powerful laser output, enabling high-quality and accurate results in a wide\nrange of applications.\n* **Optional beam expanding and collimation optics:\n**Help shape and direct the laser beam, ensuring maximum energy is delivered to the target.\n* **Optional add-ons & customizable:\n**From a red aiming beam to water cooling, beam expanding & collimation, CW operation, and beyond.\nLet us know what you need!\n\n### Options Available\n* Internal photodiode\n* Beam Expanding and Collimating optics\n* Red aiming beam\n* Heat sink\n* AC DC Power Supply\n* Custom packaging\n\n##### Check out this research study, authored by one of our successful customers, titled:\n\n**\u201cHigh-Precision Neural Modulation with RPMC\u2019s \u201cOne\u201d Nanosecond Laser: Photoacoustic vs.\nPhotothermal Insights\u201d**\n\n[ Read the Article!][91]\n\n**Summary: **RPMC\u2019s nanosecond lasers offer unmatched precision for neural modulation using\nphotoacoustic techniques. These methods enable researchers to selectively stimulate or map neural\nactivity with high spatial and temporal resolution, advancing neuroscience, biophotonics, and\nmedical applications. Ideal for academic research and clinical innovation, these lasers support\nbreakthroughs in neural therapy development, brain mapping, and non-invasive diagnostics, catering\nto the growing demand for precise, versatile tools in medical and scientific fields.\n\n##### Check out this white paper, authored by one of our successful customers, titled:\n\n**\u201cOptoacoustic Brain Stimulation at Submillimeter Spatial Precision\u201d**\n\n[ Read the Article!][92]\n\n**Summary: **Utilizing a 1030nm One Series laser from Bright Solutions, we report spatially confined\noptoacoustic neural stimulation through a miniaturized Fiber-Optoacoustic Converter (FOC). The FOC\nhas a diameter of 600\u00b5m and generates omnidirectional ultrasound wave locally at the fiber tip\nthrough the optoacoustic effect. We show that the acoustic wave generated by FOC can directly\nactivate individual cultured neurons and generate intracellular Ca^2 transients. The FOC activates\nneurons within a radius of 500\u00b5m around the fiber tip, delivering superior spatial resolution over\nconventional piezo-based low-frequency transducers. Finally, we demonstrate direct and spatially\nconfined neural stimulation of mouse brain and modulation of motor activity in vivo.\n\n**Don\u2019t hesitate to ask us anything!**\n\n[ Get answers today!][93]\n\n**[Back to all Bright Solutions products][94]**\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nWavelength\u2502[1030][95], [1047][96], [1064][97]\n(nm) \u2502\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nDescriptio\u2502[DPSS Laser, ns pulsed, 10XX nm, up to 4W, up to 200\u00b5J, 5-20 ns, passive Qsw up to\nn \u250230kHz][98]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nType \u2502[Pulsed DPSS Lasers][99], [Airborne Laser][100], [Low SWaP][101], [Ruggedized][102],\n\u2502[Adjustable Rep Rate][103], [High Peak Power][104], [Customizable][105]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n[ R0Z7-One-Brochure ][106]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n[ One-100uJ-1030nm ][107]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n[ R0Z8-Datasheet-One-3W-1um ][108]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n* [Remote Sensing & Imaging Lasers][109]\n* [Material Processing & Surface Modification Lasers][110]\n* [Seed Lasers - Fiber & DPSS][111]\n\n### How can we help you?\n\nTalk to one of our experienced product managers today!\n\n[Contact us][112]\n\n## Customers also bought\n\n**Iris: Red or Blue Nanosecond DPSS Laser**\nDPSS Laser, ns pulsed, 447 or 671nm, up to 4W, up to 100kHz ][113] [\n**Onda: Compact High Peak Power Nanosecond DPSS Laser**\nDPSS Laser, ns pulsed, 266-1064nm, up to 800\u00b5J, up to 100kHz ][114] [\n**SOL: Compact DPSS Nanosecond Laser**\nDPSS Laser, ns pulsed, 355-1064nm, up to 60W, up to 200kHz ][115] [\n**Wedge: Short Pulse Q-Switched DPSS Laser**\nDPSS Laser, ns/ps pulsed, 266-3000nm, up to 4mJ, up to 100kHz ][116]\n\n## Pulsed Lasers Blog Posts\n* [High-Energy Air-Cooled Nanosecond Lasers: How to Choose Between QLI Q-TUNE and Fixed-Wavelength\nPlatforms][117]\n* [Bright Solutions\u2019 Deep-UV Lasers: High-Resolution 266 nm Solutions for Ophthalmic Lenses,\nMarking, and Advanced Applications][118]\n* [Supercontinuum Lasers for Precision Spectral Imaging][119]\n* [Tunable Lasers for Photoacoustic Imaging: Precision Biomedical Solutions][120]\n* [Tunable OPO Lasers: Q-TUNE Series for Spectroscopy and Beyond][121]\n* [Choosing Passive vs Active Q-Switching Lasers: Solutions for High-Energy Pulsed\nApplications][122]\n* [Choosing the Right Laser for Tattoo Removal: Key Considerations][123]\n* [LIDAR Lasers: Precision 3D Mapping][124]\n* [Fluence Technology\u2019s Innovation in Ultrafast Lasers: SPIE Photonics West 2025 Spotlight][125]\n* [High-Precision Neural Modulation with Bright Solutions\u2019 \u2018One\u2019 Nanosecond Laser: Photoacoustic vs.\nPhotothermal Insights][126]\n\n## Pulsed Lasers White Papers\n* [neoMOS Laser Systems: Flexible and Versatile Solutions for Any Application][127]\n* [Laser Requirements for Time Gated Active Night Vision Imaging Systems][128]\n* [Laser Requirements for Wind Turbine Monitoring LiDAR Systems][129]\n* [Single Frequency Fiber Lasers for Doppler LiDAR][130]\n* [Laser Sources for Lidar Applications][131]\n\n## Pulsed Lasers FAQs\n\nWhat is a Pulsed Laser?\n**What is a Pulsed Laser?**\n\nA [pulsed laser][132] is any laser that does not emit a continuous-wave (CW) laser beam. Instead,\nthey emit light pulses at some duration with some period of \u2018off\u2019 time between pulses and a\nfrequency measured in cycles per second (Hz). There are several different methods for pulse\ngeneration, including passive and active q-switching and mode-locking. Pulsed lasers store energy\nand release it in these pulses or energy packets. This pulsing can be very beneficial, for example,\nwhen machining certain materials or features. The pulse can rapidly deliver the stored energy, with\ndowntime in between, preventing too much heat from building up in the material. If you would like to\nread more about q-switches and the pros and cons of passive vs active q-switche"
