2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nWavelength\u2502[1030][90]\n(nm) \u2502\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nDescriptio\u2502[Fiber Laser, fs/ps pulsed, 1030nm, up to 7W, up to 5\u00b5J, <270fs-8ps, Single Shot \u2013\nn \u250220MHz][91]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nType \u2502[Pulsed Fiber Lasers][92], [Ultrafast Lasers][93], [Ruggedized][94], [Adjustable Rep\n\u2502Rate][95], [Adjustable Pulse Width][96], [High Peak Power][97]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n* [Material Processing & Surface Modification Lasers][98]\n\n### How can we help you?\n\nTalk to one of our experienced product managers today!\n\n[Contact us][99]\n\n## Customers also bought\n\n**Jasper Flex: Compact High-Power Femtosecond Fiber Laser**\nFiber Laser, fs/ps pulsed, 1030nm, up to 30W, up to 1MHz, up to 100\u00b5J, <270fs-8ps, Single Shot -\n20MHz ][100] [\n**Jasper X1: High-Power Femtosecond Fiber Laser**\nFiber Laser, fs/ps pulsed, 1030nm, up to 60W, up to 200\u00b5J, <270fs-20ps, Single Shot - 20MHz ][101]\n\n## Pulsed Lasers Blog Posts\n* [High-Energy Air-Cooled Nanosecond Lasers: How to Choose Between QLI Q-TUNE and Fixed-Wavelength\nPlatforms][102]\n* [Bright Solutions\u2019 Deep-UV Lasers: High-Resolution 266 nm Solutions for Ophthalmic Lenses,\nMarking, and Advanced Applications][103]\n* [Supercontinuum Lasers for Precision Spectral Imaging][104]\n* [Tunable Lasers for Photoacoustic Imaging: Precision Biomedical Solutions][105]\n* [Tunable OPO Lasers: Q-TUNE Series for Spectroscopy and Beyond][106]\n* [Choosing Passive vs Active Q-Switching Lasers: Solutions for High-Energy Pulsed\nApplications][107]\n* [Choosing the Right Laser for Tattoo Removal: Key Considerations][108]\n* [LIDAR Lasers: Precision 3D Mapping][109]\n* [Fluence Technology\u2019s Innovation in Ultrafast Lasers: SPIE Photonics West 2025 Spotlight][110]\n* [High-Precision Neural Modulation with Bright Solutions\u2019 \u2018One\u2019 Nanosecond Laser: Photoacoustic vs.\nPhotothermal Insights][111]\n\n## Pulsed Lasers White Papers\n* [neoMOS Laser Systems: Flexible and Versatile Solutions for Any Application][112]\n* [Laser Requirements for Time Gated Active Night Vision Imaging Systems][113]\n* [Laser Requirements for Wind Turbine Monitoring LiDAR Systems][114]\n* [Single Frequency Fiber Lasers for Doppler LiDAR][115]\n* [Laser Sources for Lidar Applications][116]\n\n## Pulsed Lasers FAQs\n\nWhat is a Pulsed Laser?\n**What is a Pulsed Laser?**\n\nA [pulsed laser][117] is any laser that does not emit a continuous-wave (CW) laser beam. Instead,\nthey emit light pulses at some duration with some period of \u2018off\u2019 time between pulses and a\nfrequency measured in cycles per second (Hz). There are several different methods for pulse\ngeneration, including passive and active q-switching and mode-locking. Pulsed lasers store energy\nand release it in these pulses or energy packets. This pulsing can be very beneficial, for example,\nwhen machining certain materials or features. The pulse can rapidly deliver the stored energy, with\ndowntime in between, preventing too much heat from building up in the material. If you would like to\nread more about q-switches and the pros and cons of passive vs active q-switches, check out this\nblog \u201c[The Advantages and Disadvantages of Passive vs Active Q-Switching][118],\u201d or check out our\n[Overview of Pulsed Lasers][119] section on our Lasers 101 Page!\n\nWhat is the best laser for LIDAR?\n**What is the best laser for LIDAR?**\n\nThere are actually numerous laser types that work well for various [LIDAR][120] and [3D\nScanning][121] applications. The answer comes down to what you want to measure or map. If your\ntarget is s"
