502266nm \u25021W, Compact, optimized at a specific \u2502icon][PD\u2502Quote\nsilver colored OEM DPSS Laser \u2502 \u2502firm set rep. rate in the range 10 to \u2502F icon] \u2502][90]\nhousing] \u2502 \u250250 kHz \u2502][89] \u2502\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n[clean, modern, silver colored OEM \u2502Onda \u2502High Energy Laser, 266nm 80uJ, 2ns, \u2502[ [PDF \u2502[Get\nDPSS Laser housing][clean, modern, \u2502266nm-1\u2502Compact, Single Shot to 1 kHz \u2502icon][PD\u2502Quote\nsilver colored OEM DPSS Laser \u2502kHz \u2502 \u2502F icon] \u2502][92]\nhousing] \u2502 \u2502 \u2502][91] \u2502\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n[ SHOW MORE OPTIONS SHOW LESS OPTIONS ][93]\n\n* [Overview:][94]\n* [Specifications:][95]\n* [Datasheets/Downloads:][96]\n* [Applications:][97]\n* [Videos:][98]\n\nThe Onda series is a DPSS nanosecond OEM industrial laser solution, designed for high-end\napplications requiring excellent beam quality and high peak power in metals, glass, plastics, and\nvarious delicate and hard materials. This compact, air-cooled, and easy-to-use single unit laser\nseries allows for straightforward integration, is available in wavelengths of 266, 355, 532, and\n1064nm, and provides a superior performance to cost ratio. The Onda series\u2019 internal optical layout\nand accurate temperature management enable high output energies without compromising the lifetime of\nthe THG and FHG stages. Many optional add-ons and customization options.\n\n**We\u2019re experts in selecting the right laser for your application!**\n\n[ Tell us what you need!][99]\n\n##### Onda DPSS Laser Platform Examples:\n\n*Customization options are available. **Let us know what you need!***\n\n[simple text table displaying configuration options for a DPSS laser][simple text table displaying\nconfiguration options for a DPSS laser]\n\n**Let us help choose the right configuration for you!**\n\n[ Get started NOW!][100]\n\n### Benefits:\n* **Designed for industrial use:**\nFor high-end applications requiring excellent beam quality & high peak power for metal, glass,\nplastics, delicate & hard materials.\n* **Compact, air-cooled DPSS nanosecond laser:\n**Compact OEM design is easily integrated into existing systems with efficient air cooling.\n* **Rugged, lightweight single unit design:\n**Ensures durability and reliability in industrial and scientific applications, reducing downtime\nand maintenance costs.\n* **Highly reliable, stable performance:****\n**Permanently aligned monolithic design provides high-quality, reliable optical performance &\nconsistent output power.\n* **High peak power and excellent beam quality:\n**Provides precise and powerful laser output, enabling high-quality and accurate results in a wide\nrange of applications.\n* **Optional beam expanding and collimation optics:\n**Help shape and direct the laser beam, ensuring maximum energy is delivered to the target.\n* **Optional remote-control box and software interface:\n**Allows for operation, monitoring, and support along with a user-friendly GUI.\n* **Many more optional add-ons & completely customizable:\n**From a red aiming beam to water cooling, beam expanding, monitoring photodiode, and beyond. Let\nus know what you need!\n\n### Options Available\n* Beam expanding and collimating optics\n* Fiber Coupling\n* Red aiming beam\n* Extended operating temperature range\n* Extended frequency range\n* Pulse width modulation\n* Low jitter option\n* Circular Polarization\n* Air or water cooling\n* Monitoring photodiode\n* Remote control box & software interface\n* AC-DC power supply\n\n**Don\u2019t hesitate to ask us anything!**\n\n[ Get answers today!][101]\n\n**[Back to all Bright Solutions products][102]**\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nWavelength (nm)\u2502[266][103], [355][104], [532][105], [1064][106]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nDescription \u2502[DPSS Laser, ns pulsed, 266-1064nm, up to 800\u00b5J, up to 100kHz][107]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nType \u2502[Pulsed DPSS Lasers][108], [Adjustable Rep Rate][109], [High Peak Power][110],\n\u2502[Customizable][111]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n[ R0Z7-Onda-Brochure ][112]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n* [Remote Sensing & Imaging Lasers][113]\n* [Material Processing & Surface Modification Lasers][114]\n* [Seed Lasers - Fiber & DPSS][115]\n* [Spectroscopy & Analysis Lasers][116]\n* [Display and Electronics Manufacturing Lasers][117]\n\n### How can we help you?\n\nTalk to one of our experienced product managers today!\n\n[Contact us][118]\n\n## Customers also bought\n\n**Iris: Red or Blue Nanosecond DPSS Laser**\nDPSS Laser, ns pulsed, 447 or 671nm, up to 4W, up to 100kHz ][119] [\n**NPS: Narrowband Picosecond Mode-Locked Laser**\nDPSS Laser, ps pulsed, 266-1064nm, up to 10W, passive Q-switch, up to 80MHz, narrow linewidth ][120]\n**SOL: Compact DPSS Nanosecond Laser**\nDPSS Laser, ns pulsed, 355-1064nm, up to 60W, up to 200kHz ][121] [\n**Wedge: Short Pulse Q-Switched DPSS Laser**\nDPSS Laser, ns/ps pulsed, 266-3000nm, up to 4mJ, up to 100kHz ][122]\n\n## Pulsed Lasers Blog Posts\n* [High-Energy Air-Cooled Nanosecond Lasers: How to Choose Between QLI Q-TUNE and Fixed-Wavelength\nPlatforms][123]\n* [Bright Solutions\u2019 Deep-UV Lasers: High-Resolution 266 nm Solutions for Ophthalmic Lenses,\nMarking, and Advanced Applications][124]\n* [Supercontinuum Lasers for Precision Spectral Imaging][125]\n* [Tunable Lasers for Photoacoustic Imaging: Precision Biomedical Solutions][126]\n* [Tunable OPO Lasers: Q-TUNE Series for Spectroscopy and Beyond][127]\n* [Choosing Passive vs Active Q-Switching Lasers: Solutions for High-Energy Pulsed\nApplications][128]\n* [Choosing the Right Laser for Tattoo Removal: Key Considerations][129]\n* [LIDAR Lasers: Precision 3D Mapping][130]\n* [Fluence Technology\u2019s Innovation in Ultrafast Lasers: SPIE Photonics West 2025 Spotlight][131]\n* [High-Precision Neural Modulation with Bright Solutions\u2019 \u2018One\u2019 Nanosecond Laser: Photoacoustic vs.\nPhotothermal Insights][132]\n\n## Pulsed Lasers White Papers\n* [neoMOS Laser Systems: Flexible and Versatile Solutions for Any Application][133]\n* [Laser Requirements for Time Gated Active Night Vision Imaging Systems][134]\n* [Laser Requirements for Wind Turbine Monitoring LiDAR Systems][135]\n* [Single Frequency Fiber Lasers for Doppler LiDAR][136]\n* [Laser Sources for Lidar Applications][137]\n\n## Pulsed Lasers FAQs\n\nWhat is a Pulsed Laser?\n**What is a Pulsed Laser?**\n\nA [pulsed laser][138] is any laser that does not emit a continuous-wave (CW) laser beam. Instead,\nthey emit light pulses at some duration with some period of \u2018off\u2019 time between pulses and a\nfrequency measured in cycles per second (Hz). There are several different methods for pulse\ngeneration, including passive and active q-switching and mode-locking. Pulsed lasers store energy\nand release it in these pulses or energy packets. This pulsing can be very beneficial, for example,\nwhen machining certain materials or features. The pulse can rapidly deliver the stored energy, with\ndowntime in between, preventing too much heat from building up in the material. If you would like to\nread more about q-switches and the pros and cons of passive vs active q-switches, check out this\nblog \u201c[The Advantages and Disadvantages of Passive vs Active Q-Switching][139],\u201d or check out our\n[Overview of Pulsed Lasers][140] section on our Lasers 101 Page!\n\nWhat is the b"
          },
