            "text": "Single Frequency Lasers | Solid-State Laser Manufacturer \u2013 Techwin\n\nHome\nAbout\n\nProducts\n\nProduct Categories\nAll Solid-State Laser Series\nSingle-Frequency High-Energy Series\nFiber Laser Series\n\nView All Products\n\nApplications\nSupport\nContact\n\nSearch\n\nHome\nAbout\nProducts\nApplications\nSupport\nContact\n\nSearch Products\n\nSearch Products\n\n\ud83d\udd0d Quick search tips:\n\n\u2022 Try \"AOML\" for All Solid-State Lasers\n\n\u2022 Search by model number like \"150\" or \"500\"\n\n\u2022 Use keywords like \"fiber\", \"single-frequency\", \"nanosecond\"\n\nRequest a Quote\n\nFirst Name *\n\nLast Name *\n\nEmail Address *\n\nContact Number *\n\nMessage (Optional)\n\nSubmit Request\n\nTechwin - Single Frequency Lasers and Advanced Solid-State Laser Manufacturer\n\nTechwin is a high-tech enterprise dedicated to the research, development, and production of advanced solid-state and high-performance fiber laser systems.\n\nExplore Products\n\nLearn More\n\nWhy Choose Techwin as Your Solid-State Laser Manufacturer\n\n\u2022 Techwin is a leading provider of advanced solid-state and fiber laser technologies.\n\n\u2022 We specialize in research, development, and production of high-performance laser systems.\n\n\u2022 Our products serve applications in atmospheric LiDAR, biomedical research, and quantum optics.\n\n\u2022 Techwin collaborates with global research institutions and industry partners.\n\n\u2022 We offer customized laser solutions and mass production capabilities.\n\n\u2022 Our commitment is to provide stable, reliable, and cost-effective laser sources.\n\n\u2022 Techwin emphasizes technological innovation and serves the national industry.\n\n\u2022 We focus on compact design, long lifespan, and environmental reliability.\n\nAdvanced Solid-State Laser Solutions for Research and Industry\n\nShowcasing our latest advancements in laser technology\n\nCutting-Edge Research\n\nOur team continuously pushes the boundaries of laser technology with groundbreaking research and development initiatives that drive innovation across multiple scientific disciplines.\n\nAdvanced Manufacturing\n\nState-of-the-art manufacturing processes ensure the highest quality and reliability in our products, with rigorous testing and quality control measures in place.\n\nGlobal Partnerships\n\nCollaborating with international institutions and industry leaders to drive innovation, share knowledge, and solve complex challenges in laser technology applications.\n\nR&amp;D Innovation in Laser Technology\n\nOur key research and development directions in laser technology\n\nAdvanced Solid-State Laser Technologies\n\nHigh-Power Single-Frequency Fiber Lasers\n\nEfficient Nonlinear Frequency Conversion\n\nLaser Electronics & Opto-Mechanical Integration\n\nOptoelectronic Engineering & Process Optimization\n\nGlobal Collaboration\n\nCustomized Laser Systems for Scientific and Industrial Applications\n\nComprehensive laser solutions for various applications\n\nAll Solid-State Laser Series\n\n\u2022 Micro-Pulse Lasers\n\n\u2022 Sub-Nanosecond Lasers\n\n\u2022 High-Energy, High-Repetition-Rate Solid-State Lasers\n\n\u2022 High-Energy, Low-Repetition-Rate Solid-State Lasers\n\nSingle-Frequency High-Energy Series\n\n\u2022 Seed Laser Sources\n\n\u2022 Integrated Frequency-stabilized Sources\n\n\u2022 Single-Frequency High-Energy Solid-State Lasers\n\n\u2022 Frequency-Stabilized and Frequency-Shifting Sources\n\nFiber Laser Series\n\n\u2022 Single-Frequency Continuous Fiber Lasers\n\n\u2022 Single-Frequency Continuous Fiber Amplifiers\n\n\u2022 Single-Frequency Pulsed Fiber Lasers\n\n\u2022 Nanosecond Pulsed Fiber Lasers\n\nAll Solid-State Laser Series\n\n1. Micro-Pulse Lasers\n\nAOML series featuring high peak power, kHz+ repetition frequency, and 10ns-level pulse width characteristics.\n\nKey Features: Compact structure, wide temperature operation (-20~60\u00b0C), fully air-cooled design\n\nApplications: Atmospheric particulate detection, laser remote sensing, photoacoustic imaging\n\n2. Sub-Nanosecond Lasers\n\nAQNL series with pulse width\n\nKey Features: High peak power, minimum pulse width 800ps, smooth pulse waveform\n\nApplications: Atmospheric lidar, ocean exploration, laser ultrasound\n\n3. High-Energy, High-Repetition-Rate Solid-State Lasers\n\nSHSL series with repetition frequency \u2265100Hz, maximum output energy 300mJ+, expandable wavelengths.\n\nKey Features: Semiconductor pumping, 7\u00d724h operation, MOPA optical scheme\n\nApplications: Atmospheric lidar, LIBS/LIF, biomedical applications\n\n4. High-Energy, Low-Repetition-Rate Solid-State Lasers\n\nSMSL series with maximum output energy up to 100mJ, fully air-cooled design.\n\nKey Features: Opto-mechanical integration, low power consumption, wide temperature adaptability\n\nApplications: Lidar, LIBS/LIF, laser ultrasound, biomedical applications\n\nSingle-Frequency High-Energy Series\n\n5. Seed Lasers and Integrated Sources\n\nSCSL type NPRO lasers and SEFL type narrow linewidth semiconductor lasers.\n\nKey Features: Linewidth \u22643kHz, temperature/PZT tuning, space/fiber output\n\n6. Integrated Frequency-Stabilized Sources\n\nFre-Lock&Shift type with frequency stabilization and frequency shifting capabilities.\n\nKey Features: Multi-stage loop control, power feedback technology\n\n7. Single-Frequency High-Energy Solid-State Lasers\n\nSHSL-SLM series with narrow linewidth, high energy, and frequency compatibility.\n\nKey Features: Modular design, multi-wavelength output, 7\u00d724h operation\n\nFiber Laser Series\n\n8. Single-Frequency Continuous Fiber Lasers\n\nSCFL series featuring narrow linewidth, low noise, and high power characteristics.\n\nKey Features: Ultra narrow linewidth (\n\nApplications: Rb atom cooling, optical lattice, atomic clock\n\n9. Single-Frequency Pulsed Fiber Lasers\n\nSPFL series with single pulse energy 10/300\u03bcJ and linewidth as low as 1kHz.\n\nKey Features: Eye-safe laser band, high polarization extinction ratio\n\nApplications: Coherent Doppler wind measurement lidar\n\n10. Nanosecond Pulsed Fiber Lasers\n\nNPFL series with ultra-high repetition frequency (up to MHz) and single pulse energy up to 100\u03bcJ.\n\nKey Features: Compact structure, eye-safe band, tunable pulse width\n\nApplications: Surveying and imaging lidar, single photon ranging\n\nTechnical Excellence\n\nIndustry-leading specifications and performance\n\nPerformance Highlights\n\nLaser Linewidth\n\nFrequency Stability\n\nPower Stability\n\u2264 2.5% RMS\n\nPulse Energy\nUp to 1000 mJ\n\nRepetition Rate\nUp to 10 MHz\n\nPump Source Lifespan\n\u2265 4 billion shots\n\nWavelength Coverage\n\n1064 nm\n\nFundamental\n\n532 nm\n\nFrequency Doubled\n\n355 nm\n\nFrequency Tripled\n\n1550 nm\n\nFiber Lasers\n\n780 nm\n\nAtomic Physics\n\nUV Range\n\n280-590 nm\n\nTechwin Industry Co., Ltd\n\nAddress\n\n8th Floor Unit A, Block 2, No. 206 Zhenhua Road, Hangzhou City, Zip Code: 310030\n\nContact\n\nTel: +86-57188284299\n\nWhatsapp: +86-13958180450\n\nEmail\n\n[email&#160;protected]\n\n[email&#160;protected]\n\nAdvanced Solid-State and Fiber Laser Technology Center dedicated to providing stable, reliable, and cost-effective laser solutions for scientific, industrial, and defense applications worldwide.\n\nTechnological Innovation \u00b7 Industry Serving the Nation\n\nProduct Lines\n\nAll Solid-State Laser Series\n\nSingle-Frequency High-Energy Series\n\nFiber Laser Series\n\nView All Products\n\nCompany\n\nAbout Us\n\nR&D\n\nContact\n\nSupport\n\n&copy; 2025 Techwin Industry Co., Ltd. All rights reserved."
