            "url": "https://singlefrequencylaser.com/products/aqnl-series-sub-nanosecond-lasers",
            "text": "[ [Techwin Logo] ][1]\n[Home][2] [About][3]\n[Products ][4]\nProduct Categories\n[All Solid-State Laser Series][5] [Single-Frequency High-Energy Series][6] [Fiber Laser Series][7]\n[View All Products][8]\n[Applications][9] [Support][10] [Contact][11] Search\n[Home][12] [About][13] [Products][14] [Applications][15] [Support][16] [Contact][17] Search Products\n\n### Search Products\n\n\ud83d\udd0d **Quick search tips:**\n* \u2022 Try \"AOML\" for All Solid-State Lasers\n* \u2022 Search by model number like \"150\" or \"500\"\n* \u2022 Use keywords like \"fiber\", \"single-frequency\", \"nanosecond\"\n\n### Request a Quote\n\nFirst Name *\nLast Name *\nEmail Address *\nContact Number *\nMessage (Optional)\nSubmit Request\n1. [Home][18]\n2. /\n3. [Products][19]\n4. /\n5. [All Solid-State Laser Series][20]\n6. /\n7. AQNL Series Sub-Nanosecond Lasers\n[AQNL Series Sub-Nanosecond Lasers]\nAll Solid-State Laser Series\n\n# AQNL Series Sub-Nanosecond Lasers\n\nThe AQNL series sub-nanosecond lasers deliver output pulse widths of < 2 ns while maintaining\nexcellent beam quality. The timing jitter between the optical output signal and the trigger signal\nis less than 1 ns. Maximum output energy can reach 20 mJ, and the wavelength can be extended to 532\nnm, 355 nm, and other bands. This product series features excellent beam quality, high peak power,\nreliable performance, compact structure, and easy operation and maintenance. Combined with advanced\nmanufacturing processes, it can meet the requirements of harsh operating environments such as\nairborne, vehicle-mounted, and high-/low-temperature conditions.\n\nGet Quote Now\n\n### Key Features\n* High peak power\n* Minimum pulse width down to 800 ps\n* Burrfree pulse waveform\n* Mature technology, stable and reliable\n\n### Applications\n* Atmospheric lidar\n* Marine detection lidar\n* Laser ultrasonics\n* Singlephoton detection\n\n## Technical Parameters\n\n### Technical Specifications\n\n\u2500\u2500\u250