        "crawl_text": "Xcimer Energy Corporation 10325 East 47th Ave, Denver, CO 80238, USA Tucson, AZ Tucson, AZ U.S. Department of Energy approves Xcimer\u2019s fusion power plant preconceptual design and technology roadmap milestone on 06/10/2026. Xcimer Energy announces the start of operations for Phoenix, a prototype system for industrial-scale laser fusion architecture on 06/03/2026. Commercializing laser fusion technology Developing the world's first laser fusion power plant, Athena. Laser Fusion Leader\n\nSkip to content\n\nMedia\nFAQ\nNews\nTop Bar Nav\n\nXcimer Energy Corporation\n\nLaser fusion without limits\n\nCompany\nEnergy\nDefense\nCareers\nJobs\nInternships\n\nCompany\nEnergy\nDefense\nCareers\nInternships\nMedia\nFAQ\nNews\n\nLaser fusion\nwithout limits\n\nXcimer is building the world's biggest, brightest and most powerful lasers to commercialize the only scientifically validated form of fusion energy on Earth.\n\n06/10/2026\nU.S. Department of Energy approves Xcimer\u2019s fusion power plant preconceptual design and technology roadmap milestone\n\n06/03/2026\nXcimer Energy announces the start of operations for Phoenix, a prototype system for industrial-scale laser fusion architecture\n\nMore News\n\nPHOENIX\n\nXcimer is the most technically mature laser fusion company.\n\nIn 2024, we broke ground on our first high-energy laser system, Phoenix. It\u2019s now up and running.\n\nLocated in our Denver laser bay, Phoenix features the first electron-beam-pumped excimer laser built in the private sector, and the first of its kind from any organization in more than 20 years.\n\nPhoenix demonstrates long-pulse excimer laser operation (which unlocks cost savings), and a pulse compression technique known as Stimulated Brillouin Scattering (SBS) to shrink microsecond-long excimer laser pulses down to a nanosecond while avoiding all optics damage challenges.\n\nPhoenix is the world's highest-energy use of SBS. It validates key elements of Xcimer's low-cost, high-energy laser fusion architecture. Now we are ready to scale.\n\nATHENA\n\nOur work on Phoenix builds toward Athena, the world's first laser fusion power plant.\n\nAthena will represent the start of Earth's commercial fusion energy era.\n\nBy 2035, we expect Athena to deliver 400 megawatts of safe, clean, affordable energy, around the clock, with fuel derived from seawater and lithium, cost-competitive with fossil fuels and renewables.\n\nAthena is based on the most credible roadmap in fusion, relying on proven science and commercially scalable technologies. Xcimer's power plant architecture bypasses material science and maintenance challenges, resulting in extremely competitive economics.\n\nLearn More About Laser Fusion\n\nRead our detailed roadmap\n\nLaser-driven inertial fusion is the only fusion approach that has been scientifically proven. Read our February 2026 white paper with TRUMPF Laser SE to see how our gas excimer laser architecture makes it economical and scalable.\n\nRead the white paper\n\nMeet the team commercializing fusion\n\nNearly 200 engineers, physicists, and business professionals are turning proven science into crucial technology \u2014 with industry-leading execution. Learn about our mission, culture and values.\n\nDiscover Xcimer\n\nFusion: The ultimate energy source\n\nOur fusion power plants will unlock energy-intensive industries that require firm, abundant, carbon-free power, from AI training clusters to desalination and industrial decarbonization. Join the team commercializing the ultimate energy source.\n\nSafe\n\nNo chain reactions, no meltdowns. Fuel is a kind of hydrogen used in watch dials.\n\nAbundant\n\nFuel produced from seawater and lithium. Enough fuel for millions of years. No foreign supply chains.\n\nEconomical\n\nWe&#8217;ve designed our system from the ground up to compete on cost with fossil fuels and renewables.\n\nClean\n\nNo emissions. No pollutants. The only byproducts from our power plants? Helium and heat.\n\nJoin Us\n\n10325 East 47th Ave.\nDenver, CO 80238, USA\n\nLinkedin page opens in new window YouTube page opens in new window\n\nInformation\ninfo@xcimer.energy\n\nMedia\nmedia@xcimer.energy\n\nCareers\ncareers@xcimer.energy\n\nQuick Links:\n\nCompany\n\nEnergy\n\nDefense\n\nCareers\n\nMedia\n\nFAQ\n\nNews\n\nCopyright 2026. Xcimer Energy. All rights reserved.\n\nAccessibility Statement\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\nTerms Of Use\n\nConflict Of Interest Policy\n\nCookie Preferences\n\nGo to Top [Skip to content][1]\n* [Media][2]\n* [FAQ][3]\n* [News][4]\nTop Bar Nav\nXcimer Energy Corporation\nLaser fusion without limits\n[[Xcimer Energy Corporation]][5]\n* [Company][6]\n* [Energy][7]\n* [Defense][8]\n* [Careers][9]\n* [Jobs][10]\n* [Internships][11]\n* [Company][12]\n* [Energy][13]\n* [Defense][14]\n* [Careers][15]\n* [Internships][16]\n* [Media][17]\n* [FAQ][18]\n* [News][19]\n\n# Leading the Commercialization of Laser Fusion and Directed Energy Technology\n\n## Our mission is to** commercialize laser fusion** \u2014 the ultimate energy source for the 21st\n## century and beyond.\n\n### We are transforming decades of scientific progress into commercial fusion plants to deliver\n### safe, affordable, and effectively limitless energy.\n\n## Our leadership team\n\n[Conner Galloway]\n\n### Conner Galloway\n\n#### CEO, Founder\n\n[Alexander Valys]\n\n### Alexander Valys\n\n#### President, Founder\n\n[Brent Gill]\n\n### Brent Gill\n\n#### Chief Operating Officer\n\n[Giovanni Greco]\n\n### Giovanni Greco\n\n#### SVP, Engineering\n\n[Susana Reyes, Ph.D.]\n\n### Susana Reyes, Ph.D.\n\n#### VP, Chamber and Plant Design Systems\n\n[Gary Sobolevskiy]\n\n### Gary Sobolevskiy\n\n#### General Counsel\n\n[Alison Christopherson, Ph.D.]\n\n### Alison Christopherson, Ph.D.\n\n#### Head of Target Design\n\n[Silvia De Dea, Ph.D.]\n\n### Silvia De Dea, Ph.D.\n\n#### Head of Materials and Process Engineering\n\n[Brian Boggs]\n\n### Brian Boggs\n\n#### Head of Strategic Development\n\n[Dan Bauer]\n\n### Dan Bauer\n\n#### Head of Talent\n\n[Doug Weidenheimer]\n\n### Doug Weidenheimer\n\n#### Chief Pulsed Power Architect\n\n[Austin Steinforth, Ph.D.]\n\n### Austin Steinforth, Ph.D.\n\n#### Chief Laser Architect\n\n[Andrey Mironov, Ph.D.]\n\n### Andrey Mironov, Ph.D.\n\n#### Director of Experimental Science\n\n[Dennis Douglas, Ph.D.]\n\n### Dennis Douglas, Ph.D.\n\n#### Director of Optics\n\n[Milan Holec]\n\n### Milan Holec\n\n#### Director of Theory and Computation\n\n[Brad Appel]\n\n### Brad Appel\n\n#### Chief Engineer, Vulcan\n\n[Justin Brynestad]\n\n### Justin Brynestad\n\n#### SVP, Vulcan\n\n[Rachel Konrad]\n\n### Rachel Konrad\n\n#### SVP, Strategic Comms\n\n[Doug Kunzman]\n\n### Doug Kunzman\n\n#### Vice President, Defense\n\n## Science & Technology Advisory Board\n\nXcimer\u2019s Science and Technology Advisory Board, made up of experts in fusion, laser technology and\nnational security, is chaired by Mike Campbell. Feedback from the board informs Xcimer\u2019s roadmap and\nensures we remain focused on building the most scientifically credible roadmap in fusion.\n\n### Riccardo Betti, Ph.D.\n\nTarget Implosion Physics\nDistinguished Professor of Mechanical Engineering and Physics & Astronomy, University of Rochester.\nFormer Chair of the Division of Plasma Physics, American Physical Society.\n\n### Mike Campbell, D.Sc.\n\nBoard Chair\nFormer Director for University of Rochester's Laboratory For Laser Energetics (LLE). Former\nAssociate Director for Lasers, LLNL. Former Senior Vice-President Energy, General Atomics.\n\n### David Crandall, Ph.D.\n\nFusion & National Security\nFormer Chief Scientist, NNSA.\n\n### Greg Van Dyk, Ph.D.\n\nFusion & National Security\nFormer Chief Scientist, DoD.\n\n### Roger Falcone, Ph.D.\n\nPlasma Physics, HEDP\nFormer President, American Physical Society; Professor of Physics, UC Berkeley.\n\n### Javier Garay, Ph.D.\n\nLaser Science & Materials Science\nProfessor and Director of the Fusion Engineering Institute, UC San Diego.\n\n### Mark J. Kushner, Ph.D.\n\nLaser Science & Plasma Chemistry\nDistinguished Professor of EECS, University of Michigan.\n\n### Rick Spielman, Ph.D.\n\nPulsed Power\nFormer Chief Scientist and Project Manager, Sandia Z-Machine; Professor of Physics, University of\nRochester.\n\n### Jim Trebes, Ph.D.\n\nDefense, National Security\nFormer Director for Directed Energy, DoD; Former Head of Physics, LLNL.\n\n### George Tynan, Ph.D., FAPS\n\nNuclear Engineering\nNorm C. Rasmussen Adjunct Professor in Nuclear Engineering, MIT; Kazuo Iwama Endowed Distinguished\nProfessor of Engineering Science, Emeritus, UC San Diego.\n\n## Founding Scientific Advisors\n\nBefore Xcimer was officially incorporated, a small group of physicists, scientists and engineers,\nincluding the inventors of the excimer laser, contributed their time and advice to help arrive at\nthe compelling and practical power plant architecture we are now pursuing. We are grateful for their\ncontributions.\n\n### Bedros Afeyan, Ph.D.\n\nFounding Scientific Advisor\n\n### Paul Hoff, Ph.D.\n\nFounding Scientific Advisor\n\n### William Krupke, Ph.D.\n\nFounding Scientific Advisor\n\n### Joseph Mangano, Ph.D.\n\nFounding Scientific Advisor\n\n### Tom Mehlhorn, Ph.D.\n\nFounding Scientific Advisor\n\n### Allan Offenberger, Ph.D.\n\nFounding Scientific Advisor\n\n### Michael Tobin\n\nFounding Scientific Advisor\n\n### J. Gary Eden, Ph.D.\n\nFounding Scientific Advisor\n\n## Our Investors\n\n## Our Locations\n\n### \u2022 XEC Locations\n* Headquarters, Denver, CO\n* Manufacturing Operations, Tucson, AZ\n\n### \u2022 Partner Locations\n* Los Alamos National Laboratory (Los Alamos, NM)\n* Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (Livermore, CA)\n* Oak Ridge National Laboratory (Oak Ridge, TN)\n* Savannah River National Laboratory (Jackson, SC)\n* Naval Research Laboratory (Washington, DC)\n* Laboratory for Laser Energetics (Rochester, NY)\n* Massachusetts Institute of Technology (Cambridge, MA)\n* General Atomics (San Diego, CA)\n* Westinghouse (Cranberry Township, PA)\n* Universidad Nacional de Educacion a Distancia, UNED (Madrid, Spain)\n\n[10325 East 47th Ave.\nDenver, CO 80238, USA][20]\n[Linkedin page opens in new window][21][YouTube page opens in new window][22]\n**Information**\n[info@xcimer.energy][23]\n\n**Media**\n[media@xcimer.energy][24]\n\n**Careers**\n[careers@xcimer.energy][25]\nQuick Links:\n* [Company][26]\n* [Energy][27]\n* [Defense][28]\n* [Careers][29]\n* [Media][30]\n* [FAQ][31]\n* [News][32]\n* [Copyright 2026. Xcimer Energy. All rights reserved.][33]\n* [Accessibility Statement][34]\n* [Privacy Policy][35]\n* [Terms Of Use][36]\n* [Conflict Of Interest Policy][37]\n* [Cookie Preferences][38]\n[Go to Top][39]\n\n[1]: #content\n[2]: https://xcimer.energy/media/\n[3]: https://xcimer.energy/faq/\n[4]: https://xcimer.energy/news/\n[5]: https://xcimer.energy/\n[6]: https://xcimer.energy/company/\n[7]: https://xcimer.energy/energy/\n[8]: https://xcimer.energy/defense/\n[9]: https://xcimer.energy/careers/\n[10]: /careers#Job_Listings\n[11]: https://xcimer.energy/careers/internships/\n[12]: https://xcimer.energy/company/\n[13]: https://xcimer.energy/energy/\n[14]: https://xcimer.energy/defense/\n[15]: https://xcimer.energy/careers/\n[16]: https://xcimer.energy/careers/internships/\n[17]: https://xcimer.energy/media/\n[18]: https://xcimer.energy/faq/\n[19]: https://xcimer.energy/news/\n[20]: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=10325+East+47th+Ave+Denver+CO+80238\n[21]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/xcimer-energy-corporation\n[22]: https://www.youtube.com/@XcimerEnergy\n[23]: mailto:info@xcimer.energy\n[24]: mailto:media@xcimer.energy\n[25]: mailto:careers@xcimer.energy\n[26]: https://xcimer.energy/company/\n[27]: https://xcimer.energy/energy/\n[28]: https://xcimer.energy/defense/\n[29]: https://xcimer.energy/careers/\n[30]: https://xcimer.energy/media/\n[31]: https://xcimer.energy/faq/\n[32]: https://xcimer.energy/news/\n[33]: #\n[34]: https://xcimer.energy/accessibility-statement/\n[35]: https://xcimer.energy/privacy-policy/\n[36]: https://xcimer.energy/terms-of-use/\n[37]: https://xcimer.energy/conflict-of-interest-policy/\n[38]: #cookie-preferences\n[39]: # xcimer.energy Laser Fusion Leader\n\nSkip to content\n\nMedia\nFAQ\nNews\nTop Bar Nav\n\nXcimer Energy Corporation\n\nLaser fusion without limits\n\nCompany\nEnergy\nDefense\nCareers\nJobs\nInternships\n\nCompany\nEnergy\nDefense\nCareers\nInternships\nMedia\nFAQ\nNews\n\nLaser fusion\nwithout limits\n\nXcimer is building the world's biggest, brightest and m"
