        "pages": [
          {
            "url": "https://xcimer.energy",
            "text": "Laser Fusion Leader\n\nSkip to content\n\nMedia\nFAQ\nNews\nTop Bar Nav\n\nXcimer Energy Corporation\n\nLaser fusion without limits\n\nCompany\nEnergy\nDefense\nCareers\nJobs\nInternships\n\nCompany\nEnergy\nDefense\nCareers\nInternships\nMedia\nFAQ\nNews\n\nLaser fusion\nwithout limits\n\nXcimer is building the world's biggest, brightest and most powerful lasers to commercialize the only scientifically validated form of fusion energy on Earth.\n\n06/10/2026\nU.S. Department of Energy approves Xcimer\u2019s fusion power plant preconceptual design and technology roadmap milestone\n\n06/03/2026\nXcimer Energy announces the start of operations for Phoenix, a prototype system for industrial-scale laser fusion architecture\n\nMore News\n\nPHOENIX\n\nXcimer is the most technically mature laser fusion company.\n\nIn 2024, we broke ground on our first high-energy laser system, Phoenix. It\u2019s now up and running.\n\nLocated in our Denver laser bay, Phoenix features the first electron-beam-pumped excimer laser built in the private sector, and the first of its kind from any organization in more than 20 years.\n\nPhoenix demonstrates long-pulse excimer laser operation (which unlocks cost savings), and a pulse compression technique known as Stimulated Brillouin Scattering (SBS) to shrink microsecond-long excimer laser pulses down to a nanosecond while avoiding all optics damage challenges.\n\nPhoenix is the world's highest-energy use of SBS. It validates key elements of Xcimer's low-cost, high-energy laser fusion architecture. Now we are ready to scale.\n\nATHENA\n\nOur work on Phoenix builds toward Athena, the world's first laser fusion power plant.\n\nAthena will represent the start of Earth's commercial fusion energy era.\n\nBy 2035, we expect Athena to deliver 400 megawatts of safe, clean, affordable energy, around the clock, with fuel derived from seawater and lithium, cost-competitive with fossil fuels and renewables.\n\nAthena is based on the most credible roadmap in fusion, relying on proven science and commercially scalable technologies. Xcimer's power plant architecture bypasses material science and maintenance challenges, resulting in extremely competitive economics.\n\nLearn More About Laser Fusion\n\nRead our detailed roadmap\n\nLaser-driven inertial fusion is the only fusion approach that has been scientifically proven. Read our February 2026 white paper with TRUMPF Laser SE to see how our gas excimer laser architecture makes it economical and scalable.\n\nRead the white paper\n\nMeet the team commercializing fusion\n\nNearly 200 engineers, physicists, and business professionals are turning proven science into crucial technology \u2014 with industry-leading execution. Learn about our mission, culture and values.\n\nDiscover Xcimer\n\nFusion: The ultimate energy source\n\nOur fusion power plants will unlock energy-intensive industries that require firm, abundant, carbon-free power, from AI training clusters to desalination and industrial decarbonization. Join the team commercializing the ultimate energy source.\n\nSafe\n\nNo chain reactions, no meltdowns. Fuel is a kind of hydrogen used in watch dials.\n\nAbundant\n\nFuel produced from seawater and lithium. Enough fuel for millions of years. No foreign supply chains.\n\nEconomical\n\nWe&#8217;ve designed our system from the ground up to compete on cost with fossil fuels and renewables.\n\nClean\n\nNo emissions. No pollutants. The only byproducts from our power plants? Helium and heat.\n\nJoin Us\n\n10325 East 47th Ave.\nDenver, CO 80238, USA\n\nLinkedin page opens in new window YouTube page opens in new window\n\nInformation\ninfo@xcimer.energy\n\nMedia\nmedia@xcimer.energy\n\nCareers\ncareers@xcimer.energy\n\nQuick Links:\n\nCompany\n\nEnergy\n\nDefense\n\nCareers\n\nMedia\n\nFAQ\n\nNews\n\nCopyright 2026. Xcimer Energy. All rights reserved.\n\nAccessibility Statement\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\nTerms Of Use\n\nConflict Of Interest Policy\n\nCookie Preferences\n\nGo to Top"
