tation\n\n[Brad Appel]\n\n### Brad Appel\n\n#### Chief Engineer, Vulcan\n\n[Justin Brynestad]\n\n### Justin Brynestad\n\n#### SVP, Vulcan\n\n[Rachel Konrad]\n\n### Rachel Konrad\n\n#### SVP, Strategic Comms\n\n[Doug Kunzman]\n\n### Doug Kunzman\n\n#### Vice President, Defense\n\n## Science & Technology Advisory Board\n\nXcimer\u2019s Science and Technology Advisory Board, made up of experts in fusion, laser technology and\nnational security, is chaired by Mike Campbell. Feedback from the board informs Xcimer\u2019s roadmap and\nensures we remain focused on building the most scientifically credible roadmap in fusion.\n\n### Riccardo Betti, Ph.D.\n\nTarget Implosion Physics\nDistinguished Professor of Mechanical Engineering and Physics & Astronomy, University of Rochester.\nFormer Chair of the Division of Plasma Physics, American Physical Society.\n\n### Mike Campbell, D.Sc.\n\nBoard Chair\nFormer Director for University of Rochester's Laboratory For Laser Energetics (LLE). Former\nAssociate Director for Lasers, LLNL. Former Senior Vice-President Energy, General Atomics.\n\n### David Crandall, Ph.D.\n\nFusion & National Security\nFormer Chief Scientist, NNSA.\n\n### Greg Van Dyk, Ph.D.\n\nFusion & National Security\nFormer Chief Scientist, DoD.\n\n### Roger Falcone, Ph.D.\n\nPlasma Physics, HEDP\nFormer President, American Physical Society; Professor of Physics, UC Berkeley.\n\n### Javier Garay, Ph.D.\n\nLaser Science & Materials Science\nProfessor and Director of the Fusion Engineering Institute, UC San Diego.\n\n### Mark J. Kushner, Ph.D.\n\nLaser Science & Plasma Chemistry\nDistinguished Professor of EECS, University of Michigan.\n\n### Rick Spielman, Ph.D.\n\nPulsed Power\nFormer Chief Scientist and Project Manager, Sandia Z-Machine; Professor of Physics, University of\nRochester.\n\n### Jim Trebes, Ph.D.\n\nDefense, National Security\nFormer Director for Directed Energy, DoD; Former Head of Physics, LLNL.\n\n### George Tynan, Ph.D., FAPS\n\nNuclear Engineering\nNorm C. Rasmussen Adjunct Professor in Nuclear Engineering, MIT; Kazuo Iwama Endowed Distinguished\nProfessor of Engineering Science, Emeritus, UC San Diego.\n\n## Founding Scientific Advisors\n\nBefore Xcimer was officially incorporated, a small group of physicists, scientists and engineers,\nincluding the inventors of the excimer laser, contributed their time and advice to help arrive at\nthe compelling and practical power plant architecture we are now pursuing. We are grateful for their\ncontributions.\n\n### Bedros Afeyan, Ph.D.\n\nFounding Scientific Advisor\n\n### Paul Hoff, Ph.D.\n\nFounding Scientific Advisor\n\n### William Krupke, Ph.D.\n\nFounding Scientific Advisor\n\n### Joseph Mangano, Ph.D.\n\nFounding Scientific Advisor\n\n### Tom Mehlhorn, Ph.D.\n\nFounding Scientific Advisor\n\n### Allan Offenberger, Ph.D.\n\nFounding Scientific Advisor\n\n### Michael Tobin\n\nFounding Scientific Advisor\n\n### J. Gary Eden, Ph.D.\n\nFounding Scientific Advisor\n\n## Our Investors\n\n## Our Locations\n\n### \u2022 XEC Locations\n* Headquarters, Denver, CO\n* Manufacturing Operations, Tucson, AZ\n\n### \u2022 Partner Locations\n* Los Alamos National Laboratory (Los Alamos, NM)\n* Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (Livermore, CA)\n* Oak Ridge National Laboratory (Oak Ridge, TN)\n* Savannah River National Laboratory (Jackson, SC)\n* Naval Research Laboratory (Washington, DC)\n* Laboratory for Laser Energetics (Rochester, NY)\n* Massachusetts Institute of Technology (Cambridge, MA)\n* General Atomics (San Diego, CA)\n* Westinghouse (Cranberry Township, PA)\n* Universidad Nacional de Educacion a Distancia, UNED (Madrid, Spain)\n\n[10325 East 47th Ave.\nDenver, CO 80238, USA][20]\n[Linkedin page opens in new window][21][YouTube page opens in new window][22]\n**Information**\n[info@xcimer.energy][23]\n\n**Media**\n[media@xcimer.energy][24]\n\n**Careers**\n[careers@xcimer.energy][25]\nQuick Links:\n* [Company][26]\n* [Energy][27]\n* [Defense][28]\n* [Careers][29]\n* [Me