        "crawl_text": "General Atomics Not publicly traded North America Europe Asia Electromagnetic Systems Nuclear Technologies Advanced Materials High-Performance Computing Strong government contracts Innovative technology development Global presence Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) Department of Defense (DoD) 3550 General Atomics Court, San Diego, CA 92121-1122 Washington DC United States Germany Australia Switzerland Global General Atomics is a leader in defense and energy technologies, with a strong focus on innovation in unmanned systems and nuclear energy. The company has a significant global presence, operating in multiple countries and serving various markets. General Atomics received a $20 million tax credit to advance fusion energy development. The company is collaborating with the U.S. Department of Energy to design a full-scale fusion blanket test facility. Expansion of fusion energy technologies Development of advanced defense systems Enhancement of nuclear energy capabilities Regulatory challenges in the defense and nuclear sectors Competition from other defense contractors and energy firms Growing demand for clean energy solutions Increased defense spending by governments Partnerships with research institutions for advanced technologies General Atomics is positioned as a leading provider of advanced technologies in defense and energy sectors, with a strong emphasis on innovation and research. Investment in research and development Strategic partnerships with government agencies Expansion into international markets # General Atomics\n\n[[General Atomics]][1]\nSearch Search\n* [About][2]\n\n### General Atomics\n* [About General Atomics][3]\n* [Affiliated Companies][4]\n* [History][5]\n* [Neal Blue][6]\n\n### Energy Group\n* [About Energy Group][7]\n* [Energy Group Internships][8]\n* [Energy Group News & Updates][9]\n\n### Electromagnetic Systems Group\n* [About Electromagnetic Systems Group][10]\n\n### Uranium Resources\n* [About Uranium Resources][11]\n* [Products & Technology][12]\n\n### Energy\n* [Centers of Excellence][13]\n* [Energy Technologies and Services][14]\n* [Fission Energy Systems][15]\n* [Fusion Energy Systems][16]\n* [Stockpile Responsiveness][17]\n\n### Defense\n* [Aircraft Launch and Recovery Systems][18]\n* [Batteries, Power and Energy Systems][19]\n* [Demilitarization and Hazardous Waste Destruction][20]\n* [Missile Defense and Advanced Weapon Systems][21]\n* [Space Systems][22]\n* [Unmanned Aircraft Systems & Sensors][23]\n\n### Commercial Products and Services\n* [Explore All Commercial Products and Services][24]\n* [Procurement][25]\n* [News & Media][26]\n* [Careers][27]\n\n### Careers\n* [Working at General Atomics][28]\n* [GA Total Rewards ][29]\n* [Search all US Jobs ][30]\n\n### Locations & Divisions\n* [Explore Locations & Divisions][31]\n* [Search Internaltional Jobs ][32]\n\n### Early Careers\n* [About Early Careers][33]\n* [Energy Group Internships][34]\n* [Search Summer Internships ][35]\n\n### Military and Veterans\n* [DoD SkillBridge Program][36]\n* [Contact][37]\n* [Visitor Information][38]\n\nSearch Search\n1. [Home][39]\n2. About\nDownloads\n\n# General Atomics\n\n***Global Progress Through Technology***\n\nGeneral Atomics is a defense and diversified technologies company, founded in 1955 as a Division of\nGeneral Dynamics and acquired by the Blue family in 1986. GA and affiliated companies operate on\nfive continents and include GA Aeronautical Systems, Inc. (GA-ASI).\n\nGA-ASI produces a series of unmanned aircraft and provides electro-optical, radar, signals\nintelligence, and automated airborne surveillance systems. GA\u2019s Electromagnetic Systems Division\nproduces electro-magnetic aircraft launch and recovery systems for the US Navy, satellite\nsurveillance, electro-magnetic rail gun, high power laser, hypervelocity projectile, and power\nconversion systems.\n\nGA is the principal private sector participant in thermonuclear fusion research through its\ninternationally recognized DIII-D and inertial confinement programs for the US Department of Energy.\nGA developed the UCSD Supercomputer Center and has constructed more than 60 TRIGA nuclear research\nreactors in 24 countries. GA is a leader in development of next-generation nuclear fission and\nhigh-temperature materials technologies.\n\nOther GA affiliates include General Atomics Europe GmbH with principal facilities in the German\nStates of Saxony and Brandenburg, Heathgate Resources Pty Ltd (South Australia), GA Uranium\nResources Group, and the GA-Honeywell uranium conversion partnership.\n\nThe company occupies 8+ million square feet of engineering, laboratory and manufacturing facilities\nand comprises over 13,000 employees.\n\n[ Click here to download a PDF][40]\n\nGeneral Atomics Overview\n\n##### Downloads\n* [ About General Atomics][41]\n\n## GA Footer\n\n### Popular Links\n* [About Us][42]\n* [Careers][43]\n* [Contact Us][44]\n* [DIII-D National Fusion Facility][45]\n* [Newsroom][46]\n* [Visitor Information][47]\n\n### [Popular Links][48]\n* [About Us][49]\n* [Careers][50]\n* [Contact Us][51]\n* [DIII-D National Fusion Facility][52]\n* [Newsroom][53]\n* [Visitor Information][54]\n\n### Categories\n* [Commercial Products and Services][55]\n* [Defense][56]\n* [Energy Systems and Products][57]\n* [Fusion Power and Technologies][58]\n* [Satellite and Space Systems][59]\n* [Unmanned Aircraft Systems and Sensors][60]\n\n### [Categories][61]\n* [Commercial Products and Services][62]\n* [Defense][63]\n* [Energy Systems and Products][64]\n* [Fusion Power and Technologies][65]\n* [Satellite and Space Systems][66]\n* [Unmanned Aircraft Systems and Sensors][67]\n\n### Procurement\n* [Small Business Program][68]\n* [Supplier Information][69]\n* [Supplier Quality Assurance][70]\n\n### [Procurement][71]\n* [Small Business Program][72]\n* [Supplier Information][73]\n* [Supplier Quality Assurance][74]\n\n### Education\n* [Sciences Education Foundation][75]\n\n### [Education][76]\n*