        "pages": [
          {
            "url": "https://navysbir.com",
            "text": "Navy SBIR/STTR Home\n\nSmall Business Innovation Research&nbsp;&nbsp;\nSmall Business Technology Transfer&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\nHome\n\nAbout &#9660;\n\n&nbsp;&nbsp;- Program Info - &nbsp;&nbsp;- FAQs -\n\nOverview FAQs / Navy SBIR\n\nDescription FAQs / All SBIR\n\nPhase II &nbsp;&nbsp;- Legal Info -\n\nSBIR Tutorial Eligibility\n\nGetting Started Policy / Law\n\nGetting Paid Fraud, Waste, and Abuse\n&nbsp; -->\n\nBAAs &#9660;\n\nBroad Agency Announcements\n&nbsp;Current DoW SBIR/STTR BAAs\n&nbsp;Current Navy SBIR/STTR BAAs\n&nbsp;Previous Navy SBIR BAAs\n\nForms/Templates\n\nPrograms &#9660;\n\nSelect Programs to View:\n&nbsp;Navy Catapult\n&nbsp;Navy SBIR Transition Program (STP)\n&nbsp;SBIR Experimentation Cell (DON SEC)\n&nbsp;NAVY Launch\n\nSearch &#9660;\n\nNavy Awards &amp; Success Stories Database\nCurrent DoW SBIR/STTR Topics\nPrevious Navy SBIR/STTR Topics\n\nResources &#9660;\n\nPresentations / Tutorials\nReference Material / Manuals\nSuccess Stories\nCybersecurity/CUI\nTransition / Commercialization Resources\nImportant SBIR Agency Websites\nNavy STP Program\nNavy Virtual Transitions Marketplace VTM\n\nContacts\nHelp\n\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\n\n&#9776;\n\n&nbsp;\n\nNavy SBIR/STTR Home\n\nTo date, the Navy has funded over $11 billion to commercialize SBIR/STTR technologies.\n\n--> Success / Spotlight\nof the Month -->\n\nQuick Links\n\nCybersecurity/CUI\n\nDON SEC\n&nbsp; Experimentation Cell\n\nEvents Calendar\n\nFraud Waste Abuse\nNavalX -->\n\nSelections\n\nSubmission\n\nSuccess Stories\n\nTransitions - STP\n-->\n\nDoW SBIR (DSIP)\n\nSBIR.GOV\n\nSBIR/STTR\nAgency Websites\n\nSBIR/STTR is now Reauthorized\n\nThe SBIR and STTR programs have been reauthorized and the DoW is issuing BAAs on a new monthly schedule. The DoW Services and Components may elect to release topics under these monthly BAAs throughout fiscal year 2026, and the Navy will participate in several of them.\n[ more.. ]\n\nThe monthly BAAs will be pre-released on the first Wednesday of each month with each release having corresponding open and close dates applicable to the topics within that release.\n\nPlease note: Revisions to the solicitations are anticipated, based on programmatic changes required in the Small Business Innovation and Economic Security Act. You can subscribe to the DSIP Listserv and monitor\nfor announcement of revised solicitations. Please monitor DSIP for the most up to date information regarding SBIR/STTR Program impacts specific to program reauthorization.\n\nView the Calendar &amp; Info\n\nNavy SBIR News &amp; Announcements\n-->\n\nNews &amp; Announcements\n\nDoW/Navy FY-26 Release 3 SBIR/STTR Broad Agency Announcement (BAA)\n\nPre-release 6/3/26 &nbsp; Opens 6/24/26 &nbsp; Closes 7/22/26 ( 12:00pm ET )\n\nThe Department of the Navy (DON) SBIR/STTR FY-26 Release 3 topics are now in pre-release. These BAAs include 12 conventional SBIR topics, and 1 Commercial Solutions Openings (CSO) Open Topic. Awards under the CSO Open Topic will use Other Transaction (OT) agreements to accelerate prototyping and transition.\n[ more.. ]\n\nThe pre-release period is 3 June through 24 June and allows for direct communication between small businesses and Technical Points of Contact (TPOCs) to answer technical questions about the topics. The solicitations open to proposal submission on 24 June and close 22 July at 12:00 p.m. EDT.\n\nA Topic Q&A page, available on the Defense SBIR/STTR Innovation Portal (DSIP), allows firms to post technical questions publicly for TPOC response. The Topic Q&A page on DSIP will close to new questions on 8 July 2026.\n\nNavy FY-26 Release 3 SBIR Instructions &amp; Topics\n\nNavy FY-26 Release 2 STTR Instructions &amp; Topics -->\n\nDoW FY 2026 Release 3 BAA Instructions\n\nDoW SBIR R3 BAA &amp; Preface & Instructions\n\nDoW SBIR CSO R3 BAA Preface & Instructions\n\nSTTR BAA Preface & Instructions -->\n\nDoW DSIP BAA Submission &amp; Information Website\n\nDoW Topic Search Tool\n\nDoW/Navy FY-26 Release 2 SBIR/STTR Broad Agency Announcement (BAA)\n\nPre-release 5/6/26 &nbsp; Opened 5/27/26 &nbsp; Closed 6/24/26 ( 12:00pm ET )\n\nThe Department of the Navy (DON) SBIR/STTR FY-26 Release 2 topics are now closed. &nbsp; [ more... ]\n\nThese BAAs include 6 conventional SBIR topics, 3 Direct to Phase II SBIR topics and 2 conventional STTR topics. There were no Navy \"Open Topic\" Commercial Solutions Openings (CSO) in this release.\n[ more.. ]\n\nThe pre-release period is 6 May through 26 May and allows for direct communication between small businesses and Technical Points of Contact (TPOCs) to answer technical questions about the topics. The solicitations open to proposal submission on 27 May and close 24 June at 12:00 p.m. EDT.\n\nA Topic Q&A page, available on the Defense SBIR/STTR Innovation Portal (DSIP), allows firms to post technical questions publicly for TPOC response. The Topic Q&A page on DSIP will close to new questions on 10 June 2026.\n\nNavy FY-26 Release 2 SBIR Instructions &amp; Topics\n\nNavy FY-26 Release 2 STTR Instructions &amp; Topics\n\nDoW DSIP BAA Submission &amp; Information Website\n\nDoW Topic Search Tool\n\n[6/9/26] &nbsp; NAVAIR and NAVSEA Open Topic Webinar - 6/16/26\n\nNAVAIR and NAVSEA hosted an Open Topic webinar on June 16, 2026. The webinar addressed DON26BX03-NP002 - Open Topic for Counter Unmanned Air Systems (C-UAS). Details are available Here\n\n&nbsp;\n\n[6/24/26] &nbsp; Navy SBIR Office Hours 5/28/25 -->\n\nThe Navy SBIR will not present its monthly Office Hours for July. We will resume our monthly sessions on Wednesday August 26 at 12:00 p.m. ET. These are one-hour virtual session dedicated to guiding you through DON SBIR/STTR program as well as updates, and allowing you the space to ask questions.\n\nLearn more about Navy SBIR Office Hours and view the slides from our June event Here\n\n&nbsp;\n\nDoW/Navy FY-26 Release 1 SBIR/STTR Broad Agency Announcement (BAA)\n-->\nPre-released 4/13/26 &nbsp; Opened 5/6/26 &nbsp; Closed 6/3/26 ( 12:00pm ET )\n\nThe Department of the Navy (DON) SBIR/STTR FY-26 Release 1 topics are now closed. &nbsp; [ more... ]\n\nThese releases included SBIR Broad Agency Announcement (BAA), STTR BAA, SBIR Direct to Phase II, and \"Open Topic\" Commercial Solutions Opening (CSO) funding opportunities.\n\nTopics\n\nSBIR Topics 38\n\nDirect to Phase II 5\n\nCSO SBIR Topics 1\n\nSTTR Topics 19\n\nThe BAAs feature 39 SBIR Phase I, 5 SBIR Direct to Phase II, and 19 STTR Phase I Conventional topics from Marine Corps Systems Command (MCSC), Naval Air Systems Command (NAVAIR), Naval Sea Systems Command (NAVSEA), Office of Naval Research (ONR), and Strategic Systems Programs (SSP). Awardees may select from Firm Fixed Price and Cost-Plus Fixed Fee contracts in Phase II.\n[ more.. ] -->\n\nThe CSO contains one SBIR Phase I Open Topic from the Naval Information Warfare Systems Command (NAVWAR). Awards under this Open Topic will use Other Transaction (OT) agreements to accelerate prototyping and transition.\n\nThe pre-release period is through 5 May and allows for direct communication between small businesses and Technical Points of Contact (TPOCs) to answer technical questions about the topics. The solicitations open to proposal submission on 6 May and close 3 June at 12:00 p.m. EDT.\n\nA Topic Q&A page, available on the Defense SBIR/STTR Innovation Portal (DSIP), allows firms to post technical questions publicly for TPOC response. The Topic Q&A page on DSIP will close to new questions on 20 May.\n\n-->\n\nDSIP ) system until September 10, 2025 at 12:00 PM ET.\n\nThe DoW Topic Q&A system is available at\nwww.dodsbirsttr.mil/topics-app/ . Please note: In Topic Q&A, all questions and answers are posted electronically for general viewing.\nIdentifying information for the questioner and respondent is not posted. -->\n\nNavy FY-26 Release 1 SBIR Instructions &amp; Topics\n\nNavy FY-26 Release 1 STTR Instructions &amp; Topics\n\nDoW FY 2026 Release 1 BAA Instructions\n\nSBIR BAA &amp; Direct to Phase II Preface & Instructions\n\nDirect to Phase II BAA Preface & Instructions -->\n\nSBIR CSO BAA Preface & Instructions\n\nSTTR BAA Preface & Instructions\n\nDoW 25.B STTR BAA Preface &amp; Instructions -->\n\nDoW DSIP BAA Submission &amp; Information Website\n\nDoW Topic Search Tool\n\n[4/16/26] &nbsp; Navy Launch - Accelerating Commercial Success for Navy SBIR Phase II Awardees\n\nNAVY Launch is an intensely focused program for Navy SBIR Phase II awardees to explore, define (or redefine), and implement a commercialization strategy. Navy Launch has presented 8 virtual Commercialization workshops and now will be presenting 3 Private Capital Forum Events.\n\nIP and IP Protection , and will be held on March 31, 2026. -->\nThe next 2026 Navy Launch Private Capital Forum Event will take place on August 13, 2026 in Austin, TX. Learn about these great opportunities available to you! Here -->\n\nVisit Navy Launch Website -->\n\nHere .\nWe are presenting a series of live Private Capital Forums with the next one being held on November 20. [ Info &amp; Registration ] -->\n\n&nbsp;\n\n[05/27/26] &nbsp; New DoW and Navy SBIR/STTR BAA Calendar\n\nThe SBIR and STTR programs have been reauthorized and the DoW is issuing BAAs on a new monthly schedule. The DoW Services and Components may elect to release topics under these monthly BAAs throughout fiscal year 2026, and the Navy will participate in several of them.\n\nView the Calendar &amp; Info\n\n&nbsp;\n\n[04-20-26] &nbsp; New Navy Transitions Newsletter is Here!\n\n[ more.. ] -->\n\nThis edition highlights important Transitions news such as:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;[ more.. ]\n-->\n\nSBIR Reauthorization Passed! Learn about the changes from Navy SBIR/STTR Program Director Brian Shipley\n\nStrategic Breakthrough Awards\n\nFirst-time SBIR participant Pareto Frontier secures Phase III award for tactical communications solution\n\nProduct/technology positioning in Navy STP\n\nNavy\ufffds Rapid Capabilities Office accelerates capability delivery to Sailors and Marines\n\nUpcoming STP Events\n\nView/Download Your Copy Here (PDF Format)\n\n&nbsp;\n\n[02-25-26] &nbsp; NAVY SBIR/STTR FY-24 Year in Review\n\nThe Department of the Navy (DON) has just released its FY-24 SBIR/STTR Year in Review report which highlights many of the program's successes and statistics for the FY-24 period.\n[ more.. ]\n\nThis report is a comprehensive one year look at the DON SBIR/STTR programs for Fiscal Year 2024 (FY24) that examines the programs\ufffd approach, portfolio, and impact during the fiscal year.\n\nView / Download Navy SBIR/STTR FY-24 Year in Review\n------------------\n\nView / Download Navy SBIR/STTR FY-23 Year in Review\n\nView / Download Navy SBIR/STTR FY-22 Year in Review\n\n&nbsp;\n\n[10-23-23] &nbsp; Navy's Policy on Selectable, Not Funded Proposals from other Agencies:\n\n&nbsp;&nbsp; [ more.. ]\n\nIt is the policy of the Department of the Navy (DON) SBIR/STTR programs to only accept and evaluate proposals received in accordance with the SBIR/STTR Policy Directive (PD) :\n\nIn response to stated Agency topics contained in a Phase I [PD .4(a)] or direct to Phase II [PD .4(b)(1)(ii)] solicitation issued by DON\n\nIn response to DON Phase I contract deliverable requirements for merit-based Phase II evaluation [PD .4(b)(4)]\n\nIn response to a Request for Proposal for a sequential Phase II as a follow-on award to a current DON award [PD .4(b)(5)]\n\nIn response to a Request for Proposal for a subsequent Phase II from a firm that has a Phase I award from another agency. [PD .4(b)(7)]\n\nA Selectable, Not Funded proposal from another Agency is not a proposal in response to a DON solicitation nor is it an award that can be leveraged as a sequential or subsequent Phase II.\n\n&nbsp;\n\nView SBIR News &amp; Announcements Archive\n\n- Top -\n\nTo report Fraud, Waste or Abuse please visit\nwww.secnav.navy.mil/ig/Pages/ComplaintProcedure.aspx\n\nPrivacy Policy &nbsp;| NavalX &nbsp;&nbsp;| --> &nbsp;&nbsp; Navy Office of Small Business Programs | &nbsp;&nbsp; Navy Home\n\nDoW FY-26 SBIR/STTR\nRelease 3\n\nPre-release: &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp; 3-Jun-26\n\nOpens: &nbsp; &nbsp; 24-Jun-26\n\nCloses: &nbsp; &nbsp; 22-Jul-26\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; (12pm et)\n\nDoW FY-26 SBIR/STTR\nRelease 2\nNow Closed\n\nPre-release: &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp; 6-May-26\n\nOpens: &nbsp; &nbsp; 27-May-"
          }
