        "crawl_text": "Inertia Enterprises Fusion Energy Laser Technology World\u2019s most powerful laser system Mass production of fusion fuel targets 1.5 gigawatts of baseload electricity generation Not specified Inertia \u2014 The Commercial Fusion Energy Company\n\nFAQ\nPress\nJoin us\n\nStar power for life\nWe are on a mission to create limitless energy with proven fusion science. Join us\n\nWe have a clear path to commercialize fusion energy\n\nStart with science that works\n\nBuild the world\u2019s most powerful laser\n\nMass manufacture fusion fuel targets\n\nBuild a gigawatt grid-scale plant\nNIF\nIn December 2022, at the National Ignition Facility in Livermore, California, lasers struck a tiny target of fuel\n\n192 lasers\nOne tiny target\nIgnition achieved\n\nFor the first time, fusion ignition was demonstrated and net energy gain achieved.\n\nWith the science proven, now it\u2019s time to scale up\nLasers\nBuild the world\u2019s most powerful laser\n\nA thousand lasers. One million times more power. One tenth the footprint.\nOur modular laser system is the most powerful in the world. It is comprised of a thousand smaller lasers, each twenty times more efficient than at NIF.\nTargets\nOur fuel targets are produced in factories by the millions\n\nStriking 4.5mm targets\nOur lasers hit 4.5 millimeter targets, the heart of our fusion power engine.\n\n10 times per second\nOur plant shoots ten targets per second. Each target produces fifteen times more thrust than a SpaceX Falcon rocket at liftoff.\n\nLess than a dollar\nOur fusion fuel factory mass-produces targets from abundant materials for less than one dollar each.\n\nPower Plant\nOur plant generates 1.5 gigawatts of baseload, dispatchable electricity\nEnough energy to power over a million homes\n\nClean safe limitless energy\n\nOur Team\nEach day we build a more brilliant tomorrow\n\nWith the physics proven, it\u2019s time to deliver. Inertia\u2019s leaders and experts, together with partners in industry, academia and national labs, will bring limitless fusion energy to life.\n\nJeff Lawson\nCEO &amp; President\nLawson has founded and led the development of several multinational companies with billions in revenues and teams of thousands.\n[ in ]\n\nAnnie Kritcher\nChief Scientist\nDr. Kritcher led the team that designed the first and only fusion experiment to achieve net-positive ignition.\n[ in ]\n\nMike Dunne\nCTO &amp; SVP Fusion Power\nProf. Dunne led the US government program to design a fusion power plant based on NIF ignition.\n[ in ]\n\nMeet more of the team\n\nMariAnn Albrecht\nChief of Staff &amp; Research Program Manager\n\nNeil Alexander\nSVP of Target Development\n\nMichael Bratsafolis\nHead of Business\n\nJim Gaffney\nVice President &amp; Head of Integrated Plant Design\n\nDoug Hammond\nVice President &amp; Head of Lasers\n\nMelinda Lee\nChief Communications Officer &amp; Head of External Affairs\n\nGabriel Meric\nSenior Director &amp; Head of Materials and Mechanical Engineering\n\nVladimir Smalyuk\nVice President &amp; Head of Experimental Physics\n\nHenry Yang\nVice President of Industrial Engineering\nMeet our Science &amp; Technology Advisory Board\n\nMarv Adams \u2014 Advisory Board Chair\nLarge-scale nuclear program leadership and independent technical oversight across complex, multi-disciplinary systems.\n\nJeff Atherton\nEnd-to-end integration of laser, target, and facility systems for large-scale ICF program execution. Experience leading large target fab programs.\n\nBill Kruer\nExpert in laser\u2013plasma interactions and instability physics governing laser energy coupling.\n\nBrian MacGowan\nIntegrated ICF physics expert spanning LPI, diagnostics, hohlraum energetics, and facility performance.\n\nJoe Kilkenny\nNational leader in HED diagnostics and experimental validation for ignition-scale ICF.\n\nLarry Suter\nWorld-leading authority in hohlraum physics, x-ray drive, and symmetry control for indirect-drive ICF.\n\nBrian Wirth\nNuclear materials and radiation damage expert for chamber, blanket, and structural survivability.\n\nDoug Young\nAerospace-scale systems integration and execution of complex, multi-stakeholder engineering programs.\n\nJon Zuegel\nHigh-energy laser architecture and optical systems design for scalable, high-repetition-rate facilities.\nInertia in numbers\n\nLess than $1 per target\n\n10MJ Laser\n4.5x higher energy than NIF\n\n1.5GW\nPowers a city of one million people\n\nZero emissions\n\n15x\nThe thrust of a Falcon Heavy rocket\n\n1000\nBeamlines built in factories and delivered by truck\n\nLearn more about our approach.\n\nHelp light up our energy future. Join us.\n\nA message from our founders.\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms of Service\nCookie Policy\nFollow us on Linkedin\n\u00a9 2026 Inertia Enterprises. All rights reserved. inertia.com Inertia \u2014 The Commercial Fusion Energy Company\n\nFAQ\nPress\nJoin us\n\nStar power for life\nWe are on a mission to create limitless energy with proven fusion science. Join us\n\nWe have a clear path to commercialize fusion energy\n\nStart with science that works\n\nBuild the world\u2019s most powerful laser\n\nMass manufacture fusion fuel targets\n\nBuild a gigawatt grid-scale plant\nNIF\nIn December 2022, at the National Ignition Facility in Livermore, California, lasers struck a tiny target of fuel\n\n192 lasers\nOne tiny target\nIgnition achieved\n\nFor the first time, fusion ignition was demonstrated and net energy gain achieved.\n\nWith the science proven, now it\u2019s time to scale up\nLasers\nBuild the world\u2019s most powerful laser\n\nA thousand lasers. One million times more power. One tenth the footprint.\nOur modular laser system is the most powerful in the world. It is comprised of a thousand smaller lasers, each twenty times more efficient than at NIF.\nTargets\nOur fuel targets are produced in factories by the millions\n\nStriking 4.5mm targets\nOur lasers hit 4.5 millimeter targets, the heart of our fusion power engine.\n\n10 times per second\nOur plant shoots ten targets per second. Each target produces fifteen times more thrust than a SpaceX Falcon rocket at liftoff.\n\nLess than a dollar\nOur fusion fuel factory mass-produces targets from abundant materials for less than one dollar each.\n\nPower Plant\nOur plant generates 1.5 gigawatts of baseload, dispatchable electricity\nEnough energy to power over a million homes\n\nClean safe limitless energy\n\nOur Team\nEach day we build a more brilliant tomorrow\n\nWith the physics proven, it\u2019s time to deliver. Inertia\u2019s leaders and experts, together with partners in industry, academia and national labs, will bring limitless fusion energy to life.\n\nJeff Lawson\nCEO &amp; President\nLawson has founded and led the development of several multinational companies with billions in revenues and teams of thousands.\n[ in ]\n\nAnnie Kritcher\nChief Scientist\nDr. Kritcher led the team that designed the first and only fusion experiment to achieve net-positive ignition.\n[ in ]\n\nMike Dunne\nCTO &amp; SVP Fusion Power\nProf. Dunne led the US government program to design a fusion power plant based on NIF ignition.\n[ in ]\n\nMeet more of the team\n\nMariAnn Albrecht\nChief of Staff &amp; Research Program Manager\n\nNeil Alexander\nSVP of Target Development\n\nMichael Bratsafolis\nHead of Business\n\nJim Gaffney\nVice President &amp; Head of Integrated Plant Design\n\nDoug Hammond\nVice President &amp; Head of Lasers\n\nMelinda Lee\nChief Communications Officer &amp; Head of External Affairs\n\nGabriel Meric\nSenior Director &amp; Head of Materials and Mechanical Engineering\n\nVladimir Smalyuk\nVice President &amp; Head of Experimental Physics\n\nHenry Yang\nVice President of Industrial Engineering\nMeet our Science &amp; Technology Advisory Board\n\nMarv Adams \u2014 Advisory Board Chair\nLarge-scale nuclear program leadership and independent technical oversight across complex, multi-disciplinary systems.\n\nJeff Atherton\nEnd-to-end integration of laser, target, and facility systems for large-scale ICF program execution. Experience leading large target fab programs.\n\nBill Kruer\nExpert in laser\u2013plasma interactions and instability physics governing laser energy coupling.\n\nBrian MacGowan\nIntegrated ICF physics expert spanning LPI, diagnostics, hohlraum energetics, and facility performance.\n\nJoe Kilkenny\nNational leader in HED diagnostics and experimental validation for ignition-scale ICF.\n\nLarry Suter\nWorld-leading authority in hohlraum physics, x-ray drive, and symmetry control for indirect-drive ICF.\n\nBrian Wirth\nNuclear materials and radiation damage expert for chamber, blanket, and structural survivability.\n\nDoug Young\nAerospace-scale systems integration and execution of complex, multi-stakeholder engineering programs.\n\nJon Zuegel\nHigh-energy laser architecture and optical systems design for scalable, high-repetition-rate facilities.\nInertia in numbers\n\nLess than $1 per target\n\n10MJ Laser\n4.5x higher energy than NIF\n\n1.5GW\nPowers a city of one million people\n\nZero emissions\n\n15x\nThe thrust of a Falcon Heavy rocket\n\n1000\nBeamlines built in factories and delivered by truck\n\nLearn more about our approach.\n\nHelp light up our energy future. Join us.\n\nA message from our founders.\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms of Service\nCookie Policy\nFollow us on Linkedin\n\u00a9 2026 Inertia Enterprises. All rights reserved."
