el Shemesh\nVice President, Data & Digital\n* [ [Karen Smith][Karen Smith]\n][127]\nKaren Smith\nVice President, Regulatory Affairs & Quality\n* [ [Ido Warshavski][Ido Warshavski]\n][128]\nIdo Warshavski\nVice President, General Counsel & Corporate Secretary\n\n[Lumenis Logo][Lumenis Logo]\n* [\nAbout Lumenis\n][129]\n* [\nLumenis Leadership\n][130]\n* [\nCareers\n][131]\n* [\nCareers\n][132]\n* [\nLumenis App\n][133]\n* [\nLumenis Partner Zone\n][134]\n* [\nPollogen\n][135]\nAesthetics\n* [\nFacial Muscle Stimulation\n][136]\n* [\nHair Removal\n][137]\n* [\nBody\n][138]\n* [\nHair Loss\n][139]\n* [\nSkin\n][140]\n* [\nPhotofabulous\n][141]\n* [\nSmoothGlo\u2122\n][142]\n* [\nPigmentation\n][143]\n* [\nScars\n][144]\n* [\nTattoo Removal\n][145]\n* [\nVascular Lesions\n][146]\n* [\nWomen\u2019s Health\n][147]\nVision\n* [\n\ufeff\ufeffDry Eye\n][148]\n* [\nGlaucoma\n][149]\n* [\nRetina\n][150]\nPatients\n][151]\n* [\ntriLift\n][152]\n* [\nTreatMyDryEye\n][153]\n* [\nAesthetipedia\n][154]\n* [\nLightSheer Hair Removal\n][155]\n* [\nSmoothGlo\n][156]\n* [\nHopeForScars\n][157]\n* [\nFemTouch\n][158]\n][159][\n][160][\n][161][\n][162][\n][163]\n\nCopyright \u00a9 2010- Lumenis Be Ltd. All Rights Reserved\n* [\nPrivacy Statement\n][164]\n* [\nTerms of Use\n][165]\n* [\nSafety Information\n][166]\n* [\nPatents\n][167]\n* [\nYour Privacy Choices\n][168]\n* [\nPrivacy Statement\n][169]\n* [\nTerms of Use\n][170]\n* [\nSafety Information\n][171]\n* [\nPatents\n][172]\n* [\nYour Privacy Choices\n][173]\n\nSearchSubmitClear\nSearchSubmitClear\n[60 Years Pushing Boundaries.][60 Years Pushing Boundaries.]\n* [\nAesthetics\n][174]\n* [\nTreatments\n][175]\n* [\nFacial Muscle Stimulation\n][176]\n* [\nHair Removal\n][177]\n* [\nBody\n][178]\n* [\nHair Loss\n][179]\n* [\nSkin\n][180]\n* [\nPhotofabulous\n][181]\n* [\nSmoothGlo\u2122\n][182]\n* [\nPigmentation\n][183]\n* [\nScars\n][184]\n* [\nTattoo Removal\n][185]\n* [\nVascular Lesions\n][186]\n* [\nWomen\u2019s Health\n][187]\n* [\nProducts\n][188]\n* [\nFoLix\n][189]\n* [\ntriLift\n][190]\n* [\nLightSheer\n][191]\n* [\nStellar M22\n][192]\n* [\nM22\n][193]\n* [\nNuEra Tight US\n][194]\n* [\nNuEra Tight\n][195]\n* [\nLegend Pro\n][196]\n* [\nLegend Pro+\n][197]\n* [\nSPLENDOR X\n][198]\n* [\nULTRApulse^{\u00ae} Alpha\n][199]\n* [\nAcuPulse\n][200]\n* [\nFemTouch\n][201]\n* [\nTechnology\n][202]\n* [\nAblative Lasers CO2\n][203]\n* [\nIPL (Intense Pulsed Light)\n][204]\n* [\nLong Pulsed Nd:YAG\n][205]\n* [\nFractional Non Ablative\n][206]\n* [\nDiode Lasers\n][207]\n* [\nRadio-Frequency (RF)\n][208]\n* [\nRF Micro-Needling\n][209]\n* [\nQ-Switched Nd:YAG\n][210]\n* [\nBLEND X^{\u00ae} Alex YAG\n][211]\n* [\nResources\n][212]\n* [\nThe HUB\n][213]\n* [\nNews\n][214]\n* [\nEvents\n][215]\n* [\nWebinars\n][216]\n* [\nBlog\n][217]\n* [\nPatients\n][218]\n* [\nPollogen\n][219]\n* [\nCustomer Login\n][220]\n* [\nCustomer Login\n][221]\n* [\nVision\n][222]\n* [\nProducts\n][223]\n* [\nDry Eye\n][224]\n* [\nOptiLIGHT\n][225]\n* [\nOptiLIFT\n][226]\n* [\nOptiPLUS\n][227]\n* [\nIPL for Dry Eye\n][228]\n* [\nAntares\n][229]\n* [\nOPT Shields\n][230]\n* [\nOptima IPL\n][231]\n* [\nDry Eye Practices\n][232]\n* [\nCelebrity Testimonials\n][233]\n* [\nSLT + YAG Lasers\n][234]\n* [\nDigital Duet\n][235]\n* [\nDigital Trio\n][236]\n* [\nSelecta Duet\n][237]\n* [\nSelecta Trio\n][238]\n* [\nPhotocoagulators\n][239]\n* [\nSmart532\n][240]\n* [\nVision One\n][241]\n* [\nArray LaserLink\u2122\n][242]\n* [\nAccessories\n][243]\n* [\nResources\n][244]\n* [\nPress Publications\n][245]\n* [\nClinical Studies\n][246]\n* [\nWebinars\n][247]\n* [\nNews\n][248]\n* [\nBlog Posts\n][249]\n* [\nCustomer Login\n][250]\n* [\nResources\n][251]\n* [\nAesthetics\n][252]\n* [\nE-books\n][253]\n* [\nTutorials\n][254]\n* [\nWebinars\n][255]\n* [\nNews\n][256]\n* [\nUpcoming Events\n][257]\n* [\nBlog\n][258]\n* [\nVision\n][259]\n* [\nPress Publications\n][260]\n* [\nClinical Studies\n][261]\n* [\nWebinars\n][262]\n* [\nBlog Posts\n][263]\n* [\nAbout\n][264]\n* [\nCareers\n][265]\n* [\nCareers\n][266]\n* [\nCompany Overview\n][267]\n* [\nLumenis Leadership\n][268]\n* [\nSocial Responsibility\n][269]\n* [\nSupport\n][270]\n* [\nService Overview\n][271]\n* [\nService Locations\n][272]\n* [\nLumenis App\n][273]\n* [\nContact Us\n][274]\n* [\nPatients\n][275]\n* [\nGlobal, English\n][276]\n* [\nGlobal, \u4e2d\u6587\n][277]\n* [\nGlobal, \u0420\u0443\u0441\u0441\u043a\u0438\u0439\n][278]\n* [\nAustralia, English\n][279]\n* [\nFrance, Fran\u00e7ais\n][280]\n* [\nGermany, Deutsch\n][281]\n* [\nJapan, \u65e5\u672c\u8a9e\n][282]\n* [\nItaly, italiano\n][283]\n* [\nUK, English\n][284]\nTzipi Ozer-Armon\nChief Executive Officer (CEO)\n\nMs. Tzipi Ozer-Armon, CEO of Lumenis, joined the company in May 2012. Before joining Lumenis, Ms.\nOzer-Armon headed the Japanese market activities of Teva Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd. (Nasdaq:\nTEVA), a business with a turnover of more than $800M. Prior to that, Ms. Ozer-Armon served as Senior\nVice President of Sales and Marketing at SanDisk (Nasdaq: SNDK), having multi-billion dollars sales\u2019\nresponsibility; she also served as VP & General Manager of MSystems (Nasdaq: FLSH), and as VP of\nCorporate Development at Comverse (Nasdaq: CMVT). Ms. Ozer-Armon\u2019s career also includes four years\nat ATKearney, a Global Management Consulting company based in London, UK. Ms. Ozer-Armon holds a BA\nmagna cum laude in Economics from Tel Aviv University, an MBA majoring in Finance and Marketing, and\nshe is an AMP graduate of the Harvard Business School.\n\nShy Basson\nChief Financial Officer (CFO)\n\nMr. Shy Basson joined Lumenis in May 2022 as the Chief Financial Officer. Shy brings more than 20\nyears of experience in Finance, Business and Operations. Prior to joining Lumenis, Shy was the CFO\nand US COO of Itamar Medical, a MedTech company focused on leading the integration of Sleep Apnea\nmanagement into the cardiac patient care pathway. During his tenure, Shy drove continuous\nimprovement, led the company\u2019s NASDAQ IPO, and at a later stage played a pivotal role in the\ncompany\u2019s M&A process, ultimately resulting in an acquisition of Itamar Medical by Zoll Medical.\nBefore joining Itamar Medical, Shy held roles as the CFO, Business and Strategy for WeFi, the\nDirector of Business Development at AOL (a Time Warner Company), and the CFO of ICQ, the world\nleader in instant messaging. Shy earned a Master of Business Administration from the\nKellogg-Recanati International Executive MBA Program and is also a Certified Public Accountant.\n\nStacey Winter\nVice President and Regional President, North America\n\nMs. Stacey Winter joined Lumenis in 2019 as Director of Sales for the Surgical division, bringing\nwith her 15 years of experience in medical capital equipment. In 2021, she was selected to create\nand lead the Vision division, a pivotal role highlighted by the launch of OptiLIGHT, where she\nleveraged her deep sales expertise to drive adoption of the innovative new platform. In 2025, Ms.\nWinter was appointed Vice President of Operations, a role focused on standardization, process\nimprovement, and the development of medical education initiatives. In 2026, she was named President\nof Lumenis North America.\nPrior to joining Lumenis, Ms. Winter built an extensive career leading high-performing sales teams\nacross the medical device industry, developing the commercial acumen, clinical knowledge, and\nstrategic instincts that continue to define her leadership approach today.\nMs. Winter holds a Bachelor of Science degree in Business Management from the University of\nTennessee, where she served as captain of the Lady Vols golf team and graduated Magna Cum Laude.\n\nQiying Zhai\nSenior Vice President & Regional President, APAC & Japan\n\nMr. Zhai Qiying, Senior Vice President & Regional President of Lumenis APAC & Japan Region joined\nthe company in 2001. Before joining Lumenis, Mr. Qiying held senior management positions with the\nCoherent Medical Group in his region, and joined Lumenis with the company\u2019s ESC/Sharplan merger. Mr.\nQiying started Lumenis\u2019 Ophthalmic business in China in 1992 and has been with Lumenis since that\ntime responsible for Lumenis\u2019 China/APAC region.\n\nRoy Ramati\nSenior Vice President, EMEA & Business Development\n\nMr. Roy Ramati, Senior Vice President, EMEA & Business Development, joined Lumenis in June 2012. Mr.\nRamati brings to his role vast management and entrepreneurial experience. Before joining Lumenis,\nMr. Ramati served as VP & GM of the Enterprise Division at SanDisk Corp. and before that as VP\nOperations and Manager of the Memory Cards Business at Msystems, Roy was the founder and Co-CEO of\nthe Fantine Group, a provider of business development services in Europe and a Venture Capital Fund.\nMr. Ramati also served as a management consultant at Shaldor, Israel\u2019s top management consulting\nfirm. Mr. Ramati holds"
          },
