            "text": "[[Built In Logo] [Built In Logo]][1][Companies][2][Jobs][3][Articles][4]\n[View All Jobs][5]\n[ Join ][6]\n[ Log In ][7]\n[ For Employers ][8]\n[ Companies ][9] [ GitLab ][10]\n\n# GitLab\n\nSave Saved\nSan Francisco\n2,500 Total Employees\nYear Founded: 2014\n[View Website][11]\nWe're Hiring!\n[ Sales **48** ][12] [ Engineering **40** ][13] [ Customer Success & Experience **12** ][14] [\nOperations & Support **7** ][15] [ Consulting **4** ][16] [ Cybersecurity **3** ][17] [ AI & Machine\nLearning **3** ][18] [ HR & Recruiting **3** ][19] [ Legal **3** ][20] [ Marketing **3** ][21] [\nProduct Management **3** ][22] [ Design **2** ][23] [ Finance **2** ][24] [ Data & Analytics **1**\n][25] [ Program & Project Management **1** ][26]\n[View all jobs][27]\n* Overview\n* Jobs 136\n* Offices\n* Teams\n* Culture\n* Articles\n* Company Insights\n* [ Working at GitLab ][28]\n* [ Culture & Values ][29]\n* [ Inclusion & Diversity ][30]\n* [ Career Growth & Development ][31]\n* [ Compensation & Benefits ][32]\n* [ Work-Life Balance & Wellbeing ][33]\n* [ Leadership & Management ][34]\n* [ Innovation, Technology & Agility ][35]\n* [ Mission, Purpose & Impact ][36]\n* [ Stability & Growth ][37]\nCloud\n][38] [\nSecurity\n][39] [\nSoftware\n][40] [\nCybersecurity\n][41] [\nAutomation\n][42]\nThe intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps\nGitLab is the Intelligent Orchestration Platform where software teams and their AI agents stay in\nflow to amplify their capacity for innovation. Together, they automate repetitive tasks to plan,\nbuild, secure, test, deploy and maintain software. With GitLab, software teams spend less time on\ncoordination overhead and more time on the next big idea. What started in 2011 as an open source\nproject to help one team of programmers collaborate is now the intelligent orchestration platform\nmillions of people use to deliver software faster, more efficiently, while strengthening security\nand compliance. Since the beginning, we've been firm believers in remote work, open source,\nDevSecOps, and iteration. We get up and log on in the morning to work alongside the GitLab community\nto deliver new innovations every month that help teams and their AI agents ship great code faster.\n[thumbnail]\n[gallery]\nView Gallery\n\n## Recently Posted Jobs at GitLab\n\n[View All ][43]\n\n## [GitLab Logo] GitLab\n\n][44]\n\n### [Senior Product Manager, AI Platform Management][45]\n\nRemote\n3 Locations\n\n## [GitLab Logo] GitLab\n\n][46]\n\n### [Staff Forward Deployed Engineer][47]\n\nRemote\n\n## [GitLab Logo] GitLab\n\n][48]\n\n### [Commercial Legal Counsel][49]\n\nRemote\n\n## [GitLab Logo] GitLab\n\n][50]\n\n### [Senior Solutions Architect, AI / Core DevOps - EMEA][51]\n\nRemote\nUnited Kingdom\n\n## [GitLab Logo] GitLab\n\n][52]\n\n### [Public Sector Strategic Account Executive, FSI][53]\n\nRemote\n\n## [GitLab Logo] GitLab\n\n][54]\n\n### [Business Development Representative][55]\n\nRemote\nIndia\n\n## [GitLab Logo] GitLab\n\n][56]\n\n### [Solutions Architect, LATAM][57]\n\nRemote\nM\u00e9xico\n\n## [GitLab Logo] GitLab\n\n][58]\n\n### [Customer Success Manager- Public Sector][59]\n\nRemote\n\n## [GitLab Logo] GitLab\n\n][60]\n\n### [Senior Manager, Business Development][61]\n\nRemote\n4 Locations\nView all jobs\n][62]\n\n## GitLab Offices\n\n[Learn More ][63]\n\nRemote Workspace\n\nEmployees work remotely.\n\nAll-remote means that each individual in the organization is empowered to work and live where they\nare most fulfilled; it makes it clear that every team member is equal. No one, not even the\nexecutive team, meets in-person on a daily basis.\n\nSan Francisco, California, USA\nLearn more\n][64]\n\n## GitLab Teams\n\n[Learn More ][65]\n[Team]\nSales & Customer Success\nAbout our Teams\n][66]\nInside Our\nCompany Culture\nLearn More\n[Rachel Richburg]\nRachel Richburg\nSr. Account Executive, Major Accounts\n][67][\n[Lisa van de Kooj]\nLisa van de Kooj\nDirector, Regional Sales - Nordics\n][68]\n\n## Articles We're In\n\n[View All ][69]\n[[Photo: GitLab]][70]\n[Olivia McClure] Olivia McClure\nPublished on April 02, 2026\n\n## Shipping Code and Career Growth: An Engineer\u2019s Journey at GitLab\n\n][71]\n\nPromoted twice since joining GitLab in 2021, Staff Back-End Engineer Huzaifa Iftikhar explains what\nit takes to grow an engineering career in a global remote workplace.\n\n[Olivia McClure] Olivia McClure\nUpdated on December 23, 2025\n\n## What It\u2019s Like to Build a Career at GitLab in a Fast-Changing DevSecOps World\n\n][72]\n\nAfter celebrating his five-year anniversary, Account Executive Brady O\u2019Dowd shares how GitLab\nsupports internal growth, customer impact and long-term career development.\n\n[[Photo: GitLab]][73]\n[Brand Studio Logo]\n[Olivia McClure] Olivia McClure\nUpdated on April 30, 2026\n\n## What It\u2019s Like to Work on GitLab\u2019s Global CIO Team in India\n\n][74]\n\nThree members of GitLab\u2019s global CIO team in India explain how their automation and AI solutions\nsupport teams around the world and what it\u2019s like to work in a remote-first culture rooted in\nownership, and connection.\n\n[[Photo: GitLab]][75]\n[Brand Studio Logo]\n[View all articles][76]\n\n## Awards\n\n[award][award][award][award]\n[award]\n\n## Technology We Use\n* [ENGINEERING][77]\n* [PRODUCT][78]\n* [SALES & MARKETING][79]\n\n[C#]\nLANGUAGES\n[Golang]\nGolang\nLANGUAGES\n[JavaScript]\nJavaScript\nLANGUAGES\n[PostgreSQL]\nPostgreSQL\nDATABASES\n[Python]\nPython\nLANGUAGES\n[Ruby]\nRuby\nLANGUAGES\n[Ruby on Rails]\nRuby on Rails\nFRAMEWORKS\n[Snowflake]\nSnowflake\nDATABASES\n[Vue.js]\nVue.js\nFRAMEWORKS\n[AWS]\nAWS\nLANGUAGES\n[Figma]\nFigma\nDESIGN\n[Google Analytics]\nGoogle Analytics\nANALYTICS\n[Tableau]\nTableau\nANALYTICS\n[Snowplow]\nSnowplow\nANALYTICS\n[Kinesis]\nKinesis\nANALYTICS\n[GitLab]\nGitLab\nPROJECT MANAGEMENT\n[Chorus.AI]\nChorus.AI\nCRM\n[DocuSign]\nDocuSign\nCRM\n[LinkedIn SalesNavigator]\nLinkedIn SalesNavigator\nCRM\n[Marketo]\nMarketo\nLEAD GEN\n[Salesforce]\nSalesforce\nCRM\n[Troops]\nTroops\nCRM\n[ZoomInfo]\nZoomInfo\nLEAD GEN\n[Clari]\nClari\nCRM\n[Gainsight]\nGainsight\nCRM\n[Impartner]\nImpartner\nCRM\n\n## GitLab FAQs\n\n[What's It Like to Work at GitLab?][80]\n[What's the Company Culture Like at GitLab?][81]\n[GitLab Inclusion & Diversity][82]\n[GitLab Career Growth & Development][83]\n[GitLab Compensation & Benefits][84]\n[What's the Work-Life Balance Like at GitLab?][85]\n[GitLab Leadership & Management][86]\n[GitLab Innovation & Technology Culture][87]\n[GitLab Mission, Purpose & Impact][88]\n[GitLab Company Growth, Stability & Outlook][89]\n\n## GitLab's Teams\n\n[Sales & Customer Success][90]\n[View All Jobs at GitLab][91]\n* [\nCompanies\n][92]\n* [\nJobs\n][93]\n* [\nTracker\n][94]\n* [\nArticles\n][95]\n* More\n[Built In]\n[ Join ][96]\n[ Log In ][97]\n* [\nTech Jobs\n][98]\n* [\nCompanies\n][99]\n* [\nArticles\n][100]\n* [\nRemote\n][101]\n* [\nBest Places To Work\n][102]\n* [\nTech Hubs\n][103]\n[ Post Job ][104]\n[[BuiltIn]][105]\n\u00a9 2026 Built In. All rights reserved.\nAbout\n[ Our Story ][106]\n[ Careers ][107]\n[ Our Staff Writers ][108]\n[ Content Descriptions ][109]\nGet Involved\n[ Recruit With Built In ][110]\n[ Become an Expert Contributor ][111]\nResources\n[ Customer Support ][112]\n[ Share Feedback ][113]\n[ Report a Bug ][114]\n[ Tech Job Tools + Career Resources ][115]\n[ Browse Jobs ][116]\n[ Tech A-Z ][117]\nTech Hubs\n[Our Sites][118]\n\u00a9 2026 Built In. All rights reserved.\n[ Learning Lab User Agreement ][119] [ Accessibility Statement ][120] [ Copyright Policy ][121] [\nPrivacy Policy ][122] [ Terms of Use ][123] [ Your Privacy Choices/Cookie Settings ][124] [ CA\nNotice of Collection ][125]\n\n[1]: /\n[2]: /companies\n[3]: /jobs\n[4]: /tech-topics\n[5]: /jobs\n[6]: /auth/signup?destination=%2fcompany%2fgitlab\n[7]: /auth/login?destination=%2fcompany%2fgitlab\n[8]: https://employers.builtin.com?utm_medium=BIReferral&utm_source=foremploye