            "url": "https://builtin.com/company/2k/faq/workplace-perception",
            "text": "[[Built In Logo] [Built In Logo]][1][Companies][2][Jobs][3][Articles][4]\n[View All Jobs][5]\n[ Join ][6]\n[ Log In ][7]\n[ For Employers ][8]\n[ Companies ][9] [ 2K ][10]\n\n## 2K\n\nSave Saved\nNovato\nTotal Offices: **22**\n4,200 Total Employees\nYear Founded: 2005\n[View Website][11]\nWe're Hiring!\n[ Engineering **48** ][12] [ Design **40** ][13] [ Marketing **17** ][14] [ Product Management **9**\n][15] [ Data & Analytics **8** ][16] [ Operations & Support **7** ][17] [ AI & Machine Learning\n**6** ][18] [ Program & Project Management **6** ][19] [ Customer Success & Experience **4** ][20] [\nHR & Recruiting **2** ][21]\n[View all jobs][22]\n* Overview\n* Jobs 154\n* Offices\n* Articles\n* Company Insights\n* [ Working at 2K ][23]\n* [ Culture & Values ][24]\n* [ Inclusion & Diversity ][25]\n* [ Career Growth & Development ][26]\n* [ Compensation & Benefits ][27]\n* [ Work-Life Balance & Wellbeing ][28]\n* [ Leadership & Management ][29]\n* [ Innovation, Technology & Agility ][30]\n* [ Mission, Purpose & Impact ][31]\n* [ Stability & Growth ][32]\n\n# What's It Like to Work at 2K?\n\nUpdated on May 29, 2026\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n## What practices at 2K support employee job satisfaction?\n\nJob Satisfaction\n\n2K supports employee job satisfaction through collaborative game development culture, creative\nownership opportunities, flexible work models, structured career development and benefits designed\naround wellbeing, family support and long-term growth. Employees work across globally recognized\nfranchises including NBA 2K, Borderlands, BioShock, Civilization, Mafia, WWE 2K and PGA TOUR 2K,\nwhich many employees view as meaningful and motivating creative work.\n\n**Collaborative and team-oriented culture: **2K emphasizes collaboration, inclusion and open\ncommunication across studios and publishing teams. Workplace practices include open-door policies,\nOKR-based planning, hybrid flexibility and employee-driven feedback culture. Employee reviews\nfrequently describe coworkers as talented, supportive and passionate about games.\n\n**Creative ownership and meaningful work: **Employees are often given opportunities to contribute\ndirectly to major franchises and live-service experiences with global player communities. 2K\u2019s\nmulti-studio structure also allows employees to work across publishing, engineering, art, design,\nanalytics and production disciplines while contributing to highly visible launches and long-term\nfranchise development.\n\n**Career development and growth opportunities: **2K\u2019s publishing and engineering graduate programs\ninclude rotational experiences, onboarding support, mentorship, Unreal Engine 5 and C++ exposure,\nnetworking opportunities and studio placements. The programs are positioned as pathways into\nlong-term careers across the company\u2019s studio ecosystem.** **\n\n**Flexibility and employee wellbeing: **Benefits include hybrid work arrangements, wellness support,\nmental health benefits, paid parental leave, fertility support, childcare assistance, fitness\nbenefits, volunteer opportunities and employee resource groups. Employees also receive access to\ncompensation programs including bonuses, stock purchase plans and 401(k) matching.\n\n**External signals:**\n* Comparably gives 2K an A+ culture rating and places the company in the Top 5% of similarly sized\ncompanies.\n* 2K has been featured on Built In for workplace culture, employee experience and graduate career\ndevelopment programs.\n* Employee reviews on Glassdoor frequently highlight collaborative teams, strong coworkers, creative\nwork and flexibility as major positives.\n\n**Bottom line: **2K is generally viewed as a strong workplace for employees who enjoy collaborative\ncreative work, major gaming franchises, team-oriented culture and opportunities to grow within the\ninteractive entertainment industry.\n\n## Is 2K a good place to work? Do Employees Recommend it?\n\nWillingness to Recommend\n\n2K is generally viewed positively by employees, particularly among people interested in game\ndevelopment, publishing, creative technology and large-scale entertainment franchises. Reviews\nfrequently highlight collaborative teams, recognizable IP, career growth opportunities and the\nability to contribute to globally known games.\n\n**Strong creative and gaming industry reputation: **2K is one of the most recognizable publishers in\ngaming, with franchises including NBA 2K, Borderlands, BioShock, Civilization, Mafia and WWE 2K.\nEmployees frequently describe the work as exciting, creatively rewarding and highly visible within\nthe gaming industry.\n\n**Collaborative and supportive environment: **Employee reviews commonly describe coworkers as\ntalented, approachable and passionate about games. Reviews also frequently reference supportive\nmanagers, cross-functional teamwork and opportunities to contribute ideas. Workplace practices\nemphasize open communication, collaborative planning and hybrid flexibility.\n\n**Career growth and development: **2K emphasizes mentorship, internal mobility and structured\ndevelopment programs. Employees frequently mention gaining broad industry exposure and\ncareer-building experience across development and publishing functions. Graduate programs include\nrotational learning, technical training and long-term placement opportunities within the company\u2019s\nstudio network.\n\n**Compensation, flexibility and benefits: **Employees often rate 2K positively for benefits, hybrid\nflexibility and entertainment-industry perks. Benefits include health coverage, wellness programs,\nstock purchase plans, bonuses, parental leave, fertility benefits and flexible work policies.\n\n**External signals:**\n* Comparably gives 2K an A+ overall culture rating and ranks the company among the Top 5% of\nsimilarly sized employers.\n* Employee reviews on Glassdoor frequently describe 2K positively for creative work, gaming industry\nexposure and collaborative culture.\n* Built In has featured 2K for employee experience, workplace culture and career development\nopportunities.\n\n**Bottom line:** 2K is generally considered a strong place to work for employees who value creative\ncollaboration, gaming industry experience, recognizable franchises and opportunities to build\ncareers within large-scale game development and publishing.\n\n## What reputation does 2K have as a place to work?\n\nGeneral Market Perception\n\n2K has built a reputation as a collaborative, creative and franchise-driven gaming company where\nemployees can work on globally recognized entertainment properties while contributing to large-scale\ngame development and publishing initiatives. Within the gaming industry, 2K is often viewed as a\nmajor employer associated with high-profile IP, experienced development studios and long-term\nfranchise investment.\n\n**Strong reputation for recognizable franchises and creative work:** 2K\u2019s portfolio includes NBA 2K,\nBorderlands, BioShock, Civilization, Mafia, WWE 2K and PGA TOUR 2K. Employees frequently describe\nthe company as offering opportunities to work on games with large player communities and major\nglobal visibility. Its studio ecosystem includes teams such as Visual Concepts, Firaxis, Hangar 13,\nCat Daddy, HB Studios, Cloud Chamber and 31st Union.\n\n**Collaborative and people-oriented culture reputation: **Employee reviews commonly describe 2K as\ncollaborative, supportive and team-focused. Reviews frequently mention strong peer relationships,\ncreative teamwork and supportive managers. Workplace practices emphasize open communication, hybrid\nflexibility and employee-centered collaboration.\n\n**Reputation for career growth and industry exposure: **2K is also recognized for early-career and\ndevelopment opportunities through structured publishing and engineering graduate programs. Employees\nreceive rotational learning, mentorship, Game Jam experiences \u2014 where team members gather to create\ngames from scratch, Unreal Engine training and studio placements designed to build long-term gaming\ncareers.\n\n**Reputation for long-term franchise investment: **2K continues investing in major gaming\nfranchises, studio expansion and long-term development initiatives across console, PC and\nlive-service gaming experiences. Employees often describe the company as ambitious, growth-oriented\nand deeply connected to the broader gaming industry.\n\n**External signals:**\n* Comparably gives 2K an A+ culture rating and places the company in the Top 5% of similarly sized\nemployers.\n* Glassdoor reviews frequently highlight collaborative culture, talented teams and opportunities to\nwork on major franchises.\n* Built In has featured 2K for workplace culture, employee experience and graduate career\ndevelopment initiatives.\n\n**Bottom line: **2K is widely viewed as a strong workplace for employees seeking creative\ncollaboration, exposure to major gaming franchises, supportive teams and long-term career\nopportunities within the interactive entertainment industry.\n\n## What tradeoffs might come with working at 2K?\n\nTradeoffs\n\nOne tradeoff at 2K is strong cross-functional collaboration vs. highly independent, siloed work.\nTeams regularly partner across engineering, design, production, analytics, publishing and\nlive-service operations to support franchises like NBA 2K, Borderlands, Civilization and WWE 2K.\nEmployees who enjoy collaborative creative environments and shared ownership tend to thrive most.\n\nAnother tradeoff is broad ownership and accountability vs. narrowly defined responsibilities.\nEmployees are often trusted with meaningful work tied directly to gameplay systems, player\nengagement and franchise development, which creates strong visibility and impact but also rewards\nself-direction and initiative.\n\nEmployees may also experience performance- and growth-oriented rewards vs. highly predictable\ncompensation progression. 2K offers bonuses, stock purchase opportunities and career growth tied to\nfranchise and company performance, which tends to appeal most to employees motivated by long-term\nopportunity and visible impact.\n\nThere is also a tradeoff between hybrid flexibility and fully centralized in-office collaboration.\nMany teams operate with flexible hybrid structures shaped around studio and project needs, which\nsupports autonomy and balance while still requiring strong communication and collaboration skills.\n\nAnother tradeoff is supportive, engaged management vs. highly hands-off leadership styles. Employees\nfrequently describe managers as collaborative, communicative and actively involved during launches,\ndevelopment cycles and live-service updates.\n\nEmployees may also notice the tradeoff between global scale and startup-style intimacy. Working\nwithin a major gaming publisher provides exposure to globally recognized franchises, large player\ncommunities and long-term career opportunities, though naturally with more coordination and\nstructure than smaller independent studios.\n\nFinally, 2K tends to favor experimentation, iteration and evolving priorities vs. highly fixed\nlong-term roadmaps. Teams regularly adapt based on player feedback, franchise strategy and\nlive-service performance, which works especially well for employees who enjoy creative problem\nsolving and fast-moving environments.\n\n**Great match for candidates who prefer:**\n* Collaborative, cross-functional teamwork\n* Creative ownership and visible impact\n* Hybrid flexibility and autonomy\n* Fast-moving gaming and entertainment environments\n* Working on globally recognized franchises\n* Career growth tied to performance and initiative\n* Player-focused development and live-service gaming\n\n**Working here means:**\n* Supporting franchises like NBA 2K, Borderlands, Civilization and WWE 2K\n* Collaborating across studios, publishing and live-service teams\n* Working on gameplay systems, player engagement and franchise growth\n* Operating in fast-moving entertainment and gaming environments\n* Balancing creativity, collaboration, ownership and large-scale execution\n\n## 2K's Candidate Tradeoffs\n\n**If you\u2019re weighing whether 2K is the right fit, these are the core tradeoffs"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://builtin.com/company/achieve/faq/workplace-perception",
            "text": "[[Built In Logo] [Built In Logo]][1][Companies][2][Jobs][3][Articles][4]\n[View All Jobs][5]\n[ Join ][6]\n[ Log In ][7]\n[ For Employers ][8]\n[ Companies ][9] [ Achieve ][10]\n\n## Achieve\n\nSave Saved\nSan Mateo\nTotal Offices: **3**\n2,231 Total Employees\n118 Product + Tech Employees\nYear Founded: 2002\n[View Website][11]\nWe're Hiring!\n[ Sales **6** ][12] [ Finance **5** ][13] [ Cybersecurity **3** ][14] [ Product Management **3**\n][15] [ Customer Success & Experience **1** ][16] [ AI & Machine Learning **1** ][17] [ Design **1**\n][18] [ Engineering **1** ][19] [ Marketing **1** ][20] [ Operations & Support **1** ][21]\n[View all jobs][22]\n* Overview\n* Jobs 25\n* Offices\n* Teams\n* Articles\n* Company Insights\n* [ Working at Achieve ][23]\n* [ Culture & Values ][24]\n* [ Inclusion & Diversity ][25]\n* [ Career Growth & Development ][26]\n* [ Compensation & Benefits ][27]\n* [ Work-Life Balance & Wellbeing ][28]\n* [ Leadership & Management ][29]\n* [ Innovation, Technology & Agility ][30]\n* [ Mission, Purpose & Impact ][31]\n* [ Stability & Growth ][32]\n\n# What's It Like to Work at Achieve?\n\nUpdated on May 04, 2026\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n## What practices at Achieve support employee job satisfaction?\n\nJob Satisfaction\n\nAchieve supports employee job satisfaction through career growth, purpose-driven work, a culture of\nbelonging, flexibility, comprehensive benefits, and strong business stability.\n\n**Room to grow: **Achieve emphasizes internal mobility and rapid career progression supported by\nstructured development programs. Team members often experience promotions in as little as three\nmonths, and approximately 30% of roles are filled internally. The company also invests in career\ndevelopment through programs like its Career Pathing Program, Comprehensive Leadership Model,\nmentorship opportunities, and AI training initiatives. Employee stories reinforce this trajectory,\nincluding long-term career growth from entry-level roles to leadership positions and internal\ntransitions across functions.\n\n**A purpose-driven culture: **Achieve connects employee experience directly to its mission of\nhelping people improve their financial futures. Employees frequently describe strong personal\nalignment with this purpose, from building tools that simplify debt management to educating\ncustomers and improving financial literacy. The company\u2019s \u201cheart and dollar\u201d philosophy reinforces\nbalancing empathy with business outcomes, positioning work as both impactful and meaningful.\n\n**A culture of belonging: **Achieve fosters an inclusive, values-driven culture centered on Care,\nGet better, Collaborate, and Act with integrity. Employee Resource Groups\u2014including African\nAmerican/Black, LGBTQ+, Women\u2019s Leadership, Hispanic/Latinx, AAPI, and Military/Veterans\ncommunities\u2014support development, connection, and representation. Employees highlight strong\ncamaraderie, teamwork, and support from peers and leadership, reinforcing a sense of belonging and\nshared purpose.\n\n**Flexibility and well-being: **Achieve supports multiple work styles through remote, hybrid, and\nin-office options, allowing employees to choose environments that best fit their productivity and\nlifestyle. Employees cite benefits such as reduced commute stress, improved work-life balance, and\nflexibility to manage personal responsibilities. The company also supports well-being through mental\nhealth resources like Talkspace and EAP services, along with PTO and flexible scheduling.\n\n**Comprehensive benefits and whole-person support: **Achieve\u2019s benefits are designed to support\nphysical, emotional, and financial well-being. Offerings include medical, dental, and vision\ncoverage; 401(k) matching (50% up to $5,000); tuition reimbursement up to $5,250 per year; parental\nleave; paid volunteer hours; and additional perks like pet discounts and legal assistance. Benefits\nsuch as flexible time off, childcare support via Mirza, and wellness resources reinforce a\nwhole-person approach to employee care.\n\n**Recognition, leadership, and connection: **Achieve promotes engagement through peer recognition,\nopen feedback, and transparent leadership. Programs like the Peer Recognition Program encourage\nemployees to celebrate contributions, while leadership emphasizes accessibility, coaching, and\nwork-life balance. Employees note that leadership is open, supportive, and encourages setting\nboundaries, contributing to a positive work environment.\n\n**Community impact and giving back: **Achieve extends its mission beyond the workplace through\nphilanthropy and community engagement. The company has distributed over $400,000 in nonprofit\ngrants, provided $100,000 in employee family support funds, and supported more than 40 charities.\nEmployees also receive paid volunteer hours, reinforcing a culture of service and community impact.\n\n**Employer strength and stability: **Achieve combines strong financial performance with continued\ninvestment in employees. The company achieved record growth and profitability in 2025, serves more\nthan 2 million members, and has helped resolve over $20 billion in debt. It continues to expand\nhiring across key areas like sales, customer service, AI, and analytics while investing in employee\ndevelopment. External recognition includes awards for customer satisfaction and workplace\nexcellence.\n\n**Bottom line: **Achieve supports job satisfaction by combining strong career growth opportunities,\nmeaningful mission-driven work, an inclusive and supportive culture, flexible work options, and\ncomprehensive benefits\u2014creating an environment where employees can grow, feel valued, and make a\nreal impact.\n\n## Is Achieve a good place to work? Do Employees Recommend it?\n\nWillingness to Recommend\n\nAchieve is generally positioned as a strong place to work, especially for people who value career\ngrowth, purpose-driven work, supportive teams, flexibility, and the stability of a growing financial\nservices company.\n\n**Why employees recommend it: **Employees frequently highlight Achieve\u2019s mission-driven work, strong\nsense of teamwork, and supportive culture. One employee shared, \u201cIt makes my soul feel whole\u2026 I had\na hand in changing someone\u2019s life,\u201d while another emphasized transparent leadership and\nencouragement of work-life balance and boundaries. Others point to strong camaraderie and passion\nfor the mission, describing teams as collaborative and deeply committed to helping customers\nsucceed.\n\n**Growth and career opportunity: **Achieve is known for rapid internal mobility and long-term career\ndevelopment. Employees often experience promotions in as little as three months, and about 30% of\nroles are filled internally. The company supports growth through structured programs like Career\nPathing, leadership development models, mentorship, and training. Employee stories highlight career\nprogression from entry-level roles into leadership positions, as well as cross-functional movement\nand long-term tenure.\n\n**Benefits, well-being, and flexibility: **Achieve supports employees with comprehensive,\nwhole-person benefits and flexible work options. Offerings include medical, dental, and vision\ncoverage; 401(k) match (50% up to $5,000); tuition reimbursement up to $5,250 annually; parental\nleave; mental health support through Talkspace and EAP; and paid volunteer hours. Employees also\nbenefit from remote and hybrid work options, flexible time off, and policies designed to support\nwork-life balance and well-being.\n\n**Purpose-driven and empathetic culture: **Achieve\u2019s culture is deeply tied to its mission of\nhelping people improve their financial futures. Employees describe their work as meaningful and\nemotionally impactful, reinforced by the company\u2019s \u201cheart and dollar\u201d philosophy\u2014balancing empathy\nwith business outcomes. Teams are encouraged to lead with compassion, listen to customers, and make\na real difference in people\u2019s lives.** **\n\n**Inclusive culture and belonging: **Achieve fosters a culture where employees feel supported and\nincluded through its core values\u2014Care, Get better, Collaborate, and Act with integrity\u2014and its\nEmployee Resource Groups. These groups create opportunities for connection, development, and\nrepresentation across diverse communities, contributing to a strong sense of belonging. Employees\noften highlight supportive peers and leadership as key strengths of the workplace.\n\n**Stability, growth, and reputation: **Achieve combines strong business performance with continued\ninvestment in employees. The company achieved record growth and profitability, serves more than 2\nmillion members, and continues expanding hiring across areas like sales, customer service, AI, and\nanalytics. It has also earned recognition for customer satisfaction and as a top workplace,\nreinforcing its reputation as both a trusted financial partner and employer.\n\n**Bottom line: **Achieve is widely recommended by employees who value fast career growth, meaningful\nmission-driven work, supportive teams, flexible work options, and strong benefits\u2014though, like most\ncompanies, individual experiences may vary depending on role, team, and manager.\n\n## What reputation does Achieve have as a place to work?\n\nGeneral Market Perception\n\nAchieve is widely viewed as a purpose-driven, growth-oriented employer with a strong culture of\nempathy, internal mobility, and employee support, particularly appealing to those who want\nmeaningful work and career advancement in a stable, growing company.\n\n**A mission-driven and impactful workplace: **Achieve has built a reputation around helping everyday\npeople improve their financial futures, and that mission strongly shapes employee experience.\nEmployees frequently describe their work as meaningful and emotionally impactful, with a focus on\nreal-life outcomes for customers. The company\u2019s \u201cheart and dollar\u201d philosophy\u2014balancing empathy with\nbusiness results\u2014reinforces its identity as a human-centered organization.\n\n**A strong reputation for career growth and internal mobility: **Achieve is recognized for offering\nclear pathways for advancement and investing in employee development. With promotions often\noccurring within three months and about 30% of roles filled internally, the company is seen as a\nplace where employees can build long-term careers. Development is supported through structured\nprograms like Career Pathing, leadership frameworks, mentorship, and ongoing training. Long-tenured\nemployee stories further reinforce this reputation for upward mobility.\n\n**An empathetic and people-first culture: **Achieve is known for a culture rooted in empathy,\ncompassion, and human connection. Employees and leaders emphasize listening to customers, supporting\nteammates, and creating a workplace where people feel valued and understood. Hiring practices also\nprioritize empathy alongside skill, reinforcing this reputation across the organization.\n\n**A collaborative and inclusive environment: **Achieve fosters a sense of belonging through its core\nvalues\u2014Care, Get better, Collaborate, and Act with integrity\u2014and its Employee Resource Groups.\nEmployees highlight strong teamwork, open communication, and supportive leadership as key parts of\nthe experience. The workplace is often described as one where ideas are welcomed and employees feel\nseen and heard.\n\n**A flexible and supportive workplace: **Achieve has a reputation for supporting different work\nstyles through remote, hybrid, and in-office options. Employees note the benefits of flexibility,\nincluding improved work-life balance and the ability to tailor their work environment. The company\nalso provides mental health resources, wellness support, and benefits designed to support employees\nholistically.\n\n**A stable, growing, and recognized employer: **Achieve is seen as a financially stable and\nexpanding company, having achieved record growth and profitability while continuing to invest in\ninnovation and hiring. It serves more than 2 million members and has resolved over $20 billion in\ndebt. The company has also received external re"
