            "url": "https://builtin.com/company/adyen/faq/workplace-perception",
            "text": "[[Built In Logo] [Built In Logo]][1][Companies][2][Jobs][3][Articles][4]\n[View All Jobs][5]\n[ Join ][6]\n[ Log In ][7]\n[ For Employers ][8]\n[ Companies ][9] [ Adyen ][10]\n\n## Adyen\n\nSave Saved\nAmsterdam\nTotal Offices: **16**\n4,771 Total Employees\nYear Founded: 2006\n[View Website][11]\nWe're Hiring!\n[ Engineering **48** ][12] [ Customer Success & Experience **29** ][13] [ Operations & Support\n**19** ][14] [ Sales **19** ][15] [ Finance **16** ][16] [ Marketing **13** ][17] [ Product\nManagement **12** ][18] [ HR & Recruiting **11** ][19] [ Legal **9** ][20] [ Consulting **6** ][21]\n[ AI & Machine Learning **6** ][22] [ Program & Project Management **4** ][23] [ Cybersecurity **3**\n][24] [ Data & Analytics **3** ][25] [ Design **2** ][26]\n[View all jobs][27]\n* Overview\n* Jobs 200\n* Offices\n* Teams\n* Culture\n* Articles\n* Company Insights\n* [ Working at Adyen ][28]\n* [ Culture & Values ][29]\n* [ Inclusion & Diversity ][30]\n* [ Career Growth & Development ][31]\n* [ Compensation & Benefits ][32]\n* [ Work-Life Balance & Wellbeing ][33]\n* [ Leadership & Management ][34]\n* [ Innovation, Technology & Agility ][35]\n* [ Mission, Purpose & Impact ][36]\n* [ Stability & Growth ][37]\n\n# What's It Like to Work at Adyen?\n\nUpdated on June 03, 2026\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n## What practices at Adyen support employee job satisfaction?\n\nJob Satisfaction\n\nAdyen supports employee job satisfaction through high ownership, meaningful global work, strong\ncareer growth opportunities, and flexible employee support.\n* **Ownership and autonomy**: Adyen\u2019s culture is built around the Adyen Formula, which encourages\nemployees to \u201ccreate our own path,\u201d launch quickly, and make long-term decisions. Employees are\ntrusted to take initiative, solve problems directly, and work with significant autonomy across\nteams and regions.\n* **Meaningful, large-scale work: **Employees help build and scale Adyen\u2019s in-house financial\ntechnology platform used by major global brands. Teams work on payments, embedded finance,\nAI-driven commerce, and enterprise infrastructure powering \u20ac970.1 billion in processed volume in\n2023.\n* **Collaborative engineering culture:** Adyen emphasizes teamwork over ego and encourages direct\ncommunication across offices and time zones. The company\u2019s Global AI Hackathon brought together\n200+ employees across 60+ teams to rapidly prototype AI-powered merchant and internal solutions.\n* **Career growth and cross-functional exposure:** Employees are encouraged to grow beyond narrow\njob scopes. Engineers regularly collaborate with product managers, account managers, support\nteams, and pricing analysts to build broader business understanding and skills.\n* **Flexible benefits and wellbeing support:** Employees receive healthcare, mental health benefits,\nparental leave, flexible and unlimited PTO, wellness programs, and Adyen+, a monthly contribution\nemployees can use for a number of things including but not limited to childcare, wellness,\nwork-from-home setups, or personal interests.\n* **Focus and productivity culture:** Employees describe workplace culture that supports focus time,\npersonalized workflows, and productivity routines, with employees encouraged to block calendar\ntime for deep work and minimize interruptions.\n\nOverall, Adyen supports job satisfaction by combining ownership, global impact, collaboration,\ngrowth opportunities, and flexible employee support in a fast-paced fintech environment.\n\n## Is Adyen a good place to work? Do Employees Recommend it?\n\nWillingness to Recommend\n\nAdyen is generally viewed as a strong place to work for ambitious employees who enjoy ownership,\nfast-paced learning, and global collaboration.\n* **Strong ownership culture: **Employees are trusted with meaningful responsibility. Employees\ndescribe quickly gaining ownership, solving real business problems, and shaping their own career\npaths with support from leaders and teammates.\n* **Career growth opportunities: **Employees frequently highlight opportunities for development\nthrough mentorship, cross-functional work, certifications, conferences, Lunch and Learns, and\ninternal mobility programs.\n* **Collaborative and supportive teams:** Current employees emphasize approachable leadership,\ntransparent feedback, and collaborative environments where employees are encouraged to speak up\nand contribute ideas regardless of title.\n* **Innovation-focused environment:** Adyen has a strong engineering-first culture centered on\nexperimentation and long-term problem solving. Employees work on AI, payments, unified commerce,\nand enterprise-scale infrastructure challenges that impact global businesses.\n* **Strong benefits and flexibility:** Employees receive flexible and unlimited PTO, wellness\nprograms, volunteer opportunities, parental leave, hybrid work flexibility, and Adyen+, which\nallows employees to personalize benefits around their own needs and priorities.\n\nOverall, Adyen is considered a strong fit for employees looking for ownership, growth,\ncollaboration, and meaningful work in global fintech.\n\n## What reputation does Adyen have as a place to work?\n\nGeneral Market Perception\n\nAdyen has a reputation as an innovative, engineering-first fintech company known for high standards,\nownership culture, and global impact.\n* **Known for technical excellence and innovation: **Adyen is recognized for building its payments\nplatform in-house with a \u201csingle platform, one integration\u201d model that supports enterprise\nbusinesses globally. The company was named a Leader in The Forrester Wave\u2122: Merchant Payment\nProviders, Q1 2026, receiving top scores across innovation, analytics, architecture, fraud\nmanagement, and real-time payments.\n* **High-ownership, fast-moving culture:** Adyen\u2019s reputation is closely tied to the Adyen Formula,\nwhich emphasizes autonomy, direct communication, long-term thinking, and teamwork over ego.\nEmployees are expected to move quickly, solve problems proactively, and contribute beyond narrow\njob scopes.\n* **Global and collaborative workplace: **With more than 4,000 employees representing 115+\nnationalities across 28 offices, Adyen is known for strong international collaboration across\nteams, regions, and time zones.\n* **Commitment to employee growth and inclusion:** Current employees highlight supportive managers,\nmentorship, cross-functional learning, and inclusive communities supported through ERGs and DEI\ninitiatives.\n\nOverall, Adyen is regarded as a globally respected fintech employer where employees can work on\nlarge-scale technology challenges while operating in a collaborative, ownership-driven environment.\n\n## What tradeoffs might come with working at Adyen?\n\nTradeoffs\n\nOne key tradeoff is autonomy and ownership vs. highly structured guidance. Employees are trusted to\nmove quickly, make decisions independently, and create their own growth paths. This environment\ntends to work best for proactive, self-directed people who are comfortable operating with high\naccountability.\n\nEmployees may also experience execution-first culture vs. slower, more measured environments. Adyen\nvalues speed, direct communication, and rapid iteration, which creates strong momentum and visible\nimpact, though work can become intense during key launches or growth periods.\n\nThere is also a tradeoff between lean, high-ownership teams vs. narrowly scoped roles. Employees\noften collaborate across functions and take on broad responsibilities, creating faster learning and\nstronger visibility, though expectations can expand quickly.\n\nFinally, Adyen emphasizes a strong in-person office culture vs. fully remote flexibility. The\ncompany believes office collaboration strengthens teamwork and communication, while still allowing\nflexibility when needed. A minimum of three days a week in office is the norm for most roles.\n\n**Great match for candidates who prefer:**\n* High ownership and autonomy\n* Fast-paced, execution-oriented environments\n* Cross-functional collaboration\n* Building innovative, globally scaled technology\n* Direct communication and accountability\n\n**Working here means:**\n* Moving quickly and adapting to change\n* Collaborating across global teams and functions\n* Taking ownership of meaningful work\n* Operating with high standards and visibility\n* Helping shape the future of commerce and payments\n\n## Adyen's Candidate Tradeoffs\n\n**If you\u2019re weighing whether Adyen is the right fit, these are the core tradeoffs to consider.**\n* Adyen emphasizes minimal micromanagement and high trust, giving employees space to make decisions\nand move quickly, though that model favors self-directed, intrinsically motivated contributors.\n\n## Adyen Employee Perspectives\n\nWorkplace perception at Adyen is shaped by a long-term mindset and a culture built around high\nstandards, autonomy and speed. Employees are surrounded by ambitious, high-performing teammates and\nempowered to make an impact quickly, creating an environment that feels both fast-moving and deeply\nintentional.\n\n\u201cWe are not led by short-term trends, and hire specifically to meet our long-term needs. To scale\nour culture of speed and autonomy as we grow, we keep our talent standards high and only hire\nexceptional people that quickly gain traction.\u201d\n\n[Pieter van der Does]\nPieter van der Does, Co-Founder and CEO\nFrom the article: [Careers | Ambitious? So Are We][38]\n\n## Adyen Employee Reviews\n\nI always feel encouraged to speak up, ask questions, and share a solution. I am not restricted to\njust sit in front of a screen and program; I interact with product managers, account managers, tech\nsupport, and pricing analysts to the point where I can put myself in their shoes and understand\ntheir perspectives and issues as well.\n\n[Bhumika]\nBhumika, Senior Software Engineer\nBhumika, Senior Software Engineer\n\nThe best thing about working at Adyen is the people. I think this is through a combination of\nprioritizing hiring smart, capable people, but also through creating and supporting a culture where\nthose people are given the trust and flexibility to do their best work, and genuinely encouraging\nthose people to connect.\n\n[Blaine]\nBlaine, Team Lead, Software Engineering\nBlaine, Team Lead, Software Engineering\n\nPeople genuinely make time for you, even across time zones. Many little things make Adyen special,\nfrom team-building trips/events to knowledge-sharing sessions. It's a place where you can do\nmeaningful work, learn from amazing people, and still have room to breathe.\n\n[Ayesha]\nAyesha, Data Engineer\nAyesha, Data Engineer\n\nThis role has pushed me to grow both as a leader and as an engineer. Professionally, I\u2019ve expanded\nmy skills in strategic thinking, team management, and cross-functional collaboration, while staying\nhands-on with development.\n\n[Tulasi]\nTulasi, Team Lead, Software Engineering\nTulasi, Team Lead, Software Engineering\n\nWorking at Adyen has pushed me to grow both professionally and personally. The pace and critical\nthinking here have challenged me to develop sharper judgment, prioritize better, and become more\nconfident in my decision-making. As a team lead, it's been rewarding to help shape and scale the\norg.\n\n[Robbie]\nRobbie, MPL & Credit Risk Team Lead\nRobbie, MPL & Credit Risk Team Lead\n\nWhat sets Adyen apart is how tangible the company values are; they are not just words on a wall, but\nhow we operate daily. We truly build trust by empowering every team member to make good choices and\ncreate their own path.\n\n[Suzanne]\nSuzanne, Product Manager\nSuzanne, Product Manager\n\nThere are so many talented engineers here with a true passion for development, and there are plenty\nof opportunities to learn from them. I\u2019ve learned from the engineers in Chicago, but also from those\nI've met in Amsterdam and from all over the world.\n\n[Katie]\nKatie, Software Engineer\nKatie, Software Engineer\n\nAdyen is one of the more diverse companies I\u2019ve worked for. There are so many different backgrounds,\ncultures, and experiences amongst the teams. I truly feel like I can \u201cbring my full self\u201d to work.\nWithin my own te"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://builtin.com/company/amalgamated-sugar/faq/workplace-perception",
            "text": "[[Built In Logo] [Built In Logo]][1][Companies][2][Jobs][3][Articles][4]\n[View All Jobs][5]\n[ Join ][6]\n[ Log In ][7]\n[ For Employers ][8]\n[ Companies ][9] [ Amalgamated Sugar ][10]\n\n## Amalgamated Sugar\n\nSave Saved\nBoise\nTotal Offices: **4**\n768 Total Employees\nYear Founded: 1897\n[View Website][11]\nWe're Hiring!\n[ Engineering **5** ][12] [ Data & Analytics **1** ][13] [ Finance **1** ][14] [ Operations &\nSupport **1** ][15] [ Supply Chain & Procurement **1** ][16]\n[View all jobs][17]\n* Overview\n* Jobs 17\n* Offices\n* Articles\n* Company Insights\n* [ Working at Amalgamated Sugar ][18]\n* [ Culture & Values ][19]\n* [ Career Growth & Development ][20]\n* [ Compensation & Benefits ][21]\n* [ Work-Life Balance & Wellbeing ][22]\n* [ Leadership & Management ][23]\n* [ Innovation, Technology & Agility ][24]\n* [ Mission, Purpose & Impact ][25]\n* [ Stability & Growth ][26]\n\n# What's It Like to Work at Amalgamated Sugar?\n\nUpdated on June 11, 2026\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n## What practices at Amalgamated Sugar support employee job satisfaction?\n\nJob Satisfaction\n\nAmalgamated Sugar supports employee job satisfaction through meaningful work connected to the food\nsupply chain, long-term career development, employee recognition, strong retirement and healthcare\nbenefits, performance-based rewards, and a culture built on teamwork, accountability, and community\nstewardship.\n* **Purpose-driven work with visible impact: **Amalgamated Sugar employees help produce a product\nused by consumers across the country while supporting grower-owners throughout the Pacific\nNorthwest. The company\u2019s vision is to enhance the enjoyment and function of food by producing real\nsugar in a technologically advanced and socially responsible manner, giving employees a direct\nconnection between their work and the products people use every day.\n* **Career development built for long-term growth: **Amalgamated Sugar encourages employees to build\nlong-term careers through hands-on training, mentorship, regular feedback, recognition, on-the-job\nlearning, performance reviews, and mid-year check-ins. Employees are encouraged to explore\ninternal opportunities, develop new skills, and pursue leadership opportunities as they grow\nwithin the organization. The company also offers a Professional Development Assistance Program\nthat reimburses approved courses and programs to help employees advance their education and\ncareers.\n* **Recognition and employee involvement: **Employee contributions are celebrated through Employee\nSpotlights that recognize individuals and teams who demonstrate company values, commitment,\nexcellence, milestone achievements, and years of service. Employee Committees at each location\nprovide opportunities for employees to share feedback, collaborate with leadership, and help shape\nworkplace engagement initiatives.\n* **Benefits designed to support employees and families: **Amalgamated Sugar offers comprehensive\nmedical, dental, vision, disability, life insurance, and wellness benefits, along with an Employee\nAssistance Program that provides confidential counseling, financial consultations, legal guidance,\nand childcare and eldercare referrals. Employees also receive paid holidays, vacation time, sick\nleave, parental leave, and identity protection benefits.\n* **Retirement and financial wellness support: **The company offers one of its strongest\ndifferentiators through its retirement program. Amalgamated Sugar matches 100% of the first 3%\nemployees contribute to their 401(k); 50% of the next 3%; and contributes an additional fixed 4%\nof eligible compensation each pay period. Eligible employees also participate in a Short-Term\nIncentive (STI) program that rewards both individual performance and company success.\n* **Culture rooted in teamwork and accountability: **Amalgamated Sugar\u2019s culture is built on\nteamwork, accountability, pride in a job well done, employee well-being, and doing business the\nright way. As a grower-owned company, it emphasizes supporting local agriculture, operating\nresponsibly, and being a good steward of its communities and land.\n* **External signals:**\n* **Employee recommendation rate:** Employees on external review sites report generally positive\nexperiences, with approximately 73% of employees saying they would recommend Amalgamated Sugar\nto a friend. (Glassdoor)\n* **Positive candidate experience:** Approximately 80% of job candidates report a positive\ninterview experience with the company. (Glassdoor)\n* **Commonly cited strengths:** Employee reviews frequently highlight job stability, strong\nbenefits, retirement contributions, advancement opportunities, educational support, and the\ncompany\u2019s long-term presence in the agricultural and food manufacturing industries. (Glassdoor;\nIndeed)\n\n**Bottom line: **Amalgamated Sugar supports job satisfaction by combining meaningful work, career\ndevelopment opportunities, employee recognition, strong retirement and healthcare benefits,\nperformance-based rewards, and a culture centered on teamwork, accountability, and long-term\nsuccess.\n\n## Is Amalgamated Sugar a good place to work? Do Employees Recommend it?\n\nWillingness to Recommend\n\nYes. Amalgamated Sugar is often viewed positively by employees who value stability, strong benefits,\nmeaningful work, career growth opportunities, and the chance to contribute to a company that plays\nan important role in food production and agriculture.\n* **Long-term stability and purpose-driven work: **As one of the largest beet sugar producers in\nNorth America, Amalgamated Sugar combines more than a century of history with a mission centered\non supporting agriculture, producing high-quality sugar, and serving customers across the United\nStates. Employees contribute to an industry that is essential to the food supply chain while\nworking for a grower-owned organization with deep agricultural roots.\n* **Investment in employee growth: **Employees are supported through hands-on training, mentorship,\nregular feedback, on-the-job learning, performance reviews, mid-year check-ins, and internal\ncareer opportunities. The company also provides Professional Development Assistance to help\nemployees pursue additional education and skill development that supports long-term career growth.\n* **Recognition, engagement, and employee voice: **Amalgamated Sugar recognizes employees through\nEmployee Spotlights, service milestone recognition, and programs that celebrate contributions\nacross the organization. Employee Committees help strengthen communication between employees and\nleadership while supporting workplace engagement and culture initiatives.\n* **Strong benefits and financial security: **The company offers comprehensive healthcare coverage,\nretirement benefits, paid time off, parental leave, disability coverage, life insurance, wellness\nresources, and an Employee Assistance Program. The retirement program includes both a generous\ncompany match and an additional employer contribution, helping employees build long-term financial\nsecurity. Eligible employees can also participate in a performance-based Short-Term Incentive\nprogram.\n* **Culture built around teamwork and community: **Amalgamated Sugar emphasizes teamwork,\naccountability, respect, pride in workmanship, and community stewardship. The company\u2019s success is\ndriven by employees who take pride in their work and contribute to a culture where people feel\nsupported and respected.\n* **External signals:**\n* **Recommendation rate:** Approximately 73% of employees on Glassdoor report that they would\nrecommend Amalgamated Sugar to a friend. (Glassdoor)\n* **Positive interview experience:** Approximately 80% of candidates report a positive interview\nexperience. (Glassdoor)\n* **Frequently mentioned strengths:** Employee reviews commonly cite benefits, retirement\ncontributions, compensation, job security, advancement opportunities, and the company\u2019s\nsupportive environment as reasons they enjoy working at Amalgamated Sugar. (Glassdoor; Indeed)\n* **Stable industry position:** Employees benefit from working in a company tied to an essential\nindustry with longstanding relationships across agriculture, food production, and regional\ncommunities. (Amalgamated Sugar Website)\n\n**Bottom line: **Many employees recommend Amalgamated Sugar because it combines meaningful work,\nlong-term stability, career development opportunities, strong benefits, retirement support, employee\nrecognition, and a culture that values teamwork, accountability, and community impact.\n\n## Amalgamated Sugar's Candidate Tradeoffs\n\n**If you\u2019re weighing whether Amalgamated Sugar is the right fit, these are the core tradeoffs to\nconsider.**\n* Amalgamated Sugar emphasizes accessible, engaged managers who provide regular support and\nalignment, though that often includes more frequent check-ins and active collaboration.\n\n## Amalgamated Sugar Employee Perspectives\n\nAmalgamated Sugar offers employees the opportunity to work on complex, hands-on challenges in an\nenvironment where no two days are exactly alike. Employees describe the work as rewarding and\nengaging, with a strong sense of teamwork and shared purpose as they collaborate to solve problems\nand support the company\u2019s success.\n\n\u201cWorking at Amalgamated Sugar has been an incredible journey over the past 16 years. Starting as a\nLab Manager and growing through roles like Process Engineer and Assistant Plant Manager to now\nleading as Plant Manager, I\u2019ve found immense fulfillment in tackling the unique challenges of sugar\nprocessing. Every day brings a new problem to solve as we work with a dynamic, deteriorating crop,\nand that constant variability keeps the work exciting and rewarding. What makes it even more special\nis collaborating with like-minded, hardworking colleagues who share the same passion for overcoming\nchallenges and driving success together.\u201d\n\n[Trent Holcomb]\nTrent Holcomb, Plant Manager, Nampa\nFrom the article: [Careers][27]\n\nAmalgamated Sugar offers employees a dynamic work environment where new challenges and opportunities\nto learn are part of everyday life. Employees take pride in contributing to a company with a long\nhistory and strong reputation while working alongside supportive and dedicated teammates.\n\n\u201cI enjoy working at Amalgamated Sugar because I am never bored\u2014every project is different and poses\nnew challenges. I am proud to work at a Company with such a rich history and strong reputation. It\ndoesn\u2019t hurt that our people are great to work with as well!\u201d\n\n[Kaleb Churchman]\nKaleb Churchman, Project Engineer \u2013 Mechanical\nFrom the article: [Careers][28]\n\nAmalgamated Sugar offers employees the opportunity to build meaningful careers while contributing to\na company deeply connected to the communities it serves. Employees highlight the company\u2019s\nsupportive culture, commitment to work-life balance, strong benefits and investment in professional\ngrowth as key reasons they enjoy working there.\n\n\u201cExperts say that when you enjoy work you lead a happier life. Amalgamated Sugar makes enjoying work\na reality. Because the Company is owned by local family farmers, the Company supports its local\ncommunities and is genuinely committed to investing in its employees by emphasizing a healthy\nwork-life balance, providing excellent benefits, and providing abundant opportunities for career\nadvancement and development.\u201d\n\n[Christina Morrow]\nChristina Morrow, Senior Paralegal\nFrom the article: [Careers][29]\n\n## What People Are Saying About Amalgamated Sugar\n* Benefits & Perks: Benefits are described as comprehensive, including medical/dental/vision\ncoverage, retirement with match, paid time off, tuition assistance, and in some hourly groups\nzero\u2011premium health insurance under a current agreement. These offerings are often cited as a\nmeaningful part of total compensation in factory roles.\n* Market Position & Stability: As a large, grower\u2011owned beet\u2011sugar processor with long\u2011term, locally\nrooted operations, the company emphasizes steady demand for production, maintenance, and tech"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://builtin.com/company/applied-systems/faq/workplace-perception",
            "text": "[[Built In Logo] [Built In Logo]][1][Companies][2][Jobs][3][Articles][4]\n[View All Jobs][5]\n[ Join ][6]\n[ Log In ][7]\n[ For Employers ][8]\n[ Companies ][9] [ Applied Systems ][10]\n[Applied \"A\" Logo]\n\n## Applied Systems\n\nSave Saved\nChicago\nTotal Offices: **12**\n3,079 Total Employees\n1,310 Product + Tech Employees\nYear Founded: 1983\n[View Website][11]\n[Applied \"A\" Logo]\nWe're Hiring!\n[ Engineering **19** ][12] [ Customer Success & Experience **13** ][13] [ Sales **9** ][14] [\nOperations & Support **6** ][15] [ Finance **4** ][16] [ Data & Analytics **3** ][17] [ AI & Machine\nLearning **3** ][18] [ Design **3** ][19] [ HR & Recruiting **2** ][20] [ Marketing **2** ][21] [\nProduct Management **2** ][22] [ Program & Project Management **2** ][23] [ Cybersecurity **1**\n][24]\n[View all jobs][25]\n* Overview\n* Jobs 70\n* Offices\n* Teams\n* Culture\n* Articles\n* Company Insights\n* [ Working at Applied Systems ][26]\n* [ Culture & Values ][27]\n* [ Inclusion & Diversity ][28]\n* [ Career Growth & Development ][29]\n* [ Compensation & Benefits ][30]\n* [ Work-Life Balance & Wellbeing ][31]\n* [ Leadership & Management ][32]\n* [ Innovation, Technology & Agility ][33]\n* [ Stability & Growth ][34]\n\n# What's It Like to Work at Applied Systems?\n\nUpdated on May 20, 2026\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n## What practices at Applied Systems support employee job satisfaction?\n\nJob Satisfaction\n\nApplied Systems supports employee job satisfaction through mission-driven work, career mobility,\nflexibility, innovation opportunities, inclusive culture, and comprehensive employee benefits. The\ncompany employs more than 3,000 teammates globally, supports 339,000+ daily software users, and\npositions employees at the center of insurance industry transformation through cloud software, AI,\nand digital workflows.\n\n**Career growth and learning: **Applied emphasizes internal mobility and long-term development,\nreporting that 1 in 5 teammates advances into a new role annually while average teammate tenure is\n7.3 years. Employees have access to mentorship, leadership development, tuition reimbursement,\nconferences, technical certifications, on-demand learning, and customized career tracks. The company\nalso promotes employee-driven learning through hackathons, cross-functional collaboration, and\ninternal mobility opportunities across technology, product, customer success, operations, and sales\nteams.\n\n**Innovation and ownership: **Applied positions itself as the #1 investor in insurance industry R&D\nand encourages employees to shape customer-facing innovation. During Applied\u2019s annual Innovation\nHackathon, employees developed a GPT-4-powered email summarization assistant inside Applied Epic\nthat reportedly reached 2.29 million uses with 70% month-over-month retention after launch. The\ncompany emphasizes experimentation, rapid iteration, and giving employees opportunities to\ncontribute ideas regardless of level or tenure.\n\n**Flexible work environment: **Applied\u2019s \u201cWork Reimagined\u201d model supports remote, hybrid, and\nin-office work arrangements depending on where employees perform best. The company combines\nflexibility with wellbeing support through wellness incentives, mental health benefits, wellness\ndays, flexible scheduling, and paid volunteer time off.\n\n**Comprehensive benefits: **Benefits include Day 1 medical, dental, and vision coverage, 401(k) and\nRRSP matching, six weeks of paid parental leave, fertility benefits, transgender healthcare\ncoverage, mental health support, PTO, birthday leave, floating holidays, disability coverage, and\nfinancial wellness resources.\n\n**Collaborative and inclusive culture: **Applied promotes \u201cThe Applied Vibe\u201d as a culture of smart,\nhumble, hard-working teammates solving industry challenges together. The company supports belonging\nthrough Communities of Interest including Pride at Applied, Women in Technology, Veterans of\nApplied, Black at Applied, and IndispensAbility. Applied also reports more than 3,800 volunteer\nhours and support for 62 nonprofits through Applied Cares community initiatives.\n\n**External signals: **External employee reviews frequently highlight flexibility, collaborative\nteams, approachable leadership, strong benefits, career growth, and meaningful work. Employees on\nComparably rated CEO Taylor Rhodes and Applied leadership an \u201cA-,\u201d placing the company in the Top\n15% of employers with 1,001\u20135,000 employees.\n\n## Is Applied Systems a good place to work? Do Employees Recommend it?\n\nWillingness to Recommend\n\nApplied Systems is generally viewed as a strong employer for employees seeking flexibility,\nsupportive teams, career growth, and opportunities to work on large-scale insurance technology\nproducts. The company combines the scale of an established insurtech leader with a culture\nemphasizing innovation, employee development, and collaboration.\n\n**Strong employee reputation: **Employees on Comparably rated CEO Taylor Rhodes and Applied\nleadership an \u201cA-,\u201d placing Applied in the Top 15% of similarly sized employers. Employee feedback\nfrequently references supportive managers, collaborative teammates, flexibility, and opportunities\nfor advancement.\n\n**Career growth and advancement opportunities:** Applied emphasizes long-term career mobility,\nreporting that 1 in 5 teammates moves into a new role annually while average employee tenure is 7.3\nyears. Employees also gain exposure to AI, cloud software, analytics, workflow automation,\ncybersecurity, and digital transformation initiatives across the business.\n\n**Innovation-focused employee experience: **Employees have opportunities to contribute directly to\ncustomer-facing innovation through Applied\u2019s Hackathon program and product experimentation culture.\nThe company highlights that employee-developed AI tools inside Applied Epic moved rapidly from\nprototype to production and achieved millions of customer uses.\n\n**Flexible and people-first workplace: **Applied promotes remote and hybrid work flexibility through\nits \u201cWork Reimagined\u201d approach while supporting employee wellbeing through wellness incentives,\nmental health support, parental leave, flexible schedules, volunteer time off, and ongoing learning\nresources.\n\n**Inclusive culture and belonging: **Applied invests in employee-led Communities of Interest\nsupporting LGBTQIA+, veterans, women in technology, Black employees, and employees with\ndisabilities. Employees frequently describe the company as welcoming, collaborative, and supportive\nof authentic self-expression and career growth.\n\n**External signals:** External reviews commonly highlight work-life balance, collaborative culture,\nsupportive leadership, flexibility, and strong benefits as reasons employees recommend Applied.\nEmployees also frequently point to the company\u2019s stability, long tenure, and opportunities to work\non meaningful technology products used across the insurance industry.\n\n## What reputation does Applied Systems have as a place to work?\n\nGeneral Market Perception\n\nApplied Systems has built a reputation as a leading insurtech employer known for innovation,\nemployee development, flexibility, and collaborative culture. The company positions itself as a\ntechnology leader modernizing insurance through cloud software, AI, analytics, and digital customer\nexperiences.\n\n**Insurance technology leadership: **Applied supports more than 339,000 daily software users across\nseven countries and states that seven of the top 10 insurance agencies use Applied Epic and Digital\nAgency technology. The company has more than 40 years in business and employs 3,000+ teammates\nglobally.\n\n**Innovation and AI reputation: **Applied is recognized for innovation in AI, workflow automation,\ncloud software, and customer experience technology within insurance. The company\u2019s Innovation\nHackathon and experimentation culture reinforce its reputation as a workplace where employees can\nshape product direction and rapidly bring new ideas to market.\n\n**Strong career growth culture: **Employees and external workplace profiles frequently cite\nmentorship, internal mobility, leadership accessibility, certifications, and long-term career\ndevelopment as key strengths. Applied reports that 1 in 5 teammates advances roles annually while\naverage employee tenure is 7.3 years, reinforcing the company\u2019s reputation for long-term career\nopportunity.\n\n**Collaborative and people-centered culture: **Applied promotes \u201cThe Applied Vibe\u201d as a workplace\nculture built around humility, teamwork, transparency, accountability, and customer focus. Employees\nfrequently describe collaborative teams, approachable leaders, and strong cross-functional support\nsystems.\n\n**Inclusive workplace reputation: **Applied supports belonging through Communities of Interest\nfocused on LGBTQIA+ employees, veterans, women in technology, Black employees, and employees with\ndisabilities. The company also ties inclusion efforts to broader community engagement, reporting\nmore than 3,800 volunteer hours and support for 62 nonprofits through Applied Cares initiatives.\n\n**External signals: **Applied\u2019s external employer reputation is reinforced by employee reviews\nhighlighting flexibility, supportive culture, meaningful work, leadership accessibility, career\nadvancement opportunities, and strong work-life balance within a stable and established insurtech\ncompany.\n\n## Applied Systems's Candidate Tradeoffs\n\n**If you\u2019re weighing whether Applied Systems is the right fit, these are the core tradeoffs to\nconsider.**\n* Applied Systems emphasizes accessible, engaged managers who provide regular support and alignment,\nthough that often includes more frequent check-ins and active collaboration.\n\n## Applied Systems Employee Perspectives\n\nWorkplace perception at Applied Systems is shaped by a collaborative and energizing environment\nwhere employees feel both productive and supported in their growth. Teams work closely together to\nachieve meaningful results while creating a culture that encourages learning, connection and\nenjoyment in the day-to-day experience.\n\n\u201cAs a team, we\u2019ve gotten so much done. It\u2019s been productive, I\u2019ve learned so much and overall, it\nhas just been fun.\u201d\n\n[Heather Prince]\nHeather Prince, Senior Associate Product Manager\nFrom the article: [How the Right Culture, Resources and Team Can Grow an 18-Year Career at Applied\nSystems][35]\n\n## Applied Systems Employee Reviews\n\nThe great thing about this sales role is you don\u2019t work in a silo, you\u2019re reliant on the knowledge\nof others and work across all teams including Customer Success, Support, Services, Product and\nMarketing. My job is made easier due to Applied having a great suite of products that set us apart\nfrom our competitors.\n\n[Daragh Borelan]\nDaragh Borelan, Business Development Manager\nDaragh Borelan, Business Development Manager\n\n## What People Are Saying About Applied Systems\n* Work-Life Balance: Flexible \u201cWork Reimagined\u201d options\u2014remote, office, or hybrid\u2014enable people to\nchoose where they are most effective. Colleagues often point to workable balance supported by\ncollaborative teams.\n* Benefits & Perks: Day\u2011one coverage includes medical, dental, vision, PTO types such as volunteer\nand birthday time, parental leave, and a retirement match. This comprehensive package is presented\nas a core part of the employment offer.\n* Learning & Development: On\u2011demand and live learning with an emphasis on mobility and continuous\ngrowth provide clear upskilling pathways. Employee\u2011led communities and public profiles\nhighlighting career mobility reinforce development opportunities.\n\n## Applied Systems's Awards\n\n[award][award][award][award]\n[award][award][award][award][award][award]\n\n## Applied Systems's Benefits\n\n### Employee Satisfaction & Recognition\n\nCompany or teams have recognition rituals for individual work\n\nEmployee feedback used to shape policies and strategy\n\nEncourages autonomy and ownership from employees\n\nEstablished employee awards to honor work and contributions\n\nManagers give public shoutouts and celebrate employee milestones\n\nMan"
          },
