            "url": "https://builtin.com/company/block-inc/faq/workplace-perception",
            "text": "[[Built In Logo] [Built In Logo]][1][Companies][2][Jobs][3][Articles][4]\n[View All Jobs][5]\n[ Join ][6]\n[ Log In ][7]\n[ For Employers ][8]\n[ Companies ][9] [ Block ][10]\n\n## Block\n\nSave Saved\nOakland\nTotal Offices: **23**\n12,000 Total Employees\n8,000 Product + Tech Employees\nYear Founded: 2009\n[View Website][11]\nWe're Hiring!\n[ Sales **99+** ][12] [ Engineering **34** ][13] [ AI & Machine Learning **16** ][14] [ Customer\nSuccess & Experience **13** ][15] [ Marketing **6** ][16] [ Product Management **6** ][17] [\nCybersecurity **5** ][18] [ Design **5** ][19] [ Finance **3** ][20] [ Operations & Support **3**\n][21] [ Program & Project Management **3** ][22] [ Data & Analytics **2** ][23] [ HR & Recruiting\n**2** ][24] [ Legal **2** ][25]\n[View all jobs][26]\n* Overview\n* Jobs 203\n* Offices\n* Teams\n* Articles\n* Company Insights\n* [ Working at Block ][27]\n* [ Culture & Values ][28]\n* [ Career Growth & Development ][29]\n* [ Compensation & Benefits ][30]\n* [ Work-Life Balance & Wellbeing ][31]\n* [ Leadership & Management ][32]\n* [ Innovation, Technology & Agility ][33]\n* [ Stability & Growth ][34]\n\n# What's It Like to Work at Block?\n\n## Block Employee Perspectives\n\nBlock\u2019s open-source initiative aims to remove barriers to technology and promoting economic\nopportunities for all. The initiative emphasizes transparency, collaboration and shared progress,\nwith the goal of empowering both customers and the broader developer community.\n\n[Block]\nBlock,\nFrom the article: [Financial Services Provider Block Launches Open Source Offering][35]\n\nIt\u2019s very rare to work in a global, publicly-traded company that wants to invest in long-term big\nbets in a meaningful way.\n\n[Thomas Templeton]\nThomas Templeton, Proto Lead\nFrom the article: [Behind the Build: Self-Custody Solution Bitkey Offers Bitcoin Owners Greater\nSafety and Control][36]\n\nI\u2019ve always believed that economic empowerment is about leveling the playing field, providing tools\nto individuals and businesses to help them compete with people that are wealthier or people that\nhave more resources than them.\n\n[Brian Grassadonia]\nBrian Grassadonia, Ecosystem Lead\nFrom the article: [Why Block?][37]\n\nWe develop products in the open, inviting scrutiny early and often and welcoming input from external\ncommunities and within Block. This approach will help us build both better products and trust.\n\n[Thomas Templeton]\nThomas Templeton, Proto Lead\nFrom the article: [Behind the Build: Self-Custody Solution Bitkey Offers Bitcoin Owners Greater\nSafety and Control][38]\n\nSquare was built to give businesses more time, more power, and more possibility. That mission hasn\u2019t\nchanged, but the tools have. The future of commerce will be built by people who understand both AI\nand the humans it serves.\n\n[Block]\nBlock,\nFrom the article: [Calling All Future Product Builders][39]\n\nHere at Block, design is a little different than at many other companies in that we\u2019re all builders.\nIt\u2019s a builder mentality. We kind of say its button to billboard because design is responsible for\ncrafting the journey customers have with our brand and company and we want that journey to be a\ncoherent arc.\n\n[Brooke Ellis]\nBrooke Ellis, Design Lead\nFrom the article: [Build: To Make Something by Putting Parts Together][40]\n\nWe're building models that see how people actually earn, spend, save, and repay. We're proving that\ninclusive lending and responsible risk management go hand in hand.\n\n[Juan Hernandez]\nJuan Hernandez, Head of Credit and Underwriting\nFrom the article: [Block, Inc. Surpasses $200 Billion in Credit Provided to Customers, Continuing to\nAddress Global Lending Gaps][41]\n\nPeople need to make decisions for themselves. I want to build the technology so that people can make\nthose decisions and they don\u2019t have gatekeepers that are making decisions for them.\n\n[William Av\u00e9]\nWilliam Av\u00e9, Head of Product\nFrom the article: [Square\u2019s Product Chief on the Death of the Penny and the Future of Money][42]\n\nCreating the opportunity for everyone to participate in the economy is just core to who we are [here\nat Block].\n\n[Erin Neely Archuleta]\nErin Neely Archuleta, Head of Global External Affairs and Social Responsibility\nFrom the article: [Fostering Positive Social and Economic Impact with Erin Archuleta of Block][43]\n\n## Block Employee Reviews\n\nIn Compliance Engineering, we work across all product teams and have the space to really understand\nhow new features will improve the lives of customers. Since all data streams to us, we can design\nsystems that solve entire categories of problems, like visualizing money flow, cryptocurrencies, and\nstopping bad actors from causing harm.\n[Scott Maher]\nScott Maher, Engineering Lead\nScott Maher, Engineering Lead\nI find it energizing that the leaders I work with across the company are bias to action and always\nwith an eye on the customer experience. It keeps me engaged and on my toes.\n[David Grodsky]\nDavid Grodsky, Chief Compliance Officer (Square Financial Services)\nDavid Grodsky, Chief Compliance Officer (Square Financial Services)\nThe aspect I enjoy most at Block is being able to work with some of the brightest professionals out\nthere! My colleagues not only possess high IQ but also high EQ. I work in an environment where I\nfeel safe to be my authentic self and it leads to creative problem solving and risk taking.\n[Victoria Fan Azalde]\nVictoria Fan Azalde, VP, Head of International Accounting and Statutory Reporting\nVictoria Fan Azalde, VP, Head of International Accounting and Statutory Reporting\nOur purpose of economic empowerment attracts incredibly talented and mission-oriented people. What I\nfind most fulfilling is working with dedicated teams to find innovative ways to lower barriers to\nparticipation in the economy.\n[Ahmed Ali Bob]\nAhmed Ali Bob, Global Social Impact Lead\nAhmed Ali Bob, Global Social Impact Lead\nSince joining Block, I\u2019ve found that being myself is not only encouraged, it\u2019s rewarded. My advice\nto people who are neurodiverse would be to ask for support and let people know how you work best.\nKnowing I will be heard has opened new doors for my development!\n[Lynette Johnson McGee]\nLynette Johnson McGee, Customer Success Advocate\nLynette Johnson McGee, Customer Success Advocate\nCompliance Engineering works with different business units across Block to support product controls,\ncase tooling, and model development that touch on regulatory requirements. All of these are key to\nour ability to expand and operate as a Fintech company. There's a strong culture of excellence\nthroughout Block.\n[Cesar Alaniz]\nCesar Alaniz, Head of Compliance Engineering and Technology\nCesar Alaniz, Head of Compliance Engineering and Technology\nI\u2019m an explorer at heart. Block and our employee communities have allowed me to find boundaries and\ngo beyond them while being supported. Allowing for economic and personal empowerment has allowed me\nto take my skills further than I\u2019ve imagined. I\u2019ll take these skills with me wherever I go in the\nfuture.\n[Khiry Shank]\nKhiry Shank, Software Engineer | Program Manager\nKhiry Shank, Software Engineer | Program Manager\n\n## What People Are Saying About Block\n* Mission & Purpose: Work spans Square, Cash App, and other units with products used at meaningful\nscale, tied to a stated purpose of economic empowerment. Feedback suggests this multi\u2011block scope\nenables high\u2011impact problem solving across consumer and merchant domains.\n* Benefits & Perks: Official materials highlight remote\u2011friendly roles, comprehensive health\ncoverage, flexible time off, retirement matching, and a discounted employee stock purchase plan.\nFlexibility options and country\u2011specific policies are emphasized alongside standard tech benefits.\n* Learning & Development: A fast shipping cadence and exposure to regulated fintech areas\u2014risk,\ncompliance, lending, identity, and ML\u2014create accelerated skill growth for engineers, data\nscientists, and operators. Job specifications call for first\u2011principles problem solving in complex\ncredit and risk domains.\n\n## Block's Awards\n\n[award]\n\n## Block's Benefits\n\n### Promotion Policies\n\nPromote from within\n\nProvides customized development tracks\n\n### Work Environment\n\nImplements team-based strategic planning\n\nOpen office floor plan to encourage communication and collaboration\n\nUses an OKR operational model to clearly define goals and priorities\n\nUtilizes an open door policy that encourages accessibility\n\n### Work Hours Policies\n\nOffers a remote work program\n\nUtilizes a flexible work schedule\n\nUtilizes a hybrid work model\n\nUtilizes restricted work hours\n\n## Block FAQs\n\n[What's the Company Culture Like at Block?][44]\n[Block Inclusion & Diversity][45]\n[Block Career Growth & Development][46]\n[Block Compensation & Benefits][47]\n[What's the Work-Life Balance Like at Block?][48]\n[Block Leadership & Management][49]\n[Block Innovation & Technology Culture][50]\n[Block Mission, Purpose & Impact][51]\n[Block Company Growth, Stability & Outlook][52]\n* [\nCompanies\n][53]\n* [\nJobs\n][54]\n* [\nTracker\n][55]\n* [\nArticles\n][56]\n* More\n[Built In]\n[ Join ][57]\n[ Log In ][58]\n* [\nTech Jobs\n][59]\n* [\nCompanies\n][60]\n* [\nArticles\n][61]\n* [\nRemote\n][62]\n* [\nBest Places To Work\n][63]\n* [\nTech Hubs\n][64]\n[ Post Job ][65]\n[[BuiltIn]][66]\n\u00a9 2026 Built In. All rights reserved.\nAbout\n[ Our Story ][67]\n[ Careers ][68]\n[ Our Staff Writers ][69]\n[ Content Descriptions ][70]\nGet Involved\n[ Recruit With Built In ][71]\n[ Become an Expert Contributor ][72]\nResources\n[ Customer Support ][73]\n[ Share Feedback ][74]\n[ Report a Bug ][75]\n[ Tech Job Tools + Career Resources ][76]\n[ Browse Jobs ][77]\n[ Tech A-Z ][78]\nTech Hubs\n[Our Sites][79]\n\u00a9 2026 Built In. All rights reserved.\n[ Learning Lab User Agreement ][80] [ Accessibility Statement ][81] [ Copyright Policy ][82] [\nPrivacy Policy ][83] [ Terms of Use ][84] [ Your Privacy Choices/Cookie Settings ][85] [ CA Notice\nof Collection ][86]\n\n[1]: /\n[2]: /companies\n[3]: /jobs\n[4]: /tech-topics\n[5]: /jobs\n[6]: /auth/signup?destination=%2fcompany%2fblock-inc%2ffaq%2fworkplace-perception\n[7]: /auth/login?destination=%2fcompany%2fblock-inc%2ffaq%2fworkplace-perception\n[8]: https://employers.builtin.com?utm_medium=BIReferral&utm_source=foremployers\n[9]: /companies\n[10]: /company/block-inc\n[11]: https://block.xyz?utm_source=BuiltIn&utm_medium=BuiltIn&utm_campaign=BuiltIn\n[12]: /jobs/sales?companyId=105938&allLocations=true\n[13]: /jobs/engineering?companyId=105938&allLocations=true\n[14]: /jobs/ai-machine-learning?companyId=105938&allLocations=true\n[15]: /jobs/customer-success-experience?companyId=105938&allLocations=true\n[16]: /jobs/marketing?companyId=105938&allLocations=true\n[17]: /jobs/product-management?companyId=105938&allLocations=true\n[18]: /jobs/cyber-security?companyId=105938&allLocations=true\n[19]: /jobs/designer?companyId=105938&allLocations=true\n[20]: /jobs/finance?companyId=105938&allLocations=true\n[21]: /jobs/operations-support?companyId=105938&allLocations=true\n[22]: /jobs/program-project-management?companyId=105938&allLocations=true\n[23]: /jobs/data-analytics?companyId=105938&allLocations=true\n[24]: /jobs/hr-recruiting?companyId=105938&allLocations=true\n[25]: /jobs/legal?companyId=105938&allLocations=true\n[26]: /jobs?companyId=105938&allLocations=true\n[27]: /company/block-inc/faq/workplace-perception\n[28]: /company/block-inc/faq/culture-values\n[29]: /company/block-inc/faq/career-growth-development\n[30]: /company/block-inc/faq/compensation-benefits\n[31]: /company/block-inc/faq/work-life-balance-wellbeing\n[32]: /company/block-inc/faq/leadership-management\n[33]: /company/block-inc/faq/innovation-technology-agility\n[34]: /company/block-inc/faq/stability-growth\n[35]: https://builtin.com/articles/block-launches-open-source-20250127\n[36]: https://builtin.com/articles/behind-build-self-custody-solution-bitkey-offers-bitcoin-owners-g\nreater-safety-and-control\n[37]: https://www.linkedin.com/posts/joinblock_we-asked-our-leadership-team-why-block-activity-74241\n36898031300611-lITS?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAAAxT4yE"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://builtin.com/company/capco/faq/workplace-perception",
            "text": "[[Built In Logo] [Built In Logo]][1][Companies][2][Jobs][3][Articles][4]\n[View All Jobs][5]\n[ Join ][6]\n[ Log In ][7]\n[ For Employers ][8]\n[ Companies ][9] [ Capco ][10]\n\n## Capco\n\nSave Saved\nLondon\nTotal Offices: **24**\n6,000 Total Employees\nYear Founded: 1998\n[View Website][11]\nWe're Hiring!\n[ Consulting **99+** ][12] [ Engineering **95** ][13] [ AI & Machine Learning **44** ][14] [ Data &\nAnalytics **42** ][15] [ Program & Project Management **35** ][16] [ Cybersecurity **21** ][17] [\nFinance **18** ][18] [ Product Management **11** ][19] [ Operations & Support **8** ][20] [ Design\n**4** ][21] [ Sales **2** ][22] [ Customer Success & Experience **1** ][23] [ HR & Recruiting **1**\n][24] [ Marketing **1** ][25]\n[View all jobs][26]\n* Overview\n* Jobs 432\n* Offices\n* Articles\n* Company Insights\n* [ Working at Capco ][27]\n* [ Culture & Values ][28]\n* [ Inclusion & Diversity ][29]\n* [ Career Growth & Development ][30]\n* [ Compensation & Benefits ][31]\n* [ Work-Life Balance & Wellbeing ][32]\n* [ Leadership & Management ][33]\n* [ Innovation, Technology & Agility ][34]\n* [ Stability & Growth ][35]\n\n# What's It Like to Work at Capco?\n\nUpdated on June 11, 2026\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n## What practices at Capco support employee job satisfaction?\n\nJob Satisfaction\n\nCapco supports employee job satisfaction through meaningful transformation work, a people-first\nculture, flexible career growth, employee recognition and benefits that support wellbeing inside and\noutside work.\n* **Purposeful transformation work:** Capco gives employees opportunities to solve complex business\nand technology challenges across financial services and energy, including cloud migration,\nplatform modernization, digital engineering, AI, compliance, ESG data and automation. A consultant\nsaid the work includes \u201cdesigning and delivering scalable, cloud-native solutions,\u201d while an India\ncapability leader said Capco builds \u201creusable AI assets and bespoke solutions\u201d that help clients\nmove from pilots to \u201csafe, production-grade AI.\u201d\n* **Be Yourself At Work culture:** Capco\u2019s culture is built around values like \u201cMake a Difference,\u201d\n\u201cBe Yourself At Work\u201d and \u201cAct With Integrity,\u201d with employee communities including Women@Capco,\nPride@Capco, Wellbeing@Capco and R/ED, a global Affinity Group focused on supporting\nunderrepresented racially and ethnically diverse employees across the firm. A Senior Consultant\nsaid the team \u201cembraces individuality and uniqueness,\u201d while a finance specialist said employees\ncan \u201cbe genuinely you\u201d while meeting deliverables.\n* **Growth, learning and ownership:** Capco supports development through a mix of structured\ntraining, hands-on client work and employee-driven career ownership. Early-career consultants can\nbuild core consulting and technical skills through the Associate Talent Program, while newly\npromoted employees receive targeted support through Milestone Schools. Ongoing learning is\nreinforced through CAPsule, Coursera AI Academy, Udemy for Business, mentorship, coaching and\ntuition reimbursement. Employees describe that growth culture as active rather than passive: an\nAI lead said, \u201cIf I present a viable idea, I am not only free to chase it but am actively\nencouraged to do so,\u201d and a Managing Principal said leadership trusted them to own new\ncapabilities that directly shaped career growth.\n* **Recognition, support and connection:** Capco recognizes performance through awards, bonuses,\npublic shoutouts and peer recognition. A Consultant recognized with a \u201cCommunity Game Changer\u201d\naward said the experience made her feel \u201cvalued and included,\u201d while employees also point to\nsupportive teams, approachable leaders, camaraderie, events, games, CSR initiatives and wellbeing\nactivities as contributors to satisfaction.\n* **External signals:**\n* **Employer Strengths:** Employees on external review sites highlight Capco\u2019s culture, work-life\nbalance, supportive colleagues, approachable leadership, benefits, learning opportunities,\nmentorship, autonomy, inclusion and meaningful consulting work across financial services,\nenergy, technology and AI. (Glassdoor; Comparably)\n* **Positive Outlook:** Employees on external review sites rate Capco 3.8 out of 5 overall, with a\n75% recommendation rate and 81% CEO approval for Annie-Marie Rowland. Employees also rate Capco\n4.1 for diversity and inclusion, 4.0 for work-life balance and 3.9 for culture and values.\n(Glassdoor)\n* **Culture and Belonging:** Employees on external review sites describe Capco\u2019s culture as\ncollaborative, supportive and people-focused, with reviewers citing a \u201creal sense of belonging,\u201d\n\u201cgreat people and atmosphere\u201d and a \u201cBe Yourself At Work\u201d culture where employees can be\nthemselves. (Glassdoor)\n* **Benefits and Rewards:** Employees on external review sites rate Capco\u2019s perks and benefits 76\nout of 100, with 74% saying they are satisfied with their benefits. Employee reviews highlight\ncompetitive pay, health insurance, dental, 401(k), vacation, paid holidays, flexible spending\naccounts, low copays and a strong variety of benefits choices. (Comparably)\n* **Awards and Recognition:** Capco\u2019s external recognition reinforces the breadth of its consulting\nstrengths, from technical innovation to market expertise. Recent examples include recognition for\nanalytics and AI innovation through Consulting Magazine\u2019s Top Consultants 2026, mentorship\nexcellence from the Women\u2019s Energy Alliance 2026 Company Awards, and data management consulting\nthrough A-Team Group\u2019s Best North America Consultancy in Data Management award. Capco has also\nbeen recognized for ESG data and technology, regulatory consulting and digital customer experience\ntransformation.\n\n**Bottom line:** Capco supports job satisfaction by combining challenging client work, authentic\nculture, career mobility, strong learning programs, employee recognition, supportive teams and\nbenefits that reinforce wellbeing, inclusion and growth.\n\n## Is Capco a good place to work? Do Employees Recommend it?\n\nWillingness to Recommend\n\n**Is Capco a good place to work? Do people recommend it?**\n\nYes. Capco is a strong workplace for people who value consulting work with real client impact, a\ncollaborative and inclusive culture, learning opportunities, flexibility and room to shape their\ncareers.\n* **Strong culture and belonging:** Capco\u2019s culture is anchored in values like \u201cMake a Difference,\u201d\n\u201cBe Yourself At Work\u201d and \u201cAct With Integrity.\u201d Employees describe that culture as tangible: a\nsenior consultant said \u201cthe team culture \u2018be yourself at work\u2019 really manifests itself in real\nlife,\u201d while a Principal Consultant said Capco offers a \u201creal sense of belonging.\u201d Employee\ncommunities such as Women@Capco, Pride@Capco, Wellbeing@Capco and R/ED further support inclusion\nand connection.\n* **Meaningful work and growth:** Capco gives employees opportunities to work across financial\nservices, energy, cloud, AI, data, compliance, ESG and platform modernization. A Consultant said\nCapco combines \u201ctechnical excellence and people-first values,\u201d while an AI lead said, \u201cIf I\npresent a viable idea, I am not only free to chase it but am actively encouraged to do so.\u201d Capco\nalso supports growth through onboarding, the Associate Talent Program, Milestone Schools,\nmentorship, leadership development, CAPsule, Coursera AI Academy and tuition reimbursement.\n* **Supportive teams and leadership:** Employees frequently point to Capco\u2019s people as a reason to\nrecommend the company. A Senior Analyst said leadership is \u201capproachable, resourceful, and\ngenuinely invested in your growth,\u201d while an AI engineer cited \u201clots of guidance\u201d and a \u201cgreat\nteam to work with.\u201d Employees also describe skilled, helpful teams that are client-focused and\neager to help each other succeed.\n\n**External signals:**\n* **Employee Recommendation:** Employees on external review sites give Capco a positive overall\nrating of 3.8 out of 5, with 75% saying they would recommend the company to a friend. Reviewers\ndescribe Capco as a \u201cgreat place to work,\u201d a \u201cfun place to work\u201d and a company with \u201cgreat people\nand atmosphere.\u201d (Glassdoor; Indeed)\n* **Leadership Confidence:** Employees surveyed on external review sites report 81% CEO approval for\nAnnie-Marie Rowland. Recent reviews also point to \u201cfantastic leadership,\u201d \u201capproachable\u201d leaders\nand a \u201cstrong, female CEO with a clear vision for the company.\u201d (Glassdoor)\n* **Workplace Experience:** Employees on external review sites rate Capco highly for diversity and\ninclusion, work-life balance and culture, with scores of 4.1, 4.0 and 3.9 respectively. Employees\ndescribe the workplace as collaborative, supportive, inclusive and people-focused. (Glassdoor;\nIndeed)\n* **Benefits and Stability:** Employees on external review sites cite competitive pay, good\nbenefits, health insurance, 401(k), vacation, paid holidays, flexible spending accounts and strong\nwork-life balance. Capco\u2019s perks and benefits score is 76 out of 100, with 74% of employees saying\nthey are satisfied with their benefits. (Comparably; Glassdoor)\n* **Public Recognition:** Capco\u2019s external recognition includes awards for analytics and AI\ninnovation, mentorship excellence, data management consulting, ESG data and technology, regulatory\nconsulting and digital customer experience, supporting its reputation as a consulting employer\nwith recognized market expertise and employee-development commitments.\n\n**Bottom line:** Capco is recommended by many employees because it combines meaningful consulting\nwork, supportive teams, authentic culture, flexibility, career growth, recognition and benefits that\nhelp people feel included and supported.\n\n## Capco's Candidate Tradeoffs\n\n**If you\u2019re weighing whether Capco is the right fit, these are the core tradeoffs to consider.**\n* Capco emphasizes minimal micromanagement and high trust, giving employees space to make decisions\nand move quickly, though that model favors self-directed, intrinsically motivated contributors.\n\n## Capco Employee Perspectives\n\n**What is your role, and what attracted you to Capco? Describe the moment when you knew you\u2019d found\nthe right fit.**\n\nI am the tech lead for the AI dev team. I decided to join Capco because of the quality of people I\nencountered during the hiring process who seemed to be very open-minded about talented people with a\nnon-traditional tech background. I knew it was a good fit for me on my very first project \u2014 in\ntruth, even during my orientation sessions. The scrum master didn\u2019t care that I was self-taught or a\njunior. He assessed my work ethic and what I was capable of before adjusting my responsibilities\naccordingly.\n\n**What\u2019s your favorite part about working at Capco? **\n\nAs long as I demonstrate effort and deliver high-quality work, I have a lot of flexibility. When\npresented with a problem, I have very wide latitude and freedom for how I come to the solution. If I\npresent a viable idea, I am not only free to chase it but am actively encouraged to do so. The team\nwe have built around AI is a highlight. We regularly get together in the office. We have fun, joke\nwith each other and solve problems together. There\u2019s a strong startup feel to how we work.\n\nWhen it comes to opportunities for growth, it is all about you. Capco doesn\u2019t care about years or\nexperience \u2014 they care about the specific talents that you have and what level of effort you put in.\nI can attest to this personally. A little over three years ago, I began teaching myself how to code.\nA year into that, Capco gave me an opportunity. My first project, understandably, was a junior\nquality assurance role. Soon, I was presenting ideas about AI, solutions to pressing problems and\ninsights on team ethics in addition to being involved in a whole lot of problem-solving. Capco gave\nme recognition and credit every step of the way and put me out front, and today, I am an AI lead\nafter only two years into the industry.\n\n**What advice would you give to job seekers looking to join your growing team?**\n\nAs clich\u00e9 as it sounds"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://builtin.com/company/cargill/faq/workplace-perception",
            "text": "[[Built In Logo] [Built In Logo]][1][Companies][2][Jobs][3][Articles][4]\n[View All Jobs][5]\n[ Join ][6]\n[ Log In ][7]\n[ For Employers ][8]\n[ Companies ][9] [ Cargill ][10]\n\n## Cargill\n\nSave Saved\nWayzata\nTotal Offices: **3**\n155,000 Total Employees\nYear Founded: 1865\n[View Website][11]\nWe're Hiring!\n[ Engineering **62** ][12] [ Data & Analytics **19** ][13] [ Operations & Support **8** ][14] [ AI &\nMachine Learning **7** ][15] [ Consulting **4** ][16] [ Product Management **4** ][17] [\nCybersecurity **3** ][18] [ Customer Success & Experience **1** ][19]\n[View all jobs][20]\n* Overview\n* Jobs 110\n* Offices\n* Teams\n* Culture\n* Articles\n* Company Insights\n* [ Working at Cargill ][21]\n* [ Culture & Values ][22]\n* [ Inclusion & Diversity ][23]\n* [ Career Growth & Development ][24]\n* [ Compensation & Benefits ][25]\n* [ Work-Life Balance & Wellbeing ][26]\n* [ Leadership & Management ][27]\n* [ Innovation, Technology & Agility ][28]\n* [ Mission, Purpose & Impact ][29]\n* [ Stability & Growth ][30]\n\n# What's It Like to Work at Cargill?\n\nUpdated on May 29, 2026\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n## What practices at Cargill support employee job satisfaction?\n\nJob Satisfaction\n\nCargill supports employee job satisfaction through mission-driven work, development opportunities,\ninclusive culture, and comprehensive employee support programs.\n\n**Purpose-driven work: **Employees support Cargill\u2019s mission to \u201cnourish the world in a safe,\nresponsible and sustainable way\u201d through work tied to food security, regenerative agriculture,\nrenewable fuels, food safety, and resilient supply chains across 70 countries and 125 markets.\n\n**Career growth and learning: **Cargill offers mentorship, LinkedIn Learning, tuition reimbursement\nup to $6,000 annually, certifications, conferences, and customized development tracks. Programs like\nCYPN mentoring and PriceFx certification support long-term growth.\n\n**Collaborative culture: **Employees describe globally connected teams across locations like\nAtlanta, Poland, and Brazil, with strong collaboration, responsiveness, and support across time\nzones. Teams emphasize agile thinking, innovation, and customer-focused problem solving.\n\n**Inclusive workplace: **Cargill promotes inclusion through BRGs like the Cargill Women\u2019s Network,\nPride Network, Ebony Council, and Indigenous Peoples Network. Its Global Day of Inclusion reinforces\nbelonging, psychological safety, and employee voice.\n\n**Comprehensive benefits: **Benefits include healthcare, Lyra mental health support, fertility and\nadoption assistance up to $10,000, paid family leave, 401(k) matching, flexible work models, and\nwellness incentives up to $500.\n\n## Is Cargill a good place to work? Do Employees Recommend it?\n\nWillingness to Recommend\n\nCargill is generally viewed as a strong employer for people seeking meaningful work, global scale,\nand long-term career growth.\n\n**Strong employee reputation: **Diverse employees rated Cargill 77/100 on Comparably, placing the\ncompany in the Top 10% among employers with 10,000+ employees for diversity scores. CEO David\nMacLennan also ranked in the Top 10% for approval ratings.\n\n**Meaningful mission: **Employees frequently describe their work as purposeful because it supports\nfeeding the world, improving sustainability, and strengthening agriculture and food systems\nglobally. Many connect personally to the company\u2019s mission and impact.\n\n**Supportive team environment: **Employees highlight welcoming teams, mentorship, and strong\ncollaboration across functions and regions. Technology employees describe highly supportive global\nteams that encourage learning and professional development.\n\n**Career and innovation opportunities: **Employees have opportunities to work on AI, automation,\nforecasting, digital transformation, and data infrastructure projects while accessing mentorship,\nleadership development, and learning resources.\n\n**Flexible and people-first culture: **Cargill supports employee wellbeing through hybrid work,\nwellness resources, volunteer opportunities, PTO, family leave, mental health support, and employee\nrecognition programs designed to strengthen connection and belonging.\n\n## What reputation does Cargill have as a place to work?\n\nGeneral Market Perception\n\nCargill has a strong reputation as a global food and agriculture company known for meaningful work,\nstability, innovation, sustainability, and employee development.\n\n**Global food and agriculture leader: **Cargill is recognized as one of the world\u2019s largest food and\nagriculture companies, with 155,000+ employees, operations in 70 countries, delivery into 125\nmarkets, and more than 160 years of experience.\n\n**Purpose and sustainability leadership: **The company is known for regenerative agriculture,\nrenewable fuels, food safety innovation, AI-enabled farming technologies, and food waste reduction.\nIn FY2025, Cargill reduced Scope 1 and 2 emissions by 20.9% from its 2017 baseline.\n\n**People-first and inclusive culture: **Cargill emphasizes psychological safety, belonging, and\nequitable opportunity through BRGs, DEI initiatives, mentorship programs, and leadership support.\nThe company positions inclusion as central to innovation and business performance.\n\n**Ethics and integrity reputation: **Cargill\u2019s Guiding Principles and Code of Conduct emphasize\nhonesty, compliance, accountability, and responsible global citizenship. The company positions\nethics as foundational to its culture since 1865.\n\n**Employer recognition: **Cargill has been recognized by the Human Rights Campaign Foundation for\ndisability inclusion and named one of Forbes\u2019 Best Employers for Women in 2025, reinforcing its\nreputation for inclusion and workplace culture.\n\n## What tradeoffs might come with working at Cargill?\n\nTradeoffs\n\nOne key tradeoff is meaningful, real-world impact vs. lighter day-to-day expectations. Because\nCargill operates at the center of the global food system, employees often work on initiatives tied\nto food security, sustainability, agriculture, and supply chain resilience. That impact can also\nbring increased accountability and operational complexity.\n\nAnother tradeoff is broad career mobility vs. highly linear career progression. Employees have\nopportunities to move across business units, functions, and global teams, which supports long-term\nleadership development and varied experience, though career paths may evolve less predictably over\ntime.\n\nEmployees may also experience strong long-term benefits vs. faster compensation acceleration.\nCargill invests heavily in healthcare, retirement support, wellbeing, flexibility, and family\nbenefits, creating a broad total rewards package centered on long-term employee support.\n\nAnother tradeoff is sustainable performance vs. rapid, high-velocity execution. Cargill emphasizes\noperational consistency, long-term resilience, and measured progress, which can create a steadier\npace than highly aggressive growth-stage environments.\n\nThere is also a tradeoff between engaged leadership vs. highly hands-off management. Managers are\ngenerally accessible, collaborative, and focused on employee support and alignment, though employees\nmay experience more regular communication and coordination across teams.\n\nEmployees may also notice long-term stability vs. rapid organizational change. Cargill\u2019s scale,\nglobal reach, and long operating history create stability and resilience, though strategic shifts\nmay happen more gradually than at smaller or earlier-stage companies.\n\nFinally, innovation at Cargill tends to prioritize practical business and customer outcomes over\nexperimentation for its own sake. Innovation is often tied to operational improvement,\nsustainability, food systems, and measurable customer value.\n\n**Great match for candidates who prefer:**\n* Meaningful work tied to real-world impact\n* Broad career exposure and cross-functional collaboration\n* Strong long-term benefits and stability\n* Sustainable, steady work environments\n* Supportive and engaged managers\n* Practical innovation tied to customer outcomes\n\n**Working here means:**\n* Supporting global food and agriculture systems\n* Collaborating across functions, regions, and disciplines\n* Growing through long-term career development opportunities\n* Operating within structured, large-scale systems\n* Balancing innovation with operational reliability and accountability\n\n## Cargill's Candidate Tradeoffs\n\n**If you\u2019re weighing whether Cargill is the right fit, these are the core tradeoffs to consider.**\n* Cargill emphasizes accessible, engaged managers who provide regular support and alignment, though\nthat often includes more frequent check-ins and active collaboration.\n\n## Cargill Employee Perspectives\n\nWorkplace perception at Cargill is shaped by the company\u2019s broad global reach and behind-the-scenes\ninfluence across industries that touch everyday life. Employees are drawn to the organization\u2019s\nscale, impact and interconnectedness, recognizing the unique opportunity to contribute to work that\nspans food, agriculture, finance, technology and beyond.\n\n\u201cMy recruiter described Cargill as an agricultural giant behind the scenes, integral to many\nbusinesses and individuals. Whether it\u2019s food, finance, farming or technology, Cargill has a hand in\nit.\u201d\n\n[William Orgertrice]\nWilliam Orgertrice, Data Engineer \u2014 Data Function, Platforms and Product Engineering\nFrom the article: [17 Companies Hiring Top Tech Talent \u2014 and Empowering Them to Thrive][31]\n\n## Cargill Employee Reviews\n\nAs a leader in the Cargill's Women in Technology network, I'm proud to be helping young women start\ntheir careers in engineering and information technology. I love hearing their success stories and\nknow that I am paving the way for others like me.\n\n[Gaby]\nGaby, Data Engineering Lead\nGaby, Data Engineering Lead\n\nCargill provides you a unique opportunity to learn and grow and achieve your career aspirations\nwhile nourishing the world. I find it very rewarding knowing that you are part of that purpose.\n\n[Landon]\nLandon, North America Service Assurance Manager\nLandon, North America Service Assurance Manager\n\nCargill is a great place to work because it lets me be authentic. My ideas and my innovations are\nvalued. My contribution is valued, and it is creating an impact in nourishing the world.\n\n[Navita]\nNavita, Software Engineering Senior Supervisor\nNavita, Software Engineering Senior Supervisor\n\nThe most rewarding part of my role is I feel that I am making a difference, not only for Cargill but\nfor the world. It\u2019s a great feeling to work on a project that positively impacts millions of people\ndaily.\n\n[William Orgertrice]\nWilliam Orgertrice, Data Engineer\nWilliam Orgertrice, Data Engineer\n\n## What People Are Saying About Cargill\n* Mission & Purpose: Work is framed around nourishing the world across a global food and ag supply\nchain, and many roles feel consequential and connected to global impact. The company\u2019s scale links\nday-to-day tasks to outcomes that are globally connected.\n* Career Growth: Advancement across businesses and geographies is emphasized, with cross-functional\nmoves and early-career programs highlighted. Internal mobility and \u201cown your career\u201d messaging\nindicate pathways to grow.\n* Benefits & Perks: U.S. offerings include health coverage, paid family leave, retirement programs\nsuch as 401(k) and ESOP, and broader well\u2011being resources. Specifics can vary by union or\nproduction roles.\n\n## Cargill's Awards\n\n[award][award][award][award]\n[award][award][award][award][award][award][award][award]\n\n## Cargill's Benefits\n\n### Employee Satisfaction & Recognition\n\nEmployee feedback used to shape policies and strategy\n\nEstablished employee awards to honor work and contributions\n\nManagers give public shoutouts and celebrate employee milestones\n\nManagers offer consistent feedback loops\n\n### Promotion Policies\n\nEncourages lateral mobility to expand skills and impact\n\nProvides customized development tracks\n\n### Work Environment\n\nLeadership is transparent and communicative\n\nPrioritizes"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://builtin.com/company/cargurus/faq/workplace-perception",
            "text": "[[Built In Logo] [Built In Logo]][1][Companies][2][Jobs][3][Articles][4]\n[View All Jobs][5]\n[ Join ][6]\n[ Log In ][7]\n[ For Employers ][8]\n[ Companies ][9] [ CarGurus ][10]\n\n## CarGurus\n\nSave Saved\nBoston\nTotal Offices: **3**\n1,200 Total Employees\nYear Founded: 2006\n[View Website][11]\nWe're Hiring!\n[ Engineering **15** ][12] [ Sales **7** ][13] [ Operations & Support **5** ][14] [ Product\nManagement **5** ][15] [ AI & Machine Learning **4** ][16] [ HR & Recruiting **3** ][17] [ Marketing\n**3** ][18] [ Data & Analytics **2** ][19] [ Program & Project Management **2** ][20] [ Consulting\n**1** ][21] [ Cybersecurity **1** ][22] [ Design **1** ][23]\n[View all jobs][24]\n* Overview\n* Jobs 48\n* Offices\n* Culture\n* Articles\n* Company Insights\n* [ Working at CarGurus ][25]\n* [ Culture & Values ][26]\n* [ Inclusion & Diversity ][27]\n* [ Career Growth & Development ][28]\n* [ Compensation & Benefits ][29]\n* [ Work-Life Balance & Wellbeing ][30]\n* [ Leadership & Management ][31]\n* [ Innovation, Technology & Agility ][32]\n* [ Stability & Growth ][33]\n\n# What's It Like to Work at CarGurus?\n\nUpdated on May 19, 2026\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n## What practices at CarGurus support employee job satisfaction?\n\nJob Satisfaction\n\nCarGurus supports employee job satisfaction through flexibility, career growth, collaborative\nculture, AI innovation opportunities, and strong employee benefits. The company emphasizes giving\nemployees meaningful ownership while supporting long-term development and wellbeing.\n\n**Career growth and learning: **Employees have access to mentorship, LinkedIn Learning, tuition\nreimbursement, Hackathons, Science Fairs, AI training, and internal mobility opportunities.\nEarly-career employees are integrated directly into teams, while sales and engineering employees\nfrequently grow through peer learning, stretch opportunities, and cross-functional collaboration.\n\n**AI-forward innovation culture: **Through AI Forward, employees across departments are encouraged\nto experiment with AI tools and contribute to AI-powered products and workflows. Teams work on\ninitiatives like CarGurus Discover, Dealership Mode, and PriceVantage while using tools such as\nGemini, Cursor, Windsurf, and Glean.\n\n**Flexible hybrid workplace: **CarGurus supports hybrid flexibility through floating remote days,\nrecharge days, unlimited personal and sick time off, and paid sabbaticals every five years. The\nBoston headquarters was designed specifically for hybrid collaboration and employee wellbeing, with\nwellness rooms, rooftop terraces, quiet workspaces, and fitness amenities.\n\n**Collaborative and inclusive culture: **Employees frequently describe the culture as transparent,\nsupportive, and community-oriented. Leadership maintains visibility through WAMA sessions, Town\nHalls, Tech Talks, and ongoing employee feedback programs. ERGs and Communities of Practice help\nemployees build connection across teams and identities.\n\n**Strong benefits and perks: **Benefits include RSUs for full-time employees, 401(k) matching,\nfertility and adoption support, mental health resources, commuter benefits, tuition reimbursement,\nwellness reimbursements, parental leave, lunch stipends, and the Auto Perk vehicle discount\nprogram.\n\n**External signals: **CarGurus holds an A+ culture rating on Comparably with 96% positive employee\nreviews. The company has also been recognized as Built In\u2019s #1 Best Large Company to Work For in the\nU.S. and #1 Best Place to Work in Boston.\n\n## Is CarGurus a good place to work? Do Employees Recommend it?\n\nWillingness to Recommend\n\nCarGurus is generally viewed as a strong employer for people seeking flexibility, collaborative\nculture, career growth, and opportunities to work on AI-powered consumer technology products at\nscale. Employees frequently describe the company as transparent, supportive, and fast-moving without\nbeing overly corporate.\n\n**Strong employee reputation: **Employees often highlight collaborative teammates, approachable\nleadership, flexibility, and strong benefits as reasons they recommend the company. CarGurus\nmaintains an A+ culture rating on Comparably with 96% positive employee reviews. CEO Jason Trevisan\nranks in the Top 5% among CEOs of similarly sized companies.\n\n**Growth and learning opportunities: **Employees across engineering, product, sales, and operations\nteams frequently reference internal mobility, mentorship, AI learning, Hackathons, leadership\ndevelopment, and opportunities to take on broader ownership quickly.\n\n**AI and innovation exposure: **Employees work on large-scale automotive marketplace products and\nAI-powered experiences used by 45 million monthly visitors and more than 34,000 dealerships. Teams\nare encouraged to experiment quickly and contribute ideas across functions.\n\n**Flexible and employee-centered workplace: **CarGurus supports hybrid flexibility, unlimited\npersonal and sick time off, recharge days, paid sabbaticals, wellness benefits, and\nemployee-centered office design focused on collaboration and wellbeing.\n\n**Inclusive and transparent culture: **Employees frequently describe the workplace as welcoming and\ntransparent, with strong communication from leadership and active employee communities through ERGs,\nmentorship, and volunteer programs.\n\n**External signals: **CarGurus is consistently recognized by Built In and Comparably for culture,\nleadership, flexibility, and employee experience. External reviews commonly highlight work-life\nbalance, career growth, and supportive leadership as strengths of the company.\n\n## What reputation does CarGurus have as a place to work?\n\nGeneral Market Perception\n\nCarGurus has built a reputation as a collaborative, AI-forward automotive technology company known\nfor flexible hybrid work, employee development, and fast-moving innovation. The company is often\nrecognized for balancing large-scale consumer technology work with a supportive and transparent\nculture.\n\n**AI and product innovation reputation: **CarGurus is increasingly known as an AI-forward workplace,\nwith employees contributing to products like CarGurus Discover, Dealership Mode, PriceVantage, and\nconversational vehicle search experiences. The AI Forward initiative reinforces the company\u2019s\nreputation for experimentation, rapid learning, and practical AI adoption across teams.\n\n**Collaborative and transparent culture: **Employees frequently describe the company as low-ego,\nteam-oriented, and highly collaborative. Leadership emphasizes transparency through WAMA sessions,\nTown Halls, Tech Talks, and ongoing employee feedback programs.** **\n\n**Employee growth and flexibility: **CarGurus is recognized for investing in mentorship, internal\nmobility, AI learning, Hackathons, tuition reimbursement, and leadership development while also\nsupporting hybrid flexibility, recharge days, wellness programs, and paid sabbaticals.\n\n**Inclusive workplace reputation: **The company promotes belonging through ERGs, the FAIR Framework,\nvolunteer programs, and inclusive workplace policies such as no dress code and gender-inclusive\nspaces. Employees often describe the culture as welcoming and community-oriented.\n\n**Modern hybrid workplace: **CarGurus\u2019 Boston headquarters is frequently highlighted for its\nhybrid-first design, including collaborative workspaces, wellness rooms, rooftop terraces, fitness\namenities, and flexible environments designed to support both focus and teamwork.\n\n**External signals: **CarGurus has received major workplace recognition including Built In\u2019s #1 Best\nLarge Company to Work For in the U.S. and #1 Best Place to Work in Boston. Comparably also gives the\ncompany an A+ culture rating, with employees frequently highlighting flexibility, leadership\naccessibility, innovation opportunities, and supportive culture.\n\n## What tradeoffs might come with working at CarGurus?\n\nTradeoffs\n\nOne key tradeoff at CarGurus is cross-functional collaboration vs. highly independent work styles.\nTeams work closely across engineering, product, sales, analytics, and marketing, which creates\nstrong shared ownership and visibility but also requires frequent coordination and communication.\n\nAnother tradeoff is long-term career development vs. faster near-term compensation growth. CarGurus\ninvests heavily in mentorship, AI learning, internal mobility, Hackathons, and leadership\ndevelopment, emphasizing broad career growth over purely short-term compensation acceleration.\n\nEmployees may also experience equity-based rewards vs. guaranteed compensation upside. RSUs are part\nof compensation for full-time employees, giving employees the opportunity to share in long-term\ncompany growth while tying part of compensation to overall business performance.\n\nThere is also a tradeoff between transparent leadership vs. fully finalized communication. Leaders\nshare updates openly through WAMA sessions, Town Halls, and ongoing communication channels, which\ngives employees visibility into strategy and decision-making as priorities evolve in real time.\n\nAnother tradeoff is flexibility and autonomy vs. tightly structured work environments. CarGurus\u2019\nhybrid model gives employees meaningful ownership over schedules and workflows, but success often\ndepends on being proactive, organized, and self-directed.\n\nEmployees may also notice experimentation-led innovation vs. highly fixed processes. Teams are\nencouraged to move quickly, test ideas, and experiment with AI tools and new technologies, which\ncreates opportunities for ownership but can also mean priorities evolve rapidly.\n\nFinally, there is a tradeoff between organizational adaptability vs. highly stable role boundaries.\nAs CarGurus continues investing in AI and marketplace innovation, teams and responsibilities may\nshift alongside changing business priorities.\n\n**Great match for candidates who prefer:**\n* Cross-functional teamwork\n* Hybrid flexibility and autonomy\n* AI experimentation and fast-moving environments\n* Transparent leadership\n* Long-term career growth\n* Data-driven decision making\n\n**Working here means:**\n* Building products used by 45 million monthly visitors and 34,000+ dealers\n* Collaborating across technical and business teams\n* Working in an AI-forward culture focused on experimentation\n* Balancing speed and innovation with customer trust and platform reliability\n\n## CarGurus's Candidate Tradeoffs\n\n**If you\u2019re weighing whether CarGurus is the right fit, these are the core tradeoffs to consider.**\n* CarGurus emphasizes transparent leadership with open access to information and candid\ncommunication, though leaders communicate developments in real time rather than waiting for fully\npolished updates.\n\n## CarGurus Employee Perspectives\n\nOne thing that stands out to employees at CarGurus is how collaborative and grounded the engineering\nculture feels. Technical teams aren\u2019t siloed from the business \u2014 they\u2019re encouraged to understand\nthe broader company strategy and customer impact behind the work they do.\n\n\u201cIt sounds clich\u00e9, but people here are smart, nice and helpful. I\u2019ve worked with tons of engineers\nacross my career, and the engineers at CarGurus stand out because they deeply understand the\nbusiness context.\u201d\n\n[Lata Ahuja]\nLata Ahuja, Senior Director of Wholesale Engineering\nFrom the article: [CarGurus Wholesale Team Culture:: This Team Is Focused on Providing Even More\nTransparency for Car Sellers][34]\n\nWorkplace perception at CarGurus is shaped by a transparent, low-ego culture where collaboration and\nopen communication are encouraged across every level of the organization. Employees are empowered to\ncontribute ideas, share feedback and work cross-functionally in an environment where strong teamwork\nmatters more than hierarchy.\n\n\u201cIt\u2019s a very flat and transparent culture, which has been great in this cross-functional effort.\nWhat attracted me to CarGurus is that it\u2019s a place where you leave your ego at the door. We expect\nideas and feedback from all levels, from interns up to the executive team.\u201d\n\n[Anthony Solesi]\nAnthony Solesi, Direct"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://builtin.com/company/cdw/faq/workplace-perception",
            "text": "[[Built In Logo] [Built In Logo]][1][Companies][2][Jobs][3][Articles][4]\n[View All Jobs][5]\n[ Join ][6]\n[ Log In ][7]\n[ For Employers ][8]\n[ Companies ][9] [ CDW ][10]\n\n## CDW\n\nSave Saved\nVernon Hills\nTotal Offices: **9**\n15,100 Total Employees\nYear Founded: 1984\n[View Website][11]\nWe're Hiring!\n[ Sales **72** ][12] [ Engineering **40** ][13] [ Consulting **20** ][14] [ Cybersecurity **20**\n][15] [ Customer Success & Experience **10** ][16] [ HR & Recruiting **7** ][17] [ Finance **6**\n][18] [ Operations & Support **5** ][19] [ Program & Project Management **5** ][20] [ Data &\nAnalytics **3** ][21] [ AI & Machine Learning **2** ][22] [ Marketing **2** ][23] [ Product\nManagement **2** ][24] [ Supply Chain & Procurement **2** ][25] [ Legal **1** ][26]\n[View all jobs][27]\n* Overview\n* Jobs 201\n* Offices\n* Articles\n* Company Insights\n* [ Working at CDW ][28]\n* [ Culture & Values ][29]\n* [ Inclusion & Diversity ][30]\n* [ Career Growth & Development ][31]\n* [ Compensation & Benefits ][32]\n* [ Work-Life Balance & Wellbeing ][33]\n* [ Leadership & Management ][34]\n* [ Innovation, Technology & Agility ][35]\n* [ Mission, Purpose & Impact ][36]\n* [ Stability & Growth ][37]\n\n# What's It Like to Work at CDW?\n\nUpdated on May 19, 2026\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n## What practices at CDW support employee job satisfaction?\n\nJob Satisfaction\n\nCDW supports employee job satisfaction through a mix of growth, support, flexibility, and purpose.\n* **Career growth and development: **CDW invests in structured development at multiple stages,\nincluding global onboarding, Sales Academy, Tech Academy, Emerging Leaders, and Leadership\nAcademy. In 2023, 79% of coworkers activated LinkedIn Learning, completing more than 25,900\ncourses and watching 596,700+ videos. Employee stories also emphasize regular career\nconversations, mentorship, and internal mobility across roles and locations.\n* **Supportive leadership and teams: **Employee experiences consistently describe helpful managers,\nvisible leadership, and collaborative teams. Reviews highlight strong onboarding, support nets\nacross the organization, and managers who help employees grow while maintaining high expectations.\n* **Flexibility and work-life balance: **CDW\u2019s Better Together hybrid model is designed to balance\nflexibility with connection. In 2023, the company hosted 100+ Better Together events, and reviews\nfrequently mention work-from-home flexibility, supportive managers, and strong leave benefits.\n* **Recognition and listening:** CDW uses formal recognition and employee feedback systems to\nreinforce engagement. Its WeListen@CDW survey reached 89% participation in 2023, and the company\nhighlights signature recognition programs such as Coworker of the Year and other performance\nawards.\n* **Belonging and inclusive culture:** CDW emphasizes a welcoming, respectful environment where\nemployees can be themselves and feel heard. In 2023, more than 4,050 coworkers in North America\nparticipated in Business Resource Groups, up 15% from the prior year. Employee quotes frequently\ndescribe the culture as supportive, family-like, and team-oriented.\n* **Benefits and wellbeing: **CDW supports coworkers through healthcare, retirement, leave, and\nwellbeing resources. The company describes a holistic wellbeing model spanning physical,\nemotional, financial, and social support, and in 2023 it also expanded some benefits, including\nreducing the waiting period for new hires and increasing paid leave for primary parental\ncaregivers and bereavement.\n* **Purpose and community impact: **CDW ties work to a broader sense of impact through social impact\nand digital equity efforts. In 2023, 1,100 coworkers contributed 8,329 volunteer hours, and 81% of\nglobal colleagues said CDW gives them opportunities to make a positive impact in their community.\n\n**Bottom Line:** CDW appears to support job satisfaction by combining strong development\nopportunities, supportive management, flexible work practices, inclusive culture, and purpose-driven\nwork.\n\n## Is CDW a good place to work? Do Employees Recommend it?\n\nWillingness to Recommend\n\nCDW is generally seen as a good place to work, with employee feedback pointing to supportive teams,\nstrong growth opportunities, flexibility, and a culture built around collaboration and belonging.\n* **Manager support and growth: **Employees frequently point to mentorship, career conversations,\nvisible leadership, and internal mobility as reasons they would recommend CDW. CDW backs that up\nwith structured onboarding, leadership development, Sales Academy, Tech Academy, Emerging Leaders,\nand other formal growth programs. In 2023, 79% of coworkers activated LinkedIn Learning,\ncompleting 25,900+ courses, and the company\u2019s global employee survey reached 89% participation.\n* **Why employees recommend it: **Employees most often recommend CDW for its supportive culture,\nstrong teamwork, career growth, work-life balance and flexibility, helpful managers, and benefits.\nEmployee reviews also point to job stability, learning opportunities, and the ability to build a\nlong career across different roles and business areas.\n* **High-caliber peers and collaborative environment:** Employees describe CDW as a place where\ncoworkers share knowledge, help solve problems, and work across functions to deliver results.\nCDW\u2019s own materials reinforce that with an emphasis on cross-functional collaboration, BRGs, and\nhybrid connection through Better Together. In 2023, more than 4,050 coworkers in North America\nparticipated in BRGs, up 15% year over year, and CDW hosted 100+ Better Together events.\n* **Flexibility, benefits, and wellbeing:** CDW\u2019s hybrid model and benefits package are also part of\nthe recommendation story. Reviews frequently mention work-from-home flexibility, supportive\nmanagers, PTO, and good benefits. CDW\u2019s materials highlight healthcare, retirement, parental\nleave, adoption support, tuition reimbursement, and a holistic wellbeing model spanning physical,\nemotional, financial, and social support.\n* **External validation:** CDW\u2019s employer reputation is reinforced by workplace recognitions\nincluding Built In Best Places to Work 2025, Computerworld Best Places to Work in IT 2025, and\nMilitary Friendly Employer 2025\n* External review signals: External reviews across Glassdoor, Comparably, and Indeed consistently\nhighlight supportive managers, strong collaboration, growth opportunities, flexibility, and\nculture.\n\n**Bottom line:** CDW appears to be a strong fit for people who want supportive teams, room to grow,\nflexible work practices, and a collaborative culture inside a large, stable technology company.\n\n## CDW's Candidate Tradeoffs\n\n**If you\u2019re weighing whether CDW is the right fit, these are the core tradeoffs to consider.**\n* CDW emphasizes accessible, engaged managers who provide regular support and alignment, though that\noften includes more frequent check-ins and active collaboration.\n\n## CDW Employee Perspectives\n\n**What first attracted you to CDW? When did you know it was the right place for you and your\ncareer?**\n\nIn 2013, a recruiter contacted me regarding an opportunity for a Senior Technician role. Although I\nwas initially unfamiliar with CDW, the position appeared to be an excellent prospect for advancing\nmy career in Technology. Within the first week, I recognized that it was an ideal fit due to the\nextensive support from colleagues at the local office as well as my remote peers. Even before we\nadopted a hybrid work model, I felt like my team was only a few steps away if I ever needed\nanything. I also got to \u2018play\u2019 with a lot of new hardware.\n\n**Share one exciting challenge or project you are working on right now. What impact will this have\non the business?**\n\nSupporting various technology teams to advance our security initiatives including the rollout of\nWindows 11 to the organization. The impact of these projects is not just about protecting data for\nour customers but also about enabling a more efficient, productive and innovative work environment\nfor our coworkers.\n\n**If your company culture was a car, what would it be, and why? **\n\nI\u2019m not much of a car aficionado so I\u2019ll borrow this from Ferris Bueller\u2019s Day Off: 1961 Ferrari 250\nGT California. Our culture and vehicle is unique, powerful and works in harmony to deliver optimum\nperformance.\n\n[Andrew Basler]\nAndrew Basler, Manager Support & Operations\nFrom the article: [Want to Change Gears in 2025? Here are 17 Tech Companies Hiring][38]\n\nCDW is presented as a place where people build long careers, take on new challenges, and work\nalongside supportive colleagues. Its workplace reputation is shaped by strong coworker retention,\nvaried opportunities, and an environment that appeals to people who value growth, adaptability, and\ngood teams.\n\n\u201cOne of the things that continues to surprise me is the long tenure of coworkers at CDW. This really\nspeaks to the value people find in working here. If you enjoy wearing multiple hats, being\nchallenged, and most importantly, working with good people, CDW is the place for you.\u201d\n\nNam Ahuja, Senior Practice Manager, Global Delivery at CDW\nFrom the article: [Career Journey with Nam Ahuja][39]\n\n## CDW Employee Reviews\n\nMy favorite thing about my role is being involved in so many cross functional workstreams that are\nfocused on transforming our business for the future.\n\n[Kevin Denison]\nKevin Denison, Director, Strategic Initiatives \u2014 U.S. Commercial\nKevin Denison, Director, Strategic Initiatives \u2014 U.S. Commercial\n\nMy favorite thing about CDW\u2019s evolution over the years has been its ability to continuously adapt\nand innovate while staying true to its core values.\n\nDrew Bills, Senior Manager in Corporate Communications\nDrew Bills, Senior Manager in Corporate Communications\n\nThe most rewarding part of being a Technical Architect at CDW is bringing everything together. Every\nday, countless people here make impactful changes, driving growth and excellence. I take pride in\nbeing the \"glue\" that unites these efforts, creating scalable solutions for hundreds or thousands of\ncustomers.\n\nCody Weaver, Technical Architect\nCody Weaver, Technical Architect\n\nCDW has provided me with stability, security, and generous compensation, and it was the best move I\ncould have made.\n\nMike Nolan, Account Manager, K-12\nMike Nolan, Account Manager, K-12\n\nWorking for a company that is always expanding and changing can be challenging... but that is also\nmotivating because there is endless potential and opportunity if you get after it!\n\nEbony Thomas, Account Manager, Higher Education\nEbony Thomas, Account Manager, Higher Education\n\n## What People Are Saying About CDW\n* Learning & Development: Structured onboarding and ongoing enablement are emphasized, including a\nrobust new\u2011sales program and leadership development. Opportunities to learn across vendors and\nsolutions are presented as a core strength that accelerates skill growth.\n* Belonging & Inclusion: The \u201cOne CDW\u201d culture and Business Resource Groups are a visible part of\nthe employee experience. Colleagues are often seen as inclusive and collaborative, fostering\nconnection across teams.\n* Market Position & Stability: A Fortune\u2011scale solutions provider with strong brand presence offers\naccess to major customers and partners, alongside external workplace recognitions. These signals\ncreate confidence in a stable, well\u2011resourced platform for career building.\n\n## CDW's Awards\n\n[award][award][award]\n\n## CDW's Benefits\n\n### Employee Satisfaction & Recognition\n\nCompany or teams have recognition rituals for individual work\n\nEmployee feedback used to shape policies and strategy\n\nEstablished employee awards to honor work and contributions\n\nProvides resources to build team camaraderie\n\nQuarterly engagement surveys to gauge employee satisfaction\n\n### Promotion Policies\n\nDocumented career progression frameworks\n\nDocumented path to leadership development\n\nEncourages lateral mobility to expand skills and impact\n\nPromote from within\n\n### Work Environment\n\n"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://builtin.com/company/celonis/faq/workplace-perception",
            "text": "[[Built In Logo] [Built In Logo]][1][Companies][2][Jobs][3][Articles][4]\n[View All Jobs][5]\n[ Join ][6]\n[ Log In ][7]\n[ For Employers ][8]\n[ Companies ][9] [ Celonis ][10]\n[Celonis logo]\n\n## Celonis\n\nSave Saved\nNew York\nTotal Offices: **15**\n3,000 Total Employees\nYear Founded: 2011\n[View Website][11]\n[Celonis logo]\nWe're Hiring!\n[ Consulting **44** ][12] [ AI & Machine Learning **42** ][13] [ Sales **37** ][14] [ Customer\nSuccess & Experience **32** ][15] [ Engineering **26** ][16] [ Operations & Support **8** ][17] [\nProduct Management **8** ][18] [ HR & Recruiting **4** ][19] [ Cybersecurity **3** ][20] [ Data &\nAnalytics **3** ][21] [ Marketing **3** ][22] [ Finance **1** ][23] [ Legal **1** ][24] [ Program &\nProject Management **1** ][25]\n[View all jobs][26]\n* Overview\n* Jobs 217\n* Offices\n* Teams\n* Culture\n* Articles\n* Company Insights\n* [ Working at Celonis ][27]\n* [ Culture & Values ][28]\n* [ Career Growth & Development ][29]\n* [ Compensation & Benefits ][30]\n* [ Work-Life Balance & Wellbeing ][31]\n* [ Leadership & Management ][32]\n* [ Innovation, Technology & Agility ][33]\n* [ Stability & Growth ][34]\n\n# What's It Like to Work at Celonis?\n\nUpdated on June 11, 2026\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n## What practices at Celonis support employee job satisfaction?\n\nJob Satisfaction\n\nCelonis supports employee job satisfaction through a combination of meaningful work, strong career\ndevelopment opportunities, employee ownership, competitive rewards and a culture built around\ncustomer impact. As the market leader in Process Intelligence, Celonis gives employees the\nopportunity to help some of the world's largest organizations improve efficiency, sustainability and\nbusiness performance through data and AI-powered process optimization. The company serves more than\n1,400 customers globally and has delivered more than $10.8 billion in documented customer value.\n* **Career growth and learning opportunities:** Celonis invests heavily in employee development\nthrough structured learning programs, internal mobility and mentorship. Employees have access to\nlearning platforms such as Degreed and LinkedIn Learning, while early-career talent can\nparticipate in Orbit, Celonis' global graduate program. Employees credit the program with helping\nto accelerate their growth and confidence early in their careers.\n* **Employee ownership and accountability:** Celonis reinforces its value of \"We Own It\" by\nencouraging employees to take ownership of outcomes and customer impact. The company's Total\nRewards philosophy emphasizes performance recognition and long-term growth.\n* **Strong benefits and wellbeing support:** Benefits include healthcare coverage, mental health\nresources, parental leave, retirement programs, fertility support and learning investments. In\nmany locations, employees receive up to 24 weeks of paid parental leave for primary caregivers and\n12 weeks for secondary caregivers.\n* **Inclusive and collaborative culture:** Through employee-led communities and inclusion\ninitiatives, Celonis aims to create an environment where employees feel valued, respected and\nempowered to share different perspectives and bring their authentic selves to work.\n* **Purpose-driven work and sustainability:** Employees contribute to technology that helps\norganizations reduce waste, improve resource utilization and drive sustainable outcomes through\nmore efficient business processes.\n* **Employee testimonials:** Employees frequently highlight learning opportunities, international\ncollaboration and career mobility. Employees describe Celonis as a place where employees can take\nownership, learn continuously and make meaningful customer impact.\n* **External signals:**\n* Celonis maintains an A- culture rating and strong scores across leadership, diversity and career\ngrowth categories. (Comparably)\n* Reviews frequently mention talented coworkers, learning opportunities and exposure to innovative\ntechnology as strengths of the employee experience. (Glassdoor)\n* Celonis has been recognized as a leader in Process Mining and Process Intelligence, reinforcing\nits reputation as an innovation-focused technology company. (Gartner)\n\n**Bottom line:** Celonis is generally best suited for employees who are motivated by ownership,\ncustomer impact, continuous learning and the opportunity to help global organizations transform\ntheir operations through AI and Process Intelligence.\n\n## Is Celonis a good place to work? Do Employees Recommend it?\n\nWillingness to Recommend\n\nCelonis is viewed positively by employees who are looking for a high-growth technology company,\nstrong career development opportunities and the chance to work on a category-defining product. The\ncompany combines startup-style innovation with global scale, employing more than 3,000 people\nworldwide and serving more than 1,400 customers across industries.\n* **Employees frequently highlight growth opportunities:** Celonis emphasizes internal mobility,\nleadership development and continuous learning through mentorship, training programs and\ncross-functional collaboration. Employees often describe career progression across teams, regions\nand functions.\n* **Mission-driven work:** Celonis' mission to make processes work for people, companies and the\nplanet gives employees visibility into how their work creates measurable value. The company\nreports more than $10.8 billion in customer value generated through Process Intelligence.\n* **Unique Value Engineering career paths:** Celonis is known for pioneering Value Engineering, a\ncustomer-facing discipline focused on identifying, quantifying and delivering business value.\nEmployees in these roles gain experience across analytics, strategy, process improvement and\nenterprise AI.\n* **Engineering and product innovation:** Engineering teams work on large-scale data processing,\nAI-driven business insights and Process Intelligence technology. Employees describe the\nengineering culture as highly collaborative and focused on solving complex customer challenges.\n* **Sales career development:** Celonis' BDR program provides coaching, mentorship and structured\nadvancement opportunities for early-career sales professionals. Employees frequently describe the\nexperience as fast-paced and highly developmental.\n* **Benefits and employee support:** Celonis offers healthcare benefits, parental leave, retirement\nplans, wellbeing resources and learning investments designed to support long-term employee growth\nand success.\n* **External signals:**\n* Celonis is highly rated across culture, diversity, leadership and workplace experience\ncategories. (Comparably)\n* Reviews commonly cite smart colleagues, meaningful work, growth opportunities and innovative\ntechnology as reasons employees recommend the company. (Glassdoor)\n\n**Bottom line:** Employees who recommend Celonis often point to its career growth opportunities,\ntalented colleagues, customer impact, innovative technology and strong mission. The company is\ngenerally a strong fit for people who thrive in ambitious, high-performance environments where\nlearning, ownership and measurable business outcomes are highly valued.\n\n## Celonis's Candidate Tradeoffs\n\n**If you\u2019re weighing whether Celonis is the right fit, these are the core tradeoffs to consider.**\n* Celonis places greater emphasis on autonomy paired with clear accountability and measurable\nstandards than on loosely defined roles with flexible performance expectations.\n\n## Celonis Employee Perspectives\n\nCelonis offers employees a dynamic environment where no two days are the same, combining challenging\nwork with constant opportunities to learn from colleagues across different backgrounds and areas of\nexpertise. Employees describe the experience as energizing, collaborative and intellectually\nstimulating, with exposure to new ideas and perspectives on a daily basis.\n\n\u201cEach day at Celonis is different. There\u2019s always a new challenge and new people to work with, which\nkeeps me thinking, engaged and energized. I work with individuals from all backgrounds who each have\ndifferent, invaluable skills, and they teach me something personally and professionally on a daily\nbasis.\u201d\n\n[Priya Shah]\nPriya Shah, Enterprise Account Executive\nFrom the article: [Process data meets its match: How Celonis is revolutionizing how businesses\noperate ][35]\n\n## Celonis Employee Reviews\n\nOur NYC office is a super collaborative, high-energy, unique atmosphere. You can be sure to find\nbeautiful fresh flowers and live plants in the lobby, along with unlimited snacks, lunches &\nactivities that bring Celonauts together weekly. Our open floor plan makes it easy to meet new\npeople every day, and you can\u2019t beat the 360 views of Manhattan!\n\n[Laura]\nLaura, People Manager\nLaura, People Manager\n\nHelping people solve challenges using Celonis is a hugely rewarding experience - and the fact that I\ndo this with my coworkers who are also my friends makes it that much better.\n\n[Sanat]\nSanat, Account Executive\nSanat, Account Executive\n\nI\u2019ve been at Celonis for over 2 years and it\u2019s been a great experience being a part of a company\nwith a tremendous growth trajectory. I\u2019m grateful to be working with a great team that brings value\nto the company through our analytics and insights.\n\n[Ankita]\nAnkita, Team Lead Data Analytics\nAnkita, Team Lead Data Analytics\n\n## What People Are Saying About Celonis\n* Market Position & Stability: The company is widely positioned as a category leader in process\nintelligence, with a platform used by large enterprises and strong customer pull. Public materials\nemphasize substantial funding and a recognizable standing that many candidates view as signals of\nscale and stability.\n* Learning & Development: Structured learning programs and internal communities enable rapid\nskill-building and cross-functional exposure. Feedback suggests strong peer learning, mentorship,\nand mobility that help employees develop quickly.\n* Benefits & Perks: Benefits highlight hybrid flexibility, generous parental leave, wellness\nsupport, and equity participation for full-time employees. Office-based perks such as catered\nlunches, social events, and signature company gatherings contribute to a high-touch workplace\nexperience.\n\n## Celonis's Awards\n\n[award][award][award][award]\n[award][award][award][award][award]\n\n## Celonis's Benefits\n\n### Employee Satisfaction & Recognition\n\nEmployee feedback used to shape policies and strategy\n\nEncourages autonomy and ownership from employees\n\nEstablished employee awards to honor work and contributions\n\nProvides modern technology across teams\n\n### Promotion Policies\n\nDocumented career progression frameworks\n\nDocumented path to leadership development\n\nEncourages lateral mobility to expand skills and impact\n\nPosts new positions internally and encourages employees to apply\n\nPrioritizes promotion advancement based on impact\n\nPrioritizes promotion advancement based on long-term contribution\n\nPromote from within\n\nProvides customized development tracks\n\n### Work Environment\n\nDefined values and mission statements\n\nDocumented operating principles\n\nHosts in-person all-hands meetings\n\nOur All-Hands meetings, held both in person and virtually, often feature one of our founders and the\nexecutive leadership team\u2014with free lunch provided for in-person attendees.\n\nHosts in-person revenue kickoff meetings\n\nImplements team-based strategic planning\n\nLeadership encourages open, transparent debate\n\nLeadership is transparent and communicative\n\nMistakes are treated as learning opportunities\n\nOpen office floor plan to encourage communication and collaboration\n\nPolicies promote a low-ego, team-driven culture\n\nPrioritizes mission-driven work in decision-making processes\n\nPrioritizes real-world impact of work in decision-making processes\n\nUses an OKR operational model to clearly define goals and priorities\n\nUtilizes an open door policy that encourages accessibility\n\n### Work Hours Policies\n\nAsync-friendly policies, culture that encourage work flexibility\n\nEstablished expectations f"
