            "url": "https://builtin.com/company/cencora/faq/workplace-perception",
            "text": "[[Built In Logo] [Built In Logo]][1][Companies][2][Jobs][3][Articles][4]\n[View All Jobs][5]\n[ Join ][6]\n[ Log In ][7]\n[ For Employers ][8]\n[ Companies ][9] [ Cencora ][10]\n\n## Cencora\n\nSave Saved\nConshohocken\nTotal Offices: **15**\n51,000 Total Employees\nYear Founded: 2023\n[View Website][11]\nWe're Hiring!\n[ Engineering **55** ][12] [ Data & Analytics **15** ][13] [ Cybersecurity **14** ][14] [ Operations\n& Support **14** ][15] [ Customer Success & Experience **3** ][16] [ Product Management **3** ][17]\n[ Program & Project Management **3** ][18] [ Consulting **2** ][19] [ AI & Machine Learning **1**\n][20]\n[View all jobs][21]\n* Overview\n* Jobs 112\n* Offices\n* Teams\n* Culture\n* Articles\n* Company Insights\n* [ Working at Cencora ][22]\n* [ Culture & Values ][23]\n* [ Inclusion & Diversity ][24]\n* [ Career Growth & Development ][25]\n* [ Compensation & Benefits ][26]\n* [ Work-Life Balance & Wellbeing ][27]\n* [ Leadership & Management ][28]\n* [ Innovation, Technology & Agility ][29]\n* [ Mission, Purpose & Impact ][30]\n* [ Stability & Growth ][31]\n\n# What's It Like to Work at Cencora?\n\nUpdated on April 24, 2026\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n## What practices at Cencora support employee job satisfaction?\n\nJob Satisfaction\n\nCencora supports employee job satisfaction through practices that combine purpose-driven work,\ncareer growth opportunities, supportive leadership, and a collaborative global culture.\n* **Purpose and impact: **Employees are motivated by work that directly contributes to improving\nhealth outcomes and expanding access to care. Cencora\u2019s purpose\u2014\u201cWe are united in our\nresponsibility to create healthier futures\u201d\u2014is reflected in day-to-day roles, with employees\nnoting that their work \u201cimpacts society\u201d and helps patients receive critical medications (Cencora\ncompany overview; employee workplace perception quotes).\n* **Growth and career ownership:** Cencora emphasizes continuous development through internships,\nco-op programs, mentorship, and learning resources. Employees highlight strong internal mobility\nand career ownership, noting \u201cthe sky is the limit\u201d and that resources are widely available to\nsupport advancement (Cencora early careers content; career growth quotes).\n* **Supportive management and teams: **Employee feedback consistently points to approachable\nleadership and collaborative teams. Reviews describe \u201csupportive management,\u201d \u201cgreat teams,\u201d and\nenvironments where colleagues are willing to help each other succeed, while leadership messaging\nemphasizes open dialogue and trust (Glassdoor reviews; Comparably reviews; leadership quotes).\n* **Work-life balance and flexibility: **Many employees report strong work-life balance, manageable\nschedules, and flexibility depending on role. Reviews highlight \u201cgreat work-life balance,\u201d\n\u201cschedule flexibility,\u201d and supportive environments, though some roles can be fast-paced during\npeak periods (Indeed reviews; Glassdoor reviews).\n* **Comprehensive benefits and wellbeing support: **Cencora offers a broad total rewards package\nincluding healthcare, retirement matching, wellness programs, and financial support. Employees\ncite \u201cgreat benefits and 401(k)\u201d and solid compensation packages, with additional support such as\nstudent loan matching and assistance programs helping reduce financial stress (Cencora benefits\ncontent; Comparably reviews; Glassdoor reviews).\n* **Global, inclusive, and collaborative culture: **With 51,000+ employees across 50+ countries,\nCencora fosters a diverse and inclusive environment where teamwork and knowledge sharing are\ncentral. Employees describe a culture of belonging, respect, and collaboration supported by\nemployee resource groups and global initiatives (Cencora company overview; culture article;\nemployee culture quotes).\n* **Innovation and meaningful work environment: **Employees contribute to large-scale initiatives\nsuch as digital transformation, AI-driven solutions, and global healthcare supply chain\noperations. The company\u2019s adoption of agile and product-based ways of working enables teams to\ncollaborate effectively and deliver impactful results (Cencora sustainability report; tech team\npositioning; innovation quotes).\n* **Listen-and-act culture: **Cencora promotes a listening culture where employee feedback is\nencouraged and used to improve programs and workplace experience. Employees note that management\nis \u201cwilling to listen\u201d and responsive to input, reinforcing trust and continuous improvement\n(Cencora culture messaging; Comparably reviews).\n* **Key Tech Hubs: **Cencora\u2019s primary tech hubs include Conshohocken, PA, Carrollton, Texas, and\nPune, India, where they are actively hiring for new roles.** **\n\n**Employee Perspective**\n\n\u201cIf you want to work at a company that cares about its people, that gives you opportunities to grow\nand advance and expand, Cencora is your place.\u201d\n\n\u2014 Jill S., Executive Assistant, Supply Chain (employee workplace perception quotes)\n\n**At-a-Glance**\n* **Primary satisfaction drivers: **Purpose-driven work, career growth, supportive teams, global**\n**collaboration (employee reviews; culture content)\n* **Core benefits: **Healthcare coverage, 401(k) matching, wellness programs, student loan matching,\nPTO and flexibility (Cencora benefits content)\n* **Feedback culture: **Listening culture with open dialogue and leadership accessibility (Cencora\nculture messaging; leadership quotes)\n* **Employee sentiment: **Reviews highlight strong teamwork, meaningful work, and supportive\nmanagement across platforms (Glassdoor, Comparably, Indeed reviews)\n\n**External Signals**\n\nOn external review sites, employees consistently highlight (Glassdoor, Comparably, and Indeed\nreviews):\n* Supportive and approachable leadership\n* Strong team collaboration and culture\n* Career growth opportunities and mentorship\n* Good work-life balance and benefits\n\n**Cencora workplace award recognition:**\n* Fortune 500 (#10) and Fortune Global 500 (#18) rankings, reflecting scale, stability, and global\nimpact (Cencora company overview)\n\n## Is Cencora a good place to work? Do Employees Recommend it?\n\nWillingness to Recommend\n\nCencora is generally seen as a good place to work, with employee feedback pointing to strong mission\nalignment, supportive teams, and real opportunities to grow.\n\n**Impact-Driven Work: **Employees often connect their work to healthcare impact, saying their roles\n\u201cimpact society\u201d and help deliver life-saving medications. That sense of purpose is reinforced by\nCencora\u2019s mission to create healthier futures and its scale, with 51,000+ team members across 50+\ncountries (Cencora company overview; employee workplace perception quotes; mission and purpose\nquotes).\n\n**Manager support and growth: **Employees frequently describe leadership as approachable and\nsupportive, with open dialogue, trust, and development opportunities helping people advance over\ntime. Mentorship, internal mobility, learning resources, early-career programs, and access to senior\nleaders all reinforce long-term growth (leadership quotes; career growth content; early careers\ncontent).\n\n**Why employees recommend it: **Employees most often recommend Cencora for its supportive culture\nand teamwork, career growth opportunities, work-life balance and flexibility in many roles, strong\nbenefits and financial stability, and a meaningful mission tied to healthcare impact (culture\ncontent; career growth content; benefits content).\n\n**High-caliber peers: **Employees describe a collaborative environment where knowledge sharing,\nmutual support, and teamwork are central to success. The company\u2019s global operating model, digital\ntools, and increasing use of agile ways of working help teams collaborate effectively across\nfunctions and regions (employee culture and workplace perception quotes; corporate sustainability\nreport; culture article).\n\n**External validation: **Cencora\u2019s reputation is reinforced by its Fortune 500 (#10) and Fortune\nGlobal 500 (#18) rankings, reflecting scale, stability, and global impact (Cencora company\noverview).\n\n**Key Tech Hubs: **Cencora\u2019s primary tech hubs include Conshohocken, PA, Carrollton, Texas, and\nPune, India, where they are actively hiring for new roles.\n\n**External review signals: **External reviews on Glassdoor, Comparably, and Indeed consistently\nhighlight supportive leadership, strong teamwork, career growth opportunities, work-life balance,\nand benefits. Representative comments include:\n* \u201cGreat teams with areas to grow and investment in your future\u201d (Glassdoor),\n* \u201cSenior managers are approachable and want to see you succeed\u201d (Comparably)\n* \u201cGreat work-life balance\u2026 management was approachable\u201d (Indeed).\n\n**Bottom Line: **Cencora is a strong fit for people who want purpose-driven work, supportive teams,\nand room to grow inside a large, stable global organization.\n\n## What reputation does Cencora have as a place to work?\n\nGeneral Market Perception\n\nCencora is widely regarded as a purpose-driven, global healthcare leader with a supportive culture,\nstrong teams, and meaningful career opportunities, offering stability at Fortune 10 scale alongside\nopportunities to contribute to real-world impact.\n* **Purpose-led, impact-focused culture:** Cencora\u2019s reputation is strongly tied to its mission of\nimproving health outcomes worldwide. Employees frequently describe their work as meaningful,\nemphasizing that it \u201cimpacts society\u201d and helps ensure patients receive life-saving medications.\nThis connection to purpose is a defining feature of how the company is perceived as an employer.\n* **Supportive, team-oriented environment:** Across external reviews, Cencora is consistently\ndescribed as having collaborative and supportive teams. Employees highlight \u201cgreat teams with\nareas to grow\u201d (Glassdoor) and environments where \u201ceveryone works together to get work done and to\nlearn new things\u201d (Comparably). Many also note that coworkers are approachable, knowledgeable, and\nwilling to help, reinforcing a strong team culture.\n* **Accessible leadership and people-first approach: **Employees frequently point to approachable\nand responsive leadership as a strength. Reviews note that \u201csenior managers are approachable and\nwant to see you succeed\u201d (Comparably) and that management is \u201cgood and approachable, making it\neasy to get guidance when needed\u201d (Indeed). Leadership messaging emphasizes transparency, open\ndialogue, and creating safe environments for growth.\n* **Career growth and development opportunities:** Cencora is seen as a place where employees can\nbuild and grow their careers over time. Reviews highlight \u201cplenty of room for growth and\npromotion\u201d (Indeed) and \u201cinvestment in your future\u201d (Glassdoor), while employee perspectives\nreinforce that individuals are empowered to define their own paths with access to learning\nresources, mentorship, and internal mobility.\n* **Global scale with collaborative culture:** With more than 51,000 employees across 50+ countries,\nCencora is recognized for its ability to operate at global scale while maintaining a collaborative\nand inclusive culture. Employees describe a workplace that values diverse perspectives and fosters\nconnection across regions through shared goals and communication practices.\n* **Innovation tied to real-world outcomes: **Cencora\u2019s reputation in technology and innovation is\ngrounded in its impact on healthcare delivery. Teams work on digital transformation, AI-driven\nsolutions, and supply chain innovation, with a focus on improving patient outcomes rather than\nsimply adopting new tools. This gives employees exposure to complex, high-impact work.\n* **Competitive benefits and work-life balance: **Employees frequently cite strong benefits and\nwork-life balance as positives, including healthcare, retirement matching, and schedule\nflexibility. Reviews describe \u201cgreat work-life balance\u201d and \u201cdecent pay and benefits,\u201d\ncontributing to overall job satisfaction (Indeed; Glassdoor).\n* **Key Tech Hubs: **Cencora\u2019s primary tech hubs include Conshohocken, Pa., Carrollton, Texas, and\n"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://builtin.com/company/chamberlain-group/faq/workplace-perception",
            "text": "[[Built In Logo] [Built In Logo]][1][Companies][2][Jobs][3][Articles][4]\n[View All Jobs][5]\n[ Join ][6]\n[ Log In ][7]\n[ For Employers ][8]\n[ Companies ][9] [ Chamberlain Group ][10]\n[2026 Best Places To Work Award Winner]\n[Chamberlain Group logo]\n\n## Chamberlain Group\n\nSave Saved\nOak Brook\n5,769 Total Employees\nYear Founded: 1900\n[View Website][11]\n[Chamberlain Group logo]\nWe're Hiring!\n[ Engineering **13** ][12] [ Data & Analytics **11** ][13] [ Marketing **10** ][14] [ Sales **10**\n][15] [ Finance **8** ][16] [ AI & Machine Learning **6** ][17] [ Operations & Support **5** ][18] [\nProduct Management **3** ][19] [ Customer Success & Experience **2** ][20] [ Cybersecurity **2**\n][21] [ Program & Project Management **2** ][22] [ Design **1** ][23] [ HR & Recruiting **1** ][24]\n[ Legal **1** ][25]\n[View all jobs][26]\n[2026 Best Places To Work Award Winner]\n* Overview\n* Jobs 77\n* Offices\n* Teams\n* Articles\n* Company Insights\n* [ Working at Chamberlain Group ][27]\n* [ Culture & Values ][28]\n* [ Career Growth & Development ][29]\n* [ Compensation & Benefits ][30]\n* [ Work-Life Balance & Wellbeing ][31]\n* [ Leadership & Management ][32]\n* [ Innovation, Technology & Agility ][33]\n* [ Mission, Purpose & Impact ][34]\n* [ Stability & Growth ][35]\n\n# What's It Like to Work at Chamberlain Group?\n\nUpdated on May 27, 2026\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n## What practices at Chamberlain Group support employee job satisfaction?\n\nJob Satisfaction\n\nChamberlain Group supports employee job satisfaction through meaningful work, strong career\ndevelopment, a values-driven culture, and comprehensive benefits.\n\n**Purpose-driven and impactful work:** Chamberlain Group\u2019s mission to make \u201caccess simple and\nsecure\u201d gives employees a clear sense of purpose, with work focused on intelligent access solutions\nused in 50M+ homes and across smart ecosystems.\n\n**Career growth and development: **The company emphasizes internal mobility and career ownership,\noffering leadership development, mentoring, and cross-functional opportunities.\n\n**Supportive and collaborative culture (ONETEAM): **The ONETEAM philosophy promotes shared\nownership, collaboration, and open communication, encouraging employees to contribute ideas and\nchallenge assumptions.\n\n**Values-driven ways of working: **The five core values\u2014Creative, Bold, Passionate, Authentic, and\nFun\u2014guide behaviors and decision-making, reinforcing innovation, integrity, and teamwork.\n\n**Continuous learning culture: **Employees have access to training, conferences, mentorship, Lunch &\nLearns, and tuition reimbursement, supporting ongoing development.\n\n**Comprehensive benefits and wellbeing: **Chamberlain Group offers 401(k) matching, equity, bonuses,\nhealthcare, parental leave, wellness programs, and mental health support, along with PTO and onsite\nwellbeing resources.\n\n**Connection and community engagement: **Employees engage in ERGs, volunteer programs, and company\nevents, reinforcing connection and purpose.\n\n**Recognition and feedback: **Quarterly engagement surveys and employee awards support recognition\nand continuous improvement.\n\nOverall, Chamberlain Group supports job satisfaction through meaningful work, growth opportunities,\na collaborative culture, and strong benefits.\n\n## Is Chamberlain Group a good place to work? Do Employees Recommend it?\n\nWillingness to Recommend\n\nChamberlain Group is widely seen as a strong place to work, especially for those seeking innovation,\ngrowth, and meaningful impact.\n\n**Meaningful and innovative work: **Employees contribute to intelligent access technology used in\n50M+ homes and AI-powered solutions like the myQ ecosystem.\n\n**Strong career growth opportunities: **The company promotes internal mobility and development, with\nemployees taking on new roles and building skills across functions.\n\n**Supportive teams and leadership: **Employees highlight mentorship, accessible leadership, and\nstrong cross-functional collaboration.\n\n**Culture of ownership and empowerment:** Employees are encouraged to \u201clead from any seat,\u201d take\ninitiative, and drive impact early in their careers.\n\n**Work-life balance and benefits: **Flexible work options, PTO, wellness programs, and family\nbenefits support employee wellbeing.\n\n**Values-driven and inclusive environment: **The company prioritizes diversity, inclusion, and\nconnection, helping employees feel supported and engaged.\n\nOverall, Chamberlain Group is considered a strong employer for individuals seeking growth,\ninnovation, and a collaborative culture.\n\n## What reputation does Chamberlain Group have as a place to work?\n\nGeneral Market Perception\n\nChamberlain Group has a strong reputation as an innovative, growth-oriented company with a\ncollaborative and people-focused culture.\n\n**Leader in intelligent access technology: **Chamberlain Group is known for its leadership in smart\naccess solutions, with products in 51M+ homes and millions of myQ users.\n\n**Transformation and innovation: **The company is recognized for shifting from hardware to a\nsoftware-enabled platform, leveraging AI, data, and partnerships with companies like Amazon and\nTesla.\n\n**Strong culture and values: **The ONETEAM philosophy and five core values define collaboration,\ninnovation, and trust.\n\n**Commitment to career growth:** Chamberlain Group is known for internal mobility, leadership\ndevelopment, and cross-functional learning opportunities.\n\n**Balance of stability and innovation: **With a long history and Blackstone backing since 2021, the\ncompany combines stability with a fast-paced, tech-driven environment.\n\n**Focus on people and inclusion: **The company emphasizes diversity, inclusion, and employee\nconnection, supporting a positive workplace culture.\n\nOverall, Chamberlain Group is viewed as a forward-thinking employer where employees can grow their\ncareers while working on impactful, innovative technology.\n\n## What tradeoffs might come with working at Chamberlain Group?\n\nTradeoffs\n\nOne key tradeoff is customer-driven innovation vs. unconstrained experimentation. Chamberlain Group\nemphasizes customer-driven innovation that delivers meaningful, real-world impact and measurable\nvalue, while exploratory initiatives are more selectively prioritized. This results in practical,\nhigh-impact products, though innovation is often closely tied to customer needs rather than purely\nexperimental ideas.\n\nAnother tradeoff is cross-functional collaboration vs. siloed execution. Chamberlain Group places\ngreater emphasis on cross-functional collaboration that drives stronger, more integrated outcomes\nthan on siloed, team-by-team execution. This leads to better, more cohesive solutions, though it can\nrequire coordination across multiple teams.\n\nEmployees may also experience employee-driven career ownership vs. highly structured career paths.\nChamberlain Group places greater emphasis on employee-driven career ownership than on highly\nstructured, centrally defined career planning processes. This enables flexible, personalized growth,\nthough it requires individuals to be proactive in shaping their careers.\n\nAnother tradeoff is startup-style agility vs. highly defined structure. Chamberlain Group places\ngreater emphasis on startup-style agility and hands-on exposure than on highly defined scope and\nformalized planning. This creates opportunities to take on broader responsibilities, though\nprocesses and roles may continue evolving.\n\nThere is also a tradeoff between flexibility and autonomy vs. standardized schedules. Chamberlain\nGroup places greater emphasis on organization-wide flexibility and autonomy than on tightly\nstandardized schedules and uniform work structures. This supports balance and ownership, though it\nrequires strong self-management.\n\nFinally, autonomy vs. close oversight can be a tradeoff. Chamberlain Group emphasizes minimal\nmicromanagement and high trust, giving employees space to make decisions and move quickly, though\nthat model favors self-directed, intrinsically motivated contributors.\n\n**Great match for candidates who prefer:**\n* Working on real-world, customer-focused technology\n* Collaborating across cross-functional teams\n* Owning and shaping their own career path\n* Operating in a flexible, fast-evolving environment\n* Having autonomy and accountability in their work\n\n**Working here means:**\n* Delivering practical innovation tied to real customer needs\n* Collaborating across teams to build integrated solutions\n* Navigating a growth-stage, transforming organization\n* Taking initiative and driving your own development\n* Balancing flexibility with ownership and accountability\n\n## Chamberlain Group's Candidate Tradeoffs\n\n**If you\u2019re weighing whether Chamberlain Group is the right fit, these are the core tradeoffs to\nconsider.**\n* Chamberlain Group emphasizes minimal micromanagement and high trust, giving employees space to\nmake decisions and move quickly, though that model favors self-directed, intrinsically motivated\ncontributors.\n\n## Chamberlain Group Employee Reviews\n\nI've been able to work on something different and more advanced every year. Recently, I got an\nopportunity to take a big pivot in my career; I moved out of industrial design and into being the\nManager of Inclusive Employee Experience where I lead diversity, equity and inclusion practices at\nthe company.\n\n[Corey]\nCorey, Manager of Inclusive Employee Experience\nCorey, Manager of Inclusive Employee Experience\n\n\u201cWe\u2019re trying to make access simple and secure for our customers. For us, this means creating\ndelightful, simple and intuitive mobile apps that are also stable, secure and scalable. We\u2019re\nconsistently evaluating and updating our processes, technology and skills to support our growth.\u201d\n\n[Reshmi]\nReshmi, Software Engineering Manager, Front End\nReshmi, Software Engineering Manager, Front End\n\n## What People Are Saying About Chamberlain Group\n* Mission & Purpose: Work ties directly to widely used intelligent\u2011access products and the myQ\nplatform, creating tangible, real\u2011world impact. Purpose and ONETEAM values are emphasized across\nLife at CG materials.\n* Benefits & Perks: Pay and benefits are considered competitive, including medical/401(k), paid\nparental leave, and standard PTO. Programs and resources highlighted publicly aim to support\nemployees\u2019 overall experience.\n* Team Support: Collaboration and accessibility are emphasized, with hybrid norms and an\namenity\u2011rich campus designed to bring teams together. Colleagues are described as approachable and\nsupportive within an ONETEAM culture.\n\n## Chamberlain Group's Awards\n\n[award][award][award][award]\n[award][award][award][award][award]\n\n## Chamberlain Group's Benefits\n\n### Employee Satisfaction & Recognition\n\nEmployee feedback used to shape policies and strategy\n\nEncourages autonomy and ownership from employees\n\nEstablished employee awards to honor work and contributions\n\nProvides resources to build team camaraderie\n\nQuarterly engagement surveys to gauge employee satisfaction\n\n### Promotion Policies\n\nEncourages lateral mobility to expand skills and impact\n\nCG offers traditional movement, but also encourages lateral mobility, professional development, and\nbold pivots to expand skills and impact.\n\nPrioritizes promotion advancement based on impact\n\nAt CG, employees own their careers. No two paths are alike, and growth is not a one\u2011directional\nladder.\n\nPromote from within\n\nProvides customized development tracks\n\n### Work Environment\n\nDefined policies promoting a professional, respectful workplace\n\nDefined values and mission statements\n\nHosts in-person all-hands meetings\n\nImplements team-based strategic planning\n\nLeadership encourages open, transparent debate\n\nLeadership is transparent and communicative\n\nMistakes are treated as learning opportunities\n\nPolicies promote a low-ego, team-driven culture\n\nPrioritizes mission-driven work in decision-making processes\n\nPrioritizes real-world impact of work in decision-making processes\n\nPromotes a people-first, social culture\n\nUses an OKR operational model to clearly define g"
