            "url": "https://builtin.com/company/comcast-3/faq/workplace-perception",
            "text": "[[Built In Logo] [Built In Logo]][1][Companies][2][Jobs][3][Articles][4]\n[View All Jobs][5]\n[ Join ][6]\n[ Log In ][7]\n[ For Employers ][8]\n[ Companies ][9] [ Comcast ][10]\n\n## Comcast\n\nSave Saved\nPhiladelphia\nTotal Offices: **18**\n115,000 Total Employees\nYear Founded: 1963\n[View Website][11]\nWe're Hiring!\n[ Sales **99+** ][12] [ Engineering **83** ][13] [ Data & Analytics **20** ][14] [ Cybersecurity\n**9** ][15] [ AI & Machine Learning **9** ][16] [ Marketing **8** ][17] [ Operations & Support **3**\n][18] [ Customer Success & Experience **2** ][19] [ Program & Project Management **2** ][20] [\nFinance **1** ][21]\n[View all jobs][22]\n* Overview\n* Jobs 328\n* Offices\n* Articles\n* Company Insights\n* [ Working at Comcast ][23]\n* [ Culture & Values ][24]\n* [ Career Growth & Development ][25]\n* [ Compensation & Benefits ][26]\n* [ Work-Life Balance & Wellbeing ][27]\n* [ Leadership & Management ][28]\n* [ Innovation, Technology & Agility ][29]\n* [ Stability & Growth ][30]\n\n# What's It Like to Work at Comcast?\n\nUpdated on May 08, 2026\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n## What practices at Comcast support employee job satisfaction?\n\nJob Satisfaction\n\nAt[ Comcast][31], employee job satisfaction is driven by meaningful work, strong collaboration and a\nculture that encourages people to contribute ideas and build solutions that impact millions of\ncustomers.[ Teams][32] across the company work on advanced platforms spanning connectivity, media\nand advertising technology bringing together cross-functional groups including engineers, product\nleaders, analysts, and more - to collaborate and solve complex problems.. Employees often highlight\nthe opportunity to work with cutting-edge tools \u2014 including artificial intelligence, machine\nlearning, cloud infrastructure and large-scale data systems \u2014 while contributing to products and\nservices used across the global media ecosystem.\n\nComcast also supports employee satisfaction through[ career growth programs][33], mentorship and a\nculture that encourages continuous learning. Employees have access to professional development\nresources such as tuition reimbursement, certifications, conferences and mentorship opportunities,\nalong with internal mobility that allows people to explore different roles across Comcast\u2019s\nbusinesses.[ Comprehensive benefits][34] further support employee well-being, including healthcare\ncoverage, financial planning resources, parental and family support programs, wellness tools and\nemployee resource groups. Together, these practices create an environment where employees can grow\ntheir careers while feeling supported personally and professionally.\n\n**Employee Perspective**\n\n\u201cI appreciate how supportive, respectful and inclusive our teammates are. This is a place where\neveryone\u2019s contributions feel valued, respected and celebrated.\u201d\n\n\u2014Gary Bailey, Sales, Comcast Advertising\n\n**At-a-Glance**\n* **Primary satisfaction drivers:** Meaningful work, innovation and collaboration across teams\n* **Core benefits:** Comprehensive healthcare coverage, parental leave and family support programs,\nfinancial wellness resources and employee discounts\n* **Career development:** Mentorship, internal mobility opportunities, conferences and learning\nprograms\n* **Community & culture:** Employee resource groups, volunteer initiatives, recognition programs and\nopen collaboration across teams.\n\nExternal Signals\n* **Great Company Culture: **Employees give Comcast high marks for its overall culture, ranking it\nin the top 30 percent of companies on review platforms like Comparably.\n* **Innovate Technology:** Engineers and data teams highlight opportunities to work with AI, machine\nlearning, cloud technologies and large-scale data systems across Comcast\u2019s platforms.\n* **Career Mobility:** Employees report career mobility across Comcast\u2019s many business units,\nallowing exploration of new roles and skill development.\n* **Collaboration:** Collaborative Environment: Teams emphasize collaboration across engineering,\nproduct and sales functions, along with mentorship and leadership visibility that support career\ngrowth. Employees on review sites describe a supportive atmosphere, with strong team dynamics\n(Glassdoor).\n\n## Is Comcast a good place to work? Do Employees Recommend it?\n\nWillingness to Recommend\n\n[Comcast\u2019s][35] employee experience is shaped by a culture that emphasizes collaboration, innovation\nand opportunities to build impactful technology and media products at scale. Employees across the\norganization highlight the ability to work on platforms that serve millions of customers, from\nconnectivity and platform services like Xfinity and Comcast Business to advanced advertising\ntechnology through brands like Comcast Advertising, FreeWheel, Effectv and AudienceXpress. Teams\nfrequently cite the collaborative environment and the chance to contribute ideas across functions as\nimportant parts of why they enjoy working at Comcast.\n\n[Internal career mobility][36] and professional development also contribute to employees\nrecommending Comcast as a place to build a long-term career. The company provides mentorship\nprograms, learning resources, conferences and tuition reimbursement, along with internal gig\nopportunities and cross-team projects that allow employees to explore different parts of the\nbusiness. Comprehensive benefits \u2014 including healthcare coverage, parental and family support\nprograms, financial wellness resources and employee resource groups \u2014 further support employee\nwell-being and engagement.\n\nEmployees also describe a workplace culture where colleagues support each other and encourage\nlearning across teams. Engineers, product leaders and sales professionals highlight the opportunity\nto work with advanced technologies such as AI, machine learning and large-scale data systems while\ncollaborating with teams across Comcast\u2019s businesses.\n\n**At-a-Glance**\n* **Career growth:** Mentorship, internal mobility, conferences, certifications and tuition\nreimbursement\n* **Innovation environment:** Opportunities to work with AI, machine learning, cloud infrastructure\nand large-scale data systems\n* **Employee community:** Employee resource groups, volunteer initiatives and collaborative teams\n* **Benefits support:** Healthcare coverage, parental and family support programs, financial\nwellness resources and employee discounts\n\n**External Signals**\n* **Great Company Culture:** Employees give Comcast high marks for its overall culture, ranking it\nin the top 30 percent of companies on review platforms like Comparably.\n* **Large-Scale Tech Projects:** Employees across Comcast businesses highlight opportunities to work\non large-scale technology platforms and advertising systems that process billions of events and\npower media and data insights.\n* **Collaborative Environment:** Teams emphasize collaboration across engineering, product and sales\nfunctions, along with mentorship and leadership visibility that support career growth. Employees\non review sites describe a supportive atmosphere, with strong team dynamics (Glassdoor).\n* **Internal Mobility: **Employees also point to internal mobility and learning opportunities as\nreasons they recommend Comcast as a place to build a career.\n\n## What reputation does Comcast have as a place to work?\n\nGeneral Market Perception\n\n[Comcast][37] is widely recognized as a large-scale technology, media and connectivity company where\nemployees can build meaningful careers while working on products that impact millions of customers.\nAcross the organization, employees describe a collaborative culture where engineers, product\nleaders,[ data scientists][38] and sales teams work together to develop solutions spanning\nconnectivity services, streaming and advanced advertising technologies. Teams within businesses like\nComcast Advertising, FreeWheel, Effectv and AudienceXpress frequently highlight the opportunity to\nwork with emerging technologies such as artificial intelligence, machine learning and large-scale\ndata platforms that power the evolving connected-TV ecosystem.\n\nEmployee perspectives also emphasize opportunities for[ career growth][39] and learning within\nComcast\u2019s broad ecosystem of businesses. The company\u2019s size enables employees to explore internal\nmobility, cross-team collaboration and leadership exposure while developing new technical and\nprofessional skills. Mentorship networks, professional development programs and learning resources \u2014\nincluding conferences, certifications and tuition reimbursement \u2014 support long-term career\ndevelopment and contribute to Comcast\u2019s reputation as a place where employees can continue growing\nover time.\n\nComcast\u2019s reputation as an employer is also reinforced by a[ culture][40] that prioritizes\ninclusion, collaboration and community impact. Employees highlight supportive colleagues, employee\nresource groups and volunteer opportunities as important parts of the workplace experience.[\nComprehensive benefits][41] \u2014 including healthcare coverage, financial wellness resources, parental\nand family support programs and employee discounts \u2014 further contribute to the company\u2019s standing as\nan employer that invests in the well-being of its workforce.\n\nLeadership also reinforces this reputation by encouraging innovation and empowering teams to\nexperiment with new ideas and technologies. Employees frequently describe working on cutting-edge\nplatforms and solving complex challenges alongside experienced colleagues and leaders who support\nlearning and professional growth.\n\n**At-a-Glance**\n* **Workplace reputation:** Large-scale technology and media company offering meaningful work and\ncollaboration\n* **Innovation environment:** Teams working with AI, machine learning, advanced analytics and\nlarge-scale data platforms\n* **Career development:** Mentorship programs, conferences, certifications, tuition reimbursement\nand internal mobility opportunities\n* **Employee community: **Employee resource groups, volunteer opportunities and cross-team\ncollaboration\n* **Benefits support:** Healthcare coverage, parental and family support programs, financial\nwellness resources and employee discounts\n\n**External Signals**\n* **Great Company Culture:** Employees give Comcast high marks for its overall culture, ranking it\nin the top 30 percent of companies on review platforms like Comparably.\n* **Large-Scale Tech Projects:** Employees across Comcast businesses highlight opportunities to work\non large-scale technology platforms and advertising systems that process billions of events and\npower media and data insights.\n* **Collaborative Environment:** Teams emphasize collaboration across engineering, product and sales\nfunctions, along with mentorship and leadership visibility that support career growth. Employees\non review sites describe a supportive atmosphere, with strong team dynamics (Glassdoor).\n* **Internal Mobility:** Employees also point to internal mobility and learning opportunities as\nreasons they recommend Comcast as a place to build a career.\n\n**Employee Perspective:**\n\n\u201cComcast\u2019s local investment and expertise in Philadelphia powers the next-generation Internet\nexperience for our customers today and well into the future.\u201d\n\n- Dan Bonelli, Comcast Regional Senior Vice President\n\n\u201cThrough pairing our global platforms and local partnerships, we\u2019re turning major sports moments\ninto meaningful opportunities for young leaders, their families, and innovators everywhere.\u201d\n\n-Dalila Scott-Wilson, Chief Impact & Inclusion Officer, Comcast Corporate\n\n\u201cThe technology we\u2019ve put in place to enable the delivery of programming in \u2018RealTime4K\u2019, combined\nwith Dolby Vision and Dolby Atmos further differentiates Xfinity from the competition by offering\nsporting events, like the Super Bowl and Olympics, in the fastest and most immersive way possible.\nOnly made possible by our WiFi, network and entertainment platforms working better together.\u201d\n\n-Fraiser Sterling, Global Chief Product Officer, Comcast\n\n## What tradeoffs might come with working at Comcast"
          },
