            "url": "https://builtin.com/company/cox-enterprises/faq/workplace-perception",
            "text": "[[Built In Logo] [Built In Logo]][1][Companies][2][Jobs][3][Articles][4]\n[View All Jobs][5]\n[ Join ][6]\n[ Log In ][7]\n[ For Employers ][8]\n[ Companies ][9] [ Cox Enterprises ][10]\n[Cox employees working on campus]\n\n## Cox Enterprises\n\nSave Saved\nAtlanta\nTotal Offices: **12**\n50,000 Total Employees\nYear Founded: 1898\n[View Website][11]\nWe're Hiring!\n[ Sales **90** ][12] [ Engineering **58** ][13] [ HR & Recruiting **36** ][14] [ Product Management\n**21** ][15] [ Consulting **20** ][16] [ Operations & Support **17** ][17] [ Customer Success &\nExperience **11** ][18] [ Program & Project Management **11** ][19] [ Data & Analytics **10** ][20]\n[ AI & Machine Learning **7** ][21] [ Marketing **7** ][22] [ Finance **5** ][23] [ Cybersecurity\n**3** ][24]\n[View all jobs][25]\n[Cox employees working on campus]\n* Overview\n* Jobs 298\n* Offices\n* Teams\n* Articles\n* Company Insights\n* [ Working at Cox Enterprises ][26]\n* [ Culture & Values ][27]\n* [ Inclusion & Diversity ][28]\n* [ Career Growth & Development ][29]\n* [ Compensation & Benefits ][30]\n* [ Work-Life Balance & Wellbeing ][31]\n* [ Leadership & Management ][32]\n* [ Innovation, Technology & Agility ][33]\n* [ Mission, Purpose & Impact ][34]\n* [ Stability & Growth ][35]\n\n# What's It Like to Work at Cox Enterprises?\n\nUpdated on April 16, 2026\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n## What practices at Cox Enterprises support employee job satisfaction?\n\nJob Satisfaction\n\nAt [Cox Enterprises][36], job satisfaction is driven by a combination of meaningful work, steady\ncareer growth opportunities, and a people-first culture that emphasizes flexibility, inclusion, and\nemployee voice. Employees consistently connect their work to a broader purpose \u2014 whether that\u2019s\nadvancing [AI innovation][37], improving customer experiences, or contributing to community\ninitiatives like expanding digital access. This sense of impact is reinforced by a collaborative\nenvironment where teams work cross-functionally, ideas are encouraged, and employees feel empowered\nto contribute and grow.\n\nLeadership plays a central role in sustaining satisfaction through a [feedback-driven culture][38]\nwhere employee input directly shapes workplace improvements, [benefits][39], and ways of working.\nManagers prioritize mentorship, career development, and creating opportunities for employees to\nsucceed, while resources like Learn@Cox and initiatives like Cox Gigs enable continuous learning and\nadvancement. Flexible work arrangements and comprehensive benefits \u2014 from parental leave to wellness\nresources \u2014 help employees thrive at every stage of life, both professionally and personally.\n\nCox Enterprises is consistently recognized across major platforms, including Forbes (Best Employers,\nCompany Culture, Tech Workers), Fortune (Most Innovative Companies), Glassdoor (Best Places to\nWork), and USA Today Top Workplaces. It has also earned Great Place to Work certification and\nmultiple awards for work-life flexibility, employee well-being, and veteran support.\n\n**Employee Perspective**\n\n\u201cI can\u2019t imagine working anywhere else. Cox Automotive is a fantastic company to work for. We have a\ngreat culture. We care about our customers and team members. We drive positive impact for the\nautomotive industry and our communities, and we have fun using innovative technologies to achieve\nour goals.\u201d\n\n\u2014 Benjamin Flusberg, Chief Data Officer, Cox Enterprises\n\n**At-a-Glance**\n* **Primary satisfaction drivers:** Meaningful, purpose-driven work; career growth and advancement;\ncollaborative and inclusive culture\n* **Core benefits:** Flexible/hybrid work, generous PTO, parental leave, comprehensive healthcare,\n401(k) with company match, wellness programs, tuition reimbursement\n* **Feedback rhythm:** Ongoing employee feedback loops with leadership action (surveys, direct input\nshaping benefits and workplace practices)\n* **Survey insight:** Employees highlight feeling valued, supported by leadership, and empowered to\ngrow and make an impact\n\n**External Signals**\n* **Values-based Culture:** 80% of employees on external review sites would recommend Cox\nEnterprises as an employer, with reviewers highlighting the values-based culture and welcoming\nenvironment. Overall, employees rate Cox Enterprises 4.2 out of 5 stars. (Glassdoor 2026).\n* **Supportive Work Environment: **Employees on external review sites also describe Cox Enterprises\nas a supportive work environment, with one reviewer stating, \u201cThere have been ups and downs\nthroughout the years, but this company really values its employees and their career goals.\u201d\nOverall, 76% of employees surveyed hold a positive sentiment for the company (Comparably 2026).\n\n* Forbes (Best Employers, Company Culture, Tech Workers).\n* Fortune Most Innovative Companies.\n* Glassdoor Best Places to Work.\n* USA Today Top Workplaces.\n* Great Place to Work certification.\n\n## Is Cox Enterprises a good place to work? Do Employees Recommend it?\n\nWillingness to Recommend\n\n[Cox Enterprises][40] is widely regarded as a great place to work, with employee sentiment\nreflecting high levels of satisfaction driven by meaningful work, supportive leadership, and\nlong-term career growth opportunities. Employees consistently highlight the company\u2019s people-first\nculture, where flexibility, inclusion and authenticity are prioritized, and where individuals feel\nempowered to contribute ideas, shape their careers and make a tangible impact. The company\u2019s\npurpose-driven mission \u2014 focused on building a better future for this generation and the next \u2014 also\nreinforces a strong sense of pride and connection to work.\n\nEmployees frequently point to the combination of stability and opportunity as a key differentiator.\nAs a 127-year-old, family-owned organization, Cox offers long-term security alongside continuous\ninnovation across industries like automotive, cleantech and agriculture. This is paired with a\nfeedback-driven leadership culture in which employee input directly influences workplace\nimprovements, as well as strong investment in development through mentorship, internal mobility and\nlearning programs. Together, these practices create an environment where employees feel valued,\nsupported and motivated to stay and grow.\n\n**Employee Perspective**\n\n\u201cI\u2019m proud to work here. I have stayed here because I have yet to be convinced by anybody that\nthere\u2019s any better company out there to go work with.\u201d\n\n\u2014 John Chapman, National Client Sales Director, Cox Enterprises\n\n**At-a-Glance**\n* **Primary satisfaction drivers:** Supportive culture, meaningful work, career growth and\nadvancement\n* **Core benefits:** Flexible/hybrid work, generous PTO, parental leave, comprehensive healthcare,\n401(k) with company match, wellness and financial support\n* **Feedback rhythm:** Continuous employee feedback with leadership action (surveys, direct input\nshaping programs, and [benefits][41])\n* **Survey insight:** Employees report feeling valued, heard, and supported, with a strong pride and\nloyalty to the organization\n\n**External Signals**\n\nCox Enterprises is consistently recognized by leading organizations for its workplace quality and\nculture, including:\n* **Values-based Culture:** 80% of employees on external review sites would recommend Cox\nEnterprises as an employer, with reviewers highlighting the values-based culture and welcoming\nenvironment. Overall, employees rate Cox Enterprises 4.2 out of 5 stars. (Glassdoor 2026).\n* **Supportive Work Environment:** Employees on external review sites also describe Cox Enterprises\nas a supportive work environment, with one reviewer stating, \u201cThere have been ups and downs\nthroughout the years, but this company really values its employees and their career goals.\u201d\nOverall, 76% of employees surveyed hold a positive sentiment for the company (Comparably 2026).\n\n* Fortune Most Innovative Companies; Best Workplaces in Technology; Best Employers for New Grads\n* Forbes America\u2019s Best Employers for Tech Workers, Company Culture, and Large Employers\n* Glassdoor Best Places to Work; Best Place to Work in Tech & AI; Consumer Services\n* Built In Best Places to Work (2026)\n\n## What reputation does Cox Enterprises have as a place to work?\n\nGeneral Market Perception\n\n[Cox Enterprises][42] has a strong reputation as a people-first employer that combines long-term\nstability with continuous innovation. As a 127-year-old, family-owned company, it is known for\noffering employees both security and opportunity \u2014 providing a stable foundation while investing in\nemerging technologies like AI, [cybersecurity][43] and cleantech. Employees often describe the\ncompany as a place where meaningful work, collaboration and purpose intersect, with many\nhighlighting the ability to make a real impact on customers, communities and industries.\n\nThe company is also recognized for its inclusive, [feedback-driven culture][44] and commitment to\nemployee growth. Employees consistently point to supportive leadership, strong mentorship and clear\ncareer pathways as defining aspects of the experience. Resources like Learn@Cox, along with internal\nmobility opportunities and leadership development initiatives, reinforce a culture where employees\nare encouraged to grow and evolve over time. Combined with flexible work practices, [comprehensive\nbenefits][45] and a strong emphasis on well-being, Cox is widely viewed as a workplace where people\ncan build long-term, fulfilling careers.\n\nExternally, Cox\u2019s reputation is reinforced by consistent recognition across major workplace and\ninnovation rankings. These awards highlight strengths in company culture, flexibility, technology\ninnovation and employee experience, further validating employee sentiment and positioning Cox as a\ncompetitive employer across industries.\n\n**Employee Perspective**\n\n\u201cI can\u2019t imagine working anywhere else. Cox Automotive is a fantastic company to work for. We have a\ngreat culture. We care about our customers and team members. We drive positive impact for the\nautomotive industry and our communities, and we have fun using innovative technologies to achieve\nour goals.\u201d\n\n\u2014 Benjamin Flusberg, Chief Data Officer, Cox Enterprises\n\n**At-a-Glance**\n* **Reputation highlights: **People-first culture, strong innovation reputation, long-term\nstability, and career growth opportunities\n* **Employee sentiment themes:** Feeling valued, supported by leadership, empowered to grow, and\nconnected to meaningful work\n* **Career signals:** High internal mobility, mentorship culture, continuous learning and\ndevelopment investment\n* **Recognition areas:** Innovation, company culture, flexibility, inclusion and employee wellbeing.\n\n**External Awards & Recognition**\n* **Values-based Culture: **80% of employees on external review sites would recommend Cox\nEnterprises as an employer, with reviewers highlighting the values-based culture and welcoming\nenvironment. Overall, employees rate Cox Enterprises 4.2 out of 5 stars. (Glassdoor 2026).\n* **Supportive Work Environment: **Employees on external review sites also describe Cox Enterprises\nas a supportive work environment, with one reviewer stating, \u201cThere have been ups and downs\nthroughout the years, but this company really values its employees and their career goals.\u201d\nOverall, 76% of employees surveyed hold a positive sentiment for the company (Comparably 2026).\n\n* **Fortune:** Most Innovative Companies; Best Workplaces in Technology; Best Employers for New\nGrads\n* **Forbes: **America\u2019s Best Employers (Tech Workers, Company Culture, Large Employers); America\u2019s\nTop Private Companies; Dream Employers\n* **Glassdoor:** Best Places to Work; Best Place to Work in Tech & AI; Consumer Services\n* **Built In: **Best Places to Work (2026)\n\n## What tradeoffs might come with working at Cox Enterprises?\n\nTradeoffs\n\nAt [Cox Enterprises][46], one tradeoff employees experience is the balance between working in a\nstable, purpose-driven organization and operating within a large, structured enterprise environment.\nAs a 127-year-old, family-owned company, Cox emphasizes lon"
