        "crawl_text": "Laser Wars Newsletter [Laser Wars]\n][1]\n\n# [[Laser Wars]][2]\n\nSubscribeSign in\n[Home][3]\n[Chat][4]\n[Pulse][5]\n[Land][6]\n[Sea][7]\n[Air and Space][8]\n[History][9]\n[Map][10]\n[Store][11]\n[Archive][12]\n[About][13]\n][14]*Image by [Aaron Provost][15]*\n\n## \u26a1\ufe0f What Is *Laser Wars*?\n\n*[Laser Wars][16]* is a newsletter about military laser weapons and other futuristic defense\ntechnology.\n\nThe [mission][17] of *Laser Wars* is simple: to follow the development and deployment of military\nlaser weapons (and, occasionally, other frontier defense tech) [around the world][18] and chronicle\nhow they\u2019re changing modern warfare.\n\n*Laser Wars* draws its name from the title of a [May 2024 article I wrote for WIRED][19] about the\nUS military\u2019s [first official deployment of high-energy laser weapons overseas][20] for drone\ndefense.\n\n## \ud83d\udc68\ud83c\udffb\u200d\ud83d\udcbb Who Writes *Laser Wars*?\n\nI\u2019m [Jared Keller][21], a defense technology writer and former managing editor of [Military.com][22]\nand [Task & Purpose][23].\n\nI was previously a contributing editor at [Pacific Standard][24] (RIP) and held editorial roles at\nThe Atlantic, Bloomberg, and Al Jazeera America. After spending 15 years as a full-time journalist,\nI now work in strategic communications.\n\n][25]I swear to God I still look like this.\n\nSince I started covering military affairs nearly a decade ago, I\u2019ve reported on advanced defense\ntech like [powered exoskeletons][26], [jet packs][27], [electromagnetic railguns][28], and the\nstill-unfolding [drone revolution][29], among other [topics][30].\n\nMy reporting on military laser weapons has been cited in [The New York Times][31], [Axios][32],\n[Deutsche Welle][33], [Fast Company,][34] [Military Times][35], [Project on Government\nOversight][36], [Radio Free Europe/Radio Liberty][37], [Stars and Stripes][38], [Task &\nPurpose][39], [The Telegraph][40], [The War Zone][41], and [WBUR][42], as well as [New York\nmagazine\u2019s Substack][43] for some reason. I\u2019ve also discussed laser weapons on several podcasts,\nincluding [Meidas Defense][44], [Subject Matter Expert][45], and [BrainFungi][46].\n\nMeidas+\nJared Keller on Laser Weapons | Meidas Defense\nAs the United States rapidly depletes its interceptor missile stockpile in the conflict with\nIran\u2014heightening strategic risks globally\u2014laser weapons have dominated the headlines. On March 9,\nPresident Trump touted lasers as \u201cincredible technology coming out pretty soon\u201d that could replace\nPatriot systems at a fraction of the cost. To separate genuine pr\u2026\nListen now\n4 months ago \u00b7 622 likes \u00b7 47 comments \u00b7 Jared Keller, Joe Plenzler, and MeidasTouch Network\n][47]\n\n## \ud83d\udcbb Why Should I Subscribe?\n\n**Free **subscribers to *Laser Wars* receive:\n* Weekly updates on the latest developments in military laser weapons across [land][48], [sea][49],\nand [air][50] (with [infrequent excursions to outer space][51])\n* [Exclusive reporting][52] you can\u2019t find anywhere else\n* Regular [analysis][53] of directed energy and other next-generation defense tech, from [heads-up\ndisplays][54] to [flying troops][55] and beyond\n* Occasional features on the [history of laser warfare][56]\n* Access to a [subscriber chat][57]\n\nSubscribe\n\n**Paid** subscribers to *Laser Wars* receive:\n* Subscriber-only posts and full access to the [archive][58]\n* A complimentary *Laser Wars* t-shirt from our [store][59]\n* Undying gratitude (and future perks)\n\n[Upgrade to paid][60]\n\n## \u2709\ufe0f How Do I Contact You?\n\nSend tips, story ideas, and constructive criticism [here][61]:\n\n[Email Jared Keller][62]\n\n*Welcome to the Laser Wars \u2014 [hope you survive the experience!][63]*\n\n[User's avatar]\n\n## Subscribe to Laser Wars\n\nA newsletter about military laser weapons and other futuristic defense technology.\nSubscribe\n\n### People\n\n\u00a9 2026 Jared Keller \u00b7 [Privacy][64] \u2219 [Terms][65] \u2219 [Collection notice][66]\n[ Start your Substack][67][Get the app][68]\n[Substack][69] is the home for great culture\nThis site requires JavaScript to run correctly. Please [turn on JavaScript][70] or unblock scripts\n\n[1]: /\n[2]: /\n[3]: /\n[4]: /chat\n[5]: /t/pulse\n[6]: /t/land\n[7]: /t/sea\n[8]: /t/air-space\n[9]: /t/history\n[10]: /p/military-laser-weapons-map\n[11]: /p/store\n[12]: /archive\n[13]: /about\n[14]: https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!MqDc!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A\n%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff3bee4f8-f510-45f7-aa4d-d91bcf70dd0e_\n1000x1000.jpeg\n[15]: https://aaronprovost.com/\n[16]: http://laserwars.net\n[17]: https://www.laserwars.net/p/let-there-be-light\n[18]: https://www.laserwars.net/p/military-laser-weapons-map\n[19]: https://www.wired.com/story/laser-wars-us-military-laser-weapons/\n[20]: https://www.military.com/daily-news/2024/04/24/army-has-officially-deployed-laser-weapons-over\nseas-combat-enemy-drones.html\n[21]: http://jaredbkeller.com\n[22]: http://military.com\n[23]: http://taskandpurpose.com\n[24]: https://psmag.com/author/jared-keller/\n[25]: https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!XMUe!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A\n%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F47377cb9-de50-432e-8a33-c5e5a4199551_\n911x912.jpeg\n[26]: https://taskandpurpose.com/news/pentagon-powered-armor-iron-man-suit/\n[27]: https://www.fastcompany.com/91109459/pentagon-darpa-flying-troops\n[28]: https://taskandpurpose.com/news/navy-electromagnetic-railgun-budget/\n[29]: https://www.wired.com/story/china-taiwan-pentagon-drone-hellscape/\n[30]: https://www.jaredbkeller.com/work\n[31]: https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/13/business/what-to-know-about-the-us-lasers-being-used-to-cou\nnter-iranian-attacks.html\n[32]: https://www.axios.com/2025/01/22/navy-lasers-weapons-admiral-pentagon\n[33]: https://www.dw.com/en/china-us-israel-compete-in-fast-growing-laser-weapons-race/a-77174766\n[34]: https://www.fastcompany.com/91505526/why-the-military-is-obsessed-with-the-myth-of-the-infinit\ne-magazine\n[35]: https://www.militarytimes.com/industry/techwatch/2026/03/18/the-pentagon-wants-to-field-laser-\nweapons-at-scale-within-3-years/\n[36]: https://www.pogo.org/newsletters/the-bunker/2026-02-18\n[37]: https://www.rferl.org/a/iran-ukraine-russia-israel-laser-weapons-future-war/33696183.html\n[38]: https://www.stripes.com/branches/army/2026-03-25/army-valkyrie-laser-anti-missile-system-21179\n842.html\n[39]: https://taskandpurpose.com/news/army-southern-border-deployments/\n[40]: https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-news/2025/09/02/china-about-to-reveal-weapon-its-been-hiding\n-from-the-world/\n[41]: https://www.twz.com/news-features/this-is-the-locust-laser-that-reportedly-prompted-closing-el\n-pasos-airspace\n[42]: https://www.wbur.org/onpoint/2024/06/07/laser-warfare-military-combat-america\n[43]: https://nymag.substack.com/p/theres-a-new-chic-cutting-board\n[44]: https://www.meidasplus.com/p/jared-keller-on-laser-weapons-meidas\n[45]: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vq47WabmlqQ\n[46]: https://www.twitch.tv/videos/2497612615?filter=highlights&sort=time\n[47]: https://www.meidasplus.com/p/jared-keller-on-laser-weapons-meidas?utm_source=substack&utm_camp\naign=post_embed&utm_medium=web\n[48]: https://www.laserwars.net/t/land\n[49]: https://www.laserwars.net/t/sea\n[50]: https://www.laserwars.net/t/air-space\n[51]: https://www.laserwars.net/p/us-military-space-laser-satellites-strategic-defense-initiative-st\nar-wars-directed-energy\n[52]: https://www.laserwars.net/t/exclusives\n[53]: https://www.laserwars.net/t/analysis\n[54]: https://www.laserwars.net/p/anduril-eagleeye-army-helmet-mounted-display-history\n[55]: https://www.laserwars.net/p/marine-corps-powered-paraglider-aps-1-program\n[56]: https://www.laserwars.net/t/history\n[57]: https://www.laserwars.net/publish/chat?utm_source=chat-checklist\n[58]: https://www.laserwars.net/archive\n[59]: https://www.laserwars.net/p/store\n[60]: http://laserwars.net/subscribe\n[61]: mailto:jared.benjamin.keller@gmail.com\n[62]: mailto:jared.benjamin.keller@gmail.com\n[63]: https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/marveldatabase/images/7/76/X-Men_Vol_1_139.jpg/revision/late\nst?cb=20180129040331\n[64]: https://substack.com/privacy\n[65 [Laser Wars]\n][1]\n\n# [[Laser Wars]][2]\n\nSubscribeSign in\n[Home][3]\n[Chat][4]\n[Pulse][5]\n[Land][6]\n[Sea][7]\n[Air and Space][8]\n[History][9]\n[Map][10]\n[Store][11]\n[Archive][12]\n[About][13]\n][14]*Image by [Aaron Provost][15]*\n\n## \u26a1\ufe0f What Is *Laser Wars*?\n\n*[Laser Wars][16]* is a newsletter about military laser weapons and other futuristic defense\ntechnology.\n\nThe [mission][17] of *Laser Wars* is simple: to follow the development and deployment of military\nlaser weapons (and, occasionally, other frontier defense tech) [around the world][18] and chronicle\nhow they\u2019re changing modern warfare.\n\n*Laser Wars* draws its name from the title of a [May 2024 article I wrote for WIRED][19] about the\nUS military\u2019s [first official deployment of high-energy laser weapons overseas][20] for drone\ndefense.\n\n## \ud83d\udc68\ud83c\udffb\u200d\ud83d\udcbb Who Writes *Laser Wars*?\n\nI\u2019m [Jared Keller][21], a defense technology writer and former managing editor of [Military.com][22]\nand [Task & Purpose][23].\n\nI was previously a contributing editor at [Pacific Standard][24] (RIP) and held editorial roles at\nThe Atlantic, Bloomberg, and Al Jazeera America. After spending 15 years as a full-time journalist,\nI now work in strategic communications.\n\n][25]I swear to God I still look like this.\n\nSince I started covering military affairs nearly a decade ago, I\u2019ve reported on advanced defense\ntech like [powered exoskeletons][26], [jet packs][27], [electromagnetic railguns][28], and the\nstill-unfolding [drone revolution][29], among other [topics][30].\n\nMy reporting on military laser weapons has been cited in [The New York Times][31], [Axios][32],\n[Deutsche Welle][33], [Fast Company,][34] [Military Times][35], [Project on Government\nOversight][36], [Radio Free Europe/Radio Liberty][37], [Stars and Stripes][38], [Task &\nPurpose][39], [The Telegraph][40], [The War Zone][41], and [WBUR][42], as well as [New York\nmagazine\u2019s Substack][43] for some reason. I\u2019ve also discussed laser weapons on several podcasts,\nincluding [Meidas Defense][44], [Subject Matter Expert][45], and [BrainFungi][46].\n\nMeidas+\nJared Keller on Laser Weapons | Meidas Defense\nAs the United States rapidly depletes its interceptor missile stockpile in the conflict with\nIran\u2014heightening strategic risks globally\u2014laser weapons have dominated the headlines. On March 9,\nPresident Trump touted lasers as \u201cincredible technology coming out pretty soon\u201d that could replace\nPatriot systems at a fraction of the cost. To separate genuine pr\u2026\nListen now\n4 months ago \u00b7 622 likes \u00b7 47 comments \u00b7 Jared Keller, Joe Plenzler, and MeidasTouch Network\n][47]\n\n## \ud83d\udcbb Why Should I Subscribe?\n\n**Free **subscribers to *Laser Wars* receive:\n* Weekly updates on the latest developments in military laser weapons across [land][48], [sea][49],\nand [air][50] (with [infrequent excursions to outer space][51])\n* [Exclusive reporting][52] you can\u2019t find anywhere else\n* Regular [analysis][53] of directed energy and other next-generation defense tech, from [heads-up\ndisplays][54] to [flying troops][55] and beyond\n* Occasional features on the [history of laser warfare][56]\n* Access to a [subscriber chat][57]\n\nSubscribe\n\n**Paid** subscribers to *Laser Wars* receive:\n* Subscriber-only posts and full access to the [archive][58]\n* A complimentary *Laser Wars* t-shirt from our [store][59]\n* Undying gratitude (and future perks)\n\n[Upgrade to paid][60]\n\n## \u2709\ufe0f How Do I Contact You?\n\nSend tips, story ideas, and constructive criticism [here][61]:\n\n[Email Jared Keller][62]\n\n*Welcome to the Laser Wars \u2014 [hope you survive the experience!][63]*\n\n[User's avatar]\n\n## Subscribe to Laser Wars\n\nA newsletter about military laser weapons and other futuristic defense technology.\nSubscribe\n\n### People\n\n\u00a9 2026 Jared Keller \u00b7 [Privacy][64] \u2219 [Terms][65] \u2219 [Collection notice][66]\n[ Start your Substack][67][Get the app][68]\n[Substack][69] is the home for great culture\nThis site requires JavaScript to run correctly. Please [turn on JavaScript][70] or unblock scripts\n\n[1]: /\n[2]: /\n[3]: "
