        "crawl_text": "Origin Updates Australia Australia Australia Australia State of Origin 2026 Schedule, Teams, Live Stream, and Tickets\n\nState of Origin 2026 Schedule, Teams, Live Stream, and Tickets\n\nHome\nSchedule\nVenues\n\nState Clash\n\n2026 Origin series live: dates, venues, and streams.\n\nLive\n\nThe countdown has officially begun for one of the fiercest rivalries in world sport \u2014 State of Origin 2026 . The Ampol State of Origin Series returns with three blockbuster clashes between the Queensland Maroons and the New South Wales Blues, promising unmatched intensity, elite talent, and unforgettable moments.\n\nEvery year, Origin delivers drama, pride, and passion. In 2026, fans can expect the same electric atmosphere as the game\u2019s best players represent their state in a battle that goes far beyond club loyalties. Below is everything you need to know about the State of Origin 2026 schedule, teams, live streaming options, and ticket information .\n\nWatch State of Origin 2026 Live From Anywhere\n\nUse a fast and secure VPN to access your official streaming service while traveling.\n\nWatch State of Origin 2026 Live From Anywhere\n\nHow to Watch with a VPN\n\nClick the button above and sign up for ExpressVPN.\n\nDownload and install the VPN app on your device.\n\nConnect to a server location where your official streaming service is available.\n\nOpen your official State of Origin 2026 broadcaster or streaming app.\n\nSign in with your subscription and enjoy the live match securely.\n\nAffiliate Disclosure: This page may earn a commission when you sign up through our link. Always use official broadcasters and follow streaming terms.\n\nState of Origin 2026 Schedule\n\nThe State of Origin 2026 schedule will feature three Wednesday night showdowns at iconic Australian venues:\n\nGame Date Venue Kick-off Time (AEST)\nGame 1 Wednesday, 27 May 2026 Accor Stadium, Sydney 8:05 PM\nGame 2 Wednesday, 17 June 2026 MCG, Melbourne 8:10 PM\nGame 3 Wednesday, 8 July 2026 Suncorp Stadium, Brisbane 8:10 PM\n\nGame I kicks off in Sydney at Accor Stadium, setting the tone for the series. Game II heads to Melbourne\u2019s iconic MCG, where massive crowds are expected. The decider, if required, will take place at Brisbane\u2019s Suncorp Stadium \u2014 often described as the spiritual home of Queensland rugby league.\n\nMark your calendars. These dates are non-negotiable for league fans.\n\nState of Origin 2026 Teams (Expected Lineups)\n\nNote: The following squads are expected selections and are not officially confirmed.\n\nQueensland Maroons (Expected Squad)\n\nHamiso Tabuai-Fidow (The Dolphins)\n\nXavier Coates (Melbourne Storm)\n\nRobert Toia (Sydney Roosters)\n\nGehamat Shibasaki (Brisbane Broncos)\n\nValentine Holmes (St George Illawarra Dragons)\n\nCameron Munster (Melbourne Storm \u2013 Captain)\n\nTom Dearden (North Queensland Cowboys)\n\nJosh Papalii (Canberra Raiders)\n\nHarry Grant (Melbourne Storm)\n\nTino Fa&#8217;asuamaleaui (Gold Coast Titans)\n\nReuben Cotter (North Queensland Cowboys)\n\nKurt Capewell (New Zealand Warriors)\n\nTrent Loiero (Melbourne Storm)\n\nKurt Mann (Canterbury Bulldogs)\n\nLindsay Collins (Sydney Roosters)\n\nPat Carrigan (Brisbane Broncos)\n\nJeremiah Nanai (North Queensland Cowboys)\n\nReece Walsh (Brisbane Broncos)\n\nJ\u2019maine Hopgood (Parramatta Eels)\n\nJosh Kerr (The Dolphins)\n\nQueensland is expected to field a dynamic mix of speed, strength, and leadership. With Cameron Munster likely leading the squad, the Maroons will aim to combine structured attack with relentless defensive pressure.\n\nNew South Wales Blues (Expected Squad)\n\nStarting Lineup (Projected):\n\nEdwards\n\nTo&#8217;o\n\nCrichton\n\nMitchell\n\nLomax\n\nLuai\n\nCleary\n\nKing\n\nRobson\n\nHaas\n\nMartin\n\nCrichton\n\nYeo\n\nInterchange Bench:\n\nWatson\n\nLeniu\n\nYoung\n\nUtoikamanu\n\nThe Blues are anticipated to bring a balanced and powerful lineup, blending experienced Origin campaigners with explosive attacking threats. With strong combinations in the halves and a dominant forward pack, NSW will look to reclaim or defend bragging rights in 2026.\n\nOfficial team announcements will be made closer to each match.\n\nHow to Watch State of Origin 2026 Live\n\nIf you cannot attend the games in person, there are multiple ways to watch every tackle, try, and big hit live.\n\nNine Network Coverage\n\nAll men\u2019s and women\u2019s State of Origin matches in 2026 will be broadcast live and exclusive on the Nine Network , available free-to-air across Australia.\n\nThis ensures fans nationwide can tune in without a subscription.\n\nKayo Sports &amp; Foxtel Streaming\n\nFor streaming options, fans can watch selected matches, including Under-19s State of Origin fixtures, via:\n\nNine Network\n\nKayo Sports\n\nFoxtel\n\nKayo Sports offers flexible streaming packages, ideal for viewers who prefer watching on mobile devices, smart TVs, or tablets. Foxtel provides additional sports coverage for subscribers wanting comprehensive rugby league access.\n\nAlways confirm local broadcast times closer to match day.\n\nState of Origin 2026 Tickets and Pre-Sale Information\n\nFollow these simple steps to secure your official Ampol State Of Origin tickets :\n\n1\ufe0f\u20e3 Visit the Official Ticket Page\n\nGo to the official NRL 2026 Ampol State Of Origin ticket page at https://www.nrl.com/tickets/ampol-state-of-origin/ .\n\nScroll down to find the Get Tickets button next to the game you want to attend.\n\n2\ufe0f\u20e3 Click Get Tickets\n\n\u27a1\ufe0f Click the Get Tickets button for the match you\u2019re interested in. This will redirect you to the Ticketmaster Australia website.\n\n3\ufe0f\u20e3 Choose Your Ticket Type (on Ticketmaster)\n\nOnce on Ticketmaster:\n\nSelect the match date &amp; location (Sydney, Melbourne or Brisbane).\n\nChoose your seat category (e.g., general admission, reserved seating, accessible seating).\n\nReview ticket prices and number of seats you want.\n\n4\ufe0f\u20e3 Complete Your Purchase\n\nSign in or create a Ticketmaster account (if required).\n\nAdd attendee details.\n\nEnter billing/payment information.\n\nConfirm your order.\n\n\u2714\ufe0f You will receive a confirmation email with your ticket details and delivery method (e-ticket, mobile ticket etc.).\n\nWhy State of Origin 2026 Will Be Unmissable\n\nThe State of Origin series is not just another rugby league event. It is a cultural phenomenon in Australia. Players leave club allegiances behind and represent their state with unmatched pride and emotion.\n\nThe 2026 series promises:\n\nElite-level competition\n\nPacked stadiums\n\nHistoric rivalries renewed\n\nMassive television audiences\n\nUnforgettable sporting drama\n\nWhether you are cheering for the Queensland Maroons or the New South Wales Blues, the 2026 Origin series is shaping up to be one of the most anticipated in recent years.\n\nFinal Thoughts\n\nThe State of Origin 2026 Schedule, Teams, Live Stream, and Tickets information confirms one thing \u2014 rugby league fans are in for another thrilling chapter of Australia\u2019s greatest rivalry.\n\nWith confirmed venues in Sydney, Melbourne, and Brisbane, expected powerhouse squads, live free-to-air coverage, and premium ticket options, everything is set for a blockbuster series.\n\nSecure your tickets early, mark the dates in your calendar, and prepare for three unforgettable Wednesday nights of rugby league excellence in 2026.\n\nState Origin\n\nCatch every thrilling moment of the 2026 Ampol State of Origin series live, from Sydney to Brisbane.\n\nMatch Schedule\n\nGame 1: May 27, 2026, Sydney, kickoff at 8:05 PM AEST.\n\nGame 2: June 17, 2026, Melbourne, kickoff at 8:10 PM AEST.\n\nGame 3: July 8, 2026, Brisbane, kickoff at 8:10 PM AEST. originupdates.com State of Origin 2026 Schedule, Teams, Live Stream, and Tickets\n\nState of Origin 2026 Schedule, Teams, Live Stream, and Tickets\n\nHome\nSchedule\nVenues\n\nState Clash\n\n2026 Origin series live