9]\n    * [1984][180]\n    * [1984/85][181]\n    * [1985][182]\n    * [1985/86][183]\n    * [1986][184]\n    * [1986/87][185]\n    * [1987][186]\n    * [1987/88][187]\n    * [1988][188]\n    * [1988/89][189]\n    * [1989][190]\n    * [1989/90][191]\n  * 1990-1999\n    [1990-1999][192]\n    * [1990][193]\n    * [1990/91][194]\n    * [1991][195]\n    * [1991/92][196]\n    * [1992][197]\n    * [1992/93][198]\n    * [1993][199]\n    * [1993/94][200]\n    * [1994][201]\n    * [1994/95][202]\n    * [1995][203]\n    * [1995/96][204]\n    * [1996][205]\n    * [1997][206]\n    * [1998][207]\n    * [1999][208]\n  * 2000-2009\n    [2000-2009][209]\n    * [2000][210]\n    * [2001][211]\n    * [2002][212]\n    * [2003][213]\n    * [2004][214]\n    * [2005][215]\n    * [2006][216]\n    * [2007][217]\n    * [2008][218]\n    * [2009][219]\n  * 2010-2019\n    [2010-2019][220]\n    * [2010][221]\n    * [2011][222]\n    * [2012][223]\n    * [2013][224]\n    * [2014][225]\n    * [2015][226]\n    * [2016][227]\n    * [2017][228]\n    * [2018][229]\n    * [2019][230]\n  * 2020-2026\n    [2020-2026][231]\n    * [2020][232]\n    * [2021][233]\n    * [2022][234]\n    * [2023][235]\n    * [2024][236]\n    * [2025][237]\n    * [2026][238]\n  * Birthdays\n    [Birthdays][239]\n    * [Today][240]\n    * [January][241]\n    * [February][242]\n    * [March][243]\n    * [April][244]\n    * [May][245]\n    * [June][246]\n    * [July][247]\n    * [August][248]\n    * [September][249]\n    * [October][250]\n    * [November][251]\n    * [December][252]\n* [Fixtures][253]\n* [Results][254]\n* [Scorigami][255]\n* [Players][256]\n* [Coaches][257]\n* [Referees][258]\n* [Teams][259]\n* [Venues][260]\n* [2025 Annual][261]\n\n## Welcome to Rugby League Project\n\nThis is an archive of historical rugby league results, covering international, regional and domestic\ncompetitions. Our aim is to compile and present details of every top level rugby league competition,\ngame, player, coach, venue, referee and more, dating back to the game's inception in 1895. The\ninformation here is curated on an entirely voluntary, part-time basis by Shawn Dollin and Andrew\nFerguson, with the immense help of a [number of devoted individuals amongst the rugby league\ncommunity][262].\n\nYou can use the links above to get started. If you're not sure, we suggest trying the\n[Calendar][263] which makes it easy to jump to a specific year and find a corresponding list of\ncompetitions, matches and players.\n\nIf it's the latest news and scores you're after, check out the following sites:\n* [ LeagueUnlimited - Latest rugby league news and previews][264]\n* [ FlashScore - Live rugby league scores and results][265]\n\n## Latest Updates\n\n### Tuesday, 24th March, 2026\n\nWe've opened up registrations for users. From now on, you will need to create an account to comment\non players. You can also now comment on matches. [Registering is easy][266], so don't hesitate to\nlock in your preferred nickname now!\n\n### Tuesday, 6th January, 2026\n\nHappy New Year once again! We're very proud to announce the sixth edition of [Andrew Ferguson & Tim\nCostello's Rugby League Annual][267]. As always you will find the most comprehensive summary of the\nrugby league season by far, with detailed results, match-by-match reports with scorers and teams,\nteam summaries and breakdowns, as well as a look back at the first 30 years of Super League, a\nglorious tribute to Sir Billy Boston and so much more. Available now to [read for free online][268],\nor [download in PDF format][269].\n\n### Friday, 12th September, 2025\n\nThe filter on player lists now supports smarter filtering. You can put column name followed by\noperator then numeric value. EG: `tot>=50` will match players with over 50 appearances, or `w%<50`\nmatches players in the list with a win rate below 50%. This comes in handy as we head into finals\ntime. Check out which players have the best winning records in our special [NRL Finals][270] and\n[Super League Finals][271] sections.\n\n## RLP 2025 Annual\n\n[\nRead Online][272]\n\nA collaboration between Rugby League Project and [LeagueUnlimited][273], enjoy a FREE 314-page\npublication cataloguing the 2025 calendar year across Australian and UK professional and\nsemi-professional competitions, as well as a full wrap of the internationals played. Packed FULL of\nstats.\n\nYou can view the annual in your browser by clicking on the cover image, or download a PDF version to\nread offline here:\n\n**Free Download - [Rugby League 2025 Annual - PDF Version][274] (15.7mb"
      },
