            "url": "https://thebrandhopper.com/team",
            "text": "Close\n[Skip To Content][1]\n[[TBH]][2]\n\n[The Brand Hopper][3]\n\nAll Brand Stories At One Place\n\n[Menu][4]\n* [Brands][5]\n* [Startups][6]\n* [Campaigns][7]\n* [Opinions][8]\n* [Resources][9]\n* [Tools][10]\n* [In The News][11]\n* [Contact Us][12]\nFollow Us:\n[Search][13]\nSearch for:\n\n# Category: Team TBH\n* [Home][14]\n* Team TBH\n\n[ [Brand | Amazon \u2013 Delivering A To Z Of Business And Success] ][15]\n[Brand][16] [Retail][17] [Team TBH][18] [Technology][19]\n[August 16, 2020December 6, 2020][20][Team TBH][21]\n\n## [Brand | Amazon \u2013 Delivering A To Z Of Business And Success][22]\n\nAmazon is an American multinational company headquartered in Seattle, Washington, US. It provides an\narray of services that span from the online retail, AI assistant provider, cloud computing service\nprovider, live-streaming services, music, and video streaming, game streaming, and also web services\namong almost an uncountable industries and services, it has managed to enter into. [\u2026]\n\n[Continue Reading ][23]\n[ [Featured Startup | Powermat \u2013 Life At 100%] ][24]\n[Featured Startups][25] [Team TBH][26] [Technology][27]\n[September 7, 2020September 17, 2020][28][Team TBH][29]\n\n## [Featured Startup | Powermat \u2013 Life At 100%][30]\n\nPowermat is the wireless charging pioneer, who started developing inductive wireless charging\ntechnology back in 2006, before the formation of the standard organizations. Powermat has been\ngranted over 95 related patents and has submitted over 200 patents for review along the years. It\nhas more than 12,000 Charging Spots, 3.2 million cars and over 500 [\u2026]\n\nTagged [GM][31], [Powermat][32], [Starbucks][33], [wireless][34], [wireless charging][35] [Continue\nReading ][36]\n[ [Brand | Google X \u2013 The Adobe Of Google\u2019s Most Ambitious Projects] ][37]\n[Brand][38] [Entertainment][39] [Team TBH][40] [Technology][41]\n[April 17, 2020September 9, 2020][42][Team TBH][43]\n\n## [Brand | Google X \u2013 The Adobe Of Google\u2019s Most Ambitious Projects][44]\n\nGoogle needs no introduction. Today, it is one of the most valuable, profitable, and futuristic\ncompanies in the world. Innovation is in the flesh and bones here, employees treated as owners, and\nfailures embraced with truest of hearts. Out of innovation and love for big ideas, born is a company\nthat is so technically efficient [\u2026]\n\nTagged [brands][45], [Google][46], [Projects][47], [X Company][48] [Continue Reading ][49]\n[ [Brand | Axe \u2013 Making An Unconventional Yet Uncomfortable Brand Legacy] ][50]\n[Brand][51] [FMCG][52] [Healthcare][53] [Team TBH][54]\n[May 1, 2020September 9, 2020][55][Team TBH][56]\n\n## [Brand | Axe \u2013 Making An Unconventional Yet Uncomfortable Brand Legacy][57]\n\nThere\u2019s hardly anyone who goes to the market to buy deodorant and doesn\u2019t look for one exclusive\nbrand in the shop. The brand is AXE. Launched in 1999, it is one of the most successful personal\ncare brands of Hindustan Unilever and is also the best-selling brand of Unilever. Axe, the\ndeodorant, is considered as [\u2026]\n\nTagged [Axe deodorants][58], [brand][59], [Campaign][60], [Legacy][61], [marketing][62] [Continue\nReading ][63]\n[ [Brand | Oriflame \u2013 Selling Cosmetics Through Networking Marketing] ][64]\n[Brand][65] [Fashion][66] [Team TBH][67]\n[June 16, 2020September 9, 2020][68][Team TBH][69]\n\n## [Brand | Oriflame \u2013 Selling Cosmetics Through Networking Marketing][70]\n\nNot many companies in the world have tasted success without having reliable distributors and\nretailers network catering to customers. One such company that has gone this route and, in turn,\ncreated an empire with the help of Multi-Level Marketing (MLM), or popularly called Direct Selling\ntechniques is Oriflame Holding AG, the prime cosmetics brand from [\u2026]\n\nTagged [advertising][71], [Branding][72], [Cosmetics][73], [marketing][74], [Oriflame][75] [Continue\nReading ][76]\n[ [Brand | Philips \u2013 The Global Consumer Electronics Brand With Innovation At Heart] ][77]\n[Brand][78] [Healthcare][79] [Team TBH][80] [Technology][81]\n[June 30, 2020September 9, 2020][82][Team TBH][83]\n\n## [Brand | Philips \u2013 The Global Consumer Electronics Brand With Innovation At Heart][84]\n\nPhilips is a Dutch multinational conglomerate headquartered in Amsterdam, Netherlands that was\nfounded in 1891 by Frederik Philips and his son Gerard Philips. Once started as a bulk manufacturer,\nit became one of the largest electronics companies in the world, employing over 75,000 people across\n100 countries, generating revenue of \u20ac18.121 billion in 2018. With [\u2026]\n\nTagged [Branding][85], [consumer][86], [marketing][87], [philips][88], [strategies][89] [Continue\nReading ][90]\n[ [Brand | IndiaMART \u2013 The Indian B2B Solution To Sell Easy] ][91]\n[Brand][92] [Ecommerce][93] [FMCG][94] [Industry][95] [Team TBH][96]\n[August 1, 2020September 9, 2020][97][Team TBH][98]\n\n## [Brand | IndiaMART \u2013 The Indian B2B Solution To Sell Easy][99]\n\nIndiaMART InterMESH Ltd. is one of India\u2019s largest online B2B listing platforms for small and medium\nbusinesses, connecting buyers with suppliers. It also provides B2C and C2C sales service via its web\nportal. With 60% market share of the online B2B Classified space in India, the channel focuses on\nproviding a platform to Small & [\u2026]\n\nTagged [B2B][100], [Indiamart][101], [marketing][102], [SME][103] [Continue Reading ][104]\n[ [Brand | The Hershey Company \u2013 A Little Something For Everyone] ][105]\n[Brand][106] [FMCG][107] [Industry][108] [Team TBH][109]\n[September 3, 2020September 9, 2020][110][Team TBH][111]\n\n## [Brand | The Hershey Company \u2013 A Little Something For Everyone][112]\n\nThe Hershey Company was founded in 1894 by Milton Hershey and is headquartered in Hershey,\nPennsylvania. The town itself was largely built by Milton, and many places in the town bear his\nname, including Hershey\u2019s Chocolate World and Hersheypark. Hershey\u2019s Chocolatetown at Hersheypark\nwas one of the largest construction projects in the United States as [\u2026]\n\nTagged [advertising][113], [Branding][114], [Chocolate][115], [Hershey][116], [marketing][117]\n[Continue Reading ][118]\n\n#### Subscribe To The Newsletter\n\nEmail\n\n## Sign up for our free newsletter\n\nGet brand insights, industry news, and exclusive resources delivered daily.\n\nSubscribe\n\n### Resources\n* [Guides][119]\n* [Case Studies][120]\n* [Tools][121]\n* [Webinars][122]\n\n### Community\n* [Network][123]\n* [Submit Content][124]\n* [Directory][125]\n* [Interviews][126]\n\n### Company\n* [About][127]\n* [Contact][128]\n* [Advertise][129]\n* [Partners][130]\n\n### Legal\n* [Terms][131]\n* [Privacy][132]\n* [Cookies][133]\n* [Support][134]\n\n[f][135][X][136][in][137][Y][138]\n\nCopyright \ufffd 2026 The Brand Hopper. All rights reserved.\n\nThe Brand Hopper and **The Art of Start** are owned and operated by the same company. Explore\npractical startup and side-hustle how-to guides at [The Art of Start][139].\nName\nEmail *\nEmail\nSubmit\n\n[Terms and Conditions][140]\n\n[1]: #content\n[2]: https://thebrandhopper.com/\n[3]: https://thebrandhopper.com/\n[4]: javascript:void(0)\n[5]: https://thebrandhopper.com/brand/\n[6]: https://thebrandhopper.com/featured-startups/\n[7]: https://thebrandhopper.com/campaigns/\n[8]: https://thebrandhopper.com/opinions/\n[9]: https://thebrandhopper.com/learning-resources/\n[10]: https://thebrandhopper.com/tools/\n[11]: https://thebrandhopper.com/news/\n[12]: https://thebrandhopper.com/contact-us/\n[13]: javascript:void(0)\n[14]: https://thebrandhopper.com/\n[15]: https://thebrandhopper.com/brand/amazon-delivering-a-to-z-of-business-and-success/\n[16]: https://thebrandhopper.com/brand/\n[17]: https://thebrandhopper.com/retail/\n[18]: https://thebrandhopper.com/team/\n[19]: https://thebrandhopper.com/tech/\n[20]: https://thebrandhopper.com/brand/amazon-deliveri