        "crawl_text": "Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory Government Operated by the Lawrence Livermore National Security, LLC for the Department of Energy's National Nuclear Security Administration United States North America Global Laser Technology Optical Systems High Energy Density Physics Optical Diagnostics Cryogenic Target Systems State-of-the-art laser technology Unique research capabilities in fusion energy Strong partnerships with government and academic institutions Unique capabilities in high energy density science Collaboration with leading research institutions Government funding for national security applications U.S. Department of Energy regulations Nuclear regulatory compliance 7000 East Avenue, Livermore, CA 94550 United States North America Global National International NIF achieved fusion ignition on December 5, 2022, producing more energy than delivered to the target. The facility has set multiple records for laser energy output, including a recent 2.2 MJ shot on October 30, 2023. NIF continues to enhance its laser systems and operational efficiency, aiming for more frequent and powerful experiments. Advancing fusion energy research Supporting national security through high energy density science Maintaining operational efficiency with aging technology Ensuring safety in high-energy experiments Potential breakthroughs in fusion energy could lead to new energy sources. Collaboration with other research institutions to expand scientific knowledge. NIF is a leader in high energy density science and fusion research, with unique capabilities not found in other facilities. Increased funding for energy research Growing interest in fusion as a clean energy source Increased funding for national security Advancements in laser technology Growing interest in fusion energy solutions National Ignition Facility &amp; Photon Science\n\nSkip to main content\n\nAn official website of the United States government\n\nHere\u2019s how you know\n\nHere\u2019s how 