            "text": "[ Skip to main content ][1]\n[U.S. flag]\n\nAn official website of the United States government\n\nHere\u2019s how you know\n\nHere\u2019s how you know\n\n**Official websites use .gov**\nA **.gov** website belongs to an official government organization in the United States.\n\n**Secure .gov websites use HTTPS**\nA **lock** ( [Lock] ) or **https://** means you\u2019ve safely connected to the .gov website. Share\nsensitive information only on official, secure websites.\n* [Our Purpose][2]\n* [Our Science and Technology][3]\n* [Join Our Team][4]\n* [Partner with Us][5]\n* [News][6]\n* [Community and Education][7]\n* [About][8]\n\n[[LLNL Logo]][9]\n[National Ignition Facility & Photon Science][10]\n\n## Primary Menu\n* [About ][11]\n* [What Is NIF?][12]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][13]\n* [Laser Glass][14]\n* [Optical Switch][15]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][16]\n* [Deformable Mirror][17]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][18]\n* [Computer Control System][19]\n* [Target Fabrication][20]\n* [How NIF Works][21]\n* [Anatomy of a NIF Shot][22]\n* [Power Conditioning System][23]\n* [Injection Laser System][24]\n* [Amplifiers][25]\n* [Beam Transport][26]\n* [Final Optics][27]\n* [Target Chamber][28]\n* [Keys to Our Success][29]\n* [Facility Operations][30]\n* [Power and Energy][31]\n* [Control Systems][32]\n* [Optics][33]\n* [Targets][34]\n* [Diagnostics][35]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][36]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][37]\n* [Who Works for NIF][38]\n* [People Profiles][39]\n* [Management][40]\n* [Developing the Workforce][41]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][42]\n* [Enduring Partnerships][43]\n* [Technology Transfer][44]\n* [Careers][45]\n* [FAQs][46]\n* [Visit Us][47]\n* [Science ][48]\n* [NIF and Stockpile Modernization][49]\n* [High Energy Density Science][50]\n* [Advancing Weapon Physics][51]\n* [Achieving Fusion Ignition][52]\n* [National Security Applications][53]\n* [Developing New Capabilities][54]\n* [Discovery Science][55]\n* [Lab Astrophysics][56]\n* [Nuclear Astrophysics][57]\n* [Planetary Physics][58]\n* [Plasma Physics][59]\n* [Expanding Photonics Frontiers][60]\n* [DE Technology Programs][61]\n* [Advanced Optical Technologies][62]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][63]\n* [Advanced Laser Systems][64]\n* [Fiber Lasers][65]\n* [Materials for Laser Systems][66]\n* [Exploring Energy Security][67]\n* [Journal Articles][68]\n* [Livermore Inertial Fusion Energy References][69]\n* [NIF Users ][70]\n* [NIF User Portal][71]\n* [NIF User Guide][72]\n* [NIF DLI User Guide][73]\n* [Experimental Capabilities][74]\n* [Shot RI Resources][75]\n* [Call for Proposals][76]\n* [Prior Year Awards][77]\n* [2024 Awarded Campaigns][78]\n* [2023 Awarded Campaigns][79]\n* [2022 Awarded Campaigns][80]\n* [2021 Awarded Campaigns][81]\n* [2020 Awarded Campaigns][82]\n* [2019 Awarded Campaigns][83]\n* [2018 Awarded Campaigns][84]\n* [2017 Awarded Campaigns][85]\n* [2016 Awarded Campaigns][86]\n* [2015 Awarded Campaigns][87]\n* [2014 Awarded Campaigns][88]\n* [NIF User Group][89]\n* [Bylaws][90]\n* [Executive Board][91]\n* [NIF Calendar][92]\n* [Target Shot Metrics][93]\n* [Conflict of Interest Policy][94]\n* [Jupiter Laser Facility][95]\n* [Multimedia ][96]\n* [Photo Gallery][97]\n* [Playing Cards][98]\n* [Poster Gallery][99]\n* [Video Gallery][100]\n* [Education ][101]\n* [How Lasers Work][102]\n* [How to Make a Star][103]\n* [Outreach][104]\n* [Laser Roadshow][105]\n* [Summer Scholar Internship Program][106]\n* [Seminars][107]\n* [Student Spotlight][108]\n* [Scholar Tours][109]\n* [Glossary][110]\n* [External Resources][111]\n* [News ][112]\n* [The Age of Ignition][113]\n* [In the News][114]\n* [NIF in the News: Video][115]\n* [Programs ][116]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][117]\n* [Facilities][118]\n* [Publications][119]\n* [People][120]\n* [Job Postings][121]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][122]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][123]\n* [Contact][124]\n\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\n\n## Mobile Menu\n\n##### Site Menu\n* [About][125]\n* [What Is NIF?][126]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][127]\n* [How NIF Works][128]\n* [Keys to Our Success][129]\n* [Who Works for NIF][130]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][131]\n* [Careers][132]\n* [FAQs][133]\n* [Visit Us][134]\n* [Science][135]\n* [NIF Users][136]\n* [Multimedia][137]\n* [Education][138]\n* [News][139]\n* [Programs][140]\n* [Contact][141]\n\n##### LLNL Menu\n* [Missions][142]\n* [Research][143]\n* [Doing Business][144]\n* [News][145]\n* [About][146]\n* [Careers][147]\n* [Community][148]\n\nHome of the National Ignition Facility (NIF), the world\u2019s highest-energy laser system\n\n## NIF is a key element of the National Nuclear Security Administration\u2019s\n## science-based Stockpile Stewardship Program.\n\n*NIF\u2019s 192 laser beams converge at the center of the Target Chamber to implode a tiny hydrogen fuel\npellet and spark a thermonuclear fusion reaction.*\n\n# UNIQUE EXPERIMENTS\n\nThe NIF & Photon Science Directorate is a premier international center for [experimental\nscience][149]. NIF\u2019s powerful laser beams create temperatures and pressures similar to those that\nexist in the cores of stars and giant planets and inside exploding nuclear weapons. These conditions\nenable hundreds of LLNL scientists, engineers, and technicians, along with national and\ninternational collaborators and users, to conduct one-of-a-kind experiments that help ensure the\nnation\u2019s security through the National Nuclear Security Administration\u2019s [Stockpile Stewardship\nProgram][150], achieve [fusion ignition][151] in the laboratory for the first time, and [lay the\ngroundwork][152] for a safe, secure energy future through inertial fusion energy.\n\n# EXPLORING NEW FONTIERS\n\nNIF enables scientists from across the nation and around the world to conduct unprecedented\nexperiments in [nuclear physics][153],[ high energy density science][154], [materials science][155],\n[weapon physics][156], and [ many other scientific disciplines][157]. NIF laboratory experiments\nalso allow NIF researchers, collaborators, and users to [gain new insights][158] into such\nmysterious astrophysical phenomena as supernovae, giant planets and exoplanets, new and dying stars,\nand black holes. [Learn more about NIF][159]. NIF & Photon Science is a principal directorate of\nLawrence Livermore National Laboratory (LLNL) in Livermore, California. The facility is funded by\nthe U.S. Department of Energy\u2019s [National Nuclear Security Administration][160] (NNSA).\n\n# KEYS TO OUR SUCCESS\n\n[8th Wonder of NIF][161]\nNIF&PS people have carved a path rich with discovery.\n[Facility Operations][162]\nKeeping the lasers firing 24 hours a day, 7 days a week.\n[Control Systems][163]\nControl Systems operators run a symphony of shots.\n[Optics][164]\nNew technologies advance boundaries of optical science.\n[Targets][165]\nPartners in precision: big lasers, tiny targets.\n[Diagnostics][166]\nDiagnostics reveal the inner details of NIF experiments.\n[Efficiency Improvements][167]\nEfficient operations boost NIF\u2019s productivity.\n[A Legacy of Lasers][168]\nMeet some of the pioneers who paved the way.\n\n# OUR PEOPLE AND PARTNERS\n\n[Productive Partnerships][169]\n[Illustration Image of laser hitting target]\n][170]\nThe nation\u2019s investments in HED and fusion research pay dividends in our partnerships and tech\ntransfer programs.\n[Developing the Workforce][171]\n[Image of employees working in lab]\n][172]\nOur future science stars will help maintain the nation\u2019s leadership in S&T. [Learn about NIF&PS\ncareer opportunities.][173]\n[Community Outreach][174]\n[Image of employee doing a demonstration in front school students ]\n][175]\nEngaging the community and enabling future generations to contribute to society are part of our\nstewardship mission.\n\n# MORE INFORMATION\n\n[Science on a Mission][176]\nThe National Ignition Facility is the world\u2019s most energetic laser facility ever built.\n[Our Management][177]\nWorld-class leaders join together to form the NIF & Photon Science management team.\n[People Profiles][178]\nNIF hires the best and the brightest minds to help solve the most complex scientific challenges\nfacing the nation.\n[Glossary: Fusion Terms][179]\nGlossary defining key technical terms for Fusion\n[FAQs][180]\nWe answer the most frequently asked questions and give you the opportunity to ask your own.\n[Visit Us][181]\nTake an onsite or virtual tour of the National Ignition Facility and see where ignition was\ndiscovered.\n[[LLNL]][182]\nLawrence Livermore National Laboratory\n| 7000 East Avenue \u2022 Livermore, CA 94550 | LLNL-WEB-642493\nOperated by the Lawrence Livermore National Security, LLC for the Department of Energy's National\nNuclear Security Administration Learn about the Department of Energy's [Vulnerability Disclosure\nProgram][183]\n[[LLNS]][184] [[U.S. DOE]][185] [[NNSA]][186]\n[Home][187] [Disclaimer][188] [Privacy Notice][189]\n* [About][190]\n* [What Is NIF?][191]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][192]\n* [Laser Glass][193]\n* [Optical Switch][194]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][195]\n* [Deformable Mirror][196]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][197]\n* [Computer Control System][198]\n* [Target Fabrication][199]\n* [How NIF Works][200]\n* [Anatomy of a NIF Shot][201]\n* [Power Conditioning System][202]\n* [Injection Laser System][203]\n* [Amplifiers][204]\n* [Beam Transport][205]\n* [Final Optics][206]\n* [Target Chamber][207]\n* [Keys to Our Success][208]\n* [Facility Operations][209]\n* [Power and Energy][210]\n* [Control Systems][211]\n* [Optics][212]\n* [Targets][213]\n* [Diagnostics][214]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][215]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][216]\n* [Key Steps on the Path to NIF][217]\n* [50 Years of Laser Leadership][218]\n* [Building NIF][219]\n* [Who Works for NIF][220]\n* [People Profiles][221]\n* [Management][222]\n* [Developing the Workforce][223]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][224]\n* [Enduring Partnerships][225]\n* [Technology Transfer][226]\n* [Careers][227]\n* [FAQs][228]\n* [Visit Us][229]\n* [Science][230]\n* [NIF and Stockpile Modernization][231]\n* [High Energy Density Science][232]\n* [Advancing Weapon Physics][233]\n* [Achieving Fusion Ignition][234]\n* [National Security Applications][235]\n* [Developing New Capabilities][236]\n* [Discovery Science][237]\n* [Lab Astrophysics][238]\n* [Nuclear Astrophysics][239]\n* [Planetary Physics][240]\n* [Plasma Physics][241]\n* [Expanding Photonics Frontiers][242]\n* [DE Technology Programs][243]\n* [Advanced Optical Technologies][244]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][245]\n* [Advanced Laser Systems][246]\n* [Fiber Lasers][247]\n* [Materials for Laser Systems][248]\n* [Exploring Energy Security][249]\n* [Journal Articles][250]\n* [Livermore Inertial Fusion Energy References][251]\n* [NIF Users][252]\n* [NIF User Portal][253]\n* [NIF User Guide][254]\n* [NIF DLI User Guide][255]\n* [Experimental Capabilities][256]\n* [Shot RI Resources][257]\n* [Call for Proposals][258]\n* [Prior Year Awards][259]\n* [2024 Awarded Campaigns][260]\n* [2023 Awarded Campaigns][261]\n* [2022 Awarded Campaigns][262]\n* [2021 Awarded Campaigns][263]\n* [2020 Awarded Campaigns][264]\n* [2019 Awarded Campaigns][265]\n* [2018 Awarded Campaigns][266]\n* [2017 Awarded Campaigns][267]\n* [2016 Awarded Campaigns][268]\n* [2015 Awarded Campaigns][269]\n* [2014 Awarded Campaigns][270]\n* [NIF User Group][271]\n* [Bylaws][272]\n* [Executive Board][273]\n* [NIF Calendar][274]\n* [Target Shot Metrics][275]\n* [Conflict of Interest Policy][276]\n* [Jupiter Laser Facility][277]\n* [Multimedia][278]\n* [Photo Gallery][279]\n* [Playing Cards][280]\n* [Poster Gallery][281]\n* [Video Gallery][282]\n* [Education][283]\n* [How Lasers Work][284]\n* [How to Make a Star][285]\n* [Outreach][286]\n* [Laser Roadshow][287]\n* [Summer Scholar Internship Program][288]\n* [Seminars][289]\n* [Student Spotlight][290]\n* [Scholar Tours][291]\n* [Glossary][292]\n* [External Resources][293]\n* [News][294]\n* [The Age of Ignition][295]\n* [In the News][296]\n* [NIF in the News: Video][297]\n* [Programs][298]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][299]\n* [Facilities][300]\n* [Publications][301]\n* [People][302]\n* [Job Postings][303]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][304]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][305]\n* [Contact][306]\n\n[1]: #main-content\n[2]: https://www.llnl.gov/purpose\n[3]: https://www.llnl.gov/science-technology\n[4]: https://www.llnl.gov/join-our-team\n[5]: https://www.llnl."
