rophysics][57]\n* [Planetary Physics][58]\n* [Plasma Physics][59]\n* [Expanding Photonics Frontiers][60]\n* [DE Technology Programs][61]\n* [Advanced Optical Technologies][62]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][63]\n* [Advanced Laser Systems][64]\n* [Fiber Lasers][65]\n* [Materials for Laser Systems][66]\n* [Exploring Energy Security][67]\n* [Journal Articles][68]\n* [Livermore Inertial Fusion Energy References][69]\n* [NIF Users ][70]\n* [NIF User Portal][71]\n* [NIF User Guide][72]\n* [NIF DLI User Guide][73]\n* [Experimental Capabilities][74]\n* [Shot RI Resources][75]\n* [Call for Proposals][76]\n* [Prior Year Awards][77]\n* [2024 Awarded Campaigns][78]\n* [2023 Awarded Campaigns][79]\n* [2022 Awarded Campaigns][80]\n* [2021 Awarded Campaigns][81]\n* [2020 Awarded Campaigns][82]\n* [2019 Awarded Campaigns][83]\n* [2018 Awarded Campaigns][84]\n* [2017 Awarded Campaigns][85]\n* [2016 Awarded Campaigns][86]\n* [2015 Awarded Campaigns][87]\n* [2014 Awarded Campaigns][88]\n* [NIF User Group][89]\n* [Bylaws][90]\n* [Executive Board][91]\n* [NIF Calendar][92]\n* [Target Shot Metrics][93]\n* [Conflict of Interest Policy][94]\n* [Jupiter Laser Facility][95]\n* [Multimedia ][96]\n* [Photo Gallery][97]\n* [Playing Cards][98]\n* [Poster Gallery][99]\n* [Video Gallery][100]\n* [Education ][101]\n* [How Lasers Work][102]\n* [How to Make a Star][103]\n* [Outreach][104]\n* [Laser Roadshow][105]\n* [Summer Scholar Internship Program][106]\n* [Seminars][107]\n* [Student Spotlight][108]\n* [Scholar Tours][109]\n* [Glossary][110]\n* [External Resources][111]\n* [News ][112]\n* [The Age of Ignition][113]\n* [In the News][114]\n* [NIF in the News: Video][115]\n* [Programs ][116]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][117]\n* [Facilities][118]\n* [Publications][119]\n* [People][120]\n* [Job Postings][121]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][122]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][123]\n* [Contact][124]\n\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\n\n## Mobile Menu\n\n##### Site Menu\n* [About][125]\n* [What Is NIF?][126]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][127]\n* [How NIF Works][128]\n* [Keys to Our Success][129]\n* [Who Works for NIF][130]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][131]\n* [Careers][132]\n* [FAQs][133]\n* [Visit Us][134]\n* [Science][135]\n* [NIF Users][136]\n* [Multimedia][137]\n* [Education][138]\n* [News][139]\n* [Programs][140]\n* [Contact][141]\n\n##### LLNL Menu\n* [Missions][142]\n* [Research][143]\n* [Doing Business][144]\n* [News][145]\n* [About][146]\n* [Careers][147]\n* [Community][148]\n\nWhat Is the National Ignition Facility?\nWhat Is the National Ignition Facility?\nWhat Is the National Ignition Facility?\nWhat Is the National Ignition Facility?\n\n# THE WORLD'S HIGHEST-ENERGY LASER\n\n## Big Science\n\nThe National Ignition Facility (NIF) is the size of a sports stadium\u2014three football fields could fit\ninside. NIF\u2019s unique energy and power enable cutting-edge research to help keep America safe and\nsecure, explore new frontiers of science, and lay the groundwork for a clean, sustainable source of\nenergy.\n\n## Extreme Precision\n\nNIF is the world\u2019s most precise and reproducible laser system. It precisely guides, amplifies,\nreflects, and focuses 192 powerful laser beams into a target about the size of a pencil eraser in a\nfew billionths of a second, delivering more than 2 million joules of ultraviolet energy and 500\ntrillion watts of peak power.\n\n## Nuclear Fusion\n\nNIF generates temperatures in the target of more than 180 million degrees Fahrenheit and pressures\nof more than 100 billion Earth atmospheres. Those extreme conditions cause hydrogen atoms in the\ntarget to fuse and release energy in a controlled thermonuclear reaction.\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\n# MAINTAINING THE NUCLEAR DETERRENT\n\n## Stockpile Stewardship\n\nNIF is a key element of the National Nuclear Security Administration\u2019s science-based [Stockpile\nStewardship Program][149] to maintain the reliability, security, and safety of the U.S. nuclear\ndeterrent without full-scale testing.\n\n## Under Pressure: HED Science\n\nThe [High Energy Density][150] science program studies material behavior under extreme pressure,\nenabling researchers to conduct [weapon physics experiments][151] in a controlled laboratory\nenvironment once possible only with underground testing.\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\n# SCIENCE & TECHNOLOGY ON A MISSION\n\n## Achieving Ignition\n\nThese experiments contributed to NIF\u2019s ability to [achieve fusion ignition][152] in the lab for the\nfirst time. In an ignition shot, more fusion energy is generated than the amount of laser energy\ndelivered to the target.\n\n## Exploring New Horizons\n\nThe drive toward ignition helps ensure the reliability of the nuclear deterrent, while also opening\nnew frontiers in laboratory astrophysics, materials science, hydrodynamics, and many other\nscientific disciplines.\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\n# GROUNDBREAKING SCIENCE\n\n## Discovery Science\n\nNIF\u2019s research helps users [gain new insights][153] into the mechanisms driving new and dying stars,\nsupernova hydrodynamics, black holes, cosmic magnetic fields, warm dense matter, and the interiors\nof giant planets.\n\n## Energy Security\n\nNIF experiments will provide the scientific basis for a revolution in energy production. [Inertial\nfusion energy][154] offers the potential for virtually unlimited safe and sustainable clean energy\nby harnessing the power of the sun and stars.\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\n# THE FUTURE OF SCIENCE\n\n## Research for the World\n\nThe opportunity to conduct [leading-edge research][155] with NIF\u2019s world-class facilities attracts\nresearchers and academic users who are innovative thinkers and future leaders in the broader\nscientific community. The interests of NIF users are represented by the [NIF User Group][156]\n\n## A New Generation\n\nNIF experiments help maintain the skills of nuclear weapons scientists and [train the next\ngeneration][157] to carry on stewardship of the nation\u2019s nuclear stockpile. Our research constantly\nchallenges these men and women to solve hard problems.\n\n## Join Our Mission\n\nFor the NIF & Photon Science Directorate, stewardship includes attracting, training, and retaining\nfuture generations of scientists, engineers, programmers, technicians, and other skilled workers.\n[Click here][158] to learn more about available career opportunities.\n\n# MORE INFORMATION\n\n[Learn How NIF Works][159]\n\n[Setting Records][160]\n\n[Take a Virtual Tour of NIF][161]\n\n[Science of NIF][162]\n\n[The Seven Wonders of NIF][163]\n\n[The People of NIF&PS][164]\n\n[Targets][165]\n\n[Optics][166]\n\n[Diagnostics][167]\n\n[[LLNL]][168]\nLawrence Livermore National Laboratory\n| 7000 East Avenue \u2022 Livermore, CA 94550 | LLNL-WEB-642493\nOperated by the Lawrence Livermore National Security, LLC for the Department of Energy's National\nNuclear Security Administration Learn about the Department of Energy's [Vulnerability Disclosure\nProgram][169]\n[[LLNS]][170] [[U.S. DOE]][171] [[NNSA]][172]\n[Home][173] [Disclaimer][174] [Privacy Notice][175]\n* [About][176]\n* [What Is NIF?][177]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][178]\n* [Laser Glass][179]\n* [Optical Switch][180]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][181]\n* [Deformable Mirror][182]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][183]\n* [Computer Control System][184]\n* [Target Fabrication][185]\n* [How NIF Works][186]\n* [Anatomy of a NIF Shot][187]\n* [Power Conditioning System][188]\n* [Injection Laser System][189]\n* [Amplifiers][190]\n* [Beam Transport][191]\n* [Final Optics][192]\n* [Target Chamber][193]\n* [Keys to Our Success][194]\n* [Facility Operations][195]\n* [Power and Energy][196]\n* [Control Systems][197]\n* [Optics][198]\n* [Targets][199]\n* [Diagnostics][200]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][201]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][202]\n* [Key Steps on the Path to NIF][203]\n* [50 Years of Laser Leadership][204]\n* [Building NIF][205]\n* [Who Works for NIF][206]\n* [People Profiles][207]\n* [Management][208]\n* [Developing the Workforce][209]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][210]\n* [Enduring Partnerships][211]\n* [Technology Transfer][212]\n* [Careers][213]\n* [FAQs][214]\n* [Visit Us][215]\n* [Science][216]\n* [NIF and Stockpile Modernization][217]\n* [High Energy Density Science][218]\n* [Advancing Weapon Physics][219]\n* [Achieving Fusion Ignition][220]\n* [National Security Applications][221]\n* [Developing New Capabilities][222]\n* [Discovery Science][223]\n* [Lab Astrophysics][224]\n* [Nuclear Astrophysics][225]\n* [Planetary Physics][226]\n* [Plasma Physics][227]\n* [Expanding Photonics Frontiers][228]\n* [DE Technology Programs][229]\n* [Advanced Optical Technologies][230]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][231]\n* [Advanced Laser Systems][232]\n* [Fiber Lasers][233]\n* [Materials for Laser Systems][234]\n* [Exploring Energy Security][235]\n* [Journal Articles][236]\n* [Livermore Inertial Fusion Energy References][237]\n* [NIF Users][238]\n* [NIF User Portal][239]\n* [NIF User Guide][240]\n* [NIF DLI User Guide][241]\n* [Experimental Capabilities][242]\n* [Shot RI Resources][243]\n* [Call for Proposals][244]\n* [Prior Year Awards][245]\n* [2024 Awarded Campaigns][246]\n* [2023 Awarded Campaigns][247]\n* [2022 Awarded Campaigns][248]\n* [2021 Awarded Campaigns][249]\n* [2020 Awarded Campaigns][250]\n* [2019 Awarded Campaigns][251]\n* [2018 Awarded Campaigns][252]\n* [2017 Awarded Campaigns][253]\n* [2016 Awarded Campaigns][254]\n* [2015 Awarded Campaigns][255]\n* [2014 Awarded Campaigns][256]\n* [NIF User Group][257]\n* [Bylaws][258]\n* [Executive Board][259]\n* [NIF Calendar][260]\n* [Target Shot Metrics][261]\n* [Conflict of Interest Policy][262]\n* [Jupiter Laser Facility][263]\n* [Multimedia][264]\n* [Photo Gallery][265]\n* [Playing Cards][266]\n* [Poster Gallery][267]\n* [Video Gallery][268]\n* [Education][269]\n* [How Lasers Work][270]\n* [How to Make a Star][271]\n* [Outreach][