ut][125]\n* [What Is NIF?][126]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][127]\n* [Laser Glass][128]\n* [Optical Switch][129]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][130]\n* [Deformable Mirror][131]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][132]\n* [Computer Control System][133]\n* [Target Fabrication][134]\n* [How NIF Works][135]\n* [Keys to Our Success][136]\n* [Who Works for NIF][137]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][138]\n* [Careers][139]\n* [FAQs][140]\n* [Visit Us][141]\n* [Science][142]\n* [NIF Users][143]\n* [Multimedia][144]\n* [Education][145]\n* [News][146]\n* [Programs][147]\n* [Contact][148]\n\n##### LLNL Menu\n* [Missions][149]\n* [Research][150]\n* [Doing Business][151]\n* [News][152]\n* [About][153]\n* [Careers][154]\n* [Community][155]\n\n## Secondary Menu\n\n[About][156]\n* [What Is NIF?][157]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][158]\n* [Laser Glass][159]\n* [Optical Switch][160]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][161]\n* [Deformable Mirror][162]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][163]\n* [Computer Control System][164]\n* [Target Fabrication][165]\n* [How NIF Works][166]\n* [Keys to Our Success][167]\n* [Who Works for NIF][168]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][169]\n* [Careers][170]\n* [FAQs][171]\n* [Visit Us][172]\n1. [Home][173]\n2. [About][174]\n3. The Seven Wonders of NIF\n\n# The Seven Wonders of NIF\n\n[Inside a NIF Preamplifier Support Structure]\nColor-enhanced image of the inside of a NIF preamplifier support structure. Credit: Damien Jemison\n\nNIF is a *tour de force* of science and technology development. Scientists, engineers, and\ntechnicians had to overcome a daunting array of challenges in designing and constructing NIF.\nWorking closely with industrial partners, the NIF team found solutions for NIF\u2019s optics in\nrapid-growth crystals, continuous-pour glass, optical coatings, and new finishing techniques that\ncan withstand NIF\u2019s extremely high energies. The team also worked with vendors to develop\npulsed-power electronics, innovative control systems, and advanced manufacturing capabilities.\n\nInformation on each of these breakthrough technologies is available via the links on the left.\n\nNext Up: [Laser Glass][175]\n\n[[LLNL]][176]\nLawrence Livermore National Laboratory\n| 7000 East Avenue \u2022 Livermore, CA 94550 | LLNL-WEB-642493\nOperated by the Lawrence Livermore National Security, LLC for the Department of Energy's National\nNuclear Security Administration Learn about the Department of Energy's [Vulnerability Disclosure\nProgram][177]\n[[LLNS]][178] [[U.S. DOE]][179] [[NNSA]][180]\n[Home][181] [Disclaimer][182] [Privacy Notice][183]\n* [About][184]\n* [What Is NIF?][185]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][186]\n* [Laser Glass][187]\n* [Optical Switch][188]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][189]\n* [Deformable Mirror][190]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][191]\n* [Computer Control System][192]\n* [Target Fabrication][193]\n* [How NIF Works][194]\n* [Anatomy of a NIF Shot][195]\n* [Power Conditioning System][196]\n* [Injection Laser System][197]\n* [Amplifiers][198]\n* [Beam Transport][199]\n* [Final Optics][200]\n* [Target Chamber][201]\n* [Keys to Our Success][202]\n* [Facility Operations][203]\n* [Power and Energy][204]\n* [Control Systems][205]\n* [Optics][206]\n* [Targets][207]\n* [Diagnostics][208]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][209]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][210]\n* [Key Steps on the Path to NIF][211]\n* [50 Years of Laser Leadership][212]\n* [Building NIF][213]\n* [Who Works for NIF][214]\n* [People Profiles][215]\n* [Management][216]\n* [Developing the Workforce][217]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][218]\n* [Enduring Partnerships][219]\n* [Technology Transfer][220]\n* [Careers][221]\n* [FAQs][222]\n* [Visit Us][223]\n* [Science][224]\n* [NIF and Stockpile Modernization][225]\n* [High Energy Density Science][226]\n* [Advancing Weapon Physics][227]\n* [Achieving Fusion Ignition][228]\n* [National Security Applications][229]\n* [Developing New Capabilities][230]\n* [Discovery Science][231]\n* [Lab Astrophysics][232]\n* [Nuclear Astrophysics][233]\n* [Planetary Physics][