ut][125]\n* [What Is NIF?][126]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][127]\n* [Laser Glass][128]\n* [Optical Switch][129]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][130]\n* [Deformable Mirror][131]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][132]\n* [Computer Control System][133]\n* [Target Fabrication][134]\n* [How NIF Works][135]\n* [Keys to Our Success][136]\n* [Who Works for NIF][137]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][138]\n* [Careers][139]\n* [FAQs][140]\n* [Visit Us][141]\n* [Science][142]\n* [NIF Users][143]\n* [Multimedia][144]\n* [Education][145]\n* [News][146]\n* [Programs][147]\n* [Contact][148]\n\n##### LLNL Menu\n* [Missions][149]\n* [Research][150]\n* [Doing Business][151]\n* [News][152]\n* [About][153]\n* [Careers][154]\n* [Community][155]\n\n## Secondary Menu\n\n[About][156]\n* [What Is NIF?][157]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][158]\n* [Laser Glass][159]\n* [Optical Switch][160]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][161]\n* [Deformable Mirror][162]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][163]\n* [Computer Control System][164]\n* [Target Fabrication][165]\n* [How NIF Works][166]\n* [Keys to Our Success][167]\n* [Who Works for NIF][168]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][169]\n* [Careers][170]\n* [FAQs][171]\n* [Visit Us][172]\n1. [Home][173]\n2. [About][174]\n3. [The Seven Wonders of NIF][175]\n4. Computer Control System\n\n# Computer Control System\n\n[Researchers in NIF Control Room]\nLLNL researchers and collaborators from Los Alamos National Laboratory prepare for an experiment.\nEvery aspect of a NIF shot is checked and monitored in NIF\u2019s NASA-style Control Room. Credit: Damien\nJemison\n\nA NIF target shot requires all 192 laser beams to arrive within 10 trillionths of a second of each\nother and to be aligned within 50 microns\u2014half the diameter of a strand of human hair\u2014all with the\nright frequency and energy level. It takes more than 66,000 control points to achieve this\nprecision, as well as one of the world\u2019s most sophisticated computer control systems. More than two\nthousand computers running 5 million lines of code make it possible to align and fire the 192 NIF\nlaser beams with some 800 channels of target diagnostic data efficiently and reliably several times\na day. The control system uses predetermined set-up and alignment scripts with operator oversight\nwhile test and full shot countdown sequences are fully automated.\n\nThe NIF Control Room is inspired by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration\u2019s Mission\nControl room in Houston, Texas. Control Room operators access data through a hierarchy of on-screen\ngraphics menus. Operators can also view videos of the laser beams and target from camera sensors\nincorporated into the beampath and target chamber.\n\n## More Information\n\n[\u201cKeeping NIF\u2019s Symphony of Controls in Tune,\u201d][176] *NIF & Photon Science News,* February 12, 2020\n\n[\u201cJorge Castro Morales Thrives on Multiple Responsibilities,\u201d][177] *NIF & Photon Science News,*\nFebruary 12, 2020\n\n[\u201cFrom Data to Discovery,\u201d][178] *Science & Technology Review*, January/February, 2011, Page 12\n(PDF)\n\nNext Up: [Target Fabrication][179]\n\n[[LLNL]][180]\nLawrence Livermore National Laboratory\n| 7000 East Avenue \u2022 Livermore, CA 94550 | LLNL-WEB-642493\nOperated by the Lawrence Livermore National Security, LLC for the Department of Energy's National\nNuclear Security Administration Learn about the Department of Energy's [Vulnerability Disclosure\nProgram][181]\n[[LLNS]][182] [[U.S. DOE]][183] [[NNSA]][184]\n[Home][185] [Disclaimer][186] [Privacy Notice][187]\n* [About][188]\n* [What Is NIF?][189]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][190]\n* [Laser Glass][191]\n* [Optical Switch][192]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][193]\n* [Deformable Mirror][194]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][195]\n* [Computer Control System][196]\n* [Target Fabrication][197]\n* [How NIF Works][198]\n* [Anatomy of a NIF Shot][199]\n* [Power Conditioning System][200]\n* [Injection Laser System][201]\n* [Amplifiers][202]\n* [Beam Transport][203]\n* [Final