            "text": "[ Skip to main content ][1]\n[U.S. flag]\n\nAn official website of the United States government\n\nHere\u2019s how you know\n\nHere\u2019s how you know\n\n**Official websites use .gov**\nA **.gov** website belongs to an official government organization in the United States.\n\n**Secure .gov websites use HTTPS**\nA **lock** ( [Lock] ) or **https://** means you\u2019ve safely connected to the .gov website. Share\nsensitive information only on official, secure websites.\n* [Our Purpose][2]\n* [Our Science and Technology][3]\n* [Join Our Team][4]\n* [Partner with Us][5]\n* [News][6]\n* [Community and Education][7]\n* [About][8]\n\n[[LLNL Logo]][9]\n[National Ignition Facility & Photon Science][10]\n\n## Primary Menu\n* [About ][11]\n* [What Is NIF?][12]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][13]\n* [Laser Glass][14]\n* [Optical Switch][15]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][16]\n* [Deformable Mirror][17]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][18]\n* [Computer Control System][19]\n* [Target Fabrication][20]\n* [How NIF Works][21]\n* [Anatomy of a NIF Shot][22]\n* [Power Conditioning System][23]\n* [Injection Laser System][24]\n* [Amplifiers][25]\n* [Beam Transport][26]\n* [Final Optics][27]\n* [Target Chamber][28]\n* [Keys to Our Success][29]\n* [Facility Operations][30]\n* [Power and Energy][31]\n* [Control Systems][32]\n* [Optics][33]\n* [Targets][34]\n* [Diagnostics][35]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][36]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][37]\n* [Who Works for NIF][38]\n* [People Profiles][39]\n* [Management][40]\n* [Developing the Workforce][41]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][42]\n* [Enduring Partnerships][43]\n* [Technology Transfer][44]\n* [Careers][45]\n* [FAQs][46]\n* [Visit Us][47]\n* [Science ][48]\n* [NIF and Stockpile Modernization][49]\n* [High Energy Density Science][50]\n* [Advancing Weapon Physics][51]\n* [Achieving Fusion Ignition][52]\n* [National Security Applications][53]\n* [Developing New Capabilities][54]\n* [Discovery Science][55]\n* [Lab Astrophysics][56]\n* [Nuclear Astrophysics][57]\n* [Planetary Physics][58]\n* [Plasma Physics][59]\n* [Expanding Photonics Frontiers][60]\n* [DE Technology Programs][61]\n* [Advanced Optical Technologies][62]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][63]\n* [Advanced Laser Systems][64]\n* [Fiber Lasers][65]\n* [Materials for Laser Systems][66]\n* [Exploring Energy Security][67]\n* [Journal Articles][68]\n* [Livermore Inertial Fusion Energy References][69]\n* [NIF Users ][70]\n* [NIF User Portal][71]\n* [NIF User Guide][72]\n* [NIF DLI User Guide][73]\n* [Experimental Capabilities][74]\n* [Shot RI Resources][75]\n* [Call for Proposals][76]\n* [Prior Year Awards][77]\n* [2024 Awarded Campaigns][78]\n* [2023 Awarded Campaigns][79]\n* [2022 Awarded Campaigns][80]\n* [2021 Awarded Campaigns][81]\n* [2020 Awarded Campaigns][82]\n* [2019 Awarded Campaigns][83]\n* [2018 Awarded Campaigns][84]\n* [2017 Awarded Campaigns][85]\n* [2016 Awarded Campaigns][86]\n* [2015 Awarded Campaigns][87]\n* [2014 Awarded Campaigns][88]\n* [NIF User Group][89]\n* [Bylaws][90]\n* [Executive Board][91]\n* [NIF Calendar][92]\n* [Target Shot Metrics][93]\n* [Conflict of Interest Policy][94]\n* [Jupiter Laser Facility][95]\n* [Multimedia ][96]\n* [Photo Gallery][97]\n* [Playing Cards][98]\n* [Poster Gallery][99]\n* [Video Gallery][100]\n* [Education ][101]\n* [How Lasers Work][102]\n* [How to Make a Star][103]\n* [Outreach][104]\n* [Laser Roadshow][105]\n* [Summer Scholar Internship Program][106]\n* [Seminars][107]\n* [Student Spotlight][108]\n* [Scholar Tours][109]\n* [Glossary][110]\n* [External Resources][111]\n* [News ][112]\n* [The Age of Ignition][113]\n* [In the News][114]\n* [NIF in the News: Video][115]\n* [Programs ][116]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][117]\n* [Facilities][118]\n* [Publications][119]\n* [People][120]\n* [Job Postings][121]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][122]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][123]\n* [Contact][124]\n\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\n\n## Mobile Menu\n\n##### Site Menu\n* [About][125]\n* [What Is NIF?][126]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][127]\n* [Laser Glass][128]\n* [Optical Switch][129]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][130]\n* [Deformable Mirror][131]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][132]\n* [Computer Control System][133]\n* [Target Fabrication][134]\n* [How NIF Works][135]\n* [Keys to Our Success][136]\n* [Who Works for NIF][137]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][138]\n* [Careers][139]\n* [FAQs][140]\n* [Visit Us][141]\n* [Science][142]\n* [NIF Users][143]\n* [Multimedia][144]\n* [Education][145]\n* [News][146]\n* [Programs][147]\n* [Contact][148]\n\n##### LLNL Menu\n* [Missions][149]\n* [Research][150]\n* [Doing Business][151]\n* [News][152]\n* [About][153]\n* [Careers][154]\n* [Community][155]\n\n## Secondary Menu\n\n[About][156]\n* [What Is NIF?][157]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][158]\n* [Laser Glass][159]\n* [Optical Switch][160]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][161]\n* [Deformable Mirror][162]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][163]\n* [Computer Control System][164]\n* [Target Fabrication][165]\n* [How NIF Works][166]\n* [Keys to Our Success][167]\n* [Who Works for NIF][168]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][169]\n* [Careers][170]\n* [FAQs][171]\n* [Visit Us][172]\n1. [Home][173]\n2. [About][174]\n3. [The Seven Wonders of NIF][175]\n4. Target Fabrication\n\n# Target Fabrication\n\n[Technician Inspects a NIF Target]\nNIF targets are complicated engineering marvels in tiny packages.\n\nCreating targets for NIF requires interplay among target designers, materials scientists, precision\nengineers, and a precision fabrication and assembly complex. The laser drives a target capsule\ninward at nearly a million miles an hour. Because the targets are subjected to extreme\ntemperatures\u2014greater than those in the Sun\u2014and pressures\u2014similar to those found in the core of\nJupiter\u2014during experiments, the targets must be designed, fabricated, and assembled with extreme\nprecision and demanding materials requirements in a clean environment.\n\nFor example, components must be machined to within an accuracy of 1 micron (1 millionth of a meter).\nMany material structures and features can be no larger than 100 nanometers, which is just 1/1,000th\nthe width of a human hair. And a capsule must have a smoothness tolerance approaching 1\nnanometer\u2014equivalent to removing all features on the Earth\u2019s surface taller than 60 meters (about\n200 feet). Each target is characterized using an array of specialized optical, x-ray and mechanical\ninspection systems.\n\n### More Information\n\n[Partners in Precision Engineering: Big Lasers, Tiny Targets][176]\n\n[[LLNL]][177]\nLawrence Livermore National Laboratory\n| 7000 East Avenue \u2022 Livermore, CA 94550 | LLNL-WEB-642493\nOperated by the Lawrence Livermore National Security, LLC for the Department of Energy's National\nNuclear Security Administration Learn about the Department of Energy's [Vulnerability Disclosure\nProgram][178]\n[[LLNS]][179] [[U.S. DOE]][180] [[NNSA]][181]\n[Home][182] [Disclaimer][183] [Privacy Notice][184]\n* [About][185]\n* [What Is NIF?][186]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][187]\n* [Laser Glass][188]\n* [Optical Switch][189]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][190]\n* [Deformable Mirror][191]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][192]\n* [Computer Control System][193]\n* [Target Fabrication][194]\n* [How NIF Works][195]\n* [Anatomy of a NIF Shot][196]\n* [Power Conditioning System][197]\n* [Injection Laser System][198]\n* [Amplifiers][199]\n* [Beam Transport][200]\n* [Final Optics][201]\n* [Target Chamber][202]\n* [Keys to Our Success][203]\n* [Facility Operations][204]\n* [Power and Energy][205]\n* [Control Systems][206]\n* [Optics][207]\n* [Targets][208]\n* [Diagnostics][209]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][210]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][211]\n* [Key Steps on the Path to NIF][212]\n* [50 Years of Laser Leadership][213]\n* [Building NIF][214]\n* [Who Works for NIF][215]\n* [People Profiles][216]\n* [Management][217]\n* [Developing the Workforce][218]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][219]\n* [E