            "text": "[ Skip to main content ][1]\n[U.S. flag]\n\nAn official website of the United States government\n\nHere\u2019s how you know\n\nHere\u2019s how you know\n\n**Official websites use .gov**\nA **.gov** website belongs to an official government organization in the United States.\n\n**Secure .gov websites use HTTPS**\nA **lock** ( [Lock] ) or **https://** means you\u2019ve safely connected to the .gov website. Share\nsensitive information only on official, secure websites.\n* [Our Purpose][2]\n* [Our Science and Technology][3]\n* [Join Our Team][4]\n* [Partner with Us][5]\n* [News][6]\n* [Community and Education][7]\n* [About][8]\n\n[[LLNL Logo]][9]\n[National Ignition Facility & Photon Science][10]\n\n## Primary Menu\n* [About ][11]\n* [What Is NIF?][12]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][13]\n* [Laser Glass][14]\n* [Optical Switch][15]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][16]\n* [Deformable Mirror][17]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][18]\n* [Computer Control System][19]\n* [Target Fabrication][20]\n* [How NIF Works][21]\n* [Anatomy of a NIF Shot][22]\n* [Power Conditioning System][23]\n* [Injection Laser System][24]\n* [Amplifiers][25]\n* [Beam Transport][26]\n* [Final Optics][27]\n* [Target Chamber][28]\n* [Keys to Our Success][29]\n* [Facility Operations][30]\n* [Power and Energy][31]\n* [Control Systems][32]\n* [Optics][33]\n* [Targets][34]\n* [Diagnostics][35]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][36]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][37]\n* [Who Works for NIF][38]\n* [People Profiles][39]\n* [Management][40]\n* [Developing the Workforce][41]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][42]\n* [Enduring Partnerships][43]\n* [Technology Transfer][44]\n* [Careers][45]\n* [FAQs][46]\n* [Visit Us][47]\n* [Science ][48]\n* [NIF and Stockpile Modernization][49]\n* [High Energy Density Science][50]\n* [Advancing Weapon Physics][51]\n* [Achieving Fusion Ignition][52]\n* [National Security Applications][53]\n* [Developing New Capabilities][54]\n* [Discovery Science][55]\n* [Lab Astrophysics][56]\n* [Nuclear Astrophysics][57]\n* [Planetary Physics][58]\n* [Plasma Physics][59]\n* [Expanding Photonics Frontiers][60]\n* [DE Technology Programs][61]\n* [Advanced Optical Technologies][62]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][63]\n* [Advanced Laser Systems][64]\n* [Fiber Lasers][65]\n* [Materials for Laser Systems][66]\n* [Exploring Energy Security][67]\n* [Journal Articles][68]\n* [Livermore Inertial Fusion Energy References][69]\n* [NIF Users ][70]\n* [NIF User Portal][71]\n* [NIF User Guide][72]\n* [NIF DLI User Guide][73]\n* [Experimental Capabilities][74]\n* [Shot RI Resources][75]\n* [Call for Proposals][76]\n* [Prior Year Awards][77]\n* [2024 Awarded Campaigns][78]\n* [2023 Awarded Campaigns][79]\n* [2022 Awarded Campaigns][80]\n* [2021 Awarded Campaigns][81]\n* [2020 Awarded Campaigns][82]\n* [2019 Awarded Campaigns][83]\n* [2018 Awarded Campaigns][84]\n* [2017 Awarded Campaigns][85]\n* [2016 Awarded Campaigns][86]\n* [2015 Awarded Campaigns][87]\n* [2014 Awarded Campaigns][88]\n* [NIF User Group][89]\n* [Bylaws][90]\n* [Executive Board][91]\n* [NIF Calendar][92]\n* [Target Shot Metrics][93]\n* [Conflict of Interest Policy][94]\n* [Jupiter Laser Facility][95]\n* [Multimedia ][96]\n* [Photo Gallery][97]\n* [Playing Cards][98]\n* [Poster Gallery][99]\n* [Video Gallery][100]\n* [Education ][101]\n* [How Lasers Work][102]\n* [How to Make a Star][103]\n* [Outreach][104]\n* [Laser Roadshow][105]\n* [Summer Scholar Internship Program][106]\n* [Seminars][107]\n* [Student Spotlight][108]\n* [Scholar Tours][109]\n* [Glossary][110]\n* [External Resources][111]\n* [News ][112]\n* [The Age of Ignition][113]\n* [In the News][114]\n* [NIF in the News: Video][115]\n* [Programs ][116]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][117]\n* [Facilities][118]\n* [Publications][119]\n* [People][120]\n* [Job Postings][121]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][122]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][123]\n* [Contact][124]\n\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\n\n## Mobile Menu\n\n##### Site Menu\n* [About][125]\n* [What Is NIF?][126]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][127]\n* [How NIF Works][128]\n* [Anatomy of a NIF Shot][129]\n* [Power Conditioning System][130]\n* [Injection Laser System][131]\n* [Amplifiers][132]\n* [Beam Transport][133]\n* [Final Optics][134]\n* [Target Chamber][135]\n* [Keys to Our Success][136]\n* [Who Works for NIF][137]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][138]\n* [Careers][139]\n* [FAQs][140]\n* [Visit Us][141]\n* [Science][142]\n* [NIF Users][143]\n* [Multimedia][144]\n* [Education][145]\n* [News][146]\n* [Programs][147]\n* [Contact][148]\n\n##### LLNL Menu\n* [Missions][149]\n* [Research][150]\n* [Doing Business][151]\n* [News][152]\n* [About][153]\n* [Careers][154]\n* [Community][155]\n\nPlanning the Experiment\n\n## Scientists use sophisticated computer models and the results of previous research to design an\n## experiment.\n\nDesigning the Target\n\n## Designers and engineers develop the target based on the experiment\u2019s requirements.\n\nBuilding the Target\n\n## Technicians fabricate, assemble, and measure the components to millionth-of-a-meter tolerances.\n\nViewing the Target\n\n## NIF targets are designed to provide diagnostics with line-of-sight access to the capsule\n## suspended inside the hohlraum.\n\nInserting the Target\n\n## The target is mounted on an inserter and placed in the center of the Target Chamber; many targets\n## are cooled to just a few degrees above absolute zero.\n\nPositioning the Diagnostics\n\n## Diagnostics are inserted into the 10-meter-diameter Target Chamber to capture the results of the\n## experiment. More than 100 different diagnostics are available to record every aspect of NIF\n## experiments.\n\nShaping the Laser Pulse\n\n## The temporal shape, wavelength, and timing of the laser pulse are precisely set in the Master\n## Oscillator Room. Pulses of a few billionths of a joule are amplified several billion times before\n## being injected into NIF\u2019s main laser amplifiers.\n\nPreparing for the Shot\n\n## Control Room operators remotely align the laser beams and diagnostics and perform the final shot\n## countdown.\n\nEnergizing the Lasers\n\n## When the shot is fired, the NIF capacitor bays deliver 400 megajoules of stored electrical energy\n## to the main laser\u2019s 7,680 flashlamps.\n\nBoosting the Laser Power\n\n## In the laser bays, the amplifiers increase the one-joule input from the injection laser to nearly\n## 4 million joules of infrared laser light.\n\nFocusing on the Target\n\n## In the Target Bay, the final optics assemblies convert the infrared light to about 2 million\n## joules of high-energy ultraviolet light and direct the laser beams to the target at the center of\n## the Target Chamber.\n\nTriggering Nuclear Fusion\n\n## NIF's lasers compress the fusion fuel to pressures that exceed 100 billion times Earth's\n## atmosphere and temperatures of more than 100 million Kelvin (180 million degrees Fahrenheit),\n## forcing hydrogen atoms to fuse in a controlled thermonuclear reaction.\n\nAnalyzing the Data\n\n## Data from NIF experiments (right) are analyzed on LLNL supercomputers and compared with model\n## predictions (left), resulting in improved computer models and new experimental designs.\n\n[[LLNL]][156]\nLawrence Livermore National Laboratory\n| 7000 East Avenue \u2022 Livermore, CA 94550 | LLNL-WEB-642493\nOperated by the Lawrence Livermore National Security, LLC for the Department of Energy's National\nNuclear Security Administration Learn about the Department of Energy's [Vulnerability Disclosure\nProgram][157]\n[[LLNS]][158] [[U.S. DOE]][159] [[NNSA]][160]\n[Home][161] [Disclaimer][162] [Privacy Notice][163]\n* [About][164]\n* [What Is NIF?][165]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][166]\n* [Laser Glass][167]\n* [Optical Switch][168]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][169]\n* [Deformable Mirror][170]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][171]\n* [Computer Control System][172]\n* [Target Fabrication][173]\n* [How NIF Works][174]\n* [Anatomy of a NIF Shot][175]\n* [Po