rophysics][57]\n* [Planetary Physics][58]\n* [Plasma Physics][59]\n* [Expanding Photonics Frontiers][60]\n* [DE Technology Programs][61]\n* [Advanced Optical Technologies][62]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][63]\n* [Advanced Laser Systems][64]\n* [Fiber Lasers][65]\n* [Materials for Laser Systems][66]\n* [Exploring Energy Security][67]\n* [Journal Articles][68]\n* [Livermore Inertial Fusion Energy References][69]\n* [NIF Users ][70]\n* [NIF User Portal][71]\n* [NIF User Guide][72]\n* [NIF DLI User Guide][73]\n* [Experimental Capabilities][74]\n* [Shot RI Resources][75]\n* [Call for Proposals][76]\n* [Prior Year Awards][77]\n* [2024 Awarded Campaigns][78]\n* [2023 Awarded Campaigns][79]\n* [2022 Awarded Campaigns][80]\n* [2021 Awarded Campaigns][81]\n* [2020 Awarded Campaigns][82]\n* [2019 Awarded Campaigns][83]\n* [2018 Awarded Campaigns][84]\n* [2017 Awarded Campaigns][85]\n* [2016 Awarded Campaigns][86]\n* [2015 Awarded Campaigns][87]\n* [2014 Awarded Campaigns][88]\n* [NIF User Group][89]\n* [Bylaws][90]\n* [Executive Board][91]\n* [NIF Calendar][92]\n* [Target Shot Metrics][93]\n* [Conflict of Interest Policy][94]\n* [Jupiter Laser Facility][95]\n* [Multimedia ][96]\n* [Photo Gallery][97]\n* [Playing Cards][98]\n* [Poster Gallery][99]\n* [Video Gallery][100]\n* [Education ][101]\n* [How Lasers Work][102]\n* [How to Make a Star][103]\n* [Outreach][104]\n* [Laser Roadshow][105]\n* [Summer Scholar Internship Program][106]\n* [Seminars][107]\n* [Student Spotlight][108]\n* [Scholar Tours][109]\n* [Glossary][110]\n* [External Resources][111]\n* [News ][112]\n* [The Age of Ignition][113]\n* [In the News][114]\n* [NIF in the News: Video][115]\n* [Programs ][116]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][117]\n* [Facilities][118]\n* [Publications][119]\n* [People][120]\n* [Job Postings][121]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][122]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][123]\n* [Contact][124]\n\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\n\n## Mobile Menu\n\n##### Site Menu\n* [About][125]\n* [What Is NIF?][126]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][127]\n* [How NIF Works][128]\n* [Anatomy of a NIF Shot][129]\n* [Power Conditioning System][130]\n* [Injection Laser System][131]\n* [Amplifiers][132]\n* [Beam Transport][133]\n* [Final Optics][134]\n* [Target Chamber][135]\n* [Keys to Our Success][136]\n* [Who Works for NIF][137]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][138]\n* [Careers][139]\n* [FAQs][140]\n* [Visit Us][141]\n* [Science][142]\n* [NIF Users][143]\n* [Multimedia][144]\n* [Education][145]\n* [News][146]\n* [Programs][147]\n* [Contact][148]\n\n##### LLNL Menu\n* [Missions][149]\n* [Research][150]\n* [Doing Business][151]\n* [News][152]\n* [About][153]\n* [Careers][154]\n* [Community][155]\n\n## Secondary Menu\n\n[About][156]\n* [What Is NIF?][157]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][158]\n* [How NIF Works][159]\n* [Anatomy of a NIF Shot][160]\n* [Power Conditioning System][161]\n* [Injection Laser System][162]\n* [Amplifiers][163]\n* [Beam Transport][164]\n* [Final Optics][165]\n* [Target Chamber][166]\n* [Keys to Our Success][167]\n* [Who Works for NIF][168]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][169]\n* [Careers][170]\n* [FAQs][171]\n* [Visit Us][172]\n1. [Home][173]\n2. [About][174]\n3. [How NIF Works][175]\n4. Power Conditioning System\n\n# Power Conditioning System\n\n[NIF Capacitor Bay]\nDeployed throughout four 1,150-square-meter (12,500-square-foot) capacitor bays, the power\nconditioning system stores approximately 400 megajoules (million joules) of electrical energy for\neach NIF shot.\n\nThe NIF power conditioning system (PCS) drives the 7,680 flashlamps located in the NIF laser\u2019s main\nand power amplifiers, delivering nearly 330 million joules of electrical energy on each NIF shot.\nEnergy is stored over a period of 60 seconds in 3,840 high-voltage capacitors before being released\nin a 400-microsecond burst.\n\n[Power Conditioning System Cables]\nThe power conditioning system has more than 160 kilometers (100 miles) of high-voltage cable.\n\nPeak current for the system exceeds 100 million amperes and the peak power exceeds 1 terawatt (1\ntrillion watts)\u2014more power than the entire United States uses in that same fraction of a second.\n\nThe system comprises 192 modules, eight modules for each bundle of eight laser beams. In addition to\na main energy storage circuit, each module contains a pre-ionization circuit designed to prepare the\nflashlamps for the main discharge as well as provide information on the health of the system\u2019s\nflashlamps following each main discharge. Individual modules weigh more than 11 tons and are more\nthan 3 meters tall, 4 meters long, and 3 meters deep.\n\nAll modules are operated by a single operator using a custom integrated software control system.\nEvery module is equipped with an embedded controller that controls and diagnoses all components and\nfunctions inside the module and communicates to the supervisory control system over high-speed\nEthernet connections.\n\nThe modules were produced by NIF\u2019s industrial partners and delivered as working units to the\nfacility. Production of the power conditioning modules was completed in December 2007.\n\n### More Information\n\n[\u201cPowering Lasers Around the World,\u201d][176] *NIF & Photon Science News,* February, 2018\n\n[\u201cNew Power Supplies Will Keep NIF on Target,\u201d][177] *NIF & Photon Science News,* November, 2015\n\nNext Up: [Injection Laser System][178]\n\n[[LLNL]][179]\nLawrence Livermore National Laboratory\n| 7000 East Avenue \u2022 Livermore, CA 94550 | LLNL-WEB-642493\nOperated by the Lawrence Livermore National Security, LLC for the Department of Energy's National\nNuclear Security Administration Learn about the Department of Energy's [Vulnerability Disclosure\nProgram][180]\n[[LLNS]][181] [[U.S. DOE]][182] [[NNSA]][183]\n[Home][184] [Disclaimer][185] [Privacy Notice][186]\n* [About][187]\n* [What Is NIF?][188]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][189]\n* [Laser Glass][190]\n* [Optical Switch][191]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][192]\n* [Deformable Mirror][193]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][194]\n* [Computer Control System][195]\n* [Target Fabrication][196]\n* [How NIF Works][197]\n* [Anatomy of a NIF Shot][198]\n* [Power Conditioning System][199]\n* [Injection Laser System][200]\n* [Amplifiers][201]\n* [Beam Transport][202]\n* [Final Optics][203]\n* [Target Chamber][204]\n* [Keys to Our Success][205]\n* [Facility Operations][206]\n* [Power and Energy][207]\n* [Control Systems][208]\n* [Optics][209]\n* [Targets][210]\n* [Diagnostics][211]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][212]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][213]\n* [Key Steps on the Path to NIF][214]\n* [50 Years of Laser Leadership][215]\n* [Building NIF][216]\n* [Who Works for NIF][217]\n* [People Profiles][218]\n* [Management][219]\n* [Developing the Workforce][220]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][221]\n* [Enduring Partnerships][222]\n* [Technology Transfer][223]\n* [Careers][224]\n* [FAQs][225]\n* [Visit Us][226]\n* [Science][227]\n* [NIF and Stockpile Modernization][228]\n* [High Energy Density Science][229]\n* [Advancing Weapon Physics][230]\n* [Achieving Fusion Ignition][231]\n* [National Security Applications][232]\n* [Developing New Capabilities][233]\n* [Discovery Science][234]\n* [Lab Astrophysics][235]\n* [Nuclear Astrophysics][236]\n* [Planetary Physics][237]\n* [Plasma Physics][238]\n* [Expanding Photonics Frontiers][239]\n* [DE Technology Programs][240]\n* [Advanced Optical Technologies][241]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][242]\n* [Advanced Laser Systems][243]\n* [Fiber Lasers][244]\n* [Materials for Laser Systems][245]\n* [Exploring Energy Security][246]\n* [Journal Articles][247]\n* [Livermore Inertial Fusion Energy References][248]\n* [NIF Users][249]\n* [NIF User Portal][250]\n* [NIF User Guide][251]\n* [NIF DLI User Guide][252]\n* [Experimental Capabilities][253]\n* [Shot RI Resources][254]\n* [Call for Proposals][255]\n* [Prior Year Awards][256]\n* [2024 Awarded Campaigns][257]\n* [2023 Awarded Campaigns][258]\n* [2022 Awarded Campaigns][259]\n* [2021 Awarded Campaigns][260]\n* [2020 Awarded Campaigns][261]\n* [2019 Awarded Campaigns][262]\n* [2018 Awarded Campaigns][263]\n* [2017 Awarded Campaigns][264]\n* [2016 Awarded Campaigns][265]\n* [2015 Awarded Campaigns][266]\n* [2014 Awarded Campaigns][267]\n* [NIF User Group][268]\n* [Bylaws][269]\n* [Executive Board][270]\n* [NIF Calendar][271]\n* [Target Shot Metrics][272]\n* [Conflict of Interest Policy][273]\n* [Jupiter Laser Facility][274]\n* [Multimedia][275]\n* [Photo Gallery][276]\n* [Playing Cards][277]\n* [Poster Gallery][278]\n* [Video Gallery][279]\n* [Education][280]\n* [How Lasers Work][281]\n* [How to Make a Star][282]\n* [Outreach][283]\n* [Laser Roadshow][284]\n* [Summer Scholar Internship Program][285]\n* [Seminars][286]\n* [Student Spotlight][287]\n* [Scholar Tours][288]\n* [Glossary][289]\n* [External Resources][290]\n* [News][291]\n* [The Age of Ignition][292]\n* [In the News][293]\n* [NIF in the News: Video][294]\n* [Programs][295]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][296]\n* [Facilities][297]\n* [Publications][298]\n* [People][299]\n* [Job Postings][300]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][301]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][302]\n* [Contact][303]\n\n[1]: #main-content\n[2]: https://www.llnl.gov/purpose\n[3]: https://www.llnl.gov/science-technology\n[4]: https://www.llnl.gov/join-our-team\n[5]: https://www.llnl.gov/partner\n[6]: https://www.llnl.gov/news\n[7]: https://www.llnl.gov/community-education\n[8]: https://www.llnl.gov/about\n[9]: https://www.llnl.gov\n[10]: https://lasers.llnl.gov/\n[11]: /about\n[12]: /about/what-is-nif\n[13]: /about/seven-wonders\n[14]: /about/seven-wonders/laser-glass\n[15]: /about/seven-wonders/optical-switch\n[16]: /about/seven-wonders/preamplifier-modules\n[17]: /about/seven-wonders/deformable-mirror\n[18]: /about/seven-wonders/rapid-growth-crystals\n[19]: /about/seven-wonders/computer-control-system\n[20]: /about/seven-wonders/target-fabrication\n[21]: /about/how-nif-wor