rophysics][57]\n* [Planetary Physics][58]\n* [Plasma Physics][59]\n* [Expanding Photonics Frontiers][60]\n* [DE Technology Programs][61]\n* [Advanced Optical Technologies][62]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][63]\n* [Advanced Laser Systems][64]\n* [Fiber Lasers][65]\n* [Materials for Laser Systems][66]\n* [Exploring Energy Security][67]\n* [Journal Articles][68]\n* [Livermore Inertial Fusion Energy References][69]\n* [NIF Users ][70]\n* [NIF User Portal][71]\n* [NIF User Guide][72]\n* [NIF DLI User Guide][73]\n* [Experimental Capabilities][74]\n* [Shot RI Resources][75]\n* [Call for Proposals][76]\n* [Prior Year Awards][77]\n* [2024 Awarded Campaigns][78]\n* [2023 Awarded Campaigns][79]\n* [2022 Awarded Campaigns][80]\n* [2021 Awarded Campaigns][81]\n* [2020 Awarded Campaigns][82]\n* [2019 Awarded Campaigns][83]\n* [2018 Awarded Campaigns][84]\n* [2017 Awarded Campaigns][85]\n* [2016 Awarded Campaigns][86]\n* [2015 Awarded Campaigns][87]\n* [2014 Awarded Campaigns][88]\n* [NIF User Group][89]\n* [Bylaws][90]\n* [Executive Board][91]\n* [NIF Calendar][92]\n* [Target Shot Metrics][93]\n* [Conflict of Interest Policy][94]\n* [Jupiter Laser Facility][95]\n* [Multimedia ][96]\n* [Photo Gallery][97]\n* [Playing Cards][98]\n* [Poster Gallery][99]\n* [Video Gallery][100]\n* [Education ][101]\n* [How Lasers Work][102]\n* [How to Make a Star][103]\n* [Outreach][104]\n* [Laser Roadshow][105]\n* [Summer Scholar Internship Program][106]\n* [Seminars][107]\n* [Student Spotlight][108]\n* [Scholar Tours][109]\n* [Glossary][110]\n* [External Resources][111]\n* [News ][112]\n* [The Age of Ignition][113]\n* [In the News][114]\n* [NIF in the News: Video][115]\n* [Programs ][116]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][117]\n* [Facilities][118]\n* [Publications][119]\n* [People][120]\n* [Job Postings][121]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][122]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][123]\n* [Contact][124]\n\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\n\n## Mobile Menu\n\n##### Site Menu\n* [About][125]\n* [What Is NIF?][126]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][127]\n* [How NIF Works][128]\n* [Keys to Our Success][129]\n* [Facility Operations][130]\n* [Power and Energy][131]\n* [Control Systems][132]\n* [Optics][133]\n* [Targets][134]\n* [Diagnostics][135]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][136]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][137]\n* [Who Works for NIF][138]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][139]\n* [Careers][140]\n* [FAQs][141]\n* [Visit Us][142]\n* [Science][143]\n* [NIF Users][144]\n* [Multimedia][145]\n* [Education][146]\n* [News][147]\n* [Programs][148]\n* [Contact][149]\n\n##### LLNL Menu\n* [Missions][150]\n* [Research][151]\n* [Doing Business][152]\n* [News][153]\n* [About][154]\n* [Careers][155]\n* [Community][156]\n\n## Secondary Menu\n\n[About][157]\n* [What Is NIF?][158]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][159]\n* [How NIF Works][160]\n* [Keys to Our Success][161]\n* [Facility Operations][162]\n* [Power and Energy][163]\n* [Control Systems][164]\n* [Optics][165]\n* [Targets][166]\n* [Diagnostics][167]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][168]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][169]\n* [Who Works for NIF][170]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][171]\n* [Careers][172]\n* [FAQs][173]\n* [Visit Us][174]\n1. [Home][175]\n2. [About][176]\n3. Keys to Our Success\n\n# Keys to Our Success\n\n[Photo montage of NIF people at work]\n\n# People: The Eighth Wonder of NIF\n\nTeamwork among the various disciplines that contribute to experiments and directorate operations has\nbeen a major factor in NIF\u2019s success.\n\nSince the first full-scale experiments were conducted on the National Ignition Facility in 2009, the\nskilled and dedicated members of the NIF & Photon Science Team, along with their many partners and\ncollaborators, have made remarkable progress in every facet of the directorate\u2019s operations.\n\n> The uncharted path the team has carved is rich with discovery, invention, and new understanding.\n\nFrom the outset of facility construction in the early 1990s, our people have faced\u2014and met\u2014a\ndaunting array of engineering and logistics challenges (see [ \u201cThe Seven Wonders of NIF\u201d][177]) to\nbring the vision of Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory and its [laser, optics, and fusion\npioneers][178] to fruition.\n\nThanks to the untiring efforts of these pioneers and their successors, NIF has emerged as one of the\nmost reliable and productive scientific instruments ever built\u2014a highly flexible and reproducible\nlaser system capable of conducting a wide range of unique experiments in support of the nation\u2019s\nsecurity, while also advancing the frontiers of high energy density and inertial confinement fusion\nscience.\n\nYears of testing, learning through experience, and equipment and process improvements have enabled\nthe NIF&PS Team to push the envelope of laser energy and power beyond the facility\u2019s original design\ncriteria at a constant level of funding\u2014while making safety a top priority in all aspects of\ndirectorate operations.\n\n[Zarco (left) and Gutierrez at work in a NIF radiation cleanroom.]\nNIF Radiation Technicians Judy Zarco (left) and Myrna Gutierrez at work in a NIF radiation\ncleanroom. Zarco and Gutierrez were working as cleanroom custodians when they saw an opportunity for\ncareer advancement. Encouraged by NIF managers, they began a two-year full-time radiation safety\nprogram at Las Positas Community College and attended radiation control technician (RCT) training at\nNIF, all while working 13-hour shifts, to earn their certification as RCTs. Credit: Charlie Hunts\n\nThe team has stayed on top of ever-evolving scientific needs through new knowledge and techniques,\nbetter modeling and simulation based on experimental results, new experimental platforms, new\nequipment and procedures for improved efficiency, advanced diagnostics, breakthroughs in lasers and\noptics, and increasingly complex custom-made targets.\n\n\u201cWe\u2019ve all made sacrifices to get here,\" said NIF Operations Manager Bruno Van Wonterghem, \"but it\nis worth it to stand here now in a structure that many said could never be built, as it performs on\na day-to-day basis what many believed it couldn\u2019t. We converted many of the naysayers into\nsupporters of the new technology as the project proceeded. I\u2019m proud of the team and what we\u2019ve\naccomplished.\u201d\n\n**Maintaining the Stockpile**\n\nNIF is a crucial element of the science-based [ Stockpile Stewardship Program][179] to maintain the\nsafety, security, and reliability of the nation\u2019s nuclear stockpile without underground testing.\nResearchers use NIF experiments to further their understanding of [ weapon physics][180] issues and\nthe effects of aging on weapons-relevant materials. NIF experimental data validate 3D weapon\nsimulation codes and inform Life Extension programs, the regularly planned refurbishments of nuclear\nweapon systems to ensure long-term reliability. In addition, experiments devoted to [studying\ninertial confinement fusion][181] aid in investigating questions remaining from underground nuclear\ntesting.\n\nWith more than 10 years of operation and more than 3,000 shots, the NIF Team continues to [set\nrecords][182] in power, energy, and neutron yield and to provide new insights into phenomena like\nthe metallization of hydrogen and the extreme conditions in the interiors of distant planets (see\n[Discovery Science][183]). While the scientific Grand Challenge of fusion ignition remains an\nunrealized goal, each step in the journey provides new insights and helps close the gaps in our\nknowledge of unresolved issues.\n\nThe uncharted path the team has carved is rich with discovery, invention, and new understanding.\nFrom administrative professionals to x-ray technicians, and every profession and job skill in\nbetween, NIF & Photon Science people have and will continue to serve as committed stewards of the\nnation\u2019s security and scientific leadership, now and in generations to come.\n\nThe articles in \u201cKeys to Our Success\u201d highlight the people and programs that have contributed to the\nsuccess of the NIF & Photon Science Directorate and the National Ignition Facility over more than a\ndecade.\n\n### More Information\n\n[Who Works for NIF & PS?][184]\n\nNext Up: [Facility Operations][185]\n\n[[LLNL]][186]\nLawrence Livermore National Laboratory\n| 7000 East Avenue \u2022 Livermore, CA 94550 | LLNL-WEB-780932\nOperated by the Lawrence Livermore National Security, LLC for the Department of Energy's National\nNuclear Security Administration Learn about the Department of Energy's [Vulnerability Disclosure\nProgram][187]\n[[LLNS]][188] [[U.S. DOE]][189] [[NNSA]][190]\n[Home][191] [Disclaimer][192] [Privacy Notice][193]\n* [About][194]\n* [What Is NIF?][195]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][196]\n* [Laser Glass][197]\n* [Optical Switch][198]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][199]\n* [Deformable Mirror][200]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][201]\n* [Computer Control System][202]\n* [Target Fabrication][203]\n* [How NIF Works][204]\n* [Anatomy of a NIF Shot][205]\n* [Power Conditioning System][206]\n* [Injection Laser System][207]\n* [Amplifiers][208]\n* [Beam Transport][209]\n* [Final Optics][210]\n* [Target Chamber][211]\n* [Keys to Our Success][212]\n* [Facility Operations][213]\n* [Power and Energy][214]\n* [Control Systems][215]\n* [Optics][216]\n* [Targets][217]\n* [Diagnostics][218]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][219]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][220]\n* [Key Steps on the Path to NIF][221]\n* [50 Years of Laser Leadership][222]\n* [Building NIF][223]\n* [Who Works for NIF][224]\n* [People Profiles][225]\n* [Management][226]\n* [Developing the Workforce][227]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][228]\n* [Enduring Partnerships][229]\n* [Technology Transfer][230]\n* [Careers][231]\n* [FAQs][232]\n* [Visit Us][233]\n* [Science][234]\n* [NIF and Stockpile Modernization][235]\n* [High Energy Density Science][236]\n* [Advancing Weapon Physics][237]\n* [Achieving Fusion Ignition][238]\n* [National Security Applications][239]\n* [Developing New Capabilities][240]\n* [Discovery Science][241]\n* [Lab Astrophysics][242]\n* [Nuclear Astrophysics][243]\n* [Planetary Physics][244]\n* [Plasma Physics][245]\n* [Expanding Photonics Frontiers][246]\n* [DE Technology Programs][247]\n* [Advanced Optical Technologies][248]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][249]\n* [Advanced Laser Systems][250]\n* [Fiber Lasers][251]\n* [Materials for Laser Systems][252]\n* [Exploring Energy Security][253]\n* [Jou"
