            "text": "[ Skip to main content ][1]\n[U.S. flag]\n\nAn official website of the United States government\n\nHere\u2019s how you know\n\nHere\u2019s how you know\n\n**Official websites use .gov**\nA **.gov** website belongs to an official government organization in the United States.\n\n**Secure .gov websites use HTTPS**\nA **lock** ( [Lock] ) or **https://** means you\u2019ve safely connected to the .gov website. Share\nsensitive information only on official, secure websites.\n* [Our Purpose][2]\n* [Our Science and Technology][3]\n* [Join Our Team][4]\n* [Partner with Us][5]\n* [News][6]\n* [Community and Education][7]\n* [About][8]\n\n[[LLNL Logo]][9]\n[National Ignition Facility & Photon Science][10]\n\n## Primary Menu\n* [About ][11]\n* [What Is NIF?][12]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][13]\n* [Laser Glass][14]\n* [Optical Switch][15]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][16]\n* [Deformable Mirror][17]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][18]\n* [Computer Control System][19]\n* [Target Fabrication][20]\n* [How NIF Works][21]\n* [Anatomy of a NIF Shot][22]\n* [Power Conditioning System][23]\n* [Injection Laser System][24]\n* [Amplifiers][25]\n* [Beam Transport][26]\n* [Final Optics][27]\n* [Target Chamber][28]\n* [Keys to Our Success][29]\n* [Facility Operations][30]\n* [Power and Energy][31]\n* [Control Systems][32]\n* [Optics][33]\n* [Targets][34]\n* [Diagnostics][35]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][36]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][37]\n* [Who Works for NIF][38]\n* [People Profiles][39]\n* [Management][40]\n* [Developing the Workforce][41]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][42]\n* [Enduring Partnerships][43]\n* [Technology Transfer][44]\n* [Careers][45]\n* [FAQs][46]\n* [Visit Us][47]\n* [Science ][48]\n* [NIF and Stockpile Modernization][49]\n* [High Energy Density Science][50]\n* [Advancing Weapon Physics][51]\n* [Achieving Fusion Ignition][52]\n* [National Security Applications][53]\n* [Developing New Capabilities][54]\n* [Discovery Science][55]\n* [Lab Astrophysics][56]\n* [Nuclear Astrophysics][57]\n* [Planetary Physics][58]\n* [Plasma Physics][59]\n* [Expanding Photonics Frontiers][60]\n* [DE Technology Programs][61]\n* [Advanced Optical Technologies][62]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][63]\n* [Advanced Laser Systems][64]\n* [Fiber Lasers][65]\n* [Materials for Laser Systems][66]\n* [Exploring Energy Security][67]\n* [Journal Articles][68]\n* [Livermore Inertial Fusion Energy References][69]\n* [NIF Users ][70]\n* [NIF User Portal][71]\n* [NIF User Guide][72]\n* [NIF DLI User Guide][73]\n* [Experimental Capabilities][74]\n* [Shot RI Resources][75]\n* [Call for Proposals][76]\n* [Prior Year Awards][77]\n* [2024 Awarded Campaigns][78]\n* [2023 Awarded Campaigns][79]\n* [2022 Awarded Campaigns][80]\n* [2021 Awarded Campaigns][81]\n* [2020 Awarded Campaigns][82]\n* [2019 Awarded Campaigns][83]\n* [2018 Awarded Campaigns][84]\n* [2017 Awarded Campaigns][85]\n* [2016 Awarded Campaigns][86]\n* [2015 Awarded Campaigns][87]\n* [2014 Awarded Campaigns][88]\n* [NIF User Group][89]\n* [Bylaws][90]\n* [Executive Board][91]\n* [NIF Calendar][92]\n* [Target Shot Metrics][93]\n* [Conflict of Interest Policy][94]\n* [Jupiter Laser Facility][95]\n* [Multimedia ][96]\n* [Photo Gallery][97]\n* [Playing Cards][98]\n* [Poster Gallery][99]\n* [Video Gallery][100]\n* [Education ][101]\n* [How Lasers Work][102]\n* [How to Make a Star][103]\n* [Outreach][104]\n* [Laser Roadshow][105]\n* [Summer Scholar Internship Program][106]\n* [Seminars][107]\n* [Student Spotlight][108]\n* [Scholar Tours][109]\n* [Glossary][110]\n* [External Resources][111]\n* [News ][112]\n* [The Age of Ignition][113]\n* [In the News][114]\n* [NIF in the News: Video][115]\n* [Programs ][116]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][117]\n* [Facilities][118]\n* [Publications][119]\n* [People][120]\n* [Job Postings][121]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][122]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][123]\n* [Contact][124]\n\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\n\n## Mobile Menu\n\n##### Site Menu\n* [About][125]\n* [What Is NIF?][126]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][127]\n* [How NIF Works][128]\n* [Keys to Our Success][129]\n* [Facility Operations][130]\n* [Power and Energy][131]\n* [Control Systems][132]\n* [Optics][133]\n* [Targets][134]\n* [Diagnostics][135]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][136]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][137]\n* [Who Works for NIF][138]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][139]\n* [Careers][140]\n* [FAQs][141]\n* [Visit Us][142]\n* [Science][143]\n* [NIF Users][144]\n* [Multimedia][145]\n* [Education][146]\n* [News][147]\n* [Programs][148]\n* [Contact][149]\n\n##### LLNL Menu\n* [Missions][150]\n* [Research][151]\n* [Doing Business][152]\n* [News][153]\n* [About][154]\n* [Careers][155]\n* [Community][156]\n\n## Secondary Menu\n\n[About][157]\n* [What Is NIF?][158]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][159]\n* [How NIF Works][160]\n* [Keys to Our Success][161]\n* [Facility Operations][162]\n* [Power and Energy][163]\n* [Control Systems][164]\n* [Optics][165]\n* [Targets][166]\n* [Diagnostics][167]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][168]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][169]\n* [Who Works for NIF][170]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][171]\n* [Careers][172]\n* [FAQs][173]\n* [Visit Us][174]\n1. [Home][175]\n2. [About][176]\n3. [Keys to Our Success][177]\n4. Control Systems\n\n# Control Systems\n\n[Inside the Integrated Computer Control System (ICCS) Control Room]\n\n# Conducting a Symphony of Shots\n\nInside the Integrated Computer Control System (ICCS) Control Room, (from left) Rommel Lacuata, Brad\nBlackwell, David Roebel-Lancaster, Pat Kale, and Dan Koning look over test results. Credit: Jason\nLaurea\n\nAiming NIF\u2019s 192 powerful lasers at a ball-bearing sized target has been compared to throwing a\nbaseball from the pitcher\u2019s mound at San Francisco\u2019s Oracle Park into the strike zone at Dodger\nStadium in Los Angeles, some 400 miles away.\n\nFor NIF, that level of accuracy requires a mind-boggling, multi-layered symphony of events that can\nonly happen thanks to one of the largest scientific control systems in the world.\n\n> \u201cIt\u2019s like we\u2019ve been driving on the freeway at 70 mph and we\u2019ve replaced every single component\n> of the car on the fly whilst not stopping. And now we have a completely new car.\u201d\n> \u2014Control Systems Lead Gordon Brunton\n\nConsider this: NIF runs on about four million lines of software code that orchestrate some two\nmillion automated sequences for every shot, which lasts for much less time than a blink of the eye.\nThat constantly evolving software has to ensure more than 66,000 control elements\u2014like motors,\ndiodes, and cameras\u2014and 2,000 computer processors are all working together and precisely on cue.\n\nAnd every shot is different, because the laser experiments keep evolving and advancing science.\n\nWhen NIF first began operations, shots were less frequent because of the time it took to set up each\none. Over time, the gifted members of the Control Systems Team added more layers of sophisticated\nautomation that dramatically cut down on setup time, while maintaining safety levels and increasing\nthe operational productivity that sustains about 400 shots per year.\n\nAnd unlike other large facilities of similar size or scope, NIF requires constant control system\nupgrades without stopping the machine. That includes designing, testing, and integrating four major\nsoftware releases per year, even with 25 percent fewer control systems staffers than five years ago.\n\nDevelopment of a software release starts about six months before it is implemented, allowing time\nfor extensive simulations in a test-bed environment separated from NIF\u2019s actual systems. The\nsoftware and new hardware continually added to NIF as experiments and their results warrant goes\nthrough numerous quality-checking stages to identify and remove glitches before they can affect\nongoing NIF experiments.\n\n[ICCS test bed testing facility team]\nIn the ICCS test bed testing facility, the team runs numerous simulations before incorporating\nchanges into NIF. First row (from left): Yan Pan, Susheela Muralidhar, Vinod Gopalan, Cathy Chang,\nand Kelly Burns. Second row: Alan Pao and Chris Estes. Third row: Jorge Castro Morales, Mitanu Paul,\nand Lyle Beaulac.\n\nTo manage future obsolescence issues, the team also has been taking steps such as modernizing NIF\nsoftware platforms to Java from the older Ada programming language and updating computer hardware\nfrom older Power PC chips to newer Intel processors.\n\nAs Control Systems Lead Gordon Brunton puts it, \u201cIt\u2019s like we\u2019ve been driving on the freeway at 70\nmph and we\u2019ve replaced every single component of the car on the fly whilst not stopping. And now we\nhave a completely new car. With this continued maintenance and modernization program, we believe we\nare in a good position to be able to support NIF for the next decades of operation.\u201d\n\n[Lyle Beaulac and Jorge Castro Morales run system simulations]\nLyle Beaulac and Jorge Castro Morales run system simulations.\n\n### More Information\n\n[\u201cKeeping NIF\u2019s Symphony of Controls in Tune,\u201d][178] *NIF & Photon Science News,* February 12, 2020\n\n[\u201cFrom Data to Discovery,\u201d][179] *Science & Technology Review,* January/February, 2011 (PDF)\n\nNext Up: [Optics][180]\n\n[[LLNL]][181]\nLawrence Livermore National Laboratory\n| 7000 East Avenue \u2022 Livermore, CA 94550 | LLNL-WEB-780932\nOperated by the Lawrence Livermore National Security, LLC for the Department of Energy's National\nNuclear Security Administration Learn about the Department of Energy's [Vulnerability Disclosure\nProgram][182]\n[[LLNS]][183] [[U.S. DOE]][184] [[NNSA]][185]\n[Home][186] [Disclaimer][187] [Privacy Notice][188]\n* [About][189]\n* [What Is NIF?][190]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][191]\n* [Laser Glass][192]\n* [Optical Switch][193]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][194]\n* [Deformable Mirror][195]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][196]\n* [Computer Control System][197]\n* [Target Fabrication][198]\n* [How NIF Works][199]\n* [Anatomy of a NIF Shot][200]\n* [Power Conditioning System][201]\n* [Injection Laser System][202]\n* [Amplifiers][203]\n* [Beam Transport][204]\n* [Final Optics][205]\n* [Target Chamber][206]\n* [Keys to Our Success][207]\n* [Facility Operations][208]\n* [Power and Energy][209]\n* [Control Systems][210]\n* [Optics][211]\n* [Targets][212]\n* [Diagnostics][213]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][214]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][215]\n* [Key Steps on the Path to NIF][216]\n* [50 Years of Laser Leadership][217]\n* [Building NIF][218]\n* [Who Works for NIF][219]\n* [People Profiles][220]\n* [Management][221]\n* [Developing the Workforce][222]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][223]\n* [Enduring Partnerships][224]\n* [Technology Transfer][225]\n* [Careers][226]\n* [FAQs][227]\n* [Visit Us][228]\n* [Science][229]\n* [NIF and Stockpile Modernization][230]\n* [High Energy Density Science][231]\n* [Advancing Weapon Physics][232]\n* [Achieving Fusion Ignition][233]\n* [National Security Applications][234]\n* [Developing New Capabilities][235]\n* [Discovery Science][236]\n* [Lab Astrophysics][237]\n* [Nuclear Astrophysics][238]\n* [Planetary Physics][239]\n* [Plasma Physics][240]\n* [Expanding Photonics Frontiers][241]\n* [DE Technology Programs][242]\n* [Advanced Optical Technologies][243]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][244]\n* [Advanced Laser Systems][245]\n* [Fiber Lasers][246]\n* [Materials for Laser Systems][247]\n* [Exploring Energy Security][248]\n* [Journal Articles][249]\n* [Livermore Inertial Fusion Energy References][250]\n* [NIF Users][251]\n* [NIF User Portal][252]\n* [NIF User Guide][253]\n* [NIF DLI User Guide][254]\n* [Experimental Capabilities][255]\n* [Shot RI Resources][256]\n* [Call for Proposals][257]\n* [Prior Year Awards][258]\n* [2024 Awarded Campaigns][259]\n* [2023 Awarded Campaigns][260]\n* [2022 Awarded Campaigns][261]\n* [2021 Awarded Campaigns][262]\n* [2020 Awarded Campaigns][263]\n* [2019 Awa