            "text": "[ Skip to main content ][1]\n[U.S. flag]\n\nAn official website of the United States government\n\nHere\u2019s how you know\n\nHere\u2019s how you know\n\n**Official websites use .gov**\nA **.gov** website belongs to an official government organization in the United States.\n\n**Secure .gov websites use HTTPS**\nA **lock** ( [Lock] ) or **https://** means you\u2019ve safely connected to the .gov website. Share\nsensitive information only on official, secure websites.\n* [Our Purpose][2]\n* [Our Science and Technology][3]\n* [Join Our Team][4]\n* [Partner with Us][5]\n* [News][6]\n* [Community and Education][7]\n* [About][8]\n\n[[LLNL Logo]][9]\n[National Ignition Facility & Photon Science][10]\n\n## Primary Menu\n* [About ][11]\n* [What Is NIF?][12]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][13]\n* [Laser Glass][14]\n* [Optical Switch][15]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][16]\n* [Deformable Mirror][17]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][18]\n* [Computer Control System][19]\n* [Target Fabrication][20]\n* [How NIF Works][21]\n* [Anatomy of a NIF Shot][22]\n* [Power Conditioning System][23]\n* [Injection Laser System][24]\n* [Amplifiers][25]\n* [Beam Transport][26]\n* [Final Optics][27]\n* [Target Chamber][28]\n* [Keys to Our Success][29]\n* [Facility Operations][30]\n* [Power and Energy][31]\n* [Control Systems][32]\n* [Optics][33]\n* [Targets][34]\n* [Diagnostics][35]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][36]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][37]\n* [Who Works for NIF][38]\n* [People Profiles][39]\n* [Management][40]\n* [Developing the Workforce][41]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][42]\n* [Enduring Partnerships][43]\n* [Technology Transfer][44]\n* [Careers][45]\n* [FAQs][46]\n* [Visit Us][47]\n* [Science ][48]\n* [NIF and Stockpile Modernization][49]\n* [High Energy Density Science][50]\n* [Advancing Weapon Physics][51]\n* [Achieving Fusion Ignition][52]\n* [National Security Applications][53]\n* [Developing New Capabilities][54]\n* [Discovery Science][55]\n* [Lab Astrophysics][56]\n* [Nuclear Astrophysics][57]\n* [Planetary Physics][58]\n* [Plasma Physics][59]\n* [Expanding Photonics Frontiers][60]\n* [DE Technology Programs][61]\n* [Advanced Optical Technologies][62]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][63]\n* [Advanced Laser Systems][64]\n* [Fiber Lasers][65]\n* [Materials for Laser Systems][66]\n* [Exploring Energy Security][67]\n* [Journal Articles][68]\n* [Livermore Inertial Fusion Energy References][69]\n* [NIF Users ][70]\n* [NIF User Portal][71]\n* [NIF User Guide][72]\n* [NIF DLI User Guide][73]\n* [Experimental Capabilities][74]\n* [Shot RI Resources][75]\n* [Call for Proposals][76]\n* [Prior Year Awards][77]\n* [2024 Awarded Campaigns][78]\n* [2023 Awarded Campaigns][79]\n* [2022 Awarded Campaigns][80]\n* [2021 Awarded Campaigns][81]\n* [2020 Awarded Campaigns][82]\n* [2019 Awarded Campaigns][83]\n* [2018 Awarded Campaigns][84]\n* [2017 Awarded Campaigns][85]\n* [2016 Awarded Campaigns][86]\n* [2015 Awarded Campaigns][87]\n* [2014 Awarded Campaigns][88]\n* [NIF User Group][89]\n* [Bylaws][90]\n* [Executive Board][91]\n* [NIF Calendar][92]\n* [Target Shot Metrics][93]\n* [Conflict of Interest Policy][94]\n* [Jupiter Laser Facility][95]\n* [Multimedia ][96]\n* [Photo Gallery][97]\n* [Playing Cards][98]\n* [Poster Gallery][99]\n* [Video Gallery][100]\n* [Education ][101]\n* [How Lasers Work][102]\n* [How to Make a Star][103]\n* [Outreach][104]\n* [Laser Roadshow][105]\n* [Summer Scholar Internship Program][106]\n* [Seminars][107]\n* [Student Spotlight][108]\n* [Scholar Tours][109]\n* [Glossary][110]\n* [External Resources][111]\n* [News ][112]\n* [The Age of Ignition][113]\n* [In the News][114]\n* [NIF in the News: Video][115]\n* [Programs ][116]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][117]\n* [Facilities][118]\n* [Publications][119]\n* [People][120]\n* [Job Postings][121]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][122]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][123]\n* [Contact][124]\n\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\n\n## Mobile Menu\n\n##### Site Menu\n* [About][125]\n* [What Is NIF?][126]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][127]\n* [How NIF Works][128]\n* [Keys to Our Success][129]\n* [Facility Operations][130]\n* [Power and Energy][131]\n* [Control Systems][132]\n* [Optics][133]\n* [Targets][134]\n* [Diagnostics][135]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][136]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][137]\n* [Who Works for NIF][138]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][139]\n* [Careers][140]\n* [FAQs][141]\n* [Visit Us][142]\n* [Science][143]\n* [NIF Users][144]\n* [Multimedia][145]\n* [Education][146]\n* [News][147]\n* [Programs][148]\n* [Contact][149]\n\n##### LLNL Menu\n* [Missions][150]\n* [Research][151]\n* [Doing Business][152]\n* [News][153]\n* [About][154]\n* [Careers][155]\n* [Community][156]\n\n## Secondary Menu\n\n[About][157]\n* [What Is NIF?][158]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][159]\n* [How NIF Works][160]\n* [Keys to Our Success][161]\n* [Facility Operations][162]\n* [Power and Energy][163]\n* [Control Systems][164]\n* [Optics][165]\n* [Targets][166]\n* [Diagnostics][167]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][168]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][169]\n* [Who Works for NIF][170]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][171]\n* [Careers][172]\n* [FAQs][173]\n* [Visit Us][174]\n1. [Home][175]\n2. [About][176]\n3. [Keys to Our Success][177]\n4. Efficiency Improvements\n\n# Efficiency Improvements\n\n[Time-saving Shroud Assembly]\n\n# Boosting NIF\u2019s Productivity\n\nSenior mechanical engineer Kurt Boehm participates in the installation and initial checkout of a new\nshimless and integrated shroud assembly on an ignition target inserter and cryostat (ITIC) in the\nNIF cryogenic target positioner. The new design reduced shroud installation and alignment time by\nhalf.\n\nBecause NIF is a one-of-a-kind facility, it offers opportunities for research that were impossible\nuntil recently and are still unavailable anywhere else. And while its primary mission has always\nbeen to [further stockpile stewardship][178] for national security, NIF\u2019s unparalleled capabilities\nalso make it extremely useful for researchers worldwide.\n\n\u201cA long line of scientists are eager to conduct their experiments on NIF,\u201d said NIF Director Mark\nHerrmann, \u201cand we have a responsibility to make every minute of shot time count, to maximize return\non the taxpayers\u2019 investment.\u201d\n\nInnovative efficiency improvements that have dramatically increased the number of NIF\u2019s annual\nexperiments are a signature achievement of the facility. The NIF Team undertook an aggressive effort\nto boost the shot rate from 2014 to 2016, doubling NIF\u2019s capacity to carry out groundbreaking\nscience on the facility. NIF now fires about 400 shots per year, enabling stockpile stewardship\nresearch to advance more quickly and enhancing NIF\u2019s value as the preeminent facility for inertial\nconfinement fusion (ICF) and high energy density (HED) research, national security applications, and\nDiscovery Science experiments.\n\n> \u201cWe\u2019re pulling out all the stops to increase the value of the facility for our sponsors and to\n> better support stockpile stewardship.\u201d\n> \u2014NIF Facility Manager Doug Larson\n\n\u201cThis increase in available shot time at a constant level of funding is a testament to the\ncreativity and hard work of the entire NIF Team in finding ways to streamline the process,\u201d Herrmann\nsaid. \u201cThe effort involved every part of the system, from laser shots, to optics, to targets, to\ndiagnostics\u2014all contributing to creating more opportunities to support NIF\u2019s missions.\u201d\n\nNIF began operating 24 hours a day, 7 days a week in October 2010. Early improvements in the\nshot-to-shot cycle time increased the number of cryogenic (frozen-fuel) target shots, from an\naverage of 6.6 shots per month in mid-2011 to an average of 10 cryogenic shots per month by January\n2012.\n\n[Graph Showing NIF Shot Increase by Year]\nNIF shot increases by fiscal year; 2020 NIF operations were impacted by the pandemic shutdown.\n\nIn 2014, the Laboratory\u2014responding to a Congressional appropriations bill requirement\u2014completed a\nmajor study by a team of more than 80 NIF collaborators and sponsors involved in HED research. The\nstudy made organizational, engineering, scheduling, and experimental configuration recommendations\nthat were implemented in the following months and years, substantially streamlining the turnaround\ntime between experiments.\n\nNIF completed 300 shots in fiscal year (FY) 2015, reached 400 shots in FY 2016\u2014roughly double the\nnumber in FY 2013\u2014and has maintained that level of productivity in the succeeding years. NIF fired\nits 2,000th overall shot in September 2017 and is on track to reach 3,000 shots early next year.\n\nSome examples of efficiency improvements:\n* Organizing experiments into \u201cmini-campaigns\u201d\u2014sets of experiments designed to be fired in a similar\nconfiguration to minimize facility changes while optimizing data return.\n* Separating \u201cshot mode\u201d from \u201cmaintenance mode\u201d so that NIF can shoot around the clock for five\nstraight days each week, followed by 48 hours of maintenance.\n* Developing an Advanced Tracking Laser Alignment System, or ATLAS, to streamline the alignment of\nNIF\u2019s laser beams, targets, and diagnostics in the center of the Target Chamber.\n* Installing two new target and diagnostic manipulators, known as TanDMs, that provide flexibility\nin NIF shot operations by focusing on room-temperature experiments; this frees up the facility\u2019s\nother target positioners for more integrated experiments with cryogenic fuel layers.\n\n[Workers Prepare TanDM for a Shot]\nTarget Area operators prepare a target and diagnostic manipulator (TanDM) for a NIF shot. The\n9,000-kilogram (20,000-pound) mechanism is about 8.5 meters long, with a boom that can extend about\n6.75 meters. Credit: Jason Laurea\n\n### More Information\n\n[\u201cKeeping NIF\u2019s Symphony of Controls in Tune,\u201d][179] *NIF & Photon Science News,* February 12, 2020\n\n[\u201cNIF Hits 10,000 Optics Recycle Milestone,\u201d][180] *NIF & Photon Science News,* January 9, 2020\n\n[\u201cLLNL\u2019s Virtual Beam Line ++ Now Available to Users,\u201d][181] *NIF & Photon Science News,* April 3,\n2019\n\n[\u201cVirtual and Augmented Reality Yield New Insights,\u201d][182] *Science & Technology Review,* December,\n2018\n\n[\u201cNIF-Specific Radiological Training Boosts Efficiency,\u201d][183] *NIF & Photon Science News,* July,\n2018\n\n[\u201cStreamlining the Lifecycle of NIF Experiments,\u201d][184] *NIF & Photon Science News,* January, 2018\n\n[\u201cAutomation Speeds and Smooths NIF\u2019s Optics Recycle Loop,\u201d][185] *NIF & Photon Science News,*\nOctober, 2017\n\n[\u201cAn Increased Shot Rate at the National Ignition Facility,\u201d][186] *Science & Technology Review*,\nMarch, 2015\n\n[\u201cOperational Improvements Boost NIF\u2019s Productivity,\u201d][187] *NIF & Photon Science News,* October,\n2014\n\nNext Up: [A Legacy of Lasers][188]\n\n[[LLNL]][189]\nLawrence Livermore National Laboratory\n| 7000 East Avenue \u2022 Livermore, CA 94550 | LLNL-WEB-780932\nOperated by the Lawrence Livermore National Security, LLC for the Department of Energy's National\nNuclear Security Administration Learn about the Department of Energy's [Vulnerability Disclosure\nProgram][190]\n[[LLNS]][191] [[U.S. DOE]][192] [[NNSA]][193]\n[Home][194] [Disclaimer][195] [Privacy Notice][196]\n* [About][197]\n* [What Is NIF?][198]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][199]\n* [Laser Glass][200]\n* [Optical Switch][201]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][202]\n* [Deformable Mirror][203]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][204]\n* [Computer Control System][205]\n* [Target Fabrication][206]\n* [How NIF Works][207]\n* [Anatomy of a NIF Shot][208]\n* [Power Conditioning System][209]\n* [Injection Laser System][210]\n* [Amplifiers][211]\n* [Beam Transport][212]\n* [Final Optics][213]\n* [Target Chamber][214]\n* [Keys to Our Success][215]\n* [Facility Operations][216]\n* [Power and Energy][217]\n* [Control Systems][218]\n* [Optics][219]\n* [Targets][220]\n* [Diagnostics][221]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][222]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][223]\n* [Key Steps on the Path to NIF][224]\n* [50 Years of Laser Leadership][225]\n* [Building NIF][226]\n* [Who Works for NIF][227]\n* [People Profiles][228]\n* [Management][229]\n* [Developing the Workforce][230]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][231]\n* [Enduring Partnerships][232]\n* [Technology Transfer][233]\n* [Careers][234]\n* [FAQs][235]\n* [Visit Us][236]\n* [Science][237]\n* [NIF and Stockpile Modernization][238]\n* [High Energy Density Science][239]\n* [Advancing Weap"
