ut][125]\n* [What Is NIF?][126]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][127]\n* [How NIF Works][128]\n* [Keys to Our Success][129]\n* [Facility Operations][130]\n* [Power and Energy][131]\n* [Control Systems][132]\n* [Optics][133]\n* [Targets][134]\n* [Diagnostics][135]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][136]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][137]\n* [Key Steps on the Path to NIF][138]\n* [50 Years of Laser Leadership][139]\n* [Building NIF][140]\n* [Who Works for NIF][141]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][142]\n* [Careers][143]\n* [FAQs][144]\n* [Visit Us][145]\n* [Science][146]\n* [NIF Users][147]\n* [Multimedia][148]\n* [Education][149]\n* [News][150]\n* [Programs][151]\n* [Contact][152]\n\n##### LLNL Menu\n* [Missions][153]\n* [Research][154]\n* [Doing Business][155]\n* [News][156]\n* [About][157]\n* [Careers][158]\n* [Community][159]\n\n## Secondary Menu\n\n[About][160]\n* [What Is NIF?][161]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][162]\n* [How NIF Works][163]\n* [Keys to Our Success][164]\n* [Facility Operations][165]\n* [Power and Energy][166]\n* [Control Systems][167]\n* [Optics][168]\n* [Targets][169]\n* [Diagnostics][170]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][171]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][172]\n* [Key Steps on the Path to NIF][173]\n* [50 Years of Laser Leadership][174]\n* [Building NIF][175]\n* [Who Works for NIF][176]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][177]\n* [Careers][178]\n* [FAQs][179]\n* [Visit Us][180]\n1. [Home][181]\n2. [About][182]\n3. [Keys to Our Success][183]\n4. A Legacy of Lasers and Laser Fusion Pioneers\n\n# A Legacy of Lasers and Laser Fusion Pioneers\n\n[John Emmett and John Nuckolls]\n\n# Setting the Table for NIF\n\n*Physicists John Emmett (left) and John Nuckolls, early LLNL pioneers in laser and inertial\nconfinement fusion technology.*\n\nOver the six decades since the first laser was demonstrated in 1960, LLNL researchers have designed\nand built a remarkable succession of lasers\u2014each bigger, more complex, and more powerful than the\nlast. Extraordinary challenges entice and inspire great people, and the work the Laboratory and its\nlaser, optics, inertial confinement fusion (ICF), and diagnostics pioneers did to optimize laser\nperformance and measurement techniques, past and present, help make today\u2019s laser research possible,\nat LLNL and around the world.\n\n> \u201c(John Nuckolls) has always been an intellectual leader who thinks outside the box. He never even\n> knew there was a box. He embodies the way the Laboratory takes on problems.\u201d\n> \u2014Former LLNL Director Bill Goldstein\n\nFollowing the lead of visionaries like John Nuckolls, Ray Kidder, John Foster, John Emmett, and Carl\nHaussman, the Lab\u2019s laser scientists and engineers have [constructed a series][184] of\nrecord-setting lasers. These groundbreaking technologies\u2014from the single-beam, 10-joule Janus laser\nin 1974 to today\u2019s 192-beam, two-megajoule National Ignition Facility\u2014have been applied to\nLaboratory mission areas ranging from stockpile stewardship and national security to Discovery\nScience, energy security, and national competitiveness, while attracting a steady stream of\nworld-class inventors and innovators.\n\nThese unprecedented projects were the basis for numerous collaborations with universities, other\nlaboratories, outside industry, and the larger fusion research community\u2014collaborations which made\npossible the construction, some 20 years after Janus, of NIF, then the world\u2019s largest and\nhighest-energy laser system. Concurrently, researchers also developed increasingly sophisticated\noptics, targets, and the diagnostic instruments needed for measuring and observing what was\nhappening in the laser systems and their experiments.\n\nThanks to the hard work and innovation of the members of the NIF Team, our collaborators and\nindustrial partners, and our partners in ICF and high energy density science research, NIF is now\nhelping the nation maintain its credible nuclear deterrent while taking important steps toward\nachieving ignition and providing experimental access to user communities for national security,\nDiscovery Science, and the quest for clean fusion energy. None of this would have been possible\nwithout the creativity and dedication of LLNL\u2019s laser and fusion pioneers and their successors. We\ntruly do stand on the shoulders of giants.\n\n### **More Information**\n\n[Key Steps to NIF][185]\n\n[50 Years of Laser Leadership][186]\n\n[Building NIF][187]\n\n[[LLNL]][188]\nLawrence Livermore National Laboratory\n| 7000 East Avenue \u2022 Livermore, CA 94550 | LLNL-WEB-780932\nOperated by the Lawrence Livermore National Security, LLC for the Department of Energy's National\nNuclear Security Administration Learn about the Department of Energy's [Vulnerability Disclosure\nProgram][189]\n[[LLNS]][190] [[U.S. DOE]][191] [[NNSA]][192]\n[Home][193] [Disclaimer][194] [Privacy Notice][195]\n* [About][196]\n* [What Is NIF?][197]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][198]\n* [Laser Glass][199]\n* [Optical Switch][200]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][201]\n* [Deformable Mirror][202]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][203]\n* [Computer Control System][204]\n* [Target Fabrication][205]\n* [How NIF Works][206]\n* [Anatomy of a NIF Shot][207]\n* [Power Conditioning System][208]\n* [Injection Laser System][209]\n* [Amplifiers][210]\n* [Beam Transport][211]\n* [Final Optics][212]\n* [Target Chamber][213]\n* [Keys to Our Success][214]\n* [Facility Operations][215]\n* [Power and Energy][216]\n* [Control Systems][217]\n* [Optics][218]\n* [Targets][219]\n* [Diagnostics][220]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][221]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][222]\n* [Key Steps on the Path to NIF][223]\n* [50 Years of Laser Leadership][224]\n* [Building NIF][225]\n* [Who Works for NIF][226]\n* [People Profiles][227]\n* [Management][228]\n* [Developing the Workforce][229]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][230]\n* [Enduring Partnerships][231]\n* [Technology Transfer][232]\n* [Careers][233]\n* [FAQs][234]\n* [Visit Us][235]\n* [Science][236]\n* [NIF and Stockpile Modernization][237]\n* [High Energy Density Science][238]\n* [Advancing Weapon Physics][239]\n* [Achieving Fusion Ignition][240]\n* [National Security Applications][241]\n* [Developing New Capabilities][242]\n* [Discovery Science][243]\n* [Lab Astrophysics][244]\n* [Nuclear Astrophysics][245]\n* [Planetary Physics][246]\n* [Plasma Physics][247]\n* [Expanding Photonics Frontiers][248]\n* [DE Technology Programs][249]\n* [Advanced Optical Technologies][250]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][251]\n* [Advanced Laser Systems][252]\n* [Fiber Lasers][253]\n* [Materials for Laser Systems][254]\n* [Exploring Energy Security][255]\n* [Journal Articles][256]\n* [Livermore Inertial Fusion Energy References][257]\n* [NIF Users][258]\n* [NIF User Portal][259]\n* [NIF User Guide][260]\n* [NIF DLI User Guide][261]\n* [Experimental Capabilities][262]\n* [Shot RI Resources][263]\n* [Call for Proposals][264]\n* [Prior Year Awards][265]\n* [2024 Awarded Campaigns][266]\n* [2023 Awarded Campaigns][267]\n* [2022 Awarded Campaigns][268]\n* [2021 Awarded Campaigns][269]\n* [2020 Awarded Campaigns][270]\n* [2019 Awarded Campaigns][271]\n* [2018 Awarded Campaigns][272]\n* [2017 Awarded Campaigns][273]\n* [2016 Awarded Campaigns][274]\n* [2015 Awarded Campaigns][275]\n* [2014 Awarded Campaigns][276]\n* [NIF User Group][277]\n* [Bylaws][278]\n* [Executive Board][279]\n* [NIF Calendar][280]\n* [Target Shot Metrics][281]\n* [Conflict of Interest Policy][282]\n* [Jupiter Laser Facility][283]\n* [Multimedia][284]\n* [Photo Gallery][285]\n* [Playing Cards][286]\n* [Poster Gallery][287]\n* [Video Gallery][288]\n* [Education][289]\n* [How Lasers Work][290]\n* [How to Make a Star][291]\n* [Outreach][292]\n* [Laser Roadshow][293]\n* [Summer Scholar Internship Program][294]\n* [Seminars][295]\n* [Student Spotlight][296]\n* [Scholar Tours][297]\n* [Glossary][298]\n* [External Resources][299]\n* [News][300]\n* [The Age of Ignition][301]\n* [In the News][302]\n* [NIF in the News: Video][303]\n