rophysics][57]\n* [Planetary Physics][58]\n* [Plasma Physics][59]\n* [Expanding Photonics Frontiers][60]\n* [DE Technology Programs][61]\n* [Advanced Optical Technologies][62]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][63]\n* [Advanced Laser Systems][64]\n* [Fiber Lasers][65]\n* [Materials for Laser Systems][66]\n* [Exploring Energy Security][67]\n* [Journal Articles][68]\n* [Livermore Inertial Fusion Energy References][69]\n* [NIF Users ][70]\n* [NIF User Portal][71]\n* [NIF User Guide][72]\n* [NIF DLI User Guide][73]\n* [Experimental Capabilities][74]\n* [Shot RI Resources][75]\n* [Call for Proposals][76]\n* [Prior Year Awards][77]\n* [2024 Awarded Campaigns][78]\n* [2023 Awarded Campaigns][79]\n* [2022 Awarded Campaigns][80]\n* [2021 Awarded Campaigns][81]\n* [2020 Awarded Campaigns][82]\n* [2019 Awarded Campaigns][83]\n* [2018 Awarded Campaigns][84]\n* [2017 Awarded Campaigns][85]\n* [2016 Awarded Campaigns][86]\n* [2015 Awarded Campaigns][87]\n* [2014 Awarded Campaigns][88]\n* [NIF User Group][89]\n* [Bylaws][90]\n* [Executive Board][91]\n* [NIF Calendar][92]\n* [Target Shot Metrics][93]\n* [Conflict of Interest Policy][94]\n* [Jupiter Laser Facility][95]\n* [Multimedia ][96]\n* [Photo Gallery][97]\n* [Playing Cards][98]\n* [Poster Gallery][99]\n* [Video Gallery][100]\n* [Education ][101]\n* [How Lasers Work][102]\n* [How to Make a Star][103]\n* [Outreach][104]\n* [Laser Roadshow][105]\n* [Summer Scholar Internship Program][106]\n* [Seminars][107]\n* [Student Spotlight][108]\n* [Scholar Tours][109]\n* [Glossary][110]\n* [External Resources][111]\n* [News ][112]\n* [The Age of Ignition][113]\n* [In the News][114]\n* [NIF in the News: Video][115]\n* [Programs ][116]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][117]\n* [Facilities][118]\n* [Publications][119]\n* [People][120]\n* [Job Postings][121]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][122]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][123]\n* [Contact][124]\n\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\n\n## Mobile Menu\n\n##### Site Menu\n* [About][125]\n* [What Is NIF?][126]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][127]\n* [How NIF Works][128]\n* [Keys to Our Success][129]\n* [Who Works for NIF][130]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][131]\n* [Enduring Partnerships][132]\n* [Technology Transfer][133]\n* [Careers][134]\n* [FAQs][135]\n* [Visit Us][136]\n* [Science][137]\n* [NIF Users][138]\n* [Multimedia][139]\n* [Education][140]\n* [News][141]\n* [Programs][142]\n* [Contact][143]\n\n##### LLNL Menu\n* [Missions][144]\n* [Research][145]\n* [Doing Business][146]\n* [News][147]\n* [About][148]\n* [Careers][149]\n* [Community][150]\n\n## Secondary Menu\n\n[About][151]\n* [What Is NIF?][152]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][153]\n* [How NIF Works][154]\n* [Keys to Our Success][155]\n* [Who Works for NIF][156]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][157]\n* [Enduring Partnerships][158]\n* [Technology Transfer][159]\n* [Careers][160]\n* [FAQs][161]\n* [Visit Us][162]\n1. [Home][163]\n2. [About][164]\n3. Who Partners with NIF&PS?\n\n# Who Partners with NIF&PS?\n\n[Researchers Examine SLOS Imager]\nJoe Kilkenny, left, NIF scientific diagnostic leader, and Terry Hilsabeck of General Atomics examine\nNIF\u2019s groundbreaking SLOS (single-line-of-sight) framing camera. Joining LLNL to develop the SLOS\ncamera were Sandia National Laboratories, General Atomics, and UK-based Kentech Instruments Ltd.\nCredit: Kenneth Piston\n\nConstruction and operation of the National Ignition Facility, the world\u2019s highest-energy laser,\nwould not have been possible without the contributions and unique capabilities of our many partners\nfrom government, industry, and academia.\n\nLongstanding LLNL/NIF & Photon Science partners include Los Alamos and Sandia national laboratories,\nGeneral Atomics, and the Laboratory for Laser Energetics (LLE) at the University of Rochester. Other\nkey contributors include the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT), Stanford University,\nLawrence Berkeley National Laboratory, the Atomic Weapons Establishment (AWE) in the United Kingdom,\nEurope\u2019s Extreme Light Infrastructure (ELI), and the French Alternative Energies and Atomic Energy\nCommission (CEA) (see [Enduring Partnerships][165]).\n\n[[map of LLNL partners ] ][166]\n\nFor [stockpile modernization][167], the National Nuclear Security Administration (NNSA) program to\nassure the safety, security, and reliability of the U.S. nuclear stockpile, NIF experiments involve\nscientists from throughout the NNSA weapons complex. Similar experiments are also conducted with\nresearchers from the UK\u2019s AWE. NIF\u2019s unique capabilities and expertise also play an important role\nin helping the Department of Defense and other agencies enhance the nation\u2019s ability to counter\npotential security threats (see [National Security Applications][168] and [DoD Technologies][169]).\n\n### Transferring Technology\n\nNIF sits in a secure, guarded federal laboratory, but its impact stretches far beyond the gates of\nLLNL. While continuing to satisfy the Laboratory\u2019s primary goals\u2014stockpile modernization, enhancing\nnational security, and furthering Discovery Science\u2014research on NIF and within the NIF & Photon\nScience Directorate can also generate spinoffs that bring the benefits of new technologies to the\neconomy as a whole.\n\nThrough its [technology transfer][170] efforts, NIF&PS and LLNL show that the decades worth of\ninvestments by the nation and the Department of Energy in [inertial confinement\nfusion][171] and [high energy density science][172] research are paying off with tangible, positive\nbenefits to society.\n\nWorking closely with LLNL\u2019s [Innovation and Partnerships Office][173] (IPO) and many industrial\npartners, NIF&PS researchers have successfully transferred a variety of commercially important laser\nand optics technologies to the private sector, with more now available or under development. [Learn\nmore\u00bb][174]\n\n[Icarus Detector]\n\n### [International Collaboration in Diagnostics][175]\n\nMany national laboratories, universities, and other institutions have contributed to the continuing\neffort to design and build a suite of diagnostics for NIF. [Learn more\u00bb][176]\n\n[PZ Gain Fiber]\n\n### [Experimental and Technology Partnerships][177]\n\nSandia, Los Alamos, AWE, and many government and academic collaborators also lead and participate in\nongoing national security and Discovery Science experiments and technology development. [Learn\nmore\u00bb][178]\n\n[NIF Nucleosynthesis Experiment]\n\n### [Partnering With NIF Users][179]\n\nScores of researchers across the Department of Energy laboratory system and thousands of their\ncolleagues in academia and industry around the world work closely with their LLNL partners to\nconduct experiments at NIF. [Learn more\u00bb][180]\n\n[Target Chamber under construction]\n\n### [NIF Construction Partnerships][181]\n\nNIF & Photon Science also continues its relationships with many of the 3,000 U.S. companies that\ncontributed to building NIF and its tens of thousands of components. [Learn more\u00bb][182]\n\n[Technician Examines Amplifier Optic Slab]\n\n### [Multiple Advances in Optics][183]\n\nNIF is the world\u2019s largest optical instrument, with more than 7,500 meter-sized optics and 26,000\nsmaller ones. In many cases, new technologies were required to produce these optics in the numbers\nrequired for NIF. [Learn more\u00bb][184]\n\n[[LLNL]][185]\nLawrence Livermore National Laboratory\n| 7000 East Avenue \u2022 Livermore, CA 94550 | LLNL-WEB-816928\nOperated by the Lawrence Livermore National Security, LLC for the Department of Energy's National\nNuclear Security Administration Learn about the Department of Energy's [Vulnerability Disclosure\nProgram][186]\n[[LLNS]][187] [[U.S. DOE]][188] [[NNSA]][189]\n[Home][190] [Disclaimer][191] [Privacy Notice][192]\n* [About][193]\n* [What Is NIF?][194]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][195]\n* [Laser Glass][196]\n* [Optical Switch][197]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][198]\n* [Deformable Mirror][199]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][200]\n* [Computer Control System][201]\n* [Target Fabrication][202]\n* [How NIF Works][203]\n* [Anatomy of a NIF Shot][204]\n* [Power Conditioning System][205]\n* [Injection Laser System][206]\n* [Amplifiers][207]\n* [Beam Transport][208]\n* [Final Optics][209]\n* [Target Chamber][210]\n* [Keys to Our Success][211]\n* [Facility Operations][212]\n* [Power and Energy][213]\n* [Control Systems][214]\n* [Optics][215]\n* [Targets][216]\n* [Diagnostics][217]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][218]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][219]\n* [Key Steps on the Path to NIF][220]\n* [50 Years of Laser Leadership][221]\n* [Building NIF][222]\n* [Who Works for NIF][223]\n* [People Profiles][224]\n* [Management][225]\n* [Developing the Workforce][226]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][227]\n* [Enduring Partnerships][228]\n* [Technology Transfer][229]\n* [Careers][230]\n* [FAQs][231]\n* [Visit Us][232]\n* [Science][233]\n* [NIF and Stockpile Modernization][234]\n* [High Energy Density Science][235]\n* [Advancing Weapon Physics][236]\n* [Achieving Fusion Ignition][237]\n* [National Security Applications][238]\n* [Developing New Capabilities][239]\n* [Discovery Science][240]\n* [Lab Astrophysics][241]\n* [Nuclear Astrophysics][242]\n* [Planetary Physics][243]\n* [Plasma Physics][244]\n* [Expanding Photonics Frontiers][245]\n* [DE Technology Programs][246]\n* [Advanced Optical Technologies][247]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][248]\n* [Advanced Laser Systems][249]\n* [Fiber Lasers][250]\n* [Materials for Laser Systems][251]\n* [Exploring Energy Security][252]\n* [Journal Articles][253]\n* [Livermore Inertial Fusion Energy References][254]\n* [NIF Users][255]\n* [NIF User Portal][256]\n* [NIF User Guide][257]\n* [NIF DLI User Guide][258]\n* [Experimental Capabilities][259]\n* [Shot RI Resources][260]\n* [Call for Proposals][261]\n* [Prior Year Awards][262]\n* [2024 Awarded Campaigns][263]\n* [2023 Awarded Campaigns][264]\n* [2022 Awarded Campaigns][265]\n* [2021 Awarded Campaigns][266]\n* [2020 Awarded Campaigns][267]\n* [2019 Awarded Campaigns][268]\n* [2018 Awarded Campaigns][269]\n* [2017 Awarded Campaigns][270]\n* [2016 Awarded Campaigns][271]\n* [2015 Awarded Campaigns][272]\n* [2014 Awarded Campaigns][273]\n* [NIF User Group][274]\n* [Bylaws][275]\n* [Executive Board][276]\n* [NIF Calendar][277]\n* [Target Shot Metrics][278]\n* [Conflict of Interest Policy][279]\n* [Jupiter Laser Facility][280]\n* [Multimedia][281]\n* [Photo Gallery][282]\n* [Playing "
