            "text": "[ Skip to main content ][1]\n[U.S. flag]\n\nAn official website of the United States government\n\nHere\u2019s how you know\n\nHere\u2019s how you know\n\n**Official websites use .gov**\nA **.gov** website belongs to an official government organization in the United States.\n\n**Secure .gov websites use HTTPS**\nA **lock** ( [Lock] ) or **https://** means you\u2019ve safely connected to the .gov website. Share\nsensitive information only on official, secure websites.\n* [Our Purpose][2]\n* [Our Science and Technology][3]\n* [Join Our Team][4]\n* [Partner with Us][5]\n* [News][6]\n* [Community and Education][7]\n* [About][8]\n\n[[LLNL Logo]][9]\n[National Ignition Facility & Photon Science][10]\n\n## Primary Menu\n* [About ][11]\n* [What Is NIF?][12]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][13]\n* [Laser Glass][14]\n* [Optical Switch][15]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][16]\n* [Deformable Mirror][17]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][18]\n* [Computer Control System][19]\n* [Target Fabrication][20]\n* [How NIF Works][21]\n* [Anatomy of a NIF Shot][22]\n* [Power Conditioning System][23]\n* [Injection Laser System][24]\n* [Amplifiers][25]\n* [Beam Transport][26]\n* [Final Optics][27]\n* [Target Chamber][28]\n* [Keys to Our Success][29]\n* [Facility Operations][30]\n* [Power and Energy][31]\n* [Control Systems][32]\n* [Optics][33]\n* [Targets][34]\n* [Diagnostics][35]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][36]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][37]\n* [Who Works for NIF][38]\n* [People Profiles][39]\n* [Management][40]\n* [Developing the Workforce][41]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][42]\n* [Enduring Partnerships][43]\n* [Technology Transfer][44]\n* [Careers][45]\n* [FAQs][46]\n* [Visit Us][47]\n* [Science ][48]\n* [NIF and Stockpile Modernization][49]\n* [High Energy Density Science][50]\n* [Advancing Weapon Physics][51]\n* [Achieving Fusion Ignition][52]\n* [National Security Applications][53]\n* [Developing New Capabilities][54]\n* [Discovery Science][55]\n* [Lab Astrophysics][56]\n* [Nuclear Astrophysics][57]\n* [Planetary Physics][58]\n* [Plasma Physics][59]\n* [Expanding Photonics Frontiers][60]\n* [DE Technology Programs][61]\n* [Advanced Optical Technologies][62]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][63]\n* [Advanced Laser Systems][64]\n* [Fiber Lasers][65]\n* [Materials for Laser Systems][66]\n* [Exploring Energy Security][67]\n* [Journal Articles][68]\n* [Livermore Inertial Fusion Energy References][69]\n* [NIF Users ][70]\n* [NIF User Portal][71]\n* [NIF User Guide][72]\n* [NIF DLI User Guide][73]\n* [Experimental Capabilities][74]\n* [Shot RI Resources][75]\n* [Call for Proposals][76]\n* [Prior Year Awards][77]\n* [2024 Awarded Campaigns][78]\n* [2023 Awarded Campaigns][79]\n* [2022 Awarded Campaigns][80]\n* [2021 Awarded Campaigns][81]\n* [2020 Awarded Campaigns][82]\n* [2019 Awarded Campaigns][83]\n* [2018 Awarded Campaigns][84]\n* [2017 Awarded Campaigns][85]\n* [2016 Awarded Campaigns][86]\n* [2015 Awarded Campaigns][87]\n* [2014 Awarded Campaigns][88]\n* [NIF User Group][89]\n* [Bylaws][90]\n* [Executive Board][91]\n* [NIF Calendar][92]\n* [Target Shot Metrics][93]\n* [Conflict of Interest Policy][94]\n* [Jupiter Laser Facility][95]\n* [Multimedia ][96]\n* [Photo Gallery][97]\n* [Playing Cards][98]\n* [Poster Gallery][99]\n* [Video Gallery][100]\n* [Education ][101]\n* [How Lasers Work][102]\n* [How to Make a Star][103]\n* [Outreach][104]\n* [Laser Roadshow][105]\n* [Summer Scholar Internship Program][106]\n* [Seminars][107]\n* [Student Spotlight][108]\n* [Scholar Tours][109]\n* [Glossary][110]\n* [External Resources][111]\n* [News ][112]\n* [The Age of Ignition][113]\n* [In the News][114]\n* [NIF in the News: Video][115]\n* [Programs ][116]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][117]\n* [Facilities][118]\n* [Publications][119]\n* [People][120]\n* [Job Postings][121]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][122]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][123]\n* [Contact][124]\n\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\n\n## Mobile Menu\n\n##### Site Menu\n* [About][125]\n* [What Is NIF?][126]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][127]\n* [How NIF Works][128]\n* [Keys to Our Success][129]\n* [Who Works for NIF][130]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][131]\n* [Careers][132]\n* [FAQs][133]\n* [Visit Us][134]\n* [Science][135]\n* [NIF Users][136]\n* [Multimedia][137]\n* [Education][138]\n* [News][139]\n* [Programs][140]\n* [Contact][141]\n\n##### LLNL Menu\n* [Missions][142]\n* [Research][143]\n* [Doing Business][144]\n* [News][145]\n* [About][146]\n* [Careers][147]\n* [Community][148]\n\n## Secondary Menu\n\n[About][149]\n* [What Is NIF?][150]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][151]\n* [How NIF Works][152]\n* [Keys to Our Success][153]\n* [Who Works for NIF][154]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][155]\n* [Careers][156]\n* [FAQs][157]\n* [Visit Us][158]\n1. [Home][159]\n2. [About][160]\n3. Careers\n\n# Careers\n\n[Join Our World-Class Team]\n\n[Current Openings][161]\n[Postdoc Program][162]\n[Internship Program][163]\n\n# Build Your Career Where\n# You Can Make a Difference\n\nWhether you\u2019re a student, recent graduate, or budding professional, joining the NIF & Photon Science\nTeam at LLNL offers the chance to create your own unique path to success and achievement. As a\nmember of a world-class workforce committed to helping maintain the nation\u2019s security and scientific\nleadership, you can contribute to or support multi-disciplinary teams tackling grand scientific\nchallenges well beyond the scope of most other research facilities. Working at NIF&PS offers both\nlong-term stability and the opportunity to move among different jobs and pursue new research areas\nand increased responsibilities as you grow your career.\n\n> \u201cI worked for a federal contracting company before, but LLNL takes the aspects I loved about that\n> job (e.g., mission-focused, flexible work schedule and innovative science) and combines them with\n> all the job features I always wanted (e.g., more remote-flexible opportunities, better\n> compensation/benefits, bosses that actually care about me as a person and not just a means to an\n> output. LLNL invests in their employees and really cares in their development within the\n> organization.\u201d\n> \u2014LLNL research scientist quoted on Glassdoor\n\n[Glassdoor: Best Places to Work 2025 image]\n\nAs the Laboratory\u2019s consistently high ranking among [Glassdoor\u2019s Best Places to Work][164] shows,\nour employees enjoy and appreciate LLNL\u2019s job stability and flexibility, collegial culture,\nopportunities for advancement, outstanding benefit packages, commitment to work-life balance,\non-site educational, recreational and outreach opportunities, and laser focus on service to the\nnation. The Lab\u2019s prime location in the Tri-Valley area east of San Francisco, with its diverse\ncultural offerings and mild climate, is yet another reason to join our team.\n\nThe NIF & Photon Science Directorate has a rich history at LLNL, with more than 50 years of\nexperience in building and operating the world\u2019s highest-energy laser systems and pursuing\npioneering science and engineering in lasers, optics, and photon science. NIF&PS employees also\nparticipate in cutting-edge Discovery Science research, ranging from lab-based astrophysics\nexperiments to explorations of unique phases of materials under unprecedented pressures and\ntemperatures. These studies offer Lab researchers the opportunity to work with internationally\nrenowned scientists on potentially prize-winning research projects.\n\nDo your career goals include:\n* Participating in multidisciplinary, collaborative, highly skilled teams pursuing breakthrough\nscience in a stable, stimulating work environment?\n* Using world-class research equipment and helping develop innovative technology?\n* Knowing that your work serves a purpose important to the nation and the world?\n\nSee how you can reach those goals by visiting [LLNL\u2019s careers site][165] or checking out our [Summer\nScholar internships][166] page. We welcome your interest!\n\nFind out what it's like to work for one of the best research labs in the world, voted one of the\nbest places to work in the U.S. by Glassdoor. LLNL offers mentoring, educational assistance,\nwork-life balance, and a chance to have a world-class career in science and technology, all the\nwhile enhancing our national security.\n[[LLNL]][167]\nLawrence Livermore National Laboratory\n| 7000 East Avenue \u2022 Livermore, CA 94550 | LLNL-WEB-817747\nOperated by the Lawrence Livermore National Security, LLC for the Department of Energy's National\nNuclear Security Administration Learn about the Department of Energy's [Vulnerability Disclosure\nProgram][168]\n[[LLNS]][169] [[U.S. DOE]][170] [[NNSA]][171]\n[Home][172] [Disclaimer][173] [Privacy Notice][174]\n* [About][175]\n* [What Is NIF?][176]\n* [The Seven Wonders of NIF][177]\n* [Laser Glass][178]\n* [Optical Switch][179]\n* [Preamplifier Modules][180]\n* [Deformable Mirror][181]\n* [Rapid-Growth Crystals][182]\n* [Computer Control System][183]\n* [Target Fabrication][184]\n* [How NIF Works][185]\n* [Anatomy of a NIF Shot][186]\n* [Power Conditioning System][187]\n* [Injection Laser System][188]\n* [Amplifiers][189]\n* [Beam Transport][190]\n* [Final Optics][191]\n* [Target Chamber][192]\n* [Keys to Our Success][193]\n* [Facility Operations][194]\n* [Power and Energy][195]\n* [Control Systems][196]\n* [Optics][197]\n* [Targets][198]\n* [Diagnostics][199]\n* [Efficiency Improvements][200]\n* [A Legacy of Lasers][201]\n* [Key Steps on the Path to NIF][202]\n* [50 Years of Laser Leadership][203]\n* [Building NIF][204]\n* [Who Works for NIF][205]\n* [People Profiles][206]\n* [Management][207]\n* [Developing the Workforce][208]\n* [Who Partners With NIF][209]\n* [Enduring Partnerships][210]\n* [Technology Transfer][211]\n* [Careers][212]\n* [FAQs][213]\n* [Visit Us][214]\n* [Science][215]\n* [NIF and Stockpile Modernization][216]\n* [High Energy Density Science][217]\n* [Advancing Weapon Physics][218]\n* [Achieving Fusion Ignition][219]\n* [National Security Applications][220]\n* [Developing New Capabilities][221]\n* [Discovery Science][222]\n* [Lab Astrophysics][223]\n* [Nuclear Astrophysics][224]\n* [Planetary Physics][225]\n* [Plasma Physics][226]\n* [Expanding Photonics Frontiers][227]\n* [DE Technology Programs][228]\n* [Advanced Optical Technologies][229]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][230]\n* [Advanced Laser Systems][231]\n* [Fiber Lasers][232]\n* [Materials for Laser Systems][233]\n* [Exploring Energy Security][234]\n* [Journal Articles][235]\n* [Livermore Inertial Fusion Energy References][236]\n* [NIF Users][237]\n* [NIF User Portal][238]\n* [NIF User Guide][239]\n* [NIF DLI User Guide][240]\n* [Experimental Capabilities][241]\n* [Shot RI Resources][242]\n* [Call for Proposals][243]\n* [Prior Year Awards][244]\n* [2024 Awarded Campaigns][245]\n* [2023 Awarded Campaigns][246]\n* [2022 Awarded Campaigns][247]\n* [2021 Awarded Campaigns][248]\n* [2020 Awarded Campaigns][249]\n* [2019 Awarded Campaigns][250]\n* [2018 Awarded Campaigns][251]\n* [2017 Awarded Campaigns][252]\n* [2016 Awarded Campaigns][253]\n* [2015 Awarded Campaigns][254]\n* [2014 Awarded Campaigns][255]\n* [NIF User Group][256]\n* [Bylaws][257]\n* [Executive Board][258]\n* [NIF Calendar][259]\n* [Target Shot Metrics][260]\n* [Conflict of Interest Policy][261]\n* [Jupiter Laser Facility][262]\n* [Multimedia][263]\n* [Photo Gallery][264]\n* [Playing Cards][265]\n* [Poster Gallery][266]\n* [Video Gallery][267]\n* [Education][268]\n* [How Lasers Work][269]\n* [How to Make a Star][270]\n* [Outreach][271]\n* [Laser Roadshow][272]\n* [Summer Scholar Internship Program][273]\n* [Seminars][274]\n* [Student Spotlight][275]\n* [Scholar Tours][276]\n* [Glossary][277]\n* [External Resources][278]\n* [News][279]\n* [The Age of Ignition][280]\n* [In the News][281]\n* [NIF in the News: Video][282]\n* [Programs][283]\n* [Advanced Photon Technologies][284]\n* [Facilities][285]\n* [Publications][286]\n* [People][287]\n* [Job Postings][288]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][289]\n* [Directed Energy Technology Programs][290]\n* [Contact][291]\n\n[1]: #main-content\n[2]: https://www.llnl.gov/purpose\n[3]: https://www.llnl.gov/science-technology\n[4]: https://www.llnl.gov/join-our-team\n[5]: https://www.llnl.gov/partner\n[6]: https://www.llnl.gov/news\n[7]: https://www.llnl.gov/community-education\n[8]: https://www.llnl.gov/about\n[9]: https://www.llnl.gov\n[10]: https://lasers."
