        "crawl_text": "* [ FAQ ][1]\n* [ Press ][2]\n* [ Join us ][3]\n\n# Star power for life\n\nWe are on a mission to create limitless energy with proven fusion science.\n\n[ Join us ][4]\n\n# We have a clear path to commercialize fusion energy\n\n01\n\n### Start with science that works\n\n02\n\n### Build the world\u2019s most powerful laser\n\n03\n\n### Mass manufacture fusion fuel targets\n\n04\n\n### Build a gigawatt grid-scale plant\n\nNIF\n\nIn December 2022, at the National Ignition Facility in Livermore, California, lasers struck a tiny\ntarget of fuel\n\n192 lasers\nOne tiny target\nIgnition achieved\n\nFor the first time, fusion ignition was demonstrated and net energy gain achieved.\n\n# With the science proven, now it\u2019s time to scale up\n\nLasers\n\nBuild the world\u2019s most powerful laser\n\n## A thousand lasers. One million times more power. One tenth the footprint.\n\nOur modular laser system is the most powerful in the world. It is comprised of a thousand smaller\nlasers, each twenty times more efficient than at NIF.\n\nTargets\n\nOur fuel targets are produced in factories by the millions\n\n### Striking 4.5mm targets\n\nOur lasers hit 4.5 millimeter targets, the heart of our fusion power engine.\n\n### 10 times per second\n\nOur plant shoots ten targets per second. Each target produces fifteen times more thrust than a\nSpaceX Falcon rocket at liftoff.\n\n### Less than a dollar\n\nOur fusion fuel factory mass-produces targets from abundant materials for less than one dollar each.\n\nPower Plant\n\n### Our plant generates 1.5 gigawatts of baseload, dispatchable electricity\n\nEnough energy to power over a million homes\n\nCleansafelimitlessenergy\nOur Team\n\n# Each day we build a more brilliant tomorrow\n\nWith the physics proven, it\u2019s time to deliver. Inertia\u2019s leaders and experts, together with partners\nin industry, academia and national labs, will bring limitless fusion energy to life.\n\n[Portrait of Jeff Lawson]\n\n### Jeff Lawson\n\nCEO & President\n\nLawson has founded and led the development of several multinational companies with billions in\nrevenues and teams of thousands.\n\n[ [ in ] ][5] [Portrait of Annie Kritcher]\n\n### Annie Kritcher\n\nChief Scientist\n\nDr. Kritcher led the team that designed the first and only fusion experiment to achieve net-positive\nignition.\n\n[ [ in ] ][6] [Portrait of Mike Dunne]\n\n### Mike Dunne\n\nCTO & SVP Fusion Power\n\nProf. Dunne led the US government program to design a fusion power plant based on NIF ignition.\n\n[ [ in ] ][7]\nMeet more of the team\n[Portrait of MariAnn Albrecht]\n\n### MariAnn Albrecht\n\nChief of Staff & Research Program Manager\n\n[Portrait of Neil Alexander]\n\n### Neil Alexander\n\nSVP of Target Development\n\n[Portrait of Michael Bratsafolis]\n\n### Michael Bratsafolis\n\nHead of Business\n\n[Portrait of Jim Gaffney]\n\n### Jim Gaffney\n\nVice President & Head of Integrated Plant Design\n\n[Portrait of Doug Hammond]\n\n### Doug Hammond\n\nVice President & Head of Lasers\n\n[Portrait of Melinda Lee]\n\n### Melinda Lee\n\nChief Communications Officer & Head of External Affairs\n\n[Portrait of Gabriel Meric]\n\n### Gabriel Meric\n\nSenior Director & Head of Materials and Mechanical Engineering\n\n[Portrait of Vladimir Smalyuk]\n\n### Vladimir Smalyuk\n\nVice President & Head of Experimental Physics\n\n[Portrait of Henry Yang]\n\n### Henry Yang\n\nVice President of Industrial Engineering\n\nMeet our Science & Technology Advisory Board\n[Portrait of Marv Adams]\n\n### Marv Adams \u2014 Advisory Board Chair\n\nLarge-scale nuclear program leadership and independent technical oversight across complex,\nmulti-disciplinary systems.\n\n[Portrait of Jeff Atherton]\n\n### Jeff Atherton\n\nEnd-to-end integration of laser, target, and facility systems for large-scale ICF program execution.\nExperience leading large target fab programs.\n\n[Portrait of Bill Kruer]\n\n### Bill Kruer\n\nExpert in laser\u2013plasma interactions and instability physics governing laser energy coupling.\n\n[Portrait of Brian MacGowan]\n\n### Brian MacGowan\n\nIntegrated ICF physics expert spanning LPI, diagnostics, hohlraum energetics, and facility\nperformance.\n\n[Portrait of Joe Kilkenny]\n\n### Joe Kilkenny\n\nNational leader in HED diagnostics and experimental validation for ignition-scale ICF.\n\n[Portrait of Larry Suter]\n\n### Larry Suter\n\nWorld-leading authority in hohlraum physics, x-ray drive, and symmetry control for indirect-drive\nICF.\n\n[Portrait of Brian Wirth]\n\n### Brian Wirth\n\nNuclear materials and radiation damage expert for chamber, blanket, and structural survivability.\n\n[Portrait of Doug Young]\n\n### Doug Young\n\nAerospace-scale systems integration and execution of complex, multi-stakeholder engineering\nprograms.\n\n[Portrait of Jon Zuegel]\n\n### Jon Zuegel\n\nHigh-energy laser architecture and optical systems design for scalable, high-repetition-rate\nfacilities.\n\n# Inertia in numbers\n\n[Less than $1 per target]\n\nLess than $1 per target\n\n10MJ Laser\n\n4.5x higher energy than NIF\n\n1.5GW\n\nPowers a city of one million people\n\nZero emissions\n\n15x\n\nThe thrust of a Falcon Heavy rocket\n\n1000\n\nBeamlines built in factories and delivered by truck\n\n[1000]\n* [ Learn more about our approa * [ FAQ ][1]\n* [ Press ][2]\n* [ Join us ][3]\n\n# Star power for life\n\nWe are on a mission to create limitless energy with proven fusion science.\n\n[ Join us ][4]\n\n# We have a clear path to commercialize fusion energy\n\n01\n\n### Start with science that works\n\n02\n\n### Build the world\u2019s most powerful laser\n\n03\n\n### Mass manufacture fusion fuel targets\n\n04\n\n### Build a gigawatt grid-scale plant\n\nNIF\n\nIn December 2022, at the National Ignition Facility in Livermore, California, lasers struck a tiny\ntarget of fuel\n\n192 lasers\nOne tiny target\nIgnition achieved\n\nFor the first time, fusion ignition was demonstrated and net energy gain achieved.\n\n# With the science proven, now it\u2019s time to scale up\n\nLasers\n\nBuild the world\u2019s most powerful laser\n\n## A thousand lasers. One million times more power. One tenth the footprint.\n\nOur modular laser system is the most powerful in the world. It is comprised of a thousand smaller\nlasers, each twenty times more efficient than at NIF.\n\nTargets\n\nOur fuel targets are produced in factories by the millions\n\n### Striking 4.5mm targets\n\nOur lasers hit 4.5 millimeter targets, the heart of our fusion power engine.\n\n### 10 times per second\n\nOur plant shoots ten targets per second. Each target produces fifteen times more thrust than a\nSpaceX Falcon rocket at liftoff.\n\n### Less than a dollar\n\nOur fusion fuel factory mass-produces targets from abundant materials for less than one dollar each.\n\nPower Plant\n\n### Our plant generates 1.5 gigawatts of baseload, dispatchable electricity\n\nEnough energy to power over a million homes\n\nCleansafelimitlessenergy\nOur Team\n\n# Each day we build a more brilliant tomorrow\n\nWith the physics proven, it\u2019s time to deliver. Inertia\u2019s leaders and experts, together with partners\nin industry, academia and national labs, will bring limitless fusion energy to life.\n\n[Portrait of Jeff Lawson]\n\n### Jeff Lawson\n\nCEO & President\n\nLawson has founded and led the development of several multinational companies with billions in\nrevenues and teams of thousands.\n\n[ [ in ] ][5] [Portrait of Annie Kritcher]\n\n### Annie Kritcher\n\nChief Scientist\n\nDr. Kritcher led the team that designed the first and only fusion experiment to achieve net-positive\nignition.\n\n[ [ in ] ][6] [Portrait of Mike Dunne]\n\n### Mike Dunne\n\nCTO & SVP Fusion Power\n\nProf. Dunne led the US government program to design a fusion power plant based on NIF ignition.\n\n[ [ in ] ][7]\nMeet more of the team\n[Portrait of MariAnn Albrecht]\n\n### MariAnn Albrecht\n\nChief of Staff & Research Program Manager\n\n[Portrait of Neil Alexander]\n\n### Neil Alexander\n\nSVP of Target Development\n\n[Portrait of Michael Bratsafolis]\n\n### Michael Bratsafolis\n\nHead of Business\n\n[Portrait of Jim Gaffney]\n\n### Jim Gaffney\n\nVice President & Head of Integrated Plant Design\n\n[Portrait of Doug Hammond]\n\n### Doug Hammond\n\nVice President & Head of Lasers\n\n[Portrait of Melinda Lee]\n\n### Melinda Lee\n\nChief Communications Officer & Head of External Affairs\n\n[Portrait of Gabriel Meric]\n\n### Gabriel Meric\n\nSenior Director & Head of Materials and Mechanical Engineering\n\n[Portrait of Vladimir Smalyuk]\n\n### Vladimir Smalyuk\n\nVice President & Head of Experimental Physics\n\n[Portrait of Henry Yang]\n\n### Henry Yang\n\nVice President of Industrial Engineering\n\nMeet our Science & Technology Advisory Board\n[Portrait of Marv Adams]\n\n### Marv Adams \u2014 Advisory Board Chair\n\nLarge-scale nuclear program leadership and independent technical oversight across complex,\nmulti-disciplinary systems.\n\n[Portrait of Jeff Atherton]\n\n### Jeff Atherton\n\nEnd-to-end integration of laser, target, and facility systems for large-scale ICF program execution.\nExperience leading large target fab programs.\n\n[Portrait of Bill Kruer]\n\n### Bill Kruer\n\nExpert in laser\u2013plasma interactions and instability physics governing laser energy coupling.\n\n[Portrait of Brian MacGowan]\n\n### Brian MacGowan\n\nIntegrated ICF physics expert spanning LPI, diagnostics, hohlraum energetics, and facility\nperformance.\n\n[Portrait of Joe Kilkenny]\n\n### Joe Kilkenny\n\nNational leader in HED diagnostics and experimental validation for ignition-scale ICF.\n\n[Portrait of Larry Suter]\n\n### Larry Suter\n\nWorld-leading authority in hohlraum physics, x-ray drive, and symmetry control for indirect-drive\nICF.\n\n[Portrait of Brian Wirth]\n\n### Brian Wirth\n\nNuclear materials and radiation damage expert for chamber, blanket, and structural survivability.\n\n[Portrait of Doug Young]\n\n### Doug Young\n\nAerospace-scale systems integration and execution of complex, multi-stakeholder engineering\nprograms.\n\n[Portrait of Jon Zuegel]\n\n### Jon Zuegel\n\nHigh-energy laser architecture and optical systems design for scalable, high-repetition-rate\nfacilities.\n\n# Inertia in numbers\n\n[Less than $1 per target]\n\nLess than $1 per target\n\n10MJ Laser\n\n4.5x higher energy than NIF\n\n1.5GW\n\nPowers a city of one million people\n\nZero emissions\n\n15x\n\nThe thrust of a Falcon Heavy rocket\n\n1000\n\nBeamlines built in factories and delivered by truck\n\n[1000]\n* [ Learn more about our approach. ][8]\n* [ Help light up our energy future. Join us. ][9]\n* [ A message from our founders. ][10]\n* [Privacy Policy][11]\n* [Terms of Service][12]\n* [Cookie Policy][13]\n* [ Follow us on Linkedin ][14]\n* \u00a9 2026 Inertia Enterprises. All rights reserved.\n\n[1]: /faq/why-fusion-energy\n[2]: /press\n[3]: /jobs\n[4]: /jobs\n[5]: https://www.linkedin.com/in/jeffiel\n[6]: https://www.linkedin.com/in/andrea-annie-kritcher-7a649112/\n[7]: https://www.linkedin.com/in/mike-dunne-27142025\n[8]: /faq/why-fusion-energy\n[9]: /jobs\n[10]: /press/founders-message\n[11]: /privacy-policy\n[12]: /terms-of-service\n[13]: /cookie-policy\n[14]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/inertia-fusion/ inertia.com * [ FAQ ][1]\n* [ Press ][2]\n* [ Join us ][3]\n\n# Star power for life\n\nWe are on a mission to create limitless energy with proven fusion science.\n\n[ Join us ][4]\n\n# We have a clear path to commercialize fusion energy\n\n01\n\n### Start with science that works\n\n02\n\n### Build the world\u2019s most powerful laser\n\n03\n\n### Mass manufacture fusion fuel targets\n\n04\n\n### Build a gigawatt grid-scale plant\n\nNIF\n\nIn December 2022, at the National Ignition Facility in Livermore, California, lasers struck a tiny\ntarget of fuel\n\n192 lasers\nOne tiny target\nIgnition achieved\n\nFor the first time, fusion ignition was demonstrated and net energy gain achieved.\n\n# With the science 