        "crawl_text": "top of page\n[[NP-Photonics-Logo-C5.png]][1]\n\n## Designed\u00a0for Industrial operation\n* [HOME][2]\n* [PRODUCTS][3]\n  * [SINGLE FREQUENCY LASERS][4]\n  * [HIGH POWER CW LASERS][5]\n  * [HIGH ENERGY LASERS][6]\n  * [MULTI-CHANNEL LASER SYSTEMS][7]\n  * [SHORT-LENGTH FIBER AMPLIFIERS][8]\n  * [INJECTION SEEDERS][9]\n  * [ASE SOURCES][10]\n  * [MID-IR FIBERS & SOURCES][11]\n* [APPLICATIONS][12]\n  * [ACOUSTIC SENSING][13]\n  * [OPTICAL TRAPPING][14]\n  * [ENVIRONMENTAL SENSING][15]\n  * [LIDAR][16]\n  * [COHERENT COMMUNICATIONS][17]\n* [CAPABILITIES][18]\n  * [ITAR][19]\n  * [CORE TECHNOLOGIES][20]\n  * [INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY][21]\n  * [PUBLICATIONS][22]\n* [ABOUT US][23]\n  * [LEADERSHIP][24]\n  * [CAREERS][25]\n  * [CORONAVIRUS RESPONSE][26]\n* CONTACT US\n  * [REQUEST A QUOTE][27]\n  * [TECHNICAL SUPPORT][28]\n  * [DISTRIBUTORS][29]\n\n#### \u00a0\u00a0 Located in Tucson, Arizona, NP Photonics is an American owned and operated fiber laser,\n#### amplifier, and specialty glass manufacturer with over 25 years of operation. Let us be your\n#### OEM, R&D, or custom laser solution.\n\n[Logo-01.png]\nReliable Acoustic Sensing Solutions\nLaser Welding and Cutting Sources\n[Explore Our Products][30]\n[[TherockWebsite.jpg]][31]\n\n### [Single-Frequency Fiber Lasers\u00a0][32]\n\n* ### \u03bbc(nm) = [1030-1075][33]; [1530-1565][34]\n* ### 25mW-30W Output Powers\n* ### OEM & Bench-top Options\n\n[[Pencil Amp.jpg]][35]\n\n### [Short-Length Fiber Amplifier\u00a0][36]\n\n* ### 20dB Gain in 10cm\n* ### Up to 100W Average Output Power\n* ### \u2265500kW Output Peak Power\n\n[[MLS System.jpg]][37]\n\n### [Multi-Laser Systems][38]\n\n\n* ### \u03bbc(nm) = [1030-1075][39]; [1530-1565][40]\n* ### 25mW-125mW Output Powers\n* ### Up to Five Line-cards\n* ### Line-widths of 1kHz; <5kHz\n\n[[Meteor.jpg]][41]\n\n### [High-Energy Fiber Lasers][42]\n\n* ### \u03bbc(nm) = [1018-1080][43]; [1528-1575][44]\n* ### 100 \u00b5J - 1.3 mJ Output Energies\n* ### Up to 25W Output Powers\n* ### \u00a0M2\u00a0\u2264 1.5 (\u22641.3 typical)\n\n[[MIR Fiber.jpg]][45]\n\n### [MIR Transport Fiber][46]\n\n\n* ### Visible to mid-IR Transmission\n* ### AR Coating Options\n* ### High Damage Threshold\u00a0\n* ### Unaffected by Atmospheric Water\n\n[Explore Our Capabilities][47]\n\n# Company News\n\n2026, January 12 (PRESS RELEASE)\n\n[NP Photonics Showcases OEM-Proven Fiber Lasers and Amplifiers at SPIE PHOTONICS WEST 2026][48]\n\n\n2026, January 12\n\n[NP Photonics Showcases Breakthrough Advances in High-Power Fiber Lasers and Amplifiers at SPIE\nPHOTONICS WEST 2026][49]\n\n\n2026, January 12\n\n[NP Photonics Files U.S. Patents on Advanced Glass and Fiber Materials for Next Generation Fiber\nLasers and Amplifiers][50]\n\n\u00a0\n\n2025, January 22 / June 18\n\n[NP Photonics Highlights its OEM Winning Fiber Lasers and Amplifiers at PHOTONICS WEST / LASERS\nMUNICH][51]\n\n\n2024, September 24 (PRESS RELEASE)\n\n[NP Photonics and University of Arizona demonstrate compact and portable optical clock.][52]\n\n\u00a0\n\n2024, January 25\u00a0 \u00a0 (PRESS RELEASE)\n\n[NP Photonics Highlights its OEM Winning Fiber Lasers and Amplifiers at SPIE PHOTONICS WEST\n2024][53]\n\n\u00a0\n\n2019, January 21\u00a0\n\n[NP Photonics to Introduce METEOR ROCK][54]\n\n\n2019, January 21\n\n[NP Photonics to Introduce Amplifier Gain Block][55]\n\n\n2018, April 10\n\n[NP highlighted at Navy conference][56]\n\n\n2016, October\u00a0\n\n[NP recognized as a global photonic sensor and detector market leader][57]\n\n# Upcoming Events\n\nJanuary 20-22, 2026\n\nPhotonics West 2026\n\nPhotonics West Exhibition,\u00a0Booth: 563\n\nThe Moscone Center\n\nSan Francisco, California\n\n\nJune 24-27, 2025\n\nLaser World Of Photonics: Munich, Germany\u00a0\n\nBooth: A2.303\n\n\n[Visit us at Photonics West ][58]\n[[NP-Photonics-Logo-C5.png]][59]\n* [[LinkedIn - White Circle]][60]\n[\n][61]\n[\n][62]\n\n9030 S Rita Ranch Rd #120\n\nTucson, AZ 85747\n\n[520-799-7400][63]\n\n[info@npphotonics.com][64]\n\n[\n][65]\nContact Us\nbottom of page\n\n[1]: https://www.npphotonics.com\n[2]: https://www.npphotonics.com\n[3]: https://www.npphotonics.com/products\n[4]: https://www.npphotonics.com/single-frequency-lasers\n[5]: https://www.npphotonics.com/high-power-cw-lasers\n[6]: https://www.npphotonics.com/high-energy-lasers\n[7]: https://www.npphotonics.com/multi-channel-laser-systems\n[8]: https://www.npphotonics.com/short-length-fiber-amplifiers\n[9]: https://www.npphotonics.com/seeder\n[10]: https://www.npphotonics.com/ase-sources\n[11]: https://www.npphotonics.com/mid-ir-fibers-sources\n[12]: https://www.npphotonics.com/applications\n[13]: https://www.npphotonics.com/acoustic-sensing\n[14]: https://www.npphotonics.com/optical-trapping\n[15]: https://www.npphotonics.com/environmental-sensing\n[16]: https://www.npphotonics.com/lidar\n[17]: https://www.npphotonics.com/coherent-communications\n[18]: https://www.npphotonics.com/capabilities\n[19]: https://www.npphotonics.com/itar\n[20]: https://www.npphotonics.com/core-technologies\n[21]: https://www.npphotonics.com/patents\n[22]: https://www.npphotonics.com/publications\n[23]: https://www.npphotonics.com/about-us\n[24]: https://www.npphotonics.com/leadership\n[25]: https://www.npphotonics.com/careers\n[26]: https://www.npphotonics.com/copy-of-careers\n[27]: https://www.npphotonics top of page\n[[NP-Photonics-Logo-C5.png]][1]\n\n## Designed\u00a0for Industrial operation\n* [HOME][2]\n* [PRODUCTS][3]\n  * [SINGLE FREQUENCY LASERS][4]\n  * [HIGH POWER CW LASERS][5]\n  * [HIGH ENERGY LASERS][6]\n  * [MULTI-CHANNEL LASER SYSTEMS][7]\n  * [SHORT-LENGTH FIBER AMPLIFIERS][8]\n  * [INJECTION SEEDERS][9]\n  * [ASE SOURCES][10]\n  * [MID-IR FIBERS & SOURCES][11]\n* [APPLICATIONS][12]\n  * [ACOUSTIC SENSING][13]\n  * [OPTICAL TRAPPING][14]\n  * [ENVIRONMENTAL SENSING][15]\n  * [LIDAR][16]\n  * [COHERENT COMMUNICATIONS][17]\n* [CAPABILITIES][18]\n  * [ITAR][19]\n  * [CORE TECHNOLOGIES][20]\n  * [INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY][21]\n