        "crawl_text": "[[Skylark Lasers logo]][1]\n* [Core products][2]\n  * [Skylark 320][3]\n  * [Skylark 349][4]\n  * [Skylark 780][5]\n  * [Skylark 785][6]\n* [Applications][7]\n  * [Lithography][8]\n  * [Optical gratings][9]\n  * [Wide bandgap inspection][10]\n  * [Quantum][11]\n  * [Brillouin microscopy][12]\n  * [Raman spectroscopy][13]\n  * [Holography][14]\n  * [Flow cytometry][15]\n* [About][16]\n  * [News][17]\n  * [Careers][18]\n  * [Distributors][19]\n  * [Events][20]\n  * [Research and innovation][21]\n[Request quote][22]\n[\n][23]\n\u2715\n* [Core products][24]\n  * [Skylark 320][25]\n  * [Skylark 349][26]\n  * [Skylark 780][27]\n  * [Skylark 785][28]\n* [Applications][29]\n  * [Lithography][30]\n  * [Optical gratings][31]\n  * [Wide bandgap inspection][32]\n  * [Quantum][33]\n  * [Brillouin microscopy][34]\n  * [Raman spectroscopy][35]\n  * [Holography][36]\n  * [Flow cytometry][37]\n* [About][38]\n  * [News][39]\n  * [Careers][40]\n  * [Distributors][41]\n  * [Events][42]\n  * [Research and innovation][43]\n\n# Ultra-stable\n# single frequency\n# CW DPSS lasers\n\n[View lasers][44]\n[Request quote][45]\n\n### SKYLARK DPSS LASERS\n\n## Single frequency CW\n## diode-pumped solid-state lasers\n\n### SKYLARK UV\n\n## Ultraviolet DPSS lasers\n\nSkylark UV laser systems achieve the highest output power available in single frequency DPSS lasers,\nengineered with proprietary technology for sustained long-term operation.\n\n##### 320 nm\n\n##### up to 200 mW\n\n##### Skylark 320\n\n320 nm single frequency DPSS UV laser\n\n[View specifications][46]\n\n##### 349 nm\n\n##### up to 400 mW\n\n##### Skylark 349\n\n349 nm single frequency DPSS UV laser\n\n[View specifications][47]\n\n### SKYLARK NIR\n\n## Near-infrared DPSS lasers\n\nSkylark NIR laser systems combine single frequency, low noise output and high optical efficiency \u2014\ndelivering precise, repeatable performance and ample power margin for complex or lossy setups.\n\n##### 780 nm\n\n##### up to 400 mW\n\n##### Skylark 780\n\n780 nm single frequency DPSS NIR laser\n\n[View specifications][48]\n\n##### 785 nm\n\n##### up to 400 mW\n\n##### Skylark 785\n\n785 nm single frequency DPSS NIR laser\n\n[View specifications][49]\n\n#### \"It\u2019s taken 15 years to find a suitable replacement for our HeCd laser. The Skylark 320 DPSS\n#### laser has a clean mode without filters.\"\n\nOPTICAL GRATING MANUFACTURER\n\n### Pushing the capabilities of photonics to engineer ultra-stable single frequency DPSS lasers\n\nFrom optomechanical design to software development, our team pushes the capabilities of laser\ntechnology to engineer ultra-stable, spectrally pure single frequency DPSS lasers.\n\nGuided by our core values, we collaborate with our customers and research partners to develop DPSS\nlasers tailored to your application.\n\nAmbition\nOur team pursues the challenge of miniaturising laser technology to enable the world\u2019s most\ndemanding and cutting-edge applications \u2013 reducing cost, weight, and size while maximising power and\nperformance.\nInnovation\nWe develop and commercialise lasers with the purest spectral properties to reveal the unseen, detect\nthe imperceptible, and measure the unknown.\nCollaboration\nWe work with our customers and partners to gain a deep understanding of their needs - connecting the\ndots between lasers and application to deliver tailored solutions.\nContinuous learning\nEmbodying a growth mindset, we value continuous learning and thrive in an environment of curiosity\nand exploration.\n\n### ROBUST AND RELIABLE DPSS LASERS\n\n## Built for system integration and efficient performance in demanding environments\n\n#### [Semiconductor inspection][50]\n\n#### [Quantum][51]\n\n#### [Holography][52]\n\n#### Materials analysis\n\n#### [Laser interference lithography][53]\n\n#### [Flow cytometry][54]\n\n#### [Grating manufacturing][55]\n\n#### [Brillouin microscopy][56]\n\n#### Raman + photoluminescence\n\n#### [Raman spectroscopy][57]\n\n## Request a quote\n\nTell us more about your laser and application requirements. No application is too small or too large\n- we are happy to collaborate with you to develop a solution suited to your requirements.\n\nIf you'd prefer to skip the form and chat to us directly, please email us at\nsales@skylarklasers.com.\n\nFirst name\n\nLast name\n\nEmail\n\nPhone number\n\nOrganisation\n\nWhere did you hear about Skylark Lasers?\n\nWavelength320 nm349 nm780 nm785 nmOther (specify in your message)\n\nOutput power\n\nTell us about your application area and laser requirements\n\n\n#### \"The Skylark 780 DPSS laser is very stable, we never lose the Rubidium frequency.\"\n\nMICROSCOPE SYSTEM MANUFACTURER\n\n#### \"It\u2019s taken 15 years to find a suitable replacement for our HeCd laser. The Skylark 320 DPSS\n#### laser has a clean mode without filters.\"\n\nOPTICAL GRATING MANUFACTURER\n\n#### \"I looked at 182 lasers from all different manufacturers. Skylark Lasers was the final choice.\"\n\nSEMICONDUCTOR INSPECTION OEM\n\n[[Skylark Lasers logo]][58]\nSkylark Lasers Limited\nRatho Park Phase One,\n88 Glasgow Rd\nRatho Station,\nEdinburgh, EH28 8PP\n+44 (0)131 333 2200\n\n\u00a9 2026 Skylark Lasers Limited\nRegistered in Scotland SC 445 554\n* [Privacy policy][59 [[Skylark Lasers logo]][1]\n* [Core products][2]\n  * [Skylark 320][3]\n  * [Skylark 349][4]\n  * [Skylark 780][5]\n  * [Skylark 785][6]\n* [Applications][7]\n  * [Lithography][8]\n  * [Optical gratings][9]\n  * [Wide bandgap inspection][10]\n  * [Quantum][11]\n  * [Brillouin microscopy][12]\n  * [Raman spectroscopy][13]\n  * [Holography][14]\n  * [Flow cytometry][15]\n* [About][16]\n  * [News][17]\n  * [Careers][18]\n  * [Distributors][19]\n  * [Events][20]\n  * [Research and innovation][21]\n[Request quote][22]\n[\n][23]\n\u2715\n* [Core products][24]\n  * [Skylark 320][25]\n  * [Skylark 349][26]\n  * [Skylark 780][27]\n  * [Skylark 785][28]\n* [Applications][29]\n  * [Lithography][30]\n  * [Optical gratings][31]\n  * [Wide bandgap inspection][32]\n  * [Quantum][33]\n  * [Brillouin microscopy][34]\n  * [Raman spectroscopy][35]\n  * [Holography][36]\n  * [Flow cytometry][37]\n* [About][38]\n  * [News][39]\n  * [Careers][40]\n  * [Distributors][41]\n  * [Events][42]\n  * [Research and innovation][43]\n\n# Ultra-stable\n# single frequency\n# CW DPSS lasers\n\n[View lasers][44]\n[Request quote][45]\n\n### SKYLARK DPSS LASERS\n\n## Single frequency CW\n## diode-pumped solid-state lasers\n\n### SKYLARK UV\n\n## Ultraviolet DPSS lasers\n\nSkylark UV laser systems achieve the highest output power available in single frequency DPSS lasers,\nengineered with proprietary technology for sustained long-term operation.\n\n##### 320 nm\n\n##### up to 200 mW\n\n##### Skylark 320\n\n320 nm single frequency DPSS UV laser\n\n[View specifications][46]\n\n##### 349 nm\n\n##### up to 400 mW\n\n##### Skylark 349\n\n349 nm single frequency DPSS UV laser\n\n[View specifications][47]\n\n### SKYLARK NIR\n\n## Near-infrared DPSS lasers\n\nSkylark NIR laser systems combine single frequency, low noise output and high optical efficiency \u2014\ndelivering precise, repeatable performance and ample power margin for complex or lossy setups.\n\n##### 780 nm\n\n##### up to 400 mW\n\n##### Skylark 780\n\n780 nm single frequency DPSS NIR laser\n\n[View specifications][48]\n\n##### 785 nm\n\n##### up to 400 mW\n\n##### Skylark 785\n\n785 nm single frequency DPSS NIR laser\n\n[View specifications][49]\n\n#### \"It\u2019s taken 15 years to find a suitable replacement for our HeCd laser. The Skylark 320 DPSS\n#### laser has a clean mode without filters.\"\n\nOPTICAL GRATING MANUFACTURER\n\n### Pushing the capabilities of photonics to engineer ultra-stable single frequency DPSS lasers\n\nFrom optomechanical design to software development, our team pushes the capabilities of laser\ntechnology to engineer ultra-stable, spectrally pure single frequency DPSS lasers.\n\nGuided by our core values, we collaborate with our customers and research partners to develop DPSS\nlasers tailored to your application.\n\nAmbition\nOur team pursues the challenge of miniaturising laser technology to enable the world\u2019s most\ndemanding and cutting-edge applications \u2013 reducing cost, weight, and size while maximising power and\nperformance.\nInnovation\nWe develop and commercialise lasers with the purest spectral properties to reveal the unseen, detect\nthe imperceptible, and measure the unknown.\nCollaboration\nWe work with our customers and partners to gain a deep understanding of their needs - connecting the\ndots between lasers and application to deliver tailored solutions.\nContinuous learning\nEmbodying a growth mindset, we value continuous learning and thrive in an environment of curiosity\nand exploration.\n\n### ROBUST AND RELIABLE DPSS LASERS\n\n## Built for system integration and efficient performance in demanding environments\n\n#### [Semiconductor inspection][50]\n\n#### [Quantum][51]\n\n#### [Holography][52]\n\n#### Materials analysis\n\n#### [Laser interference lithography][53]\n\n#### [Flow cytometry][54]\n\n#### [Grating manufacturing][55]\n\n#### [Brillouin microscopy][56]\n\n#### Raman + photoluminescence\n\n#### [Raman spectroscopy][57]\n\n## Request a quote\n\nTell us more about your laser and application requirements. No application is too small or too large\n- we are happy to collaborate with you to develop a solution suited to your requirements.\n\nIf you'd prefer to skip the form and chat to us directly, please email us at\nsales@skylarklasers.com.\n\nFirst name\n\nLast name\n\nEmail\n\nPhone number\n\nOrganisation\n\nWhere did you hear about Skylark Lasers?\n\nWavelength320 nm349 nm780 nm785 nmOther (specify in your message)\n\nOutput power\n\nTell us about your application area and laser requirements\n\n\n#### \"The Skylark 780 DPSS laser is very stable, we never lose the Rubidium frequency.\"\n\nMICROSCOPE SYSTEM MANUFACTURER\n\n#### \"It\u2019s taken 15 years to find a suitable replacement for our HeCd laser. The Skylark 320 DPSS\n#### laser has a clean mode without filters.\"\n\nOPTICAL GRATING MANUFACTURER\n\n#### \"I looked at 182 lasers from all different manufacturers. Skylark Lasers was the final choice.\"\n\nSEMICONDUCTOR INSPECTION OEM\n\n[[Skylark Lasers logo]][58]\nSkylark Lasers Limited\nRatho Park Phase One,\n88 Glasgow Rd\nRatho Station,\nEdinburgh, EH28 8PP\n+44 (0)131 333 2200\n\n\u00a9 2026 Skylark Lasers Limited\nRegistered in Scotland SC 445 554\n* [Privacy policy][59]\n* [Terms and conditions of sale][60]\n* [Support][61]\n\n[1]: https://skylarklasers.com\n[2]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/\n[3]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/320-nx/\n[4]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/349-nx/\n[5]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/780-nx/\n[6]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/785-nx/\n[7]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/\n[8]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-lithography/\n[9]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/optical-grating-mastering-lasers/\n[10]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-semiconductor/\n[11]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-quantum/\n[12]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-brillouin/\n[13]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-raman-spectroscopy/\n[14]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/holography/\n[15]: https://skylarklasers.com/applications/lasers-for-flow-cytometry/\n[16]: https://skylarklasers.com/about/\n[17]: https://skylarklasers.com/news/\n[18]: https://skylarklasers.com/careers/\n[19]: https://skylarklasers.com/distributors/\n[20]: https://skylarklasers.com/events/\n[21]: https://skylarklasers.com/research-development-innovation/\n[22]: /product-quote-request\n[23]: #\n[24]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/\n[25]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/320-nx/\n[26]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/349-nx/\n[27]: https://skylarklasers.com/products/780-nx/\n[28]: https://skyla