        "crawl_text": "[Skip to content][1]\n* [Media][2]\n* [FAQ][3]\n* [News][4]\nTop Bar Nav\nXcimer Energy Corporation\nLaser fusion without limits\n[[Xcimer Energy Corporation]][5]\n* [Company][6]\n* [Energy][7]\n* [Defense][8]\n* [Careers][9]\n  * [Jobs][10]\n  * [Internships][11]\n* [Company][12]\n* [Energy][13]\n* [Defense][14]\n* [Careers][15]\n  * [Internships][16]\n* [Media][17]\n* [FAQ][18]\n* [News][19]\n\n# **Laser fusion**\n# without limits\n\n## Xcimer is building the world's biggest, brightest and most powerful lasers to commercialize the\n## only scientifically validated form of fusion energy on Earth.\n\n[ 06/10/2026 U.S. Department of Energy approves Xcimer\u2019s fusion power plant preconceptual design and\ntechnology roadmap milestone ][20] [ 06/03/2026 Xcimer Energy announces the start of operations for\nPhoenix, a prototype system for industrial-scale laser fusion architecture ][21]\n[ More News ][22]\n\n## PHOENIX\n\nXcimer is the most technically mature laser fusion company.\n\nIn 2024, we broke ground on our first high-energy laser system, Phoenix. It\u2019s now up and running.\n\nLocated in our Denver laser bay, Phoenix features the first electron-beam-pumped excimer laser built\nin the private sector, and the first of its kind from any organization in more than 20 years.\n\nPhoenix demonstrates long-pulse excimer laser operation (which unlocks cost savings), and a pulse\ncompression technique known as Stimulated Brillouin Scattering (SBS) to shrink microsecond-long\nexcimer laser pulses down to a nanosecond while avoiding all optics damage challenges.\n\nPhoenix is the world's highest-energy use of SBS. It validates key elements of Xcimer's low-cost,\nhigh-energy laser fusion architecture. Now we are ready to scale.\n\n[Technical CAD illustration of Xcimer\u2019s Phoenix high-energy excimer laser system in the Denver laser\nbay.]\n[Aerial view of Xcimer\u2019s Phoenix laser facility, parking, and surrounding industrial buildings.]\n\n## ATHENA\n\nOur work on Phoenix builds toward Athena, the world's first laser fusion power plant.\n\nAthena will represent the start of Earth's commercial fusion energy era.\n\nBy 2035, we expect Athena to deliver 400 megawatts of safe, clean, affordable energy, around the\nclock, with fuel derived from seawater and lithium, cost-competitive with fossil fuels and\nrenewables.\n\nAthena is based on the most credible roadmap in fusion, relying on proven science and commercially\nscalable technologies. Xcimer's power plant architecture bypasses material science and maintenance\nchallenges, resulting in extremely competitive economics.\n\n[Isometric architectural rendering of Athena, Xcimer\u2019s planned commercial laser fusion power plant.]\n[Supplemental diagram inset for the Athena fusion power plant visualization.]\n[Exterior rear-view architectural rendering of the Athena laser fusion power plant campus.]\n[ Learn More About Laser Fusion ][23]\n\n## Read our **detailed roadmap**\n\nLaser-driven inertial fusion is the only fusion approach that has been scientifically proven. Read\nour February 2026 white paper with TRUMPF Laser SE to see how our gas excimer laser architecture\nmakes it economical and scalable.\n\n[Read the white paper][24]\n\n## **Meet the team** commercializing fusion\n\nNearly 200 engineers, physicists, and business professionals are turning proven science into crucial\ntechnology \u2014 with industry-leading execution. Learn about our mission, culture and values.\n\n[Discover Xcimer][25]\n\n## **Fusion:** The ultimate energy source\n\nOur fusion power plants will unlock energy-intensive industries that require firm, abundant,\ncarbon-free power, from AI training clusters to desalination and industrial decarbonization. Join\nthe team commercializing the ultimate energy source.\n\n#### **Safe**\n\nNo chain reactions, no meltdowns. Fuel is a kind of hydrogen used in watch dials.\n\n#### **Abundant**\n\nFuel produced from seawater and lithium. Enough fuel for millions of years. No foreign supply\nchains.\u00a0\n\n#### **Economical**\n\nWe\u2019ve designed our system from the ground up to compete on cost with fossil fuels and renewables.\n\n#### **Clean**\n\nNo emissions. No pollutants. The only byproducts from our power plants? Helium and heat.\n\n[Join Us][26]\n[10325 East 47th Ave.\nDenver, CO 80238, USA][27]\n[Linkedin page opens in new window][28][YouTube page opens in new window][29]\n**Information**\n[info@xcimer.energy][30]\n\n**Media**\n[media@xcimer.energy][31]\n\n**Careers**\n[careers@xcimer.energy][32]\nQuick Links:\n* [Company][33]\n* [Energy][34]\n* [Defense][35]\n* [Careers][36]\n* [Media][37]\n* [FAQ][38]\n* [News][39]\n* [Copyright 2026. Xcimer Energy. All rights reserved.][40]\n* [Accessibility Statement][41]\n* [Privacy Policy][42]\n* [Terms Of Use][43]\n* [Conflict Of Interest Policy][44]\n* [Cookie Preferences][45]\n[Go to Top][46]\n\n[1]: #content\n[2]: https://xcimer.energy/media/\n[3]: https://xcimer.energy/faq/\n[4]: https://xcimer.energy/news/\n[5]: https://xcimer.energy/\n[6]: https://xcimer.energy/company/\n[7]: https://xcimer.energy/energy/\n[8]: https://xcimer.energy/defense/\n[9]: https://xcimer.energy/caree [Skip to content][1]\n* [Media][2]\n* [FAQ][3]\n* [News][4]\nTop Bar Nav\nXcimer Energy Corporation\nLaser fusion without limits\n[[Xcimer Energy Corporation]][5]\n* [Company][6]\n* [Energy][7]\n* [Defense][8]\n* [Careers][9]\n  * [Jobs][10]\n  * [Internships][11]\n* [Company][12]\n* [Energy][13]\n* [Defense][14]\n* [Careers][15]\n  * [Internships][16]\n* [Media][17]\n* [FAQ][18]\n* [News][19]\n\n# **Laser fusion**\n# without limits\n\n## Xcimer is building the world's biggest, brightest and most powerful lasers to commercialize the\n## only scientifically validated form of fusion energy on Earth.\n\n[ 06/10/2026 U.S. Department of Energy approves Xcimer\u2019s fusion power plant preconceptual design and\ntechnology roadmap milestone ][20] [ 06/03/2026 Xcimer Energy announces the start of operations for\nPhoenix, a prototype system for industrial-scale laser fusion architecture ][21]\n[ More News ][22]\n\n## PHOENIX\n\nXcimer is the most technically mature laser fusion company.\n\nIn 2024, we broke ground on our first high-energy laser system, Phoenix. It\u2019s now up and running.\n\nLocated in our Denver laser bay, Phoenix features the first electron-beam-pumped excimer laser built\nin the private sector, and the first of its kind from any organization in more than 20 years.\n\nPhoenix demonstrates long-pulse excimer laser operation (which unlocks cost savings), and a pulse\ncompression technique known as Stimulated Brillouin Scattering (SBS) to shrink microsecond-long\nexcimer laser pulses down to a nanosecond while avoiding all optics damage challenges.\n\nPhoenix is the world's highest-energy use of SBS. It validates key elements of Xcimer's low-cost,\nhigh-energy laser fusion architecture. Now we are ready to scale.\n\n[Technical CAD illustration of Xcimer\u2019s Phoenix high-energy excimer laser system in the Denver laser\nbay.]\n[Aerial view of Xcimer\u2019s Phoenix laser facility, parking, and surrounding industrial buildings.]\n\n## ATHENA\n\nOur work on Phoenix builds toward Athena, the world's first laser fusion power plant.\n\nAthena will represent the start of Earth's commercial fusion energy era.\n\nBy 2035, we expect Athena to deliver 400 megawatts of safe, clean, affordable energy, around the\nclock, with fuel derived from seawater and lithium, cost-competitive with fossil fuels and\nrenewables.\n\nAthena is based on the most credible roadmap in fusion, relying on proven science and commercially\nscalable technologies. Xcimer's power plant architecture bypasses material science and maintenance\nchallenges, resulting in extremely competitive economics.\n\n[Isometric architectural rendering of Athena, Xcimer\u2019s planned commercial laser fusion power plant.]\n[Supplemental diagram inset for the Athena fusion power plant visualization.]\n[Exterior rear-view architectural rendering of the Athena laser fusion power plant campus.]\n[ Learn More About Laser Fusion ][23]\n\n## Read our **detailed roadmap**\n\nLaser-driven inertial fusion is the only fusion approach that has been scientifically proven. Read\nour February 2026 white paper with TRUMPF Laser SE to see how our gas excimer laser architecture\nmakes it economical and scalable.\n\n[Read the white paper][24]\n\n## **Meet the team** commercializing fusion\n\nNearly 200 engineers, physicists, and business professionals are turning proven science into crucial\ntechnology \u2014 with industry-leading execution. Learn about our mission, culture and values.\n\n[Discover Xcimer][25]\n\n## **Fusion:** The ultimate energy source\n\nOur fusion power plants will unlock energy-intensive industries that require firm, abundant,\ncarbon-free power, from AI training clusters to desalination and industrial decarbonization. Join\nthe team commercializing the ultimate energy source.\n\n#### **Safe**\n\nNo chain reactions, no meltdowns. Fuel is a kind of hydrogen used in watch dials.\n\n#### **Abundant**\n\nFuel produced from seawater and lithium. Enough fuel for millions of years. No foreign supply\nchains.\u00a0\n\n#### **Economical**\n\nWe\u2019ve designed our system from the ground up to compete on cost with fossil fuels and renewables.\n\n#### **Clean**\n\nNo emissions. No pollutants. The only byproducts from our power plants? Helium and heat.\n\n[Join Us][26]\n[10325 East 47th Ave.\nDenver, CO 80238, USA][27]\n[Linkedin page opens in new window][28][YouTube page opens in new window][29]\n**Information**\n[info@xcimer.energy][30]\n\n**Media**\n[media@xcimer.energy][31]\n\n**Careers**\n[careers@xcimer.energy][32]\nQuick Links:\n* [Company][33]\n* [Energy][34]\n* [Defense][35]\n* [Careers][36]\n* [Media][37]\n* [FAQ][38]\n* [News][39]\n* [Copyright 2026. Xcimer Energy. All rights reserved.][40]\n* [Accessibility Statement][41]\n* [Privacy Policy][42]\n* [Terms Of Use][43]\n* [Conflict Of Interest Policy][44]\n* [Cookie Preferences][45]\n[Go to Top][46]\n\n[1]: #content\n[2]: https://xcimer.energy/media/\n[3]: https://xcimer.energy/faq/\n[4]: https://xcimer.energy/news/\n[5]: https://xcimer.energy/\n[6]: https://xcimer.energy/company/\n[7]: https://xcimer.energy/energy/\n[8]: https://xcimer.energy/defense/\n[9]: https://xcimer.energy/careers/\n[10]: /careers#Job_Listings\n[11]: https://xcimer.energy/careers/internships/\n[12]: https://xcimer.energy/company/\n[13]: https://xcimer.energy/energy/\n[14]: https://xcimer.energy/defense/\n[15]: https://xcimer.energy/careers/\n[16]: https://xcimer.energy/careers/internships/\n[17]: https://xcimer.energy/media/\n[18]: https://xcimer.energy/faq/\n[19]: https://xcimer.energy/news/\n[20]: https://xcimer.energy/news/u-s-department-of-energy-approves-xcimers-fusion-power-plant-precon\nceptual-design-and-technology-roadmap-milestone/\n[21]: https://xcimer.energy/news/xcimer-energy-announces-the-start-of-operations-for-phoenix-a-proto\ntype-system-for-industrial-scale-laser-fusion-architecture/\n[22]: https://xcimer.energy/news/\n[23]: /energy\n[24]: /wp-content/uploads/2026/04/XEC-20260224-Commercialization-of-LFE-Whtppr-SHARED-24-FEB-26.pdf\n[25]: https://xcimer.energy/company/\n[26]: https://xcimer.energy/careers/\n[27]: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=10325+East+47th+Ave+Denver+CO+80238\n[28]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/xcimer-energy-corporation\n[29]: https://www.youtube.com/@XcimerEnergy\n[30]: mailto:info@xcimer.energy\n[31]: mailto:media@xcimer.energy\n[32]: mailto:careers@xcimer.energy\n[33]: https://xcimer.energy/company/\n[34]: https://xcimer.energy/energy/\n[35]: https://xcimer.energy/defense/\n[36]: https://xcimer.energy/careers/\n[37]: https://xcimer.energy/media/\n[38]: https://xcimer.energy/faq/\n[39]: https://xcimer.energy/news/\n[40]: #\n[41]: https://xcimer.energy/accessibility-statement/\n[42]: https://xcimer.energy/privacy-policy/\n[